menseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T01:32:10-08:00","id":70425,"title":"","content":"Zane is probably in her 20s, but looks younger (she has eternal youth) and behaves in a somewhat childlike manner sometimes, other times she is more adultlike.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T02:49:09-08:00","id":76160,"title":"","content":"Between Session update, Background of Edmond Cross who will be appearing in the next session. He should be a long term PC<br /> <br /> <b>Edmond Cross, Scion of Dionysus, Dodekatheon</b><br /> <br /> <u>The Wreck of Edmond Cross</u><br /> <br /> \u201cHello, you\u2019re on the air.\u201d<br /> The voice on the other end of the phone was courteous, with a practiced politeness. Edmund had no idea who the voice belonged to.<br /> \u201cUm\u2026what? What\u2019s going on?\u201d A muttered confusion was all Edmund could offer. He tried to remember why he was on the telephone or what he was supposed to be doing.<br /> \u201cYou\u2019re on the air, sir,\u201d the nice voice encouraged. \u201cGo ahead and tell us what you think.\u201d<br /> \u201cUm\u2026\u201d the only recourse Edmund could fall back on was honesty. \u201cI think\u2026I think I feel like I\u2019m going to throw up.\u201d<br /> \u201cExactly my point,\u201d another voice came in. This one wasn\u2019t nice. It was loud and demanding. \u201cThe politics in this country makes us sick. It is a mess, and quite frankly it\u2019s an insult to the average voter\u2026\u201d<br /> Not sure what to do, and afraid that if he hung up he\u2019d wreck whatever it was he was supposed to be doing, Edmund carefully laid the receiver down on the scuffed top of an end table and slowly backed away from the phone.<br /> Edmund Cross was an artist, but usually that was just an excuse made to cover up how broken he was. There were often times, like this one, when Edmund would come to himself, the fog in his mind clearing like a light switch being thrown, and he would have no idea where he was or what he was doing. <br /> Living in a fugue state is only a problem when rational thought intrudes. <br /> He had read somewhere how concussion victims would describe returning to consciousness like waking from a dream, only to discover that they were in the midst of an unknown situation and would slowly have to reconstruct the sequence of events. Edmund often felt that way, but he didn\u2019t blame head trauma so much as the massive amounts of drugs and alcohol he habitually consumed.<br /> The room he was in was chaotic. It held a couch which was torn in places, worn odds and ends of furniture, the phone, and a lamp without a lampshade. It was student squalor, the kind one might find around art college people. Edmund didn\u2019t know if it was some sort of low-rent flat or an abandoned building where squatters had taken up residence.<br /> He found other people in the next room. The air was filled with a haze of smoke, some of it tobacco. Two men with guitars chatted quietly with each other while a third seemed to doze behind a massive set of drums. Another man stood in the center of the room, eyes closed and arms outstretched, spinning slowly in a beatific trance all his own. In the hand of the spinning man was an open bottle of Cabernet Sauvignon wine. The bottle was half-empty. Edmund was a pessimist. Microphones, wires and a variety of amplifiers littered the claustrophobic space.<br /> There was also a surprisingly attractive girl there. She wore a torn t-shirt which showed off her bare midriff and a pair of strikingly tight pants. Perched, as she was, on top of a battered bar stool, the hip-hugging waistband of those pants wasn\u2019t up to the task of modesty. Edmund tried not to stare.<br /> When Edmund entered the wine-bottle-guy opened his eyes and asked, \u201cDude, did you order our pizzas?\u201d<br /> \u201cUm\u2026\u201d Edmund stammered, \u201cI\u2026I think we\u2019re on the radio.\u201d He gestured vaguely to where he had come from.<br /> \u201cRockin\u2019!\u201d one of the guitar men exclaimed. The drummer snapped back to life as the group of them proceeded to produce a raucous racket which might have been music. It was easily loud enough to be heard over the phone in the other room, but by that time the switchboard operator had cut them off.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Edmund never really fit in anywhere. He was often seen as weird and an outsider. It didn\u2019t help that he always heard voices, and had done so ever since he was young. Sometimes he would see things that weren\u2019t there, and the semi-reality of the world around him seemed normal. Some people said that he had a dark, brooding nature which lent an air of mystery to his art. Others merely called him psychotic. When he couldn\u2019t be sure if the person talking to him was real or just in his head, it didn\u2019t help convince people to think otherwise.<br /> Edmund came from a family full of artists and creative souls. He was raised on the Isle of Mann, the self-governed island between England and Ireland. Even though the Isle of Mann had its own government, it was still a protectorate of England, so most everyone thought of Edmund as British, even though he always introduced himself as being \u201cMann-ish.\u201d<br /> He grew up surrounded by musicians, poets and painters who instilled in him the idea that truth was beauty and that details didn\u2019t really matter. When he was very young, he was told that he had been named after a particular musical ballad. It wasn\u2019t until years later that Edmund Fitzgerald Cross learned that the song he had been named for described a real life maritime disaster in America which had claimed the lives of twenty-nine men. His childhood was full of uncomfortable revelations like that.<br /> The family he belonged to was more of a sprawling, semi-nomadic commune. They saw themselves as \u201cfree-spirits,\u201d whereas locals often called them \u201cvagrants\u201d and the police called them \u201ctax-dodgers.\u201d<br /> The most important person in his life growing up was his mother, Sylvia; often called \u201cSilly Sylvie.\u201d She was strongly bohemian, a believer in nature spirits and a self-professed psychic. Her first love was music, but she constantly embraced new crafts, latching onto pottery or wood block prints and the like. She was always making things and giving them away as gifts, be it a slightly slumped glazed vase or a knit square of yarn which couldn\u2019t really serve as a blanket. Her creativity was only matched by her lack of focus.<br /> Edmund was also close to a half-brother named Mark. Mark was several years older than Edmund. At some point Mark disappeared mysteriously, only to reemerge in America, in some artist colony somewhere in New England.<br /> Then there were his aunts, his mother\u2019s sisters, who also had a hand in shaping young Edmund. There was Auntie Mary, who was legitimately good at sculpture and was the only one with any money sense. There was Auntie Nelda who was a professional leech. She used her charm and the sufferance of friends and family to get by. And most notably there was Auntie Lori, Edmund\u2019s favorite. Auntie Lori was unpredictable and gregarious. Her main occupation seemed to be travel. She would constantly disappear to some strange corner of the world, only to return with exotic gifts and fantastic stories. There was never a suitable explanation as to how Auntie Lori could afford her globe-trotting life-style, other than the fact that she seemed to live a blessed life. Good things always seemed to happen to her.<br /> When he was a teenager, Edmund discovered that Lori was, in fact, his real mother and Sylvia was the aunt who had raised him. Lori had met a dashing stranger on one of her many adventures and had returned home, after wine, roses and romance, with little Edmund growing inside her. She had made the decision to leave Edmund with her sisters in the hopes that a \u201cmore stable\u201d upbringing would be better for him. Edmund was not embittered by this revelation. In fact, it helped explain quite a lot.<br /> As a young man, Edmund somehow managed to scrape together the funds to enter the Edinburgh College of Art at the University of Edinburgh. Living life at the University was a dream come true for him, while the main voice inside his head was telling Edmund to get out and see more of the world. When his studies took him to Spain, the birthplace of Picasso, Edmund simply never came back.<br /> Ever since then Edmund has wandered from country to country and continent to continent, more as a series of accidents than with any real agenda. Like with his mother\u2014his real mother\u2014life seemed to find a way to keep Edmund moving.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Edmund turned twenty in America. He was in Arizona, where the hot desert days faded to cold, windy nights. It was on just such a night that he found himself in a drive-in theater off of some barren stretch of road. The days of the drive-in had come to an end, but the dilapidated property had been bought by an art-house collective. Every year they hosted a film festival where they showed avant-garde and independent films for three days straight. People would come from miles around to camp out for the duration. Inevitably it turned into a bacchanalian carnival.<br /> Edmund had borrowed a convertible from a friend and had driven it down for the film festival. With a cooler, a sleeping bag and a pair of blankets, that car became his home for those three days.<br /> The last night of the festival was amazing. The sky was clear, the stars were intensely bright and a full moon slowly rose over the desert. They were playing a series of films from Latin America, with no subtitles. Edmund didn\u2019t speak Spanish, but there was a vitality and a passion to the films that made the need for language secondary.<br /> He was so enraptured by the screen that he didn\u2019t see the stranger until she leaned a hip against the side of the car door. She had the smoky, sultry mystery of a Mexican beauty. With trim, tan limbs, full, glossy black hair and dangerous eyes, it was as if a Latino goddess had stepped off the screen. She stood there in a halter top and cut-off jean shorts, leaning against the car as though she were in an advertisement. Edmund wondered whether or not she was cold, but felt too embarrassed to voice the question. Without a word this woman reached out an imploring hand to Edmund.<br /> Edmund didn\u2019t know what he was supposed to do. Who was this woman? What was her expectation? After a moment of indecision he handed her the open wine bottle in his hand. He preferred wine to beer. It was more artsy, and generally there was more of it per bottle.<br /> The stranger not only took the wine, but what Edmund was smoking. She took a couple of puffs and then a long drink from the bottle. When she was done she gave a pleased sigh and threw both the wine and the joint dismissively behind her. Edmund made a small noise of dismay, but his complaint was cut off when the stranger climbed over the top of the door and into the car. Seeing as how she had entered from the driver\u2019s side, she ended up straddling Edmund.<br /> Edmund was beginning to feel scared, now. She was so pretty Edmund found it hard to look at her. But given where she was, he didn\u2019t have much of a choice. Her smoldering stare kept him pinned to the seat. Though the position they shared was very provocative, the glint in her eye was one of mischief more than lust.<br /> On the big screen the film continued unheeded.<br /> She spoke for a long moment in the rapid-fire, lyrical speech of American Spanish. Edmund looked left and right, but there was no help forthcoming.<br /> \u201cUm\u2026I don\u2019t speak\u2026that language,\u201d he muttered.<br /> \u201cYou, I have been watching,\u201d she switched to English, the hints of her accent as attractive as the rest of her. \u201cYou pass through life as the wind passes through the trees. You bask in the sun and soak up the dark; embracing the gifts of life without begrudging what it is you lack. I say to you, the beings of heaven look upon those like you and smile.\u201d<br /> \u201cUm\u2026\u201d Edmund had nothing to say to that. \u201cYour\u2026um\u2026hair looks pretty in the moonlight.\u201d The words just came out on their own.<br /> The stranger smiled.<br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s this?\u201d she asked. Her slim fingered hand reached down to his jeans. She reached in and pulled out the film festival ticket-stub from his pocket.<br /> \u201cMoonlight is the sister to darkness and candles,\u201d she said. \u201cIt is inside intoxicating wine and elusive music; the setting of romance. But it is also the light of lunacy and the harbinger of madness. For your heart of openness and acceptance I bring you ecstasy and insanity; enlightenment beyond the corners of the rational world.\u201d<br /> She spoke in a soft, subtle chant, as though the words belonged to some ancient song or were from some spell older than mortal magic. She kissed the ticket-stub, leaving lipstick marks over the printed words, \u201cMoon-Lite Drive-In,\u201d and slid the slip of paper back into his pocket. Then she started to unzip his jeans.<br /> That was the night Edmund lost his virginity. His recollection of the evening ended up confused but grateful.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Edmund slowly became aware of his surroundings. His ears were filled with the hum of florescent lights. He was in a brightly lit room. It was too bright. The light hurt his eyes and the shabby white acoustic tiles of the ceiling reflected the glare. Looking down, Edmund saw white again. He was holding a Styrofoam cup. The cup was partially filled with coffee which looked like it had been there for a while. It didn\u2019t steam and it had stained the interior of the cup with brown rings. Its inky blackness seemed mysterious, as though its depths held secrets Edmund was better off not knowing. He took a sip and it was cold and bitter.<br /> There were voices in the room with him. Voices with American accents. They held the soft susurration of Southern accents, or perhaps were from the Mid-West. He would discover some time later that he was in the northern part of Texas, somewhere along the border of Oklahoma, and for days afterward the theme song from the Rodgers and Hammerstein musical <i>Oklahoma!</i> would be stuck in his head.<br /> Edmund was seated on a hard, metal folding chair, in a circle of other people in similar chairs. One person was on his feet\u2014in cowboy boots\u2014and he was talking in his Texan drawl. He had been talking for some time, Edmund realized.<br /> \u201cAnd that\u2019s why, because my family, I\u2019ll never touch another drop again.\u201d<br /> There was a smattering of applause from the group in response to this impassioned declaration. Edmund couldn\u2019t both clap and hold his coffee, so he just cradled his cup in both hands. A dowdy woman wearing too much red lipstick hugged the speaker, murmuring, \u201cThank you, Bill. That was very moving.\u201d Then they both sat down and the lipstick lady said, \u201cOkay, who\u2019s next?\u201d<br /> There was a moment of brittle silence. Edmund sipped his coffee again; its taste instantly reminding him why he wasn\u2019t drinking it, but the unintended sound of his slurp came out uncomfortably loud. Then another man stood up. This man was large, not too tall, but heavy-set. However he carried his heaviness well, with a natural grace that said he was exactly as big as he was supposed to be. He had dark hair and eyes which seemed distinctly Mediterranean, but Edmund couldn\u2019t place his accent. He wasn\u2019t American.<br /> \u201cThis\u2026whole thing,\u201d the man began uncertainly, spreading his hands to encompass the room, \u201cit\u2019s supposed to be anonymous, right?\u201d<br /> \u201cYes,\u201d the lipstick lady assured encouragingly, \u201cit\u2019s okay to tell us whatever you want. It won\u2019t leave this building.\u201d<br /> The big man nodded, scanning the people around him. He looked at each person\u2019s face in turn with a scrutiny that said his next words were going to be important.<br /> \u201cMy name is Bacchus, the god of wine,\u201d the man announced. \u201cSome of you may know me as Dionysus. I\u2019m not an alcoholic, but I love to drink.\u201d<br /> \u201cSir,\u201d the lipstick lady interrupted. Her caring demeanor was replaced with a waspish disapproval. \u201cIf you\u2019re not going to take this meeting seriously, then we\u2019re going to have to ask you to leave.\u201d<br /> \u201cWait. Hear me out,\u201d the big man countered. Then he launched into a speech which was nothing short of mythical. He was like a preacher at his pulpit, delivering a sermon on the grace of grapes. In many ways it was quite conservative. He spoke of how one should \u201cdrink to live, not live to drink\u201d and how drinking one\u2019s self into oblivion was contrary to the purpose of spirits. But he also talked of the wonders of fermentation and how alcohol was a gift of the gods for men to live well and enjoy life; how it was meant to inspire, not destroy. It seemed so very contradictory, but at the time, the way he told it, it all seemed to make perfect sense.<br /> When he was done there was enthusiastic applause from the other members there. All except the lipstick lady, who was trying to constructively channel her anger and Edmund, who was still holding his coffee. The others were all up on their feet, hugging the big man, thanking him for his words. It dawned on Edmund that he was expected to join in, or worse, that he may be asked to speak next. With a sense of panic he hurriedly left the building.<br /> Outside he found he was still at a loss of what to do with his coffee. Looking right and left to make sure he was alone, Edmund dumped his cup and its contents behind some bushes.<br /> \u201cThey are something, you know?\u201d said a voice. It was the big man, the one who called himself Bacchus, emerging from the shadows behind Edmund.<br /> \u201cThey? Who?\u201d Edmund asked, worried about being caught littering.<br /> \u201cMortals. They get so much wonderfully right, and yet\u2026fall so short.\u201d He shook his head in kind bemusement.<br /> \u201cI don\u2019t understand,\u201d Edmund said. He was just being honest.<br /> \u201cA \u2018twelve-step program\u2019,\u201d the big man mused, \u201cso many good ideas, but not quite right. Life is a journey, as the poets say, but the mistakes made along the way are just as valid as any of the other steps a person may take.\u201d<br /> Edmund bit his lip and wondered if he had a car nearby. Not that he knew where he was going to go if he did.<br /> \u201cHere, take this,\u201d the big man flipped something like a coin over to Edmund. \u201cKeep it. It may come in useful one day.\u201d<br /> Edmund looked at what the man had given him. It was an AA token. He put it in his pocket, not because he wanted to keep it, but because he hoped that by appeasing this strange man he might stop talking to him.<br /> The big man walked past Edmund, patting him on the shoulder.<br /> \u201cEmbrace the journey, Edmund,\u201d the stranger said. \u201cEven when you stumble you still make progress.\u201d<br /> \u201cHow..?\u201d Edmund turned around, but he was alone in a parking lot on a muggy Texan night.<br /> That was the first time Edmund met his father.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Edmund was in a robe, like a bath robe, tied closed with a sash. It was actually a Yukata, a Japanese robe from an Onsen, a hot-spring resort somewhere in Hokkaido. How it came to be with him in Amsterdam Edmund couldn\u2019t recall, but he often wore it when he couldn\u2019t remember what had happened to the rest of his clothes.<br /> He stared intently at his coffee pot. It was an electric percolator from the 1950s. Soon enough the ancient appliance made the gurgling sounds that meant it was working. It sat on a hot plate on a table in the middle of his studio. The hot plate itself was defunct. Bad wiring kept Edmund from plugging it in for fear that it might start a fire, but it served as a suitable resting spot for his coffee pot, which itself might also have been a fire hazard. In Edmund\u2019s art studio, with paint thinner, old rags, canvas and bits of wood, fire was a real concern. That didn\u2019t stop him from smoking, though.<br /> \u201cOh, Edward, you\u2019re in!\u201d said a bright voice.<br /> \u201cJi-Woo?\u201d Edmund asked. He knew that voice and he knew it meant trouble. But usually a good kind of trouble.<br /> A figure breezed into the room as though she had every right to be there. Ji-Woo was a young Korean woman, perfectly at ease in her own skin and completely beautiful. Secretly he felt envious. At her worst Ji-Woo was a beautiful disaster, while at his best Edmund was still a bit scruffy looking. She always called him \u201cEdward.\u201d Edmund suspected that she knew his real name, but she just didn\u2019t care. And Ji-Woo always appeared as sudden as a storm. She blew in unannounced, tumbled things around like a tempest and then left without warning, leaving behind artful wreckage in her path. Edmund had often been a victim of her unpredictable enthusiasm.<br /> \u201cWhy\u2026\u201d Edmund began, \u201cWhat are you doing here?\u201d<br /> \u201cOh,\u201d Ji-Woo gave her best disarming smile, \u201cI was in town and needed a place to stay.\u201d<br /> \u201cI\u2026um\u2026well\u2026\u201d<br /> \u201cThanks, I knew you wouldn\u2019t mind. Do you have anything to eat?\u201d<br /> \u201cUm\u2026coffee.\u201d<br /> \u201cHmm\u2026\u201d Ji-Woo tapped her lips with a colorful fingernail and regarded Edmund critically over the tops of her sunglasses. \u201cWe\u2019re going to need more than that.\u201d<br /> She tucked a long strand of black hair behind an ear and reached into her bag. She pulled out a handful of coins and tossed them into the air with an experienced fluidity. The coins landed with nice metallic clinks. Ji-Woo studied the way the coins had landed sedulously, and then she gathered them up and tossed them again. And again. She was doing an I Cheng reading.<br /> After a number of tosses, interspersed with the odd, \u201cThat\u2019s interesting,\u201d and a \u201cHuh, I\u2019ve never gotten anything like that before,\u201d Ji-Woo remarked about things like \u201cno transforming lines\u201d and how it \u201cexactly altered Yin and Yang for every bar.\u201d Then she returned her attention back to Edmund.<br /> \u201cWhen was the last time you left the studio?\u201d she asked him.<br /> \u201cI\u2026what month is it?\u201d Edmund couldn\u2019t honestly remember.<br /> \u201cI got the \u2018Already Fording\u2019 reading,\u201d Ji-Woo told him gravely. \u201cIt tells me that it\u2019s time to ford the stream of events. It also tells me that it\u2019s time to end the cycle of disarray.\u201d She peered around the studio. \u201cAnd you are surrounded by disarray. We need to find you a girlfriend.\u201d<br /> Edmund failed to follow her logic.<br /> \u201cI have friends\u2026who are girls,\u201d he defended.<br /> \u201cThat\u2019s not what I mean.\u201d<br /> \u201cI have female sexual companions. It\u2019s exactly what you mean.\u201d In his experience lovers did nothing to lessen disarray, but rather added to the confusion of his life.<br /> \u201cWell, yes, you\u2019re right,\u201d Ji-Woo admitted, \u201cbut that doesn\u2019t make me wrong. Get dressed. We\u2019re going out.\u201d<br /> \u201cUm\u2026\u201d Edmund felt a sense of rising panic. Part of him was glad, the part of him that was delighted by the unexpected and the strange. Another part of him, however, the part which was afraid and just wanted to be left alone\u2014the larger part\u2014wanted to ask her to leave. But one did not ask Ji-Woo to leave. One only weathered the storm. It wasn\u2019t unknown for Ji-Woo to sweep Edmund up in her torrent of activity only to forget about him later, abandoning him at some techno dance club where he had no friends, no idea where he was, and no way to get home. That didn\u2019t mean that they weren\u2019t good times. Nonetheless Edmund had the feeling that \u201cending the cycle of disarray\u201d was only going to lead to chaos.<br /> And he wasn\u2019t wrong.<br /> Days later, when Edmund returned to his studio, he found that Ji-Woo had disappeared again. With his coffee pot.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Edmund stared silently at the canvas before him. The studio was a mess. It was an apocalypse of paint, drop cloths, brushes and clutter; but the canvas stood on its easel blandly, mockingly blank. It was untouched and Edmund couldn\u2019t find any artistic resources to fill its taunting emptiness. The voices in his head were quiet tonight. Edmund\u2019s mood darkened. He turned a bottle of red wine over and over in his hands. He had lost his bottle opener.<br /> \u201cHello?\u201d Hello?\u201d a voice floated up from the doorway to the studio. For a countless time Edmund thought to himself that he should lock his door; or at the very least buy a lock for the door.<br /> The unexpected guest made his way through the mess, carefully choosing his steps until he joined Edmund, turning to face the empty canvas as well. The stranger was a large man, with a Mediterranean duskiness. They shared a moment of contemplative silence.<br /> \u201cI remember you,\u201d Edmund said.<br /> \u201cYeah?\u201d the stranger asked.<br /> \u201cYeah, you\u2019re the guy who claimed to be Bacchus.\u201d<br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d the man answered simply.<br /> There was another lengthy pause.<br /> \u201cYou\u2019re actually him, aren\u2019t you?\u201d Edmund said. He was still rolling the bottle in his hands. \u201cThe god of wine?\u201d<br /> \u201cI am.\u201d<br /> \u201cI believe you. I shouldn\u2019t, but I do.\u201d<br /> \u201cI think divine revelation is as good a reason as any for a drink, don\u2019t you agree?\u201d Bacchus said.<br /> \u201cI can\u2019t open it,\u201d Edmund confessed.<br /> Bacchus turned to search through the jumble of tools, paints and brushes on a nearby work table. He came up with a scratched and battered claw hammer, its handle wrapped in ageing duct tape and its head darkened by rust.<br /> \u201cHere we go,\u201d he said, \u201cIn case of emergency, break glass.\u201d Bacchus took the wine bottle from Edmund and smashed the neck off with an expert flick of the hammer. There was a crash of glass, a splash of wine and a muffled voice from the back of the room which sleepily complained, \u201cWhat the fuck?\u201d<br /> \u201cDo you have company over?\u201d Bacchus asked.<br /> \u201cUm\u2026yeah,\u201d Edmund said. \u201cThat\u2019s Sharon, Sandra\u2026and that\u2019s Alex.\u201d<br /> \u201cOh, I didn\u2019t see her there.\u201d<br /> \u201cYeah, she sleeps like the dead, but she was very\u2026energetic\u2026not too long ago.\u201d<br /> Bacchus found an empty glass and poured paint thinner from another one. He filled them both with wine for himself and Edmund.<br /> Edmund sipped his wine, wondering if he was swallowing tiny shards of glass.<br /> More silence.<br /> \u201cThere\u2019s something else you should know,\u201d Bacchus said after a while.<br /> \u201cUm?\u201d Edmund answered.<br /> \u201cI\u2019m also your father.\u201d Bacchus poured more wine.<br /> \u201cOh,\u201d Edmund said softly. \u201cThat\u2026that explains a lot.\u201d Then after a bit he continued, \u201cYou know, I always felt I might be...special.\u201d<br /> \u201cEveryone feels that way,\u201d Bacchus said. \u201cIt\u2019s part of the human condition. People need to feel important, need to feel like their lives mean something. It helps them get by. Sadly, however, you <i>are</i> special.\u201d<br /> \u201cUm?\u201d<br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not good news, I\u2019m afraid,\u201d he refilled their glasses again, the ruin of the bottle miraculously still held its wine. \u201cI wish I could promise you a simple life, filled with wine, women and song. Believe me when I say that\u2019s the best kind of life there is. But fate, I\u2019m afraid, wants you to play a larger role. The blood of divinity runs through your veins, which means the threads of destiny bind more tightly around you than for others. It\u2019s a terrible responsibility, but it can also be glorious. The tread of your footfalls will echo more profoundly down the halls of history.\u201d<br /> \u201cUm...what?\u201d<br /> \u201cDon\u2019t worry. You\u2019ll figure it out.\u201d<br /> The silence returned like an old friend.<br /> \u201cSo tell me, son,\u201d Bacchus said, \u201cWhy, when you have three willing and beautiful women in your house and the god of wine by your side are you spending your time looking at this scrap of white cloth?\u201d<br /> \u201cI can\u2019t paint,\u201d Edmund lifted a shoulder in a half shrug. \u201cWhen I can\u2019t paint\u2026when I can\u2019t create then I\u2026then nothing else really matters.\u201d It was a long speech for Edmund.<br /> Bacchus pondered the canvas.<br /> \u201cHere,\u201d he declared, \u201cI can\u2019t promise you happiness or success, but I can make you a gift.\u201d He poured the rest of the wine over the hammer he had used to open the bottle. \u201cNow, I have anointed this tool. Win or lose, whatever may come, you will always have the gift of inspiration.\u201d<br /> Edmund dubiously took the wine drenched hammer from his father. He looked back at the boringly blank canvas, and an idea occurred to him. He scrapped a clump of paint from his pallet onto the head of the hammer. He slung it at the canvas and a splatter of paint and wine landed just so. He spun the hammer around and scraped a line of color down the canvas with the claw end. Edmund tilted his head to one side to gauge the effect. He liked how it looked. With his free hand he spread more paint on the canvas and smashed it with the hammer. Before long Edmund was furiously painting, lost to the rest of the world.<br /> \u201cThat\u2019s my boy,\u201d Bacchus said, patting Edmund on the shoulder. \u201cYou\u2019ll be fine.\u201d Then the god of wine left, disappearing into the night as mysteriously as he arrived.<br /> Sharon, Sandra and Alex cautiously approached Edmund. They watched in awe as he worked. They weren\u2019t sure what they were seeing, but they had the feeling that they were watching the creation of something wonderful.<br /> \u201cHello, you\u2019re on the air.\u201d<br /> The voice on the other end of the phone was courteous, with a practiced politeness. Edmund had no idea who the voice belonged to.<br /> \u201cUm\u2026what? What\u2019s going on?\u201d A muttered confusion was all Edmund could offer. He tried to remember why he was on the telephone or what he was supposed to be doing.<br /> \u201cYou\u2019re on the air, sir,\u201d the nice voice encouraged. \u201cGo ahead and tell us what you think.\u201d<br /> \u201cUm\u2026\u201d the only recourse Edmund could fall back on was honesty. \u201cI think\u2026I think I feel like I\u2019m going to throw up.\u201d<br /> \u201cExactly my point,\u201d another voice came in. This one wasn\u2019t nice. It was loud and demanding. \u201cThe politics in this country makes us sick. It is a mess, and quite frankly it\u2019s an insult to the average voter\u2026\u201d<br /> Not sure what to do, and afraid that if he hung up he\u2019d wreck whatever it was he was supposed to be doing, Edmund carefully laid the receiver down on the scuffed top of an end table and slowly backed away from the phone.<br /> Edmund Cross was an artist, but usually that was just an excuse made to cover up how broken he was. There were often times, like this one, when Edmund would come to himself, the fog in his mind clearing like a light switch being thrown, and he would have no idea where he was or what he was doing. <br /> Living in a fugue state is only a problem when rational thought intrudes. <br /> He had read somewhere how concussion victims would describe returning to consciousness like waking from a dream, only to discover that they were in the midst of an unknown situation and would slowly have to reconstruct the sequence of events. Edmund often felt that way, but he didn\u2019t blame head trauma so much as the massive amounts of drugs and alcohol he habitually consumed.<br /> The room he was in was chaotic. It held a couch which was torn in places, worn odds and ends of furniture, the phone, and a lamp without a lampshade. It was student squalor, the kind one might find around art college people. Edmund didn\u2019t know if it was some sort of low-rent flat or an abandoned building where squatters had taken up residence.<br /> He found other people in the next room. The air was filled with a haze of smoke, some of it tobacco. Two men with guitars chatted quietly with each other while a third seemed to doze behind a massive set of drums. Another man stood in the center of the room, eyes closed and arms outstretched, spinning slowly in a beatific trance all his own. In the hand of the spinning man was an open bottle of Cabernet Sauvignon wine. The bottle was half-empty. Edmund was a pessimist. Microphones, wires and a variety of amplifiers littered the claustrophobic space.<br /> There was also a surprisingly attractive girl there. She wore a torn t-shirt which showed off her bare midriff and a pair of strikingly tight pants. Perched, as she was, on top of a battered bar stool, the hip-hugging waistband of those pants wasn\u2019t up to the task of modesty. Edmund tried not to stare.<br /> When Edmund entered the wine-bottle-guy opened his eyes and asked, \u201cDude, did you order our pizzas?\u201d<br /> \u201cUm\u2026\u201d Edmund stammered, \u201cI\u2026I think we\u2019re on the radio.\u201d He gestured vaguely to where he had come from.<br /> \u201cRockin\u2019!\u201d one of the guitar men exclaimed. The drummer snapped back to life as the group of them proceeded to produce a raucous racket which might have been music. It was easily loud enough to be heard over the phone in the other room, but by that time the switchboard operator had cut them off.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Edmund never really fit in anywhere. He was often seen as weird and an outsider. It didn\u2019t help that he always heard voices, and had done so ever since he was young. Sometimes he would see things that weren\u2019t there, and the semi-reality of the world around him seemed normal. Some people said that he had a dark, brooding nature which lent an air of mystery to his art. Others merely called him psychotic. When he couldn\u2019t be sure if the person talking to him was real or just in his head, it didn\u2019t help convince people to think otherwise.<br /> Edmund came from a family full of artists and creative souls. He was raised on the Isle of Mann, the self-governed island between England and Ireland. Even though the Isle of Mann had its own government, it was still a protectorate of England, so most everyone thought of Edmund as British, even though he always introduced himself as being \u201cMann-ish.\u201d<br /> He grew up surrounded by musicians, poets and painters who instilled in him the idea that truth was beauty and that details didn\u2019t really matter. When he was very young, he was told that he had been named after a particular musical ballad. It wasn\u2019t until years later that Edmund Fitzgerald Cross learned that the song he had been named for described a real life maritime disaster in America which had claimed the lives of twenty-nine men. His childhood was full of uncomfortable revelations like that.<br /> The family he belonged to was more of a sprawling, semi-nomadic commune. They saw themselves as \u201cfree-spirits,\u201d whereas locals often called them \u201cvagrants\u201d and the police called them \u201ctax-dodgers.\u201d<br /> The most important person in his life growing up was his mother, Sylvia; often called \u201cSilly Sylvie.\u201d She was strongly bohemian, a believer in nature spirits and a self-professed psychic. Her first love was music, but she constantly embraced new crafts, latching onto pottery or wood block prints and the like. She was always making things and giving them away as gifts, be it a slightly slumped glazed vase or a knit square of yarn which couldn\u2019t really serve as a blanket. Her creativity was only matched by her lack of focus.<br /> Edmund was also close to a half-brother named Mark. Mark was several years older than Edmund. At some point Mark disappeared mysteriously, only to reemerge in America, in some artist colony somewhere in New England.<br /> Then there were his aunts, his mother\u2019s sisters, who also had a hand in shaping young Edmund. There was Auntie Mary, who was legitimately good at sculpture and was the only one with any money sense. There was Auntie Nelda who was a professional leech. She used her charm and the sufferance of friends and family to get by. And most notably there was Auntie Lori, Edmund\u2019s favorite. Auntie Lori was unpredictable and gregarious. Her main occupation seemed to be travel. She would constantly disappear to some strange corner of the world, only to return with exotic gifts and fantastic stories. There was never a suitable explanation as to how Auntie Lori could afford her globe-trotting life-style, other than the fact that she seemed to live a blessed life. Good things always seemed to happen to her.<br /> When he was a teenager, Edmund discovered that Lori was, in fact, his real mother and Sylvia was the aunt who had raised him. Lori had met a dashing stranger on one of her many adventures and had returned home, after wine, roses and romance, with little Edmund growing inside her. She had made the decision to leave Edmund with her sisters in the hopes that a \u201cmore stable\u201d upbringing would be better for him. Edmund was not embittered by this revelation. In fact, it helped explain quite a lot.<br /> As a young man, Edmund somehow managed to scrape together the funds to enter the Edinburgh College of Art at the University of Edinburgh. Living life at the University was a dream come true for him, while the main voice inside his head was telling Edmund to get out and see more of the world. When his studies took him to Spain, the birthplace of Picasso, Edmund simply never came back.<br /> Ever since then Edmund has wandered from country to country and continent to continent, more as a series of accidents than with any real agenda. Like with his mother\u2014his real mother\u2014life seemed to find a way to keep Edmund moving.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Edmund turned twenty in America. He was in Arizona, where the hot desert days faded to cold, windy nights. It was on just such a night that he found himself in a drive-in theater off of some barren stretch of road. The days of the drive-in had come to an end, but the dilapidated property had been bought by an art-house collective. Every year they hosted a film festival where they showed avant-garde and independent films for three days straight. People would come from miles around to camp out for the duration. Inevitably it turned into a bacchanalian carnival.<br /> Edmund had borrowed a convertible from a friend and had driven it down for the film festival. With a cooler, a sleeping bag and a pair of blankets, that car became his home for those three days.<br /> The last night of the festival was amazing. The sky was clear, the stars were intensely bright and a full moon slowly rose over the desert. They were playing a series of films from Latin America, with no subtitles. Edmund didn\u2019t speak Spanish, but there was a vitality and a passion to the films that made the need for language secondary.<br /> He was so enraptured by the screen that he didn\u2019t see the stranger until she leaned a hip against the side of the car door. She had the smoky, sultry mystery of a Mexican beauty. With trim, tan limbs, full, glossy black hair and dangerous eyes, it was as if a Latino goddess had stepped off the screen. She stood there in a halter top and cut-off jean shorts, leaning against the car as though she were in an advertisement. Edmund wondered whether or not she was cold, but felt too embarrassed to voice the question. Without a word this woman reached out an imploring hand to Edmund.<br /> Edmund didn\u2019t know what he was supposed to do. Who was this woman? What was her expectation? After a moment of indecision he handed her the open wine bottle in his hand. He preferred wine to beer. It was more artsy, and generally there was more of it per bottle.<br /> The stranger not only took the wine, but what Edmund was smoking. She took a couple of puffs and then a long drink from the bottle. When she was done she gave a pleased sigh and threw both the wine and the joint dismissively behind her. Edmund made a small noise of dismay, but his complaint was cut off when the stranger climbed over the top of the door and into the car. Seeing as how she had entered from the driver\u2019s side, she ended up straddling Edmund.<br /> Edmund was beginning to feel scared, now. She was so pretty Edmund found it hard to look at her. But given where she was, he didn\u2019t have much of a choice. Her smoldering stare kept him pinned to the seat. Though the position they shared was very provocative, the glint in her eye was one of mischief more than lust.<br /> On the big screen the film continued unheeded.<br /> She spoke for a long moment in the rapid-fire, lyrical speech of American Spanish. Edmund looked left and right, but there was no help forthcoming.<br /> \u201cUm\u2026I don\u2019t speak\u2026that language,\u201d he muttered.<br /> \u201cYou, I have been watching,\u201d she switched to English, the hints of her accent as attractive as the rest of her. \u201cYou pass through life as the wind passes through the trees. You bask in the sun and soak up the dark; embracing the gifts of life without begrudging what it is you lack. I say to you, the beings of heaven look upon those like you and smile.\u201d<br /> \u201cUm\u2026\u201d Edmund had nothing to say to that. \u201cYour\u2026um\u2026hair looks pretty in the moonlight.\u201d The words just came out on their own.<br /> The stranger smiled.<br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s this?\u201d she asked. Her slim fingered hand reached down to his jeans. She reached in and pulled out the film festival ticket-stub from his pocket.<br /> \u201cMoonlight is the sister to darkness and candles,\u201d she said. \u201cIt is inside intoxicating wine and elusive music; the setting of romance. But it is also the light of lunacy and the harbinger of madness. For your heart of openness and acceptance I bring you ecstasy and insanity; enlightenment beyond the corners of the rational world.\u201d<br /> She spoke in a soft, subtle chant, as though the words belonged to some ancient song or were from some spell older than mortal magic. She kissed the ticket-stub, leaving lipstick marks over the printed words, \u201cMoon-Lite Drive-In,\u201d and slid the slip of paper back into his pocket. Then she started to unzip his jeans.<br /> That was the night Edmund lost his virginity. His recollection of the evening ended up confused but grateful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T02:49:39-08:00","id":76163,"title":"","content":"<br /> Edmund slowly became aware of his surroundings. His ears were filled with the hum of florescent lights. He was in a brightly lit room. It was too bright. The light hurt his eyes and the shabby white acoustic tiles of the ceiling reflected the glare. Looking down, Edmund saw white again. He was holding a Styrofoam cup. The cup was partially filled with coffee which looked like it had been there for a while. It didn\u2019t steam and it had stained the interior of the cup with brown rings. Its inky blackness seemed mysterious, as though its depths held secrets Edmund was better off not knowing. He took a sip and it was cold and bitter.<br /> There were voices in the room with him. Voices with American accents. They held the soft susurration of Southern accents, or perhaps were from the Mid-West. He would discover some time later that he was in the northern part of Texas, somewhere along the border of Oklahoma, and for days afterward the theme song from the Rodgers and Hammerstein musical <i>Oklahoma!</i> would be stuck in his head.<br /> Edmund was seated on a hard, metal folding chair, in a circle of other people in similar chairs. One person was on his feet\u2014in cowboy boots\u2014and he was talking in his Texan drawl. He had been talking for some time, Edmund realized.<br /> \u201cAnd that\u2019s why, because my family, I\u2019ll never touch another drop again.\u201d<br /> There was a smattering of applause from the group in response to this impassioned declaration. Edmund couldn\u2019t both clap and hold his coffee, so he just cradled his cup in both hands. A dowdy woman wearing too much red lipstick hugged the speaker, murmuring, \u201cThank you, Bill. That was very moving.\u201d Then they both sat down and the lipstick lady said, \u201cOkay, who\u2019s next?\u201d<br /> There was a moment of brittle silence. Edmund sipped his coffee again; its taste instantly reminding him why he wasn\u2019t drinking it, but the unintended sound of his slurp came out uncomfortably loud. Then another man stood up. This man was large, not too tall, but heavy-set. However he carried his heaviness well, with a natural grace that said he was exactly as big as he was supposed to be. He had dark hair and eyes which seemed distinctly Mediterranean, but Edmund couldn\u2019t place his accent. He wasn\u2019t American.<br /> \u201cThis\u2026whole thing,\u201d the man began uncertainly, spreading his hands to encompass the room, \u201cit\u2019s supposed to be anonymous, right?\u201d<br /> \u201cYes,\u201d the lipstick lady assured encouragingly, \u201cit\u2019s okay to tell us whatever you want. It won\u2019t leave this building.\u201d<br /> The big man nodded, scanning the people around him. He looked at each person\u2019s face in turn with a scrutiny that said his next words were going to be important.<br /> \u201cMy name is Bacchus, the god of wine,\u201d the man announced. \u201cSome of you may know me as Dionysus. I\u2019m not an alcoholic, but I love to drink.\u201d<br /> \u201cSir,\u201d the lipstick lady interrupted. Her caring demeanor was replaced with a waspish disapproval. \u201cIf you\u2019re not going to take this meeting seriously, then we\u2019re going to have to ask you to leave.\u201d<br /> \u201cWait. Hear me out,\u201d the big man countered. Then he launched into a speech which was nothing short of mythical. He was like a preacher at his pulpit, delivering a sermon on the grace of grapes. In many ways it was quite conservative. He spoke of how one should \u201cdrink to live, not live to drink\u201d and how drinking one\u2019s self into oblivion was contrary to the purpose of spirits. But he also talked of the wonders of fermentation and how alcohol was a gift of the gods for men to live well and enjoy life; how it was meant to inspire, not destroy. It seemed so very contradictory, but at the time, the way he told it, it all seemed to make perfect sense.<br /> When he was done there was enthusiastic applause from the other members there. All except the lipstick lady, who was trying to constructively channel her anger and Edmund, who was still holding his coffee. The others were all up on their feet, hugging the big man, thanking him for his words. It dawned on Edmund that he was expected to join in, or worse, that he may be asked to speak next. With a sense of panic he hurriedly left the building.<br /> Outside he found he was still at a loss of what to do with his coffee. Looking right and left to make sure he was alone, Edmund dumped his cup and its contents behind some bushes.<br /> \u201cThey are something, you know?\u201d said a voice. It was the big man, the one who called himself Bacchus, emerging from the shadows behind Edmund.<br /> \u201cThey? Who?\u201d Edmund asked, worried about being caught littering.<br /> \u201cMortals. They get so much wonderfully right, and yet\u2026fall so short.\u201d He shook his head in kind bemusement.<br /> \u201cI don\u2019t understand,\u201d Edmund said. He was just being honest.<br /> \u201cA \u2018twelve-step program\u2019,\u201d the big man mused, \u201cso many good ideas, but not quite right. Life is a journey, as the poets say, but the mistakes made along the way are just as valid as any of the other steps a person may take.\u201d<br /> Edmund bit his lip and wondered if he had a car nearby. Not that he knew where he was going to go if he did.<br /> \u201cHere, take this,\u201d the big man flipped something like a coin over to Edmund. \u201cKeep it. It may come in useful one day.\u201d<br /> Edmund looked at what the man had given him. It was an AA token. He put it in his pocket, not because he wanted to keep it, but because he hoped that by appeasing this strange man he might stop talking to him.<br /> The big man walked past Edmund, patting him on the shoulder.<br /> \u201cEmbrace the journey, Edmund,\u201d the stranger said. \u201cEven when you stumble you still make progress.\u201d<br /> \u201cHow..?\u201d Edmund turned around, but he was alone in a parking lot on a muggy Texan night.<br /> That was the first time Edmund met his father.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Edmund was in a robe, like a bath robe, tied closed with a sash. It was actually a Yukata, a Japanese robe from an Onsen, a hot-spring resort somewhere in Hokkaido. How it came to be with him in Amsterdam Edmund couldn\u2019t recall, but he often wore it when he couldn\u2019t remember what had happened to the rest of his clothes.<br /> He stared intently at his coffee pot. It was an electric percolator from the 1950s. Soon enough the ancient appliance made the gurgling sounds that meant it was working. It sat on a hot plate on a table in the middle of his studio. The hot plate itself was defunct. Bad wiring kept Edmund from plugging it in for fear that it might start a fire, but it served as a suitable resting spot for his coffee pot, which itself might also have been a fire hazard. In Edmund\u2019s art studio, with paint thinner, old rags, canvas and bits of wood, fire was a real concern. That didn\u2019t stop him from smoking, though.<br /> \u201cOh, Edward, you\u2019re in!\u201d said a bright voice.<br /> \u201cJi-Woo?\u201d Edmund asked. He knew that voice and he knew it meant trouble. But usually a good kind of trouble.<br /> A figure breezed into the room as though she had every right to be there. Ji-Woo was a young Korean woman, perfectly at ease in her own skin and completely beautiful. Secretly he felt envious. At her worst Ji-Woo was a beautiful disaster, while at his best Edmund was still a bit scruffy looking. She always called him \u201cEdward.\u201d Edmund suspected that she knew his real name, but she just didn\u2019t care. And Ji-Woo always appeared as sudden as a storm. She blew in unannounced, tumbled things around like a tempest and then left without warning, leaving behind artful wreckage in her path. Edmund had often been a victim of her unpredictable enthusiasm.<br /> \u201cWhy\u2026\u201d Edmund began, \u201cWhat are you doing here?\u201d<br /> \u201cOh,\u201d Ji-Woo gave her best disarming smile, \u201cI was in town and needed a place to stay.\u201d<br /> \u201cI\u2026um\u2026well\u2026\u201d<br /> \u201cThanks, I knew you wouldn\u2019t mind. Do you have anything to eat?\u201d<br /> \u201cUm\u2026coffee.\u201d<br /> \u201cHmm\u2026\u201d Ji-Woo tapped her lips with a colorful fingernail and regarded Edmund critically over the tops of her sunglasses. \u201cWe\u2019re going to need more than that.\u201d<br /> She tucked a long strand of black hair behind an ear and reached into her bag. She pulled out a handful of coins and tossed them into the air with an experienced fluidity. The coins landed with nice metallic clinks. Ji-Woo studied the way the coins had landed sedulously, and then she gathered them up and tossed them again. And again. She was doing an I Cheng reading.<br /> After a number of tosses, interspersed with the odd, \u201cThat\u2019s interesting,\u201d and a \u201cHuh, I\u2019ve never gotten anything like that before,\u201d Ji-Woo remarked about things like \u201cno transforming lines\u201d and how it \u201cexactly altered Yin and Yang for every bar.\u201d Then she returned her attention back to Edmund.<br /> \u201cWhen was the last time you left the studio?\u201d she asked him.<br /> \u201cI\u2026what month is it?\u201d Edmund couldn\u2019t honestly remember.<br /> \u201cI got the \u2018Already Fording\u2019 reading,\u201d Ji-Woo told him gravely. \u201cIt tells me that it\u2019s time to ford the stream of events. It also tells me that it\u2019s time to end the cycle of disarray.\u201d She peered around the studio. \u201cAnd you are surrounded by disarray. We need to find you a girlfriend.\u201d<br /> Edmund failed to follow her logic.<br /> \u201cI have friends\u2026who are girls,\u201d he defended.<br /> \u201cThat\u2019s not what I mean.\u201d<br /> \u201cI have female sexual companions. It\u2019s exactly what you mean.\u201d In his experience lovers did nothing to lessen disarray, but rather added to the confusion of his life.<br /> \u201cWell, yes, you\u2019re right,\u201d Ji-Woo admitted, \u201cbut that doesn\u2019t make me wrong. Get dressed. We\u2019re going out.\u201d<br /> \u201cUm\u2026\u201d Edmund felt a sense of rising panic. Part of him was glad, the part of him that was delighted by the unexpected and the strange. Another part of him, however, the part which was afraid and just wanted to be left alone\u2014the larger part\u2014wanted to ask her to leave. But one did not ask Ji-Woo to leave. One only weathered the storm. It wasn\u2019t unknown for Ji-Woo to sweep Edmund up in her torrent of activity only to forget about him later, abandoning him at some techno dance club where he had no friends, no idea where he was, and no way to get home. That didn\u2019t mean that they weren\u2019t good times. Nonetheless Edmund had the feeling that \u201cending the cycle of disarray\u201d was only going to lead to chaos.<br /> And he wasn\u2019t wrong.<br /> Days later, when Edmund returned to his studio, he found that Ji-Woo had disappeared again. With his coffee pot.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Edmund stared silently at the canvas before him. The studio was a mess. It was an apocalypse of paint, drop cloths, brushes and clutter; but the canvas stood on its easel blandly, mockingly blank. It was untouched and Edmund couldn\u2019t find any artistic resources to fill its taunting emptiness. The voices in his head were quiet tonight. Edmund\u2019s mood darkened. He turned a bottle of red wine over and over in his hands. He had lost his bottle opener.<br /> \u201cHello?\u201d Hello?\u201d a voice floated up from the doorway to the studio. For a countless time Edmund thought to himself that he should lock his door; or at the very least buy a lock for the door.<br /> The unexpected guest made his way through the mess, carefully choosing his steps until he joined Edmund, turning to face the empty canvas as well. The stranger was a large man, with a Mediterranean duskiness. They shared a moment of contemplative silence.<br /> \u201cI remember you,\u201d Edmund said.<br /> \u201cYeah?\u201d the stranger asked.<br /> \u201cYeah, you\u2019re the guy who claimed to be Bacchus.\u201d<br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d the man answered simply.<br /> There was another lengthy pause.<br /> \u201cYou\u2019re actually him, aren\u2019t you?\u201d Edmund said. He was still rolling the bottle in his hands. \u201cThe god of wine?\u201d<br /> \u201cI am.\u201d<br /> \u201cI believe you. I shouldn\u2019t, but I do.\u201d<br /> \u201cI think divine revelation is as good a reason as any for a drink, don\u2019t you agree?\u201d Bacchus said.<br /> \u201cI can\u2019t open it,\u201d Edmund confessed.<br /> Bacchus turned to search through the jumble of tools, paints and brushes on a nearby work table. He came up with a scratched and battered claw hammer, its handle wrapped in ageing duct tape and its head darkened by rust.<br /> \u201cHere we go,\u201d he said, \u201cIn case of emergency, break glass.\u201d Bacchus took the wine bottle from Edmund and smashed the neck off with an expert flick of the hammer. There was a crash of glass, a splash of wine and a muffled voice from the back of the room which sleepily complained, \u201cWhat the fuck?\u201d<br /> \u201cDo you have company over?\u201d Bacchus asked.<br /> \u201cUm\u2026yeah,\u201d Edmund said. \u201cThat\u2019s Sharon, Sandra\u2026and that\u2019s Alex.\u201d<br /> \u201cOh, I didn\u2019t see her there.\u201d<br /> \u201cYeah, she sleeps like the dead, but she was very\u2026energetic\u2026not too long ago.\u201d<br /> Bacchus found an empty glass and poured paint thinner from another one. He filled them both with wine for himself and Edmund.<br /> Edmund sipped his wine, wondering if he was swallowing tiny shards of glass.<br /> More silence.<br /> \u201cThere\u2019s something else you should know,\u201d Bacchus said after a while.<br /> \u201cUm?\u201d Edmund answered.<br /> \u201cI\u2019m also your father.\u201d Bacchus poured more wine.<br /> \u201cOh,\u201d Edmund said softly. \u201cThat\u2026that explains a lot.\u201d Then after a bit he continued, \u201cYou know, I always felt I might be...special.\u201d<br /> \u201cEveryone feels that way,\u201d Bacchus said. \u201cIt\u2019s part of the human condition. People need to feel important, need to feel like their lives mean something. It helps them get by. Sadly, however, you <i>are</i> special.\u201d<br /> \u201cUm?\u201d<br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not good news, I\u2019m afraid,\u201d he refilled their glasses again, the ruin of the bottle miraculously still held its wine. \u201cI wish I could promise you a simple life, filled with wine, women and song. Believe me when I say that\u2019s the best kind of life there is. But fate, I\u2019m afraid, wants you to play a larger role. The blood of divinity runs through your veins, which means the threads of destiny bind more tightly around you than for others. It\u2019s a terrible responsibility, but it can also be glorious. The tread of your footfalls will echo more profoundly down the halls of history.\u201d<br /> \u201cUm...what?\u201d<br /> \u201cDon\u2019t worry. You\u2019ll figure it out.\u201d<br /> The silence returned like an old friend.<br /> \u201cSo tell me, son,\u201d Bacchus said, \u201cWhy, when you have three willing and beautiful women in your house and the god of wine by your side are you spending your time looking at this scrap of white cloth?\u201d<br /> \u201cI can\u2019t paint,\u201d Edmund lifted a shoulder in a half shrug. \u201cWhen I can\u2019t paint\u2026when I can\u2019t create then I\u2026then nothing else really matters.\u201d It was a long speech for Edmund.<br /> Bacchus pondered the canvas.<br /> \u201cHere,\u201d he declared, \u201cI can\u2019t promise you happiness or success, but I can make you a gift.\u201d He poured the rest of the wine over the hammer he had used to open the bottle. \u201cNow, I have anointed this tool. Win or lose, whatever may come, you will always have the gift of inspiration.\u201d<br /> Edmund dubiously took the wine drenched hammer from his father. He looked back at the boringly blank canvas, and an idea occurred to him. He scrapped a clump of paint from his pallet onto the head of the hammer. He slung it at the canvas and a splatter of paint and wine landed just so. He spun the hammer around and scraped a line of color down the canvas with the claw end. Edmund tilted his head to one side to gauge the effect. He liked how it looked. With his free hand he spread more paint on the canvas and smashed it with the hammer. Before long Edmund was furiously painting, lost to the rest of the world.<br /> \u201cThat\u2019s my boy,\u201d Bacchus said, patting Edmund on the shoulder. \u201cYou\u2019ll be fine.\u201d Then the god of wine left, disappearing into the night as mysteriously as he arrived.<br /> Sharon, Sandra and Alex cautiously approached Edmund. They watched in awe as he worked. They weren\u2019t sure what they were seeing, but they had the feeling that they were watching the creation of something wonderful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T17:33:55-08:00","id":81831,"title":"","content":"Holy crap this is late. Sorry people. Well, it\u2019s here now, so time to introduce Edmond.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XVIII</i><br /> <br /> <u>One Night in Bangkok Part III</u><br /> <b><br /> Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> . . . continued from previous entry.<br /> <b><br /> Bangkok</b><br /> <br /> Just as the statue cracked open to reveal its candy-colored ogre center, Rajani kicked open the temple doors and charged in the help us slaughter the rest of the ogres. From that point on, she and I teamed up to take down one ogre after another. She danced and leaped from one to the next, slicing them open and throwing them off balance while I followed up her strikes with a couple of bullets to finish them off. While we took care of the ogres, Zane beat the shit out of the remaining shadow monks and Andy wove his magic to help us fight. Magnus challenged the big Skittles ogre to one-on-one combat and they spent the next minute or so smashing each other in the face. Boys will be boys, I guess. Magnus won that contest, by the way. And of course he struck a statuesque heavy metal pose atop the thing\u2019s corpse after he chopped off its head as a trophy. I would have sketched it or taken a photo, but I was having way too much fun playing with one of the pitch-black giants, who was trying his hardest to hit me as I flitted and jumped around him, shooting his friends. The poor guy never even came close, but he did manage to destroy most of the remaining support pillars of the temple in the process. In the end, I shot the last load-bearing joist, bringing the temple down on the ogre while we escaped.<br /> <br /> Then we stopped for ice cream on the way back to the hotel. It was yummy.<br /> <br /> Once we arrived back at the hotel, I was concerned about Pipa since she\u2019d been summoned by Laughing Carp. I strummed on the pipa she gave me and tried to tell her I was worried, but the hollow sound of the strings convinced me that she wasn\u2019t hearing it. So I tried texting her and got no response. All the sudden my bright day started to get cloudy.<br /> <br /> So I plopped myself down on the hotel bed and fixed a cup of complimentary hotel tea. The tea was good, but the leaves were better, and they showed me what I needed to see. Pipa was imprisoned in an exorcism room at Laughing Carp\u2019s temple! That was hardly fair. I decided that we needed to go rescue her, and so we hatched a plan. Andy, Magnus and Rajani will go with Zane and me to the temple to present the Skittles ogre\u2019s head to Laughing Carp, and while she is distracted, Zane will slip away invisibly to go get the pearl. Meanwhile, I will casually wander upstairs to the exorcism room and rescue Pipa Jing. I\u2019m leaving the pipa she gave me in my hotel room so that she can transport herself there once I\u2019ve freed her. She said next time we hooked up it would be at my place anyway. But Zane and I were sharing a room and I could tell she wasn\u2019t really comfortable with me and Pipa making out there, so I arranged a room for myself.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> The plan was a miserable failure, and I\u2019m feeling really anxious and trapped right now. Also, Zane\u2019s upset, and that makes me really sad. On the brighter side, my good friend Edward is in Bangkok. It\u2019s been months since I saw him last!<br /> <br /> He was standing outside the temple, looking completely confused (as usual) while he talked to the temple lions. Edward is a fun guy. He\u2019s an artist like me, but his art is aggressive and perplexing and abstract in ways that mine isn\u2019t. Edward is a son of Bacchus. I could tell he was a scion the first time I met him because he smelled of warm olive oil with the sour hint of wine, and that\u2019s why I asked him to dance. He\u2019s not a very good dancer. But otherwise his life is a bit like mine\u2014he ends up traveling all over the Europe and beyond, living the Bohemian dream . . . sort of. Unlike me, Edward doesn\u2019t seem to have a clue what\u2019s going on most of the time and can never remember how he got where he is. That is, when he bothers to leave his studio. He\u2019s such a homebody sometimes that I feel compelled to drag him out with me, and we always have a blast, even if he is insane. I eventually lose track of him, of course. Last time I found him living with a coffee pot in Amsterdam. He hadn\u2019t been out in WEEKS, so I took him out clubbing and we ended up in Marseilles before I lost him again.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I was thrilled to introduce Edward to my friends. I even introduced him to Zane, who was invisible at the time. That was probably my biggest misstep of the day since it tipped off the temple lions that we were up to something. Edward followed us into the temple, though, and became mired in a conversation with the monks while we enacted our plan. Since Edward can\u2019t speak Thai, the conversation was largely meaningless, though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, things went okay at first. Laughing Carp was duly impressed by the ogre\u2019s head, though the mortals in the temple freaked out a bit. Zane slipped off to get the pearl and I crept upstairs to find the exorcism room. Then something struck me from behind and everything went black. I woke up in Zane\u2019s arms in front of Laughing Carp, who glared imperiously down at me. Zane and I were both wrapped in mystical silver coils, and as soon as I realized I was bound, I started to panic. It\u2019s like my claustrophobia . . . I can\u2019t handle being trapped or bound. Zane begged Laughing Carp to release me. It was really sweet. Zane always looks out for me. Fortunately, Laughing Carp graciously released us both. We weren\u2019t going to get into any trouble with the temple lions standing guard over us anyway. THEY were the ones who knocked me out and caught Zane.<br /> <br /> Laughing Carp was furious, and it\u2019s pretty amazing how ferocious such an adorable little woman can be when riled. I felt like I was being lectured by a songbird. She was very disappointed in us, but I was just upset that I wasn\u2019t able to rescue Pipa Jing. I suppose we got off easy. Laughing Carp banished us from the temple and made us swear an oath not to enter it again. For me, that was almost worse than being bound. I felt like the restrictive weight of that oath was strangling me, and the feeling was made worse because the oath kept me away from Pipa.<br /> <br /> Magnus, Andy and Rajani were really disappointed in me as well, but I don\u2019t know why. They were all behind the plan until it failed. Well, maybe not the part about stealing the pearl. The worst part is how much this has hurt Zane, though. I put her in a really bad spot, and I think she\u2019s mad at herself because Laughing Carp is so disappointed with her. And with me, but I don\u2019t really care what Laughing Carp thinks about ME. I just don\u2019t like seeing Zane so upset, especially since it\u2019s my fault. Stealing the pearl goes against her better judgment, and she never would have tried if it weren\u2019t for me. I feel awful.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not giving up on rescuing Pipa. I really like her, and she\u2019s in trouble because of me. And to be honest, I want to impress her, so I REALLY want to be the one who rescues her. I\u2019m perfectly willing to break the oath to do so, but Magnus got really scary and told me I shouldn\u2019t do that. Oaths and honor are way more important to him than they are to me. Andy agreed with Magnus. I was so miserable over my failure and the oath and Zane that I couldn\u2019t really think of any good plans to break out Pipa Jing, but fortunately, my friends are amazing. Between Magnus, Edward and Andy, we came up with an amazing scheme that we hope will force Laughing Carp to lift the oath and invite me back into the temple. I\u2019ll get to that in a moment.<br /> <br /> We went to recover at Jean\u2019s club. I needed absinthe, and lots of it. Apparently Zane really IS upset; she immediately started drinking and hasn\u2019t actually stopped. When Jean learned we were there, he came by our table by with more information. It seems one of the artifacts being imported by the Unpronounceable is a creepy grotesque. It\u2019s going on auction, and has generated way more interest than it should, so it must be important, which brings me to our plan. We\u2019re going to steal grotesque, and make sure the servants of the Unpronounceable KNOW we\u2019ve stolen it so that they will chase us back to Laughing Carp\u2019s temple. Once they are trashing her temple, she\u2019ll have no choice but to give me and Zane permission to enter the place to help Magnus and the others deal with the beasts. No more oath! I\u2019ll be able to breath again!<br /> <br /> Of course, I plan to break away from the fighting as soon as I can and use it as a distraction to rescue Pipa Jing. Those obnoxious temple lions should be occupied and the coast clear, I hope. The omens are good, in any event. And I did see a wicked gleam in Edward\u2019s eye. I think he might make a play for the pearl now that we\u2019ve explained the situation to him.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, Jean has agreed to go make sure Pipa is okay, and to let her know that I\u2019m doing all I can to secure her release. I don\u2019t like the idea of HER being trapped any more that the thought of being trapped myself, so I hope she\u2019s okay and that the message brings her some small comfort.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> (cont.)<br /> <br /> Also, right when the stonking rainbow ogre thing came busting out, Rajani showed up! That was good, seeing as she and Ji-Woo were a proper good team, taking down ogres like they was nothing, bam bam! one right after another. I kept after the ninja wankers, specially after they kept going for Ji-Woo, since they couldn\u2019t hurt Mags none. One did hurt her a bit (not for real or nothing, just her boosted health). I showed him what for any road. They were strong and all, yeah, but not tough or nothing.<br /> <br /> I did leave the big guy alone, seeing as he was knocking people off balance too, and looked well tough. Mags did for him but good, on account of he\u2019s tougher. He did get a bit beat up looking, but then he went all berserk-y and sat there trading blows with him up until the giant bloke fell down, just in time for some more ogres and another ninja to join the fun. Then he cut the giant\u2019s head off and put it on his axe! It were well hard, and right brill to watch the looks on the faces of the new ogres when Mags turned on them.<br /> <br /> There was still one of the before ogres left, that Ji-Woo was having a bit of fun with - she hid behind him, ducking this way and that so\u2019s that he couldn\u2019t find her and even had him hold one of her guns for a bit. He stayed alive to the very end, while Ji-Woo bounced some bullets off Rajani\u2019s sword to help her kill one of the new ogres and the other played the berk and tried to do a shadow jump thing to get Mags by surprise. Mags just kind of reacted without even noticing him proper and between that and Rajani getting a bit out of him before he even jumped through the shadow, he was done for but good.<br /> <br /> Now, only Ji-Woo\u2019s ogre friend was left and he was winding up to have a go at Mags before I jumped on his shoulders and held him still. I also popped on one of my chaos superpowers, on account of the ogre\u2019s having torn down enough of the pillars that the ceiling were about to fall down. That was good for me, seeing as Ji-Woo finished off the ogre by shooting the ceiling down proper. I managed to find me a small hole, so\u2019s it just kind of fell all around me. The others all made it out the door, cept Mags who got clipped a bit, being so big and all. Not that it hurt him or nothing, and he\u2019s well strong, so he just tossed it off him. And then cut down the last pillar, what was the only thing left still up.<br /> <br /> After, we found an ice cream man. I didn\u2019t know if they had ice cream mans in Bangkok, but Ji-Woo said they did everywhere. We were able to find one alright, for certain. I got me a skittles lolly, on account of the rainbow ogres, yeah? It were ace, even if the ice cream man gave us some funny looks, probably cause of the giant head Mags had tied to his axe. And Mags and me were covered over in blood and things.<br /> <br /> Any road, then things started going not so good. The pipa that Pipa gave Ji-Woo was all magic-y and lets Ji-Woo talk with her, but it weren\u2019t working. Her phone wasn\u2019t neither. So Ji-Woo got out her coins to try and suss out where she was, and found out she was in a locked up room at the temple, with an invisible door and all. Laughing Carp and her pearl were at the temple too. So we made a plan - Mags would go with Rajani and Andy and give Laughing Carp the giant head, and make a big deal about it, while I sneaked off all invisible to get the peal and Ji-Woo snuck off to save her boyfriend. Girlfriend. Whatever.<br /> <br /> Mags and Ji-Woo think it\u2019s proper odd that I call Pipa her boyfriend, even though I know she\u2019s a girl, but I want to be a boy before I be somebody\u2019s boyfriend. I don\u2019t know how a girl can be a boyfriend either, but she for sure is. I\u2019d maybe ask her, if she weren\u2019t such a bitch. Sides, I want to be a good boyfriend, any road.<br /> <br /> But that was our plan and all. Ji-Woo even got a different room and put the pipa in it, seeing as Pipa could teleport to it, when she weren\u2019t trapped. She also got fussy at me about keeping the pearl, but she was mostly alright when I said I probably wouldn\u2019t keep it forever. Not that it matters now. I mean, it started off alright, we even met a new superhero friend! His name is Edmund, and Ji-Woo knew him already but she calls him Edward, so I\u2019m going to call him Ned. I think Mags is calling him Eddie. He seems like he\u2019s always confused anyways, so it probably won\u2019t make it too much worse. He\u2019s another artist bloke, all covered in paint, but he says he paints with his hammer so that makes sense, yeah? He also thought the lions weren\u2019t real cause they said so. He\u2019s not all there, I don\u2019t think. He\u2019s from the same place Andy is, but they didn\u2019t know each other before. Andy did make his clothes look like Ned\u2019s after a bit, which confused Ned even more I think, cause he didn\u2019t remember wearing that.<br /> <br /> He followed along though, talking with Mags about music. Mags\u2019 part of everything went well and all, I guess, seeing as Laughing Carp seemed impressed. For my part, I found the invisible door alright, and ran smack into one of the nice lion statues. He were invisible too, like me, and knocked me off balance, like I do to things. He grabbed me up in his mouth, but he didn\u2019t hurt me none, even when I tried hard to get out. The other lion found Ji-Woo and hit her over the head hard. I\u2019m a little cross with him, he didn\u2019t have to hurt her so bad. My lion let me go though, when I saw her passed out and all, so I got her all fixed up. We was all tied up in some kind of silvery stuff though, so Ji-Woo got all panic-y. They wouldn\u2019t take it off at first, on account of me trying to get out before. I said they could leave it on me and I\u2019d promise to stay and all if they\u2019d let her out, cause she was not in a good way, but then Laughing Carp said they could let us both out.<br /> <br /> So, I guess I can\u2019t say I\u2019ve never been nicked anymore. Laughing Carp was nicer than lots of marks when they nick a thief. She didn\u2019t even yell too much, she was just disappointed at us. I tried to say I didn\u2019t try and nick the pearl for Pipa, and Ji-Woo tried to use a superpower to be all innocent, but it didn\u2019t work so good. I even tried to help convince her that Pipa was right helpful finding the chaos blokes to mash up, but Laughing Carp didn\u2019t believe either of us, or just didn\u2019t care. She did believe Mags when he played the innocent, but that meant he was looking all disappointed at us too. And the lions was disappointed... It were right strange. I\u2019d gotten all kinds of disappointed lectures - from peelers, or social workers, or the random wankers who\u2019d finish by handing us religious papers printed up like money - but I\u2019d never felt like such a shit as I did in the temple with an adorable tiny fishy dragon and 2 fuckoff metal lions disappointed in me. It didn\u2019t help that Ji-Woo was all sad again and it were my fault partly.<br /> <br /> See, Laughing Carp let us off after a bit, on account of Mags being good, She made us promise not to come back to the temple and Andy said the lions marked us so\u2019s they\u2019d know where we was. Ji-Woo weren\u2019t too happy being tied up, even just with words and promises. It didn\u2019t help none when Andy and Mags started talking all big on promises. She was thinking hard on plans and all, mostly at first to steal the pearl, then sex Laughing Carp up so\u2019s that she\u2019d give Pipa back like as a present. I didn\u2019t like that none, but I don\u2019t think she did neither. I don\u2019t think she likes Laughing Carp much.<br /> <br /> We went to Jean\u2019s club to keep making more plans and to get summat to drink. I was bad and mostly just tried to get drunk. I\u2019m not smart like the others and I never tried to make somebody not be disappointed at me cause I never cared before. Jean said it probably wouldn't work just to give the lions a nip of something, even though they like drinking, cause they might not trust it, so I didn't have any ideas. He came out and talked with us once we got there. Mags still had the giant head and it scared somebody working there, so he came right quick too. He\u2019d found out there was a ship coming later tonight with a small gross statue that he thought might be a chaos thing, on account of some blokes was interested that had no reason to be.<br /> <br /> He also thought that the pearl should get nicked and that someone should have a go at Laughing Carp. Then Andy started talking some bollocks about people being more laid back after a shag. He hasn\u2019t met the same bints I have, I guess. Any road, Ned and Saorse offered to get the pearl. Ned can walk through walls, and Saorse\u2019s a ghost and all. She was right sad she weren\u2019t more help with the lions, but they were proper big and all, it weren\u2019t on her.<br /> <br /> Mags kept talking about getting leverage instead, like helping out with the chaos blokes and all, to get a favor from Laughing Carp, yeah? Then we could ask her to let Pipa go, or give up the pearl for just a bit and show them she didn\u2019t need it proper, or maybe show her that it were bad for her. Jean did say he\u2019d take a message to Pipa from Ji-Woo, so\u2019s she\u2019d know she was looking out for her, but Ji-Woo was still sad and all, with the promise and being scolded and all. I think she wanted to be a superhero and save Pipa proper. It\u2019s a little backwards, but I guess Pipa is her mate and her boyfriend and you have to watch out for your mates. I mean, I\u2019d go get Ji-Woo, or Mags, or Rajani, or Andy, or the ladies, or Jester, or the littles, yeah? I gots lots of mates now. It\u2019s good having a gang again, even if they are silly sometimes.<br /> <br /> Any road, Andy came up with a bloody brill plan and Mags helped make it perfect. See, we\u2019re going to grab up the gross little statue so\u2019s the chaos blokes can see and all, then Andy and Ned are going to run with it, making sure everything works out proper with their super powers, right for the temple. Me and Ji-Woo are going to go with and help protect the temple, so\u2019s maybe Laughing Carp will take back our promise so we can help better and not get all hurt right outside. Mags and Rajani are going to work and make sure there aren\u2019t too many that make it to the temple, on account of not wanting Laughing Carp or the lions to get properly hurt.<br /> <br /> It sounds proper ace, and means Ji-Woo\u2019s not tied up with promises and maybe Laughing Carp won\u2019t be so mad at me no more. At the very least, busting up some chaos buggers is always fun, least so far.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XVIII</i><br /> <br /> Overall, Session went well, Edmond was introduced and got along well with the group.<br /> <br /> From a GM perspective, things flew right off the rails with this story, in a good way. I was not planning for Pipa Jing to be captured, as I noted before, nor did I plan for the PC\u2019s plans to rescue her to fail (or succeed). The Lions are competent guards, however, and while Zane could easily sneak past their ability to spot, the rest of the group similarly had little hope of spotting them, as they possessed 3 boons each from Stars, Sun, and Moon as well as an impressive array of Epics and some Guardian Boons.<br /> <br /> Next time daring rescue take two and crazy chase across Bangkok.<br /> <br /> Not much more to add, Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T02:56:31-07:00","id":89367,"title":"","content":"Our heroes continue their hijinx in Bangkok, as we work toward finishing up the Hero prologue of the story. Let\u2019s check in on them.<br /> <i><br /> Session IXX</i><br /> <u><br /> One Night In Bangkok Part IV</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bangkok</b><br /> <br /> We were all hanging out at the hotel, waiting until nightfall to enact our brilliant plan, when Jean found me. He wanted to report that he had seen Pipa, and she was fine. Not happy, but not under duress or anything. That put my mind at ease. And it made me feel even BETTER when Jean candidly told me that he thought Pipa was quite fond of me. I must have caught her fancy somehow, because according to Jean, she doesn\u2019t normally go around hooking up with people.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I confessed that I thought Jean was quite a catch, but explained why I consider him off limits. I don\u2019t want to become the mother of a new pantheon, and while a fling with him would be amazing, I\u2019m actually afraid I might grow attached. Maybe the whole changing cycle thing from my prophecy has me spooked. I really only have eyes for Pipa right now anyway. Jean understood. Somehow Edward came up in the conversation and Jean asked why Ed and I had never slept together. I mean, Edward is strange and confused, but he has an odd sort of charisma. I recalled that we had ALMOST ended up in bed together once or twice, but somehow we always got distracted and nothing ever happened. Weird.<br /> <br /> Jean also had some advice for me. He\u2019s already picked up on the fact that I don\u2019t exactly get along with my pantheon. It\u2019s not that I dislike the Bureaucracy. I mean, my divine father and my real mother are great. So much of my pantheon is just so oppressively rule-bound that I feel threatened just thinking about it. Jean\u2019s afraid that might get me in trouble. He knows a thing or two about the Bureaucracy, enough to know that many of my pantheon\u2019s enemies were once its servants who were corrupted by Hundun, becoming agents of unrestrained chaos. He doesn\u2019t want my attitude toward the Bureaucracy to be a seed that the titans can nurture in order to corrupt me. I hadn\u2019t really thought about it that way, but he\u2019s right. I need to be cautious.<br /> <br /> I was worried that he was cautioning me about Pipa, but that wasn\u2019t the case at all. He likes Pipa, and he likes ME being with Pipa. Pipa and Da Ji are a sort of \u201crighteous evil.\u201d They serve an important if questionable role in the Bureaucracy, and they aren\u2019t agents of the titans. So associating with them won\u2019t necessarily lead me astray. It\u2019s really my own issues that could be a problem, but as long as I maintain my own balance, I should be okay. My prophecy was definitely right about Jean representing Balance. He\u2019s pretty good at it too. I think he\u2019ll be a good addition to White Gloves if we can convince him to leave his club behind and return to Berlin. I have no idea how we\u2019re going to do that, though, or even if I WANT to. He has a good thing going on here, and Bangkok is kinda awesome.<br /> <br /> I felt a hell of a lot better about things after talking with Jean, and it made me reflect on my recent behavior, so I sought out Magnus and Andy and apologized to them for being so petulant earlier. They were right. Honor is important. I mean, I don\u2019t think it\u2019s as important as THEY do, but I suppose it IS important for someone to be able to trust your word when you make promises. I guess I\u2019ve always sort of avoided making promises. I\u2019ll have to be careful about it in the future.<br /> <br /> I also apologized to Zane for putting her in a bad spot with Laughing Carp. She seems to like Laughing Carp for some reason, and I guess it\u2019s kinda my fault that she got in trouble over the pearl and all. I\u2019m not repentant, but Zane feels guilty about it all, and she\u2019s pretty upset. Or at least she was. She seems okay now, and brushed off my apology like it wasn\u2019t even necessary. We\u2019re good again, so I\u2019m happy.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Our plan was an amazing success! We headed to the docks and found the cargo ship that held the grotesque we planned to steal. We scoped it out from a safe distance and sent Zane in to check the place out. She reported that the statue was in a large cargo bay. It was sitting on some crates next to a TV, and several human-headed serpent women were watching some reality TV show and texting a lot, so it would be hard to just take the grotesque without them noticing unless we caused a distraction. The snake women sound familiar. If I recall the legends, each of them can split into two younger \u201ctwins\u201d if badly hurt, and can reform if their twins aren\u2019t destroyed quickly enough. Zane said they were acting like teenage girls, though. There were also some weird, gray goblin-like things on the ship, and a number of ho-shen. The ho-shen otherwise known as black calamities, are amorphous, shadowy agents of chaos. Definitely bad news. There was also a monstrous fish thing circling the cargo ship in the water of the bay, but none of us except maybe Magnus, Andy and Rajani (so really, like half of us) wanted to tangle with it. And actually, Andy didn\u2019t want to tangle with it, he just wanted to taunt it.<br /> <br /> Once we knew what we were dealing with, I took to the skies to keep an eye on things from above while Zane sneaked back in to steal the grotesque. Then Andy exerted his power over water to shift the boat just enough to draw the attention of the titanspawn inside it. Meanwhile, as the boat rocked dangerously to one side, Magnus froze a path over the water next to the ship and slammed his axe into the boat\u2019s exposed hull below the water line, tearing a huge gash down its side that rapidly began filling with water when the boat righted itself.<br /> <br /> The titanspawn weren\u2019t happy about their floundering boat, especially not once Zane reappeared with the grotesque and flipped them off. Then Edward directed everyone to a bus that just happened to be parked at the docks. The bus was filled with fuel barrels for some reason. I have no idea WHY such an explosive conveyance was there, but these things happen when Edward is around. Ed jumped behind the wheel and took off at full speed once Magnus, Rajani, Andy and Zane were aboard, while I flew after them.<br /> <br /> A bunch of ho-shen chased us. They took the form of shadowy humans with glowing reddish eyes and bounded over the street traffic to reach us, but Rajani and Magnus cut them down as they leapt onto the bus. Rajani even kicked a few barrels off to discourage our pursuers. Unfortunately, we had another problem. Zane must not have seen the taotie masks when she was scouting, or maybe she thought they were just part of the ship\u2019s decor. But several of them came flying out of the ship after us. They didn\u2019t look intimidating; they were just eerie, flying stone masks. But I knew that their mastery of chaos made them very dangerous, and sure enough, one of them used its powers to strike Zane senseless with a sort of paralyzing confusion that left her in a daze for the entire chase. I made it my priority to take out the taotie masks since I could shoot them more effectively than Magnus or Rajani could hit them. Andy must have known how dangerous they were too, because he used his magic to bless my shots, and if it weren\u2019t for him, I might not have been able to destroy the masks as handily as I did. Still, I learned a thing or two. The masks might SEEM solid, but like most of Hundun\u2019s titanspawn, they are actually bound in chaos that obscures their eyes, which is the only part of them that is truly vulnerable. Now that I know how to see through that chaos, I should be able to aim my shots better, so hopefully I won\u2019t have as much trouble with them in the future.<br /> <br /> As we drove through the Bangkok city streets, weaving through traffic and dodging brightly lit buildings and hapless pedestrians, several other creatures joined the chase, drawn by something Magnus did to make himself the center of his own amazing party. They weren\u2019t dangerous, just curious and excited, so Andy and Magnus tried to keep them safe from the titanspawn. One of the creatures was a child-stealing witch thing that was tickling a stolen baby to make it cry, as though it were a musical instrument or something. Zane looks out for kids, so when she regained her senses, she snatched the baby from the witch and sent the creature packing. Laughing Carp is going to return the child to its parents.<br /> <br /> I finished off the last taotie mask by shooting an explosive barrel as it bounced out of the bus and past the mask. By then, we had arrived at the temple, and for a moment it looked like the bus was going to plow right through the main gate and blow up the front of the building. That would have been very, very bad. Edward threw himself out of the driver\u2019s seat and rolled to a painful stop on the pavement while Magnus and Rajani jumped off. Magnus grabbed Zane too, who was just shaking off her confusion, and Andy was flying near me by then, so we were safe. Fortunately, the bus veered to the left at the last moment, and then turned too sharply, toppling onto its side a short distance from the temple. Then it exploded.<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t have much time to enjoy the explosion, however, because more titanspawn were arriving in their own vehicles. A host of goblins and ho-shen converged on the temple. Laughing Carp hurried out and stood stunned by the sight until Magnus shouted at her and asked if we could take refuge inside to fight off the horde. She readily agreed and as soon as she said those words, I felt the weight of my promise lifted from my shoulders.<br /> <br /> The titanspawn followed us inside, but we fought them off. Magnus went berserk and tore through ho-shen left and right with his axe. Rajani danced like a bladed wind through the enemy ranks, cutting them down one after the other. Zane leapt around the room, smashing and throwing goblins and ho-shen around like toys. Andy used his magic to support the rest of us, including Laughing Carp, who transformed into her dragon form and attacked a group of goblins. Her fight looked pretty epic until Magnus wandered by and it became obvious that her carp-dragon form is less than two meters long. The temple lions were right in the thick of things as well, and were fortunately so distracted by the melee that they weren\u2019t paying any attention to me.<br /> <br /> I dodged and flitted around the temple, shooting ho-shen and goblins while I carefully maneuvered myself onto the second floor. Once I landed in front of the door to the exorcism room, I quietly picked the lock and slipped inside. As soon as I did, I triggered a mystical ward that attempted to turn my clothing to stone, trapping me there. But I expected something like that. I used a yin-yang destruction technique to channel the Earth chi into and through one of my I Ching coins, safely containing and destroying it.<br /> <br /> And there was Pipa, sitting in a wooden chair in the middle of the exorcism room. Her expression was a mixture of pleasant relief and shocked confusion. The ensuing conversation went a bit like this:<br /> <br /> \u201cPipa! I\u2019m so glad you\u2019re safe! I\u2019ve come to get you out of here!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou . . . you\u2019re here to rescue me?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course. I couldn\u2019t let Laughing Carp keep you prisoner, could I? And you would not believe what I\u2019ve been through to see you again.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut . . . I\u2019m the villain. I don\u2019t GET rescued.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t be silly. You\u2019ve not a villain. At least not now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c. . . I . . . I think I\u2019m love with you.\u201d<br /> <br /> When she said that, I froze for just a moment as joy and panic warred within me. She meant it. She\u2019d never been treated like this before, and what started as a romantic fling suddenly became much more serious. My gut reaction was to flee from that sort of attachment, but then I realized that I didn\u2019t WANT to flee. For the first time in my life, I\u2019d actually WORKED for a relationship and it was paying off. Something about that made it all more real than any relationship I\u2019d ever had before. Sure, I started to feel a little trapped, but I didn\u2019t mind.<br /> <br /> My heart was racing as I took Pipa\u2019s hand and pulled her into a kiss, but we couldn\u2019t take the time to enjoy the moment. We fled the exorcism chamber together, and once we were outside, I told her she should transport herself to the pipa she gave me, which was in my hotel room. Once she was safely gone, I rejoined the battle. I almost missed the fact that Edward was nowhere to be seen until the fight was over, so I suspect that he was busy stealing the pearl while I was rescuing Pipa.<br /> <br /> The temple suffered some damage in the fight, but nothing that can\u2019t be repaired. The priests were completely overwhelmed by the incident, but at least we kept them safe. Laughing Carp was terribly grateful for our help, which made Zane happy again. Zane also bonded with the lions a bit as they fought together during the fight, and I could tell she was happy that they weren\u2019t disappointed in her anymore. We didn\u2019t stick around long after the battle, though. Magnus announced that he was hungry, and we all headed to a Bangkok IHOP for pancakes. Once we were safely away from the temple, however, I said we should head by the hotel first because Pipa might want to join us. No one was surprised that I had rescued Pipa, of course. It was sort of an unspoken part of the plan, really. And if Edward DID steal the pearl he didn\u2019t say anything about it, but he might have forgotten he has it.<br /> <br /> I rushed to my hotel room and found Pipa sitting calmly on the bed, waiting for me. When I entered, she gave me one of her sassy, confident smiles, but there was also a hint of vulnerability in her eyes. She really WAS falling in love with me! It made my heart soar like the boundless winds in the clear blue sky. I crawled onto the bed to kiss her . . . and we didn\u2019t exactly make it to IHOP.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters </b><br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> That were proper brill, Dad, it really were. Everything worked just right, and we can go back in the temple and the lions are my friends again and Laughing Carp\u2019s not mad anymore, I think. Sides, I got to mash up a bunch of little goblin things. It were right ace, even if it does mean Pipa\u2019s gonna be around all the time now.<br /> <br /> I was feeling better right off, after having a plan and all, writing everything down and having a bit of a drink. Saoirse was still sad some, on account of not thinking of getting the pearl when I got nicked. It weren\u2019t on her though, and, being honest and all, I\u2019m mostly glad Laughing Carp\u2019s still got it. Maybe we can do what Mags said and talk her into letting it up for a bit, but I\u2019m not too bothered, either way.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo came and talked with me some, being all apologize-y too. I tried to tell her it were alright, that it weren\u2019t on her neither - it\u2019s Pipa\u2019s fault, really, if anybody\u2019s. Well, I didn\u2019t say that last bit, it wouldn\u2019t have helped none. She did say she cared about me and how what she did made me feel, even though she didn\u2019t usually care about summat like that. That\u2019s kinda sad - it\u2019ll be good for Ji-Woo to have proper mates, to look after her and for her to look after. It\u2019s good having a gang. So I gave her a hug and said I was better since we had a plan and all.<br /> <br /> The plan went like this - I\u2019d grab the statue up off the boat and get so\u2019s I could get away then let them see me, yeah? Then I\u2019d throw it off to Andy or Ned. Ji-Woo would be flying along and I was going to run close behind Ned and Andy, while Mags and Rajani dealt with enough of the chaos things to be safe. But it turned out there was a schoolbus, full of explode-y things, right there at the docks! So we decided to have Ned drive it, and we\u2019d all ride along up top. Ji-Woo was still going to fly.<br /> <br /> We decided to wait until dark though, so we all sat around for a bit. It was fun just being a gang together while we waited. Caoimhe went missing for a bit, which had Andy all bothered, even though I told him she were safe and all. She was at the docks, so we thought maybe she was just having a bit of a butchers for us, but she never said nothing about it. Ned thinks she\u2019s invisible, so Andy started talking this bollocks about watching invisible in the shower, the gobby bugger. Least, I think he was talking bollocks. I might have to make sure next time. Mags almost made Ji-Woo cry, on account of he drunk himself a whole bottle of absinthe without even any sugar or water or nothing. My friends is right strange.<br /> <br /> Eventually, after forever, it got dark, so we buggered off to the docks. I went to check on the statue, first off, and it were good I did. The boat was full up with tons and tons of little gray goblin things, and a few people and animals made of black sand-looking stuff. There were a stonking huge fish, bigger even than the boat, staying nearby and sometimes the goblins would throw things at it, like dead little fishes or sticks and things they found. Not the fancy masks they had up on the walls though. In the room with the statue, there was eight snake things with human lady heads. I think I saw summat like them before, what exploded with poison if you hit them. I might have fallen asleep at that movie though, cause Ji-Woo said they didn\u2019t. These ones were using phones, even though they didn\u2019t have hands and watching TV, something about some gobby bint what was getting hitched. One of the cakes were bigger than me! The statue was sitting right next to the TV that they all was watching, so we needed a distraction, summat more distracting than the goblins even - they kept coming in and dropping trou, but the snake bints just ignored them.<br /> <br /> I came back and told the others. Ji-Woo said the snakes were proper bad news - if they got hurt too much, they could split into 2 smallish snakes, with littles\u2019 faces, then come back together and be all better. The goblins were puny buggers, just alot of them, and the sand things - they were called calamities- hurt like a mother.<br /> <br /> Andy had a brill idea for a distraction, so we got all prepped. Ji-Woo started flying and I caught her ankle just in time to give her a boost. I got Ned and Andy a boost too, and figured out that Ned could boost people! He didn\u2019t know where I was, seeing as I was still invisible, so I whistled proper loud. He jumped right out of his skin, but still couldn\u2019t find me, so Ji-Woo helped him. Andy said I ought have put his pants up over his head, cause that\u2019s how you say hi where they\u2019re from. That sounds like a well horrid place. I\u2019d make sure to never see nobody.<br /> <br /> Any road, we got all set and I sneaked back in. After a bit, the whole boat started tilting! See, Andy took all the water on one side of the boat, and moved it a little bit away, so\u2019s there was nothing holding up the boat anymore. Then Mags started tearing into the bottom of the boat. The snake bints were proper upset when the TV fell over and started swallowing goblins, cause... I don\u2019t really know. But they all had big goblin sized lumps in their throats, or snake bodies, I guess, and they even started hitting the other goblins with the lumps. So, they were proper distracted, and I got the statue up and out of the room and they didn\u2019t notice nothing.<br /> <br /> After that I got a bit fuzzy. I know I stopped being invisible before I got away proper, and tossed the statue to Andy. He made a bloody ace show with all the water, with three 1-finger salutes and a big fuck off wing, like Ji-Woo\u2019s but with water. And then Mags was playing music, and I think I was shooting at goblins, after I jumped off the boat and Ji-Woo was yelling about the masks. I kinda remember some falling stars, or maybe they was explosions. The most confusing thing was that there was siren noises, but we didn\u2019t have one, and maybe it was Ned doing it.<br /> <br /> Any road, things got clearer when Ned almost rammed the explode-y bus into the temple. He didn\u2019t - it missed just barely - and he yelled at us to get off first, so me and Mags and Rajani and Ned and 2 naked giant bints and a little-sized thing with a bowl for a hat and a glowing trash bin and a dancing street lamp all jumped off. Andy and Ji-Woo were flying, so they didn\u2019t have to. I dunno where all the other came from. They buggered off once the bus exploded, but I was able to nick the little that one of the naked giant ladies was pretending was a guitar.<br /> <br /> I gave him to Laughing Carp, once she let us in, on account of she was worried about the littles on the bus, since it were a school bus and all. She even let Ji-Woo and me in, cause she didn\u2019t want us trapped outside, with all the goblins. It was a proper brawl, it was. Laughing Carp turned into a dragon that was gold all over and dived into the goblins, shooting at them with water. The goblins were short buggers, so it looked well serious, until Mags waded through the goblins and she didn\u2019t even come up to his pocket quite. He was clearing loads of the buggers, every time he swung his axe, until one of the sand things got themselves a good hit. Then he went well mad and bashed the sand things up good. I was using the tall walls to jump down on the goblins\u2019 heads and distracting the sand things a bit, so they didn\u2019t go after Laughing Carp at least. Then I started playing goblin cricket with the lions, bowling the wankers at them and letting them bat them away with their paws while they mashed up their own goblins and sand things. One of them took to catching a goblin up in his tail instead, and using it for a bat. They gave me a high five after, so they aren\u2019t very mad at me anymore. Laughing Carp looked not mad too and we decided to talk tomorrow, seeing as we were all hungry.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo was well chuffed when we left, so I figured she\u2019d got Pipa out. She had, and Pipa had teleported to the pipa in Ji-Woo\u2019s room, so we went back to the hotel before we left to find out if there was a IHOP in Bangkok, cause Mags wanted pancakes. Ji-Woo went up to her room to get Pipa, and then didn\u2019t come back for forever. The others said she was alright, but we ought leave her with Pipa and get Jean instead. I didn\u2019t try listening - from the looks on their faces, I didn\u2019t want to hear any road. But pancakes are always good - I\u2019ll just make sure to bring some back for Ji-Woo. Probably should bring enough back so she can share and not be hungry, I guess.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <i><br /> End Session IXX</i><br /> <br /> Edmond did, in fact, steal the pearl.<br /> <br /> Most PCs had a short conversation at the start of the session. Ji-Woo talked to Jean, Zane to Saoirse, Gia to Rajani, and Caoimhe to Edmond, some longer than others. Gia was trying to understand the culture, Caoimhe wanted to help with things but Andy did not want her endangering herself. Also, Caoimhe made it clear she was a Leanhuan Sidhe who could help Edmond, but it would eventually cost him his life. Caoimhe promised she would not try to trick or cajole him into becoming her dinner, but would not hesitate to consume his life and soul utterly given the option, in exchange for him creating work far beyond what he could normally do. It was Caoimhe who placed the school bus with fuel barrels conveniently nearby.<br /> <br /> The random lesser immortals were drawn to the bus due to Magnus\u2019s use of Divine Figurehead, which added to the chaos. Zane was zapped with Paralyzing Confusion by a Taotie Mask, and unable to participate. The Taotie Masks are old \u201cfriends\u201d for my Scion groups, small fast masks that throw around Chaos Boons and Magic Spells, in this case such as Paralyzing Confusion, Evil Eye and Illwind Curse. They are infamous for their use of Crawling Chaos and Fate and Switch in previous games. They are fragile if hit but have very high DVs.<br /> <br /> We will see what the fallout for this is as we continue the story next time. See you in two weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T23:46:07-07:00","id":89997,"title":"","content":"Actiony and dramatic Herr Baron.<br /> <br /> Question. I wiki-ed Pipa Jing and shape shifting was mentioned as one of her abilities. Does your rendition of Pipa have this power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T01:21:16-07:00","id":90034,"title":"","content":"Yes. It did not come up in that session, but iin tonight's session they saw hints that she has more sinister forms. Shapeshifting was an important part of her role in <i>Investiture of the Gods</i>, and that remains one of her major abilities. Also, some seriously heinous claws that add her opponent's highest virtue to her damage roll in dice.<br /> <br /> Tongihts session went well. Rajani's player had to miss due to power outages, but hopefully we are done with such madness for awhile. Should be one more session of &quot;One Night in Bangkok&quot; then Demigod visitations and we start &quot;Rock it for Me.&quot; Demigod will last longer than Hero; the current plan is 1-2 stories at Legend 5, then ~3 stories each at Legend 6-8. Edmond seems a good addition; we miss Phaedra's being the voice of responsibility, but he adds an interesting something to the interactions.<br /> <br /> Hope folks continue to enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T16:33:24-07:00","id":90486,"title":"","content":"I am enjoying.<br /> <br /> Good to know about Pipa. I imagine she'll be an interesting father.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T01:51:27-07:00","id":99026,"title":"","content":"We push toward the climax of our story, as our heroes see Chaos and Division working their wiles on the local shen. Even so, they unite to stop the chaos. And some of them go shopping.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XX</i><br /> <br /> <u>One Night in Bangkok Part V</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bangkok</b><br /> <br /> Pipa is an early riser. She got up way before I did this morning, which sucked because I would have liked to snuggle a bit while I dozed through the morning. I think she was examining some of my stuff and trying on my clothes. I finally reached out and grabbed her hand while when she wandered close and pulled her back into bed with me, which delayed us from joining the others in the hotel lobby until close to noon.<br /> <br /> When we did eventually make it down, Pipa was wearing the denim miniskirt and flashy white top I was wearing the other night when we first met. She was definitely trying to show off our relationship, kinda like she did when she left me with those love bites yesterday, but this time she was the one that was \u201cmarked,\u201d so it kinda showed that neither of us really \u201cowned\u201d the other one, if that makes sense. It was strange, but it helped ease my subconscious fear of being trapped in the relationship. I\u2019m really trying to ignore that nagging anxiety because for the first time in as long as I can remember, I really want this to work. I don\u2019t even know why, exactly. Maybe it\u2019s because Pipa is so interesting and mysterious and dangerous. It\u2019s like flying in a thunderstorm. You see things no one else sees there, lost in the torrent of flashing white and shadowed clouds, dodging bolts of lightning and riding gusts of turbulent wind. The thunder feels different from inside the storm. It reverberates through you because you\u2019re a part of it, and it\u2019s a part of you. And all of these things are more precious because the entire experience feels like it\u2019s all yours alone.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s kinda how I feel when I\u2019m with Pipa, except the experience belongs to both of us.<br /> <br /> Everyone else was already in the lobby except for Rajani, who it seems wandered off to look into something else again. Hopefully she\u2019ll rejoin us later. Magnus was softly strumming chords on his guitar and greeted us warmly. He seemed to be in a pretty good mood. Edward looked ill, but he always looks a bit ill. The others said he was guzzling syrup at IHOP last night, but that\u2019s nothing to be worried about. I\u2019ve seen him chug down worse stuff than THAT and be just fine. However, Caoimhe was flirting with him pretty heavily. I hope she hasn\u2019t taken any of Edward\u2019s soul already; if THAT\u2019S why he was looking ill, I\u2019ll be a little upset. I don\u2019t care if Edward and Caoimhe hook up and sleep together, of course. I just don\u2019t want her devouring his spirit like she did Aristides\u2019. I\u2019ve already lost one friend to her, and that was okay because it\u2019s what he wanted. But I know a lot of artists, and I am not comfortable with Caoimhe systematically siphoning their sensitive souls.<br /> <br /> Zane saved some pancakes for Pipa and me, so we went back upstairs to put them in my room\u2019s mini-fridge. While we were there, I asked Pipa if she could hear the sounds of the pipa when I strummed it to speak to her. She can, of course, so I asked her to teach me to play it properly. If I\u2019m going to strum it, I want it to sound beautiful. So we sat together and she began teaching me until Caoimhe came up to remind us that the others were waiting downstairs. I took the opportunity to discuss Jean a bit, which is when I shared my prophecy with Pipa and Caoimhe. Pipa was amused that Jean represents Balance, but she could see how the role fit him. I also asked Pipa and Caoimhe about being bad people, since they both tend to be a bit morally questionable. The thing is, they aren\u2019t serving the titans, and they ARE following the path they are supposed to follow. Objectively they might be evil, but it\u2019s righteous evil, at least in Pipa\u2019s case. They\u2019re just following their dharma. And I\u2019m comfortable with that, as long as Caoimhe doesn\u2019t follow her dharma all the way to the bottom of Edward\u2019s soul. I guess it\u2019s ultimately Edward\u2019s choice, though.<br /> <br /> By the time we made it back downstairs, it was after noon, and we headed to Club Tragos to see if Jean had any more information for us. Laughing Carp was already there, and she was behaving strangely, staring at Jean like she had never seen him before. I\u2019ve seen that look on the faces of plenty of young club girls, usually before they get in over their heads with some womanizing bravo. It was pretty clear that Edward had stolen the pearl, leaving Laughing Carp susceptible to Jean\u2019s wiles. Pipa and I found this to be really entertaining. Still, I should do a divination for them later, just to make sure it\u2019ll be okay.<br /> <br /> Zane was also really worried about Laughing Carp. I think Zane and Laughing Carp would make a fantastic couple, even if it means I\u2019d have to see Laughing Carp all the time. I don\u2019t think she\u2019ll be as much of a stick in the mud now that the pearl\u2019s gone, though, so it probably wouldn\u2019t be so bad. Anyway, I kept encouraging Zane to look after Laughing Carp, especially when Laughing Carp got so flustered that she had to step out of the room to cool down a bit. Zane is wonderful and I love her to death, but she\u2019s a bit dense when it comes to romance, so she didn\u2019t really get it. I think she missed her window and has forever lost Laughing Carp to Jean. C\u2019est pour le mieux.<br /> <br /> Jean did have some good information for us. He\u2019s quite resourceful, and I get the feeling that he\u2019s been using us as muscle this whole time. But I suppose we owe him since we kinda came in and upset the delicate balance between Pipa and Laughing Carp. Besides, he\u2019s helping us defeat one of Hundun\u2019s schemes, which means we\u2019re doing something good for the Bureaucracy. Hopefully that will reflect well on me because I don\u2019t think Fu Xi\u2019s going to like my girlfriend.<br /> <br /> Jean says another grotesque is arriving tonight, and he has managed to have a tracking device planted on the vehicle the enemy will use to move it from the docks to where they are storing the artifacts. All the artifacts are similar grotesques, and they are being imported at great expense, one at a time among shipments of other antiques and mundane relics. Laughing Carp believes that the grotesques harmonize with one another and grow more powerful the more are gathered together. If enough are brought to the same place, something big will happen. We\u2019re not sure what, but since the Unpronounceable is behind it, it\u2019s bound to be terrible.<br /> <br /> Something else that\u2019s terrible is that Pipa is not ticklish. I found that out last night. During the meeting with Jean, I decided to test others too. I found that Zane, Andy, and Edward are all very ticklish. I got Zane to tickle Laughing Carp, and Laughing Carp may be the most ticklish of all. She turned into her dragon form wiggled around like an eel when Zane tickled her. It was hilarious. I thought so, anyway. Magnus is totally ticklish too, but when I tried tickling him, he acted all stoic, like it wasn\u2019t affecting him. But it was, especially after I got Pipa to help me. She was a bit put out by it though, and just rolled her eyes. She probably thinks tickling is too saccharine. Also, I suspect that being ticklish would be a problem for her. I mean, she\u2019s originally a jade pipa spirit, right? If she were ticklish, then she\u2019d start laughing any time someone played her when she was a pipa. Can you imagine how weird it would be to start strumming beautiful chords on a pipa only to have it burst out in uncontrollable giggling? I had an absinthe dream like that once.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I\u2019m sure that\u2019s why Pipa isn\u2019t ticklish.<br /> <br /> So our plan is for Andy, Zane and Magnus to arrange a couple of cars for us so that we can track the grotesque when it is moved from its cargo ship later tonight. Hopefully that will lead us to the place they are storing the rest so we can get them all and completely derail the Unpronounceable\u2019s plot. In the meantime, we have the afternoon free. Pipa and I talked about taking in a drag show later this evening, but I don\u2019t think we\u2019ll have time before we have to be back for the mission. So instead, the two of us are going to spend the afternoon shopping and visiting some of the city\u2019s gardens. It\u2019ll give me a chance to get to know her better.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <b>On Jean and Laughing Carp - Liu (Polarizing) transforming into Lu (Treading)</b><br /> <br /> Uh oh. This isn\u2019t good. It looks like it\u2019s a bad idea for Jean and Laughing Carp to hook up. The oracle says that they should remain separate, acknowledging and respecting their essential connection to one another without joining. Unfortunately, it\u2019s probably a little late for that. I mean, sure, Pipa and I only left Club Tragos a couple hours ago, but the way Laughing Carp was behaving, I\u2019m not sure she hasn\u2019t acted on all her repressed passions by now. Well, I suppose a little fling won\u2019t hurt. I\u2019ll just have to warn them about this later.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Pipa and I spent the afternoon shopping and visiting some of Bangkok\u2019s nicer sights. I learned a bit about my girlfriend, so it was an afternoon well spent.<br /> <br /> First off, she\u2019s kinda clueless about fashion. She\u2019s clever and knows how to observe and adapt what she\u2019s seen other fashionable young ladies wearing, but she doesn\u2019t really understand it. So I tried to explain why I wanted this skirt or that top or those shoes, and how they all fit together. Pipa\u2019s talents run toward music, but by the time we were done, I think she also began to understand the melody of colors, patterns and textures in fashion.<br /> <br /> While we were chatting by the side of a lily pad pond in Bangkok\u2019s Rama IX park, I gushed a bit about how much I like the little experiences. You know, like the delicate reflections on dewdrops in the morning, the ghostly touch of snowflakes brushing your skin as they fall, the particular way the green of a lily pad complements the pink of its flower. I wanted to know if, after thousands of years, Pipa still enjoyed the little things like that. She said that Tian kind of spoils you. Everything is more vivid there, and once you\u2019ve experienced it, the mortal world seems dull by comparison. At first I thought that was sad. But then I realized that Tian must be a lot like the world I see when I\u2019m on absinthe, and I had to admit to myself that I drink absinthe because I WANT to live in the more vivid, evocative world it reveals to me. It makes me wonder what Tian would be like when I\u2019m on absinthe. I suppose I\u2019ll have a chance to find out soon enough. Pipa has promised to take me to her place there sometime.<br /> <br /> Then Pipa said that she probably needs to get away from Bangkok and the Bureaucracy for awhile, so after she ties up a few loose ends, she wants to move in to my place in Berlin. I was caught off guard by that, and probably stared at her like a deer caught in headlights. I\u2019ve never actually had to deal with this before. I\u2019m always the one moving in with my boyfriends or girlfriends, not the other way around. So I told Pipa that I just wander a lot, and I don\u2019t actually HAVE a place. She seemed surprised and maybe a little disappointed, so I quickly told her that I would make sure to arrange something by the time she arrives in Berlin. She liked that a lot. It\u2019ll be our place. Maybe I can send her pictures before I buy it to make sure she likes it.<br /> <br /> Oh my god. Now I have to find a flat in Berlin! I have no idea what I\u2019m doing. Maybe Andy will help me. I\u2019m panicking a little on the inside, because I\u2019ve never liked the idea of being tied down to one place, but the omens say this is all a part of my change of cycle. I need to take responsibility and deal with this. I mean, I\u2019m going to be a demigod soon, right? So the least I can do is buy a flat or something. Pipa\u2019s definitely worth it, isn\u2019t she? Or is it too soon? Fuck, I\u2019ve never freaked out about a relationship like this before!<br /> <br /> Ironically, I\u2019m NOT freaking out at all about the fact that my girlfriend has been known to devour people. I asked her about it. In the Fengshen Yanyi, it says she used to devour a few palace maids every time she visited Da Ji in Zhaoge. I asked her if that was true, and she said yes. She was very casual about it, and didn\u2019t seem particularly proud OR guilty. So I asked her if she still devours people regularly. She said, no, not regularly, though it does happen on occasion. After a bit of thought, I decided I\u2019m comfortable with that. It sounds awful, but as I said before, Pipa is righteous evil, so it\u2019s her nature to do these things, and I don\u2019t WANT to change who she is. After all, Lao Tzu says, \u201cIf you try to change it, you will ruin it.\u201d I\u2019m not sure I\u2019m taking that quote in context, but my policy has always been to live and let live, and I don\u2019t see any reason to change that now. I just needed to know if she was going to routinely devour people before I found us a place in Berlin.<br /> <br /> On a related note, she did admit that her tendency to cover me in love bites is related to her appetite for human flesh. But she assured me that I was in no danger of being devoured, no matter how tasty I am. I guess we\u2019re meant for each other, because I found that to be completely endearing, even though I know it should absolutely freak me out.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Pipa and I returned to the hotel a few minutes later than planned. I didn\u2019t think it would be a problem, but everyone else was gone. Saoirse was waiting for us, though, and told us that the grotesque was on the move and the others had already left to follow it. So Pipa and I took the other car. I don\u2019t really drive, so Pipa took the wheel. We didn\u2019t know where to go, though, so I leaned out the window and gazed at the moon. I could see the city reflected in it, and my keen eyesight allowed me to find the others\u2019 car after I called Zane to find out what it looked like. Zane was doing the same thing, and she even waved at me from the sun roof of their car!<br /> <br /> After that it was a simple matter of feeding Pipa directions as she sped through the streets of Bangkok like a bat out of hell, swerving through alleys, skidding over sidewalks, and scattering crowds. It\u2019s amazing we didn\u2019t hit any pedestrians. I think Pipa was being more careful than usual since I was there, but even so, she has some crazy driving skills! We even ramped over some garbage and ended up streaking through an intersection on two wheels, narrowly avoiding the cars that skidded to a stop around us. It\u2019s like we were untouched by all the chaos we were causing. It was beautiful. Then the cops showed up and started chasing us, so I summoned my pistols and shot off our license plate by ricocheting a couple shots off a metal light pole as we passed it. The police stayed on our tail for several minutes before Pipa managed to lose them.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never been in a car chase before, and it was amazing! I haven\u2019t had that much fun in ages. Pipa and I totally bonded during the experience. And yeah, I think she\u2019s a bad influence on me, but we didn\u2019t hit anyone, so I must be a good influence on her. That makes it all good, right? I\u2019m sure that Jean would agree since he represents Balance. Also, Zane watched the whole thing in the moon\u2019s reflection, and she thought the chase was awesome too. I think she\u2019s starting to warm up to Pipa, which is very good. It would be unpleasant for my best friend and my girlfriend to hate one another.<br /> <br /> When we arrived at the docks, Pipa told me to fly out of the car. I summoned my wings and launched myself free of the car and Pipa jumped clear just as she sent the car ramping off the docks and into the bay. We were going to have to get rid of it anyway, what with the cops and all. We quickly found the others. Edward wasn\u2019t with them, and I was going to ask where he was, but then Saoirse floated from heaven carrying him and Caoimhe. The poor ghost was exhausted by the effort of carrying both of them across the city like that. Apparently, Edward got lost in his art, which is completely understandable, and Caoimhe had to practically drag him out to join the rest of us. He\u2019s like that.<br /> <br /> The van carrying the grotesque stopped at a disgusting, run-down meat packing plant. If the grotesques were there, they wouldn\u2019t be unguarded, so we all powered up. Pipa asked if she should go in with us, and I was all for it, so she grew long black claws. I made sure Zane bolstered her health too.<br /> <br /> The interior was spacious and open but dimly lit. It smelled of rotting meat. Several vats with processed meat sat evenly spaced around the room, and conveyor belts threaded through machinery filled with blades. As we fanned out inside, several of the Unpronounceable\u2019s goblin minions began cursing and running around carrying all manner of objects as weapons, including a stop sign, a dead clown, and a flaming Barbie Doll. I\u2019ve seen paintings like that. One of the goblins turned on the lights and machinery, including a bank of huge fans. The lights revealed ten gaunt figures dressed in Thai robes crouching on the catwalk overhead. They were qing shi, Chinese vampires, and each had a paper exorcism charm plastered to its face. Unfortunately, the fans blew the charms free, awakening the vampires.<br /> <br /> With a bellow that sounded clearly even over the roar of the fans and machinery, Magnus smashed the catwalk with his axe, dropping several vampires into meat vats while Zane began beating up other qing shi. Edward screamed and slammed his hammer into a vampire\u2019s mouth over and over again, and Pipa tore the heart right out of the chest of a goblin who wandered too close. Then she ate it. Honestly, the sight of blood streaming down my girlfriend\u2019s chin and neck was NOT a turn on for me.<br /> <br /> I flew here and there, shooting vampires at first. But then Zane got mobbed by a bunch of goblins and vampires, so I dropped in beside her and put some bullets through in their brains. We look out for each other. Magnus and Edward maneuvered some of the titanspawn onto the conveyor belts, which resulted in minced vampires, and Pipa finished off a few more goblins, leaving her covered in gore. Then a couple of taotie masks showed up. I grabbed one, tossed it into the other, and then shot them both into stone shards.<br /> <br /> In the end, only one goblin survived, and Edward somehow got it in his head that the goblin was on OUR side. The goblin seemed to go along with this, so the rest of us shrugged and left it alone. Besides, it seemed terrified of its new \u201cbuddy,\u201d Edward. I\u2019ve never found Edward the least bit terrifying, but I suppose if you\u2019ve just had several of your friends\u2019 heads beaten in by his hammer, you would have a different perspective.<br /> <br /> As I shot the last of the goblins, Magnus began searching crates for the grotesques. He could sense them from the low, reverberating sound of the harmonics they were generating. Once he pointed it out, I could hear it too. We managed to find five grotesques, and then Zane warned us that Jean and Laughing Carp were in grave danger. She could sense their peril through the vigil marks she placed on them. We all dashed out of the meat plant, and I flew as high as I dared to get a look across the city at Club Tragos. It wasn\u2019t hard to spot. The purple lights were pouring from large holes in its exterior, and a gargantuan fish beast, probably the same thing we saw in the harbor protecting the cargo ship, was doing its best Godzilla impression. Flitting black shapes and smaller things were weaving around the club as well, and with my telescopic sense I could clearly see that they were ho shen and taotie masks.<br /> <br /> We have to go rescue Jean and Laughing Carp!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Dad-<br /> <br /> Ned is right strange. Did you know, he went and stole the pearl while we were fighting gobbos and sand things? Least she didn\u2019t notice. Well, she didn\u2019t notice the pearl missing. Mostly she just noticed Jean. And blushed a lot.<br /> <br /> See, we had a meeting, like I said before, after we got ourselves some rest. Ned was acting like he had a hangover, even though all he had was pancakes and loads of syrup. I never esen anyone have that much syrup. He started drinking it by itself when summat bet him he couldn\u2019t, and then he just kept on. Everybody else were alright, and even Ji-Woo showed up, with Pipa. They kept getting distracted though, specially when I gave her pancakes that she had to put upstairs, and we had to send Caoimhe up to go get them. It were ok any road, Mags was showing us videos of littles singing cutesy songs and a metal thing, with a big fuck-off lady statue what scared Ned, and a different band called White Scorpion, that is not White Snake.<br /> <br /> After they finally came down again, we went over to Jean\u2019s club. Even from across the room, we could all see Laughing Carp were staring at Jean like she\u2019d never saw him before. Ji-Woo figured it was cause Ned nicked the pearl. Laughing Carp was proper into him and had to be nudged to notice we got there. I guess the others were right, and the pearl were not letting her do things she might have wanted to. Least Jean weren\u2019t encouraging nothing, except by not wearing pants and having his shirt half open, but he is a satyr. A nice satyr though, and he\u2019s already looked out for her, even when she weren\u2019t giving him sex. He\u2019d make a good boyfriend for her, I don\u2019t know what Ji-Woo was fussing about.<br /> <br /> Her being distracted was good, kinda, seeing as she didn\u2019t try and arrest Pipa again, like Mags was afraid. She weren\u2019t too happy about seeing her, all dressed up in Ji-Woo\u2019s clothes and all, but she didn\u2019t make a fuss, even when Pipa was acting like one of the bints what goes around crowing about how they\u2019ve got the best boyfriend. I mean, Ji-Woo is right ace, but she\u2019s my mate too and just cause Pipa got someone brassed off enough we had to come rescue her, it don\u2019t make her special.<br /> <br /> Any road, Jean had found another gross statue that he thought the chaos blokes wanted. He figured we could follow it back to where they was keeping the others and so he tagged the can the chaos blokes had and gave me a beepy thing that knew where it was and when it moved. Laughing Carp said the statues would harmonize with each other and then maybe something would come out, so they probably oughtn\u2019t be all together like. But then Ned said something about rubbing Jean\u2019s chest, so Laughing Carp blushed and ran off. I was little worried, on account of her running out into the club all distracted without knowing her pearl was missing, and Ji-Woo noticed, and said I should go, so I gave her the beepy thing.<br /> <br /> Laughing Carp was alright, just run off to the bog to wash her face. She kept talking about not being distracted by the sins of the city, which was clearly a bunch of cobblers. I\u2019m not really looking forward to growing up and all, if it\u2019s that distracting. Though maybe for Laughing Carp it\u2019s just cause it\u2019s all at once, instead of like it\u2019s supposed to go, with no pearls or nothing. Still. she were all flushed and bothered, so I stayed and talked with her a bit until she felt better and then we went back to the others.<br /> <br /> Right when we got back, Mags was talking about taking off shirts, so all the blokes did (except Mags at first, but then he did later). But they was also talking about how we were going to follow the van. I\u2019d thought maybe I\u2019d ride invisible on the roof, so\u2019s I know when the statues weren\u2019t in the van no more, but Saoirse was all worried about that. In the end, we decided to follow a ways off and just use the moon to check when it stopped. That probably weren\u2019t near as fun, but there was a hole in the top of my car, so that were pretty ace.<br /> <br /> We did decide to wait for it to be dark again, so we had more time to sit around. Ji-Woo and Pipa talked about going to a drag show, but I don\u2019t think they got to go, seeing as they\u2019re mostly at nights. Saoirse asked me what that was and I told her, so I said it were where blokes dress up like bints and sometimes bints like blokes. Then she asked me what language I was talking! Seemed clear to me. That was when Ji-Woo decided to figure out if everyone was ticklish. Turns out Mags isn\u2019t, and it\u2019s a secret if Pipa is, but everybody else was. Laughing Carp were proper cute when I tickled her, she turned into her tiny dragon form and laughed all over.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo was acting right queer about Laughing Carp too. She kept saying Laughing Carp needed a boyfriend and nudging me like, when she ran off to the bog again after Ned or Caoimhe said summat about Jean again, and having me be the one who tickled her and all. I don\u2019t know what she thought happened when I went after Laughing Carp that first time, but she\u2019s a little silly sometimes. I watched over her for a bit, once the others left, but she stayed close to Jean, so she was safe and all. He\u2019ll be a good boyfriend, so I went and found Andy and Mags after a bit, since it were Mags I gave the beepy thing to.<br /> <br /> They were off getting a car, well, two cars. I gave Andy some advice with the wires on the second one, not that he weren\u2019t doing a bang up job. Once we\u2019d got it, he tried apologizing for Caoimhe, but she hadn't been bothering me none. She was just acting like them hanger ons what like it when blokes get all jealous and think about shagging them. I don\u2019t think Andy were really jealous, even if he did act like it a bit. Not that he would have hit her or nothing, but he would have finished with her if he were really jealous, specially after she started calling Ned food names.<br /> <br /> Andy and Mags had found a right ace red car, with the hole up top and black stripes going down the sides. There was a blue one too, that were pretty cool,I guess. We left that one for the others. See, right when we got to the meetup at the hotel, the van started up moving! Ned and Caoimhe and Ji-Woo and Pipa weren\u2019t there yet, so me and Andy and Mags went off in the red one, and Mags left Saoirse with the keys to the blue one so\u2019s the others could catch up.<br /> <br /> Our ride was not bad. I got to give directions using the beepy thing and stick my head out the top of the car, and Andy got all dressed up like some kinda pilot bloke, with a shiny helmet and a breath-y thing. But Ji-Woo\u2019s ride was bloody brill! She had to call, seeing as she didn\u2019t know what our car looked like, but then she used the moon. I used the moon too, once we\u2019d got there and it were like watching the fun part of a film! Pipa was driving on the sidewalk, and going up on two wheels - I think she had it on one wheel for a few seconds! She zoomed between peelers and down alleys and then Ji-Woo shot off the plate, pew! Somehow, there was still a few peelers following them when they were about here, so Pipa sent the car foosh over the water and they jumped out just in time.<br /> <br /> Ned and Caoimhe weren\u2019t with them and just as Andy said summat about it, Saoirse flew down out of the sky right next to him, carrying both of them. Mags got on him to ask for something else next, but nobody showed up with lots of money or weed. Well, Ned had a joint but that was all. Any road, we got all boosted. Ned gave me a brick, right before Andy yanked his underwear up over his head, so I flicked it back off again. To be fair, Andy also pulled his own underwear up over his own head. Once we\u2019d gotten all boosted, Ji-Woo asked for one for Pipa, since she was coming with. If I were nice and good, I would have before she asked, but Ji-Woo smiled at me anyways, after I boosted her. Pipa is pretty alright, when she\u2019s not being a bitch. Specially when she\u2019s driving!<br /> <br /> She were well hard in a fight too. She kept pulling the hearts out of loads of gobbos and eating them, right there! See, the van had stopped at some kind of factory for meat. It was right tank, and full of boxes and tubs of some kinda meat goop and a moving belt thing with all kinds of choppy bits hitting it. It were also full of goblins and then, when they\u2019d turned the fan on and all, a whole bunch of blokes that had paper on their foreheads that the fan blew off, that Ji-Woo called hopping vampires.<br /> <br /> It were a good thing Ned was there to boost me. The gobbos weren\u2019t strong or nothing, but there was loads of the wankers and they kept getting little hits in, with urinals and stop signs and dolls what were on fire and dead clowns. It would have been proper uncomfortable without a boost. Ji-woo avenged me this time, not that I fell down or nothing, I were fine really, but she weren\u2019t after the little bastards causing me the most problems, the ones with the stop sign and the dead clown, telling the rest to stop clowning around. I started for the vampires first, then they started coming after me too. I told them that\u2019s not how it works, and they was supposed to hit Mags or Ned, but they weren\u2019t listening too good. So Ji-Woo shot them too.<br /> <br /> Ned and Mags had been doing a number on the vampires. Mags got one by nutting it, and Ned laid into them with his hammer. So I started bowling with goblins again, this time into the choppy bits, seeing as they weren\u2019t no lions. I tried to get one of the calamities what joined up later to play, but I had to bother him a lot until he started batting and he didn\u2019t do it proper. Two of those masks showed up again too, but Ji-Woo did for them but good, specially after Andy pulled her underwear up over her head to boost her. Then it were mostly clean up, finishing off the three calamities with Mags magic black ord and Ji-Woo\u2019s shooting. One of the gobbos tried so hard to get away from Ji-Woo he lit himself on fire. I grabbed onto the last one, cause Ned wanted it for a friend. Like I said, he\u2019s well strange.<br /> <br /> Any road, just before we finished them off, I could tell Jean and Laughing Carp were in trouble. I thought at first that maybe her dad got mad at him for being her boyfriend and her for getting a boyfriend, but then Saorse told us to look outside and there was a big stonking fishy monster thing plus loads of masks and calamity thing attacking Jean\u2019s club! Mags had found the five boxes what had gross statues in them, on account of them making a very soft noise that got louder when they got close. We had to figure out a way to get them out safe and far apart, seeing as we didn\u2019t want to call up whatever they was trying to call up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XX</i><br /> <br /> OK well then. Cliffhanger.<br /> <br /> A lot of the session was role-playing. A lot of in character discussion of the previous night\u2019s hijinx, and in character planning discussion.<br /> <br /> Most of the enemies faced were the same as earlier. The Hopping Vampires were relatively minor Undead, not really using the Vampire template from Demigod. They were sort of somewhere between that and the Hungry Dead. The intent was a really big set piece fight in the meat processing plant with some vague description and a lot of leeway given to the players. It worked pretty well.<br /> <br /> The video Zane discusses was the video for Gimme Chocolate by Babymetal. Look it up if you want, I take no responsibility for it. The Underwear thing was because in the previous session Andy claimed it was a Manx greeting/show of respect and Zane should do it to Edmond while invisible. He referenced that when he did it as a stunt pulling hard enough to jerk himself into the air for Winds Freedom. His reasons for doing it to Ji-Woo could only have been his alone.<br /> <br /> Rajani\u2019s player had to miss due to weather. It had been Icy and she just got power back after about 5 days that afternoon so there was a lot of jugging going on.<br /> <br /> Conclusion to the story and the Hero portion of our tale next time. Come along if you would. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T03:01:05-07:00","id":99042,"title":"","content":"So the effects of the pearl's absence is being felt. Just waiting for that other shoe to drop. Mwahaha *cough cough*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T01:56:23-07:00","id":109102,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s the closing of the last Hero story for the campaign. This one was mostly one big rumble. Here we go.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXI</i><br /> <br /> <u>One Night in Bangkok Part VI</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bangkok</b><br /> <br /> You know, fighting a gigantic kaiju fish monster as it tore apart my friend\u2019s flashy night club may not be the most exciting thing that\u2019s ever happened to me, but it\u2019s definitely the most epic. My friends and I had only just finished liberating the strange grotesques from the clutches of Hundun\u2019s titanspawn, but we wasted no time returning to Club Tragos to rescue Jean and Laughing Carp. First, though, Magnus tossed each of us one of the grotesques for safekeeping. It was the best way we could think of to keep them all safe and separated. I played hot potato and tossed mine to Zane, who tossed it to Edward, and so on until Magnus glared at me and tossed me another one. I held on to that one.<br /> <br /> We awakened our divine powers and Zane and Edward bolstered our health. Zane even bolstered Pipa\u2019s without me asking this time, and she didn\u2019t even seem to mind! See, I knew she and Pipa would get along eventually. Then Edward, Zane, Magnus, and Andy piled into the car to drive back to the club, while I decided to fly on my own. Edward shoved his goblin into the trunk.<br /> <br /> Pipa stayed with me, and knowing the danger we were about to face, she transformed fully into her monstrous battle form so that she could fly along with me. She became both terrifying and beautiful (I mean, not more beautiful than usual, but still beautiful). Her skin took on the pale luster of white jade covered with a web of gossamer cracks and accented by her blood-red lips and the wisps of dark smoke drifting from her night-black eyes. The black claws on her hands grew even longer and more wicked. Several locks of her long, black hair wove together into sinuous pipa strings that lashed fiercely behind her, weaving in and out of the silken scarves that fluttered around her back and shoulders. She smelled of incense, and her movements were accompanied by the elegant and frightening sound of a pipa. She looked like a terrifying doll, a tempestuous Taoist immortal, and a white-faced demon all in one, and the sight of her captivated me.<br /> <br /> She looked at me and told me to kiss her. It broke the spell a bit, and then I kissed her passionately, all the while enjoying the odd sensation of her lips, which felt like soft, warm jade. When we separated, she smiled at me with genuine happiness and said, \u201cYou really DO love me, don\u2019t you?\u201d It was a statement, not a question, and I realized that the kiss had been a test to see if I would recoil from her monstrous visage when I saw one of her other true forms, or if my love for her let me see past that. Honestly, I wouldn\u2019t saw I saw PAST it. I found her terrifying appearance fascinating! But I\u2019m able to appreciate beauty in many forms, and every time I experience a new facet of Pipa, it just makes her more compelling to me. I think I really AM in love.<br /> <br /> After that, the two of us took to the skies while the others raced through the Bangkok streets to Club Tragos. When we arrived, we found that the kaiju had destroyed half the club already. Club-goers were fleeing in chaos, and some had already been crushed in the rubble or killed by the ogres, ho shen, and shadow monks that were rampaging through the place. Pipa dropped into the club from above through one of the gaping holes the kaiju had made while Magnus charged into the club through one of its windows. Andy started flying too and dragged Edward onto the roof. Meanwhile, I began circling the kaiju and dogfighting with a couple of taotie masks that were defending it. Zane stuck with me and helped me take them out by knocking them off course and right into my gun sights!<br /> <br /> Then Edward jumped on the kaiju, screaming hysterically as he slammed his hammer into its head over and over again until he realized it wasn\u2019t really doing much to the beast. Then he jumped down onto a crumbling wall and stared the monster in the eye. I don\u2019t know what he said to it, but it stopped attacking the club, and just kinda stumbled around in confusion after that. I popped off a few shots but barely hurt it, and then I heard Magnus shout something about masks to Rajani from inside the club. Rajani was already on the scene!<br /> <br /> But the masks were a problem. They\u2019re so nimble that the others have a hard time hitting them, so I dove for the ground and shot into the club through a broken ground floor window. Zane followed me in, but Edward stayed outside. I think he lost track of what he was doing, as usual. He ended up discussing philosophy with the kaiju for awhile and drawing faux-mystical symbols on it.<br /> <br /> I arrived inside just in time to see Magnus and Rajani tearing their way through ho shen and giants while Andy moved from shadow to shadow, carefully hiding while he tossed curses at our enemies. I shouted a greeting to Rajani, and then focused my attention on the taotie masks. Those little bastards are really quick! Zane took a swing at one and threw it off balance for me, and I was able to finish the rest off with a few shots. Not bad considering I was dodging lots of fleeing club-goers and dancing to Cosmic Gate\u2019s Omnia remix of \u201cCalm Down,\u201d which the club happened to be playing at that moment. I love that song! Andy could tell that all the fighting was taking its toll on me, though, so he came out of hiding and dip-kissed me to rekindle my fighting spirit. He\u2019s so random!<br /> <br /> I figured that Magnus, Andy and Rajani had things covered from there, and my insight told me that Jean and Laughing Carp were down a hall to the left, so I turned to Zane and said, \u201cThat way?\u201d and she nodded. We hurried deeper into the ruins of the club until we reached Jean\u2019s office, and then we carefully peered inside.<br /> <br /> Jean was there, facing a tall, pale, androgynous being that floating inches above the floor and spoke in two melodic voices, one masculine and one feminine. I didn\u2019t recognize what it was, but it was explaining to Jean that his interference would not go unpunished. Fortunately, it was so focused on Jean that it didn\u2019t notice Zane and me until we charged into the room and attacked it. Unfortunately, it possessed a sort of mystical serenity that allowed it to ignore my first shot as though I hadn\u2019t really hit it. It was okay, though, because Zane tackled it and another shot or two left it bleeding on the floor. It wasn\u2019t quite dead, though, until Jean walked up and angrily placed a hand on its forehead. He did something to make it bleed out more quickly, and THEN it was dead. At least Jean got some revenge for losing his club.<br /> <br /> We made sure Jean and Laughing Carp were okay. Laughing Carp was hiding in a room beyond the office, and Jean was going to try and get her to safety while we finished the fight. Then Zane and I flew back out into the club and found our way to the others. Everyone else, including Edward by this point, was fighting in the club\u2019s casino. One whole wall and a good portion of the floor and ceiling had already been torn out by the kaiju, but the beast was still perplexed and unable to do much more than stand still and look around in confusion thanks to Edward.<br /> <br /> Pipa was finishing off an ogre when I flew into the casino, so I called out, \u201cThere you are, you evil little minx!\u201d She seemed to enjoy that, and answered, \u201cHey lover. I saved you some.\u201d And with that, we all finished the rest of the ho shen, shadow monks, and ogres in the club.<br /> <br /> That just left the kaiju, so once the club was cleared, all of us focused our attacks on the hulking beast. It was so big that at first we did little more than lightly wound it, and in its state of confusion, it didn\u2019t even react to being attacked. Magnus got mad at it because he thought it was ignoring him, and his rage (plus Andy\u2019s blessings) helped his axe cut deep. Finally, Zane jumped on its head and shot it with her gun right in the middle of one of the faux-mystical symbols Edward drew on it. Edwards has always had an odd sort of luck, and apparently this time he marked the kaiju\u2019s weak spot, because Zane\u2019s shot blasted into its brain and killed it. Zane jumped clear as the kaiju collapsed into the club, taking out another quarter of the building on its way down.<br /> <br /> We fled the scene as the police and fire departments converged on the club, or what was left of it. As for the grotesques, we turned them over to Laughing Carp, who is making sure they are disposed of properly through the correct Bureaucracy channels. Jean was saddened by the destruction of his club, but it was fated to happen, and he seemed resigned to its loss. On the bright side, there\u2019s nothing tying him to Bangkok anymore, so it looks like he\u2019s returning to Berlin with Caoimhe after all! I\u2019m certain now that the reunion of the White Gloves troupe is destined, and that we are fated to help that come to pass.<br /> <br /> Sadly, Pipa and I are going our separate ways for a few weeks. She has to take care of a few things before joining me in Berlin, and I need to arrange an apartment. One of my art agents in Berlin, Erich Sunderhaus, can probably help me out with that, so I\u2019ll give him a call. In the mean time, Zane has invited me to go meet her mortal father in France. I don\u2019t even think SHE has ever met him in person, though she writes to him regularly. It should be exciting! Also, you can get some damn good absinthe in France.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> (cont.)<br /> So, to keep them safe and apart, we decided we\u2019d all take one of them gross little statues, seeing as we weren\u2019t going to be bunched up on top of each other or nothing, and there was 5 of us, just like the statues. Mags started tossing them about, first to Ji-Woo, but then she tossed it to me, like the hot potato game, so I throwed it to Ned, but he\u2019s not a very good catcher. He weren\u2019t hurt or nothing though, so it were well funny.<br /> <br /> Once we\u2019d passed them about and all got one, we got all boosted for a fight again. Andy made the dead clown get the stop sign and come along, and called it Captain Gigglesnort. I dunno what to do with the man sometimes. Ned took a picture with his phone of him and Ogden - that\u2019s what he called the goblin I grabbed up for him - then stuffed him in the boot of the car and got to the driver\u2019s seat. Come to think of it, I don\u2019t think we ever got him out of the boot. Oops...<br /> <br /> Any road, Mags called bagsy on the roof of the car, so I had to ride inside. It were still pretty brill though, on account of Mags busting up all sorts of shit on the way. I couldn\u2019t of done that, on account of not having a stonking huge axe and all. I got Mags all boosted up when I used him to dive in the hole on the top of the car, and got Ned when I bopped him in the head cause he weren\u2019t listening when I told him to turn some place.<br /> <br /> I got Ji-Woo and Pipa too, before we left, seeing as they was flying. Pipa was proper ace looking, with hollow-y eyes with smoke coming out and strings like a guitar (or a pipa maybe) on her back that spread out into wings and long, long scratchy nails and her skin was all crackly, but like some kinda posh doll face skin. Ji-Woo gave me one of her lucky coins, what made me feel even more super powered, so\u2019s I could knock things way off balance and all.<br /> <br /> We got there right quick - Ned\u2019s a proper good driver, even if it weren\u2019t as exciting as Pipa driving. The giant fishy monster thing were tearing a hole in the first floor and he had a few mask friends guarding him. Ji-Woo decided to deal with them first, so I stayed out to make sure she didn\u2019t get into any trouble of nothing. Pipa went in the hole the fishy made and Mags and Captain Gigglesnort went into the ground floor. Andy and Ned went up to the roof, but then Ned came back, falling down onto the fishy from way up high to hit him but good. It didn\u2019t seem to bother it none though, it just kept ignoring him and tearing the club up. At least until Ned peeled its eyelid up and started talking about Berlin, then the fish monster was too confused to do anything for forever.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo did a number on those masks, taking one out proper before I even knocked it off balance. It were close, when I did get to the other two to knock them off balance. See, I thought I\u2019d run up the wall and jump on them and kinda bounce between them, but I sorta missed a little. They\u2019re tricksy little wankers. I did grab ahold of the corner of one and swung myself kinda to the other. I did catch onto a windowsill thing proper, so I didn\u2019t actually fall down or nothing.<br /> <br /> They weren\u2019t too pleased with me after that even so. One of them tried to confuse me, but I saw through it! The other one cursed me, the wanker. Ji-Woo did for them though, doing a bloody ace spinny thing in the air. Then we turned on the fishy. It were a tough fishy - I couldn\u2019t do anything with my hands but knock it off balance, not that it weren\u2019t right easy to hit any road. Ji-Woo shot it once too and used some kinda super power thing, cause her bullet got reflected off a window and all, and all the reflections went for the monster too.<br /> <br /> Before we could do anything else, we heard Mags roaring about masks, so Ji-Woo and me ran inside. Ned stayed to talk with the fishy some more, so he was probably safe. Mags had done a number to the lobby. He came in through a window, like he does and it were probably him what throwed an ogre through the inside glass door. Also, Rajani was there! She\u2019d done for an ogre and some ninjas too.<br /> <br /> Inside proper, where Mags was yelling, there were a bunch of ogres and calamity things and 2 masks. I got one of them off balance right off, jumping from Mags\u2019 back, but Ji-Woo danced in with the music and got both of them before I could go for the other. So I bothered the calamities, though I had to hide behind Mags when they decided I looked proper tasty. He didn\u2019t notice though, on account of being well focused on the ogres, specially after one hurt him a bit. That one, he stuck his axe in the ground, put the giant on the other blade of the axe, then picked it up and slammed it into the floor again, ogre side down. Then he hit a calamity with the ogre-axe! It were well hard.<br /> <br /> He and Rajani had everything there all set, with the masks all gone, so me and Ji-Woo went after Jean. Laughing Carp weren\u2019t in proper trouble no more, but he was. He were talking with some kinda floating person who weren\u2019t a bird or a bloke, but sounded like both sometimes, who was talking all kinds of bollocks about how we wasn\u2019t going to be able to stop them. They were proper distracted, so when Ji-Woo gave me a hand signal thing I could sneak up without even going invisible and give them a drubbing and Ji-Woo followed up before they even really noticed us. That didn\u2019t quite do for them, so I grabbed them up at the waist to hold them still and all and Ji-Woo got all the posters in the room to shoot them alot. Jean finished them off, making them be sick enough to die.<br /> <br /> After all that, he went to go get Laughing Carp and make sure she stayed safe. So me and Ji-Woo joined the others up on the first floor where Pipa was. Ned got in there too, when he got tired of talking with the fishy. Rajani joined us too, after finishing off two of the calamities. Mags went for the fishy though.<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t take us long to finish off the ogres up there, specially with Andy buffing us up. He got Ned fixed up good, calling Ned Ji-Woo after he kissed him, seeing as he kissed her to buff her before. Not Mags though. There was some ninja blokes too, so I nutted on of them for old times and all. The other, I threw at the fishy, and the fishy thought he was food, so he ate him. I got an ogre too - I thought maybe the fishy\u2019d eat him too, but he was too big to throw, so I just gave him an elbow to the goolies and he fell over dead!<br /> <br /> Mags was getting proper cheesed off at the fishy, on account of it ignoring him. He thought maybe it were already dead, but then it ate the ninja, so it weren\u2019t. He did this well hard thing where he stuck the fishy way up high and rode his axe down to the ground, but the fishy were still confused about Berlin. We all ganged up on it then - I even pulled out my gun, seeing as I didn\u2019t need to knock it off balance any more or nothing. At first I shot at the scribble-y thing Ned put on its head, cause he said to, but then he got upset and had to fix it. So I jumped down to it and shot with my gun right next to it. And then it died.<br /> <br /> That were it for all the chaos blokes. Jean decided to come back to Berlin with the ladies, seeing as his club was all in pieces. So I guess we got all done that we came for, even though it were a bit sad that Jean\u2019s ace club got all broked. I just hope Laughing Carp\u2019ll be all right.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> I was thinking maybe I\u2019d make that visit here in a bit. If it\u2019s alright. Ji-Woo wants to come along, so you can meet some of my mates too. Just a few things to pick up, then we\u2019ll be heading to France.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <i><br /> End Session XXI</i><br /> <br /> Not much to add\u2026most critters were ones they had fought as the story went on reprised here at the end. The sea monster was insanely easy to hit as I tend to assign really huge creatures like building size a massive DV penalty (they make it up with lots of health and often soak) and only the heavy hitters could damage it, but everyone had stuff to do. There really was all sorts of enemies to fight this time.<br /> <br /> Next session will be visitations. Nature of the beast is such that you will mostly hear about Zane and Ji-Woo\u2019s (though you may hear a little about Edmond\u2019s from those two\u2026we will see) But in the meantime, comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T23:00:05-07:00","id":117865,"title":"","content":"This session was demigod visitations, as such being Ji-Woo and Zane\u2019s journals you are only really getting a direct accounting of their visitations. Still, I hope it is enjoyable, and I will have some very brief mention of others below.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXII</i><br /> <u><br /> What\u2019s Up? Complete</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <i>[Player\u2019s Note: I realized that I was being inconsistent in the transliterations I was using for various Chinese terms. To make things more consistent, I will henceforth be using the modern pinyin method for transliterating everything. This means that I will use \u201cYi Jing\u201d instead of \u201cI Ching\u201d from this point forward]</i><br /> <b><br /> France</b><br /> <br /> I\u2019ve spent the last week with Zane at her mortal father\u2019s home in France. It\u2019s a beautiful home, full of love and the laughter of children, though a bit mundane and domestic for my tastes. Zane\u2019s father is caring and kind, and he made me a bit homesick for my own mortal father. I haven\u2019t seen or spoken to my real father in over four years, and I miss him sometimes. I\u2019m also a bit envious; my mortal step-mother resented me, but Zane\u2019s step-mother, Violette, accepts Zane even if she doesn\u2019t always seem to approve of her antics. Actually, I probably make things a bit worse. Violette did not approve of Zane and me wrestling in the back yard. But who cares what the neighbors think anyway?<br /> <br /> We were wrestling in the backyard because I asked Zane to teach me how to fight like she does. I\u2019ve begun to master the winds in new ways, and I know that I will soon be able to coax them into fighting with me. So I really just needed Zane to teach me the underlying philosophy of grappling and wrestling. That way I could interpret the philosophy to the winds so they will be able to help me better. But Zane looked at me funny when I said that, and told me that she didn\u2019t know about any philosophy, but that she could teach me some of her street-smart grappling moves. She didn\u2019t actually say the street-smart part, though. I added that because it sounds better. We\u2019ve been practicing grappling and wrestling in her family\u2019s back yard. Our sessions inevitably break down when I start playing keep away and launch myself into the air on my ink-painted wings. But Zane is really strong, so she can jump quite high and keeping away from her isn\u2019t easy! It IS loads of fun, though.<br /> <br /> Zane\u2019s siblings are all delightful. Mathieu is a teenager, and I don\u2019t think he was ready for a couple of hot twenty-somethings to come storming into his life. The others, Jeanne, Gabrielle and Timothe, are younger, and they enjoy listening to Zane\u2019s stories even more than I do. Zane is really good with kids. I\u2019m not.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Zane\u2019s father doesn\u2019t keep any absinthe in the house, so I had to make several trips to get my own. That\u2019s okay, though, because I went to the best spots in France to get some really nice contemporary vintages, including some good La Berthe de Joux. I even took a trip into Paris to visit Vert d\u2019Absinthe, which is my favorite shop in the whole world. I picked up a few bottles of 2007 Belle Amie and a 1895 bottle of vintage Fritz Duval. I looked for another bottle of Dornier Tuller, but they didn\u2019t have any.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <b>France - Qian (Creative Force) transforming into Xiao Chu (Restraint)</b><br /> <br /> I contacted my art agent after we left Thailand and asked him to arrange an apartment for me. He told me that wasn\u2019t part of his job but I sweet talked him a little and he did it anyway. He found the perfect place! I haven\u2019t been there to see it in person, but he sent tons of pictures. It\u2019s a small but airy apartment with plenty of outside lighting. There\u2019s a bathroom, bedroom, kitchen, and a central area that I\u2019m going to use as a studio and living room. Everything is very artsy, and the best part is that it come with a big rooftop terrace! A beautiful hardwood stairway leads up to the terrace, and the door out to the terrace also serves as a skylight, letting plenty of natural light into the studio! I can\u2019t wait to see it!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m buying the apartment all at once with a chunk of my savings, not renting. I don\u2019t want that sort of monthly commitment. Erich says I\u2019ll have to pay taxes on it though, so that\u2019s annoying, but I got him to agree to manage that too in exchange for a bigger percentage on his commission from my art sales.<br /> <br /> I will confess that I\u2019ve still been worrying about the apartment, though. I can\u2019t help but feel like I jumped into it without thinking just because of Pipa. But I performed a divination to find out whether I\u2019m doing the right thing or not, and it set my mind at ease.<br /> <br /> The Yi Jing says this is the right time for me to seek a place to call my own. It\u2019s all part of my new cycle, another aspect of my transformation into a goddess. I suppose it\u2019s time I took on a bit more responsibility. The last few months have proven that my destiny is made of more than absinthe, art, and an endless European vacation, so I may as well accept that, even if it does make me nervous.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the omens are clear that I\u2019m approaching a major increase in my creative force and divine presence. Unfortunately, that means making important decisions, and I hate making important decisions! I have to figure out whether to dedicate myself toward serving the Bureaucracy or to follow a different path and work on my inner development. As long as I follow my intuition, I can\u2019t go wrong, and right now my intuition is telling me that I don\u2019t want to be stuck in the boring mire of celestial red tape. I\u2019m much more interested in hanging out with Pipa. Besides, the omens suggest that ambition is dangerous for me. No worries there!<br /> <br /> Sadly, Zane and I are destined to part ways soon. When I told her so, a look of terror crossed her face until I explained that it was only for a few weeks. It\u2019s weird. Zane and I have been together since we met. I\u2019ve been with her longer than I think I\u2019ve been with ANYONE since I left Korea. And going our separate ways, even if only for a little while, seems lonely. It obviously frightens Zane. But there\u2019s no avoiding it. The portents are clear. We are both rapidly approaching the next cycle of our divine existence, and we must face our transcendence independently of each other. To that end, I\u2019ll be heading back to Berlin in a couple of days. My apartment should be furnished and ready to go by then, and hopefully Pipa will arrive soon.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <b>Berlin</b><br /> <br /> My apartment is wonderful. It still feels strange having a place of my own, but I\u2019m getting used to it. And I like it. It suits me. Since I\u2019ve returned to Berlin, I\u2019ve had a surge of creativity, just like I predicted. I\u2019ve produced several paintings already, including an impressionist painting of the rooftop crowd at Weekend based on a series of photos I took there one night. I love the colors and mood of the piece. I thought about hanging it in my apartment, but maybe I\u2019ll have Erich see if the club wants to buy it instead.<br /> <br /> The upswing in my creativity is only the beginning. If only Pipa were here, things would be perfect! Sadly, she\u2019s not here. We\u2019ve spoken a few times, but she\u2019s not exactly sure when she\u2019ll be able to join me. Hopefully within the next few days. I haven\u2019t been lonely, though. I have tons of friends in Berlin, and of course I visited the sisters. Hermione, Aoide, Iris and me all went out clubbing last night and had a lot of fun. I haven\u2019t told them about Pipa yet; I think I\u2019ll wait until she comes to Berlin so they can meet her in person.<br /> <br /> Iris is still grumpy toward me, but she joined us anyway. I think she just didn\u2019t want to seem like she was avoiding me, or maybe she didn\u2019t want to seem like she was spending all of her time mooning over Caoimhe, because according to Chloris, that\u2019s all she\u2019s been doing lately. I don\u2019t really get what it is about Caoimhe that makes everyone fall for her like that. I think she\u2019s scary. I warned Iris to be careful. I\u2019ve already lost one friend to Caoimhe, and I don\u2019t want to lose Iris too. I mean, if she REALLY wants to sell her soul for the sake of her art, then I won\u2019t stop her, but I would have a really hard time dealing with that. And I\u2019m pretty sure Kalypso would blame ME.<br /> <br /> Oh, I also took Mr. Duck back from Aoide. She seemed reluctant to part with him, and that\u2019s when I realized that she really DOES have a crush on me. Which is good, because I still have a crush on her, but also bad, because I\u2019m very happily attached to Pipa. I should get Aoide another plush doll, something meaningful that she can keep to remember me.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <b><br /> Berlin</b><br /> <br /> Yesterday, I was reading while sunning myself on my apartment\u2019s rooftop terrace when I felt a tap on my shoulder. Normally I would have heard someone approaching, but I was listening to my headphones, so it startled me. At first I thought it must be Edward, since I\u2019d seen omens that he would be dropping by sometime that day. Instead, it was my mother! My real mother, that is, Chang\u2019e. She is such an amazing mom. Really, we\u2019re more like close sisters, so I was thrilled to see her! She said that she and Fu Xi had come by to talk to me about something wonderful and important, and he was waiting at the door to my apartment. He felt it would be improper to enter without being invited in first. I was going to go ask him in, but then mom and I got distracted catching up and it was probably ten minutes later before we remembered that he was patiently waiting.<br /> <br /> Once I invited my divine father inside and offered tea to my guests, Fu Xi and Chang\u2019e got to the purpose of their visit. Of course, I already knew why they had come. I\u2019ve been seeing omens and having prophecies about it for something like a month or two now. But it still felt really special to have my divine father tell me that my recent efforts have earned me a true place in the Bureaucracy. He pointed out that I can accomplish quite a bit when I apply myself. He\u2019s a wonderful father, you know. Instructive but patient. Even so, I got the impression that he\u2019s glad I\u2019m finally starting to amount to something. Also, Fu Xi is very handsome and distinguished, and Chang\u2019e is super hot. They actually made a really good pair. It\u2019s too bad Fu Xi\u2019s married to Nuwa, because I think it would be awesome if mom hooked up with him. Sure, she\u2019s married to Hou Yi, but he\u2019s a short-tempered jerk and she deserves better.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, they gave me presents too! First, they gave me a pair of stylish sunglasses imbued with the elemental spirit of fire and the golden warmth of the sun. Then they gave me a jade make-up compact fashioned from a celestial compass mirror, inscribe with the eight bagua trigrams. It\u2019s really posh, but it also serves as an anchor for my magic and Taiyi. It should make both much easier for me. And finally, my mom gave me a new charm for my charm bracelet/anklet: a little ice cream cone charm that\u2019s attuned to frost.<br /> <br /> I was admiring my gifts when there was a knock on the door. I assumed that Edward had arrived, but when I went to answer it, there was Pipa Jing, looking amazing and smiling at me with bedroom eyes. She tossed her bags into the foyer, pushed me against the wall and kissed me. Gods, it felt good to kiss her after over two weeks apart. She clearly wanted to make love right there, and I was pretty interested in giving her what she wanted, but after enjoying her kisses for a minute or two, I indicated that I had company. She seemed disappointed until I told her who was in the other room, and then her disappointed frown turned into a slightly mischievous smile.<br /> <br /> We walked into my studio/living room hand in hand. Of course Fu Xi and Chang\u2019e already knew Pipa, so I just told them that we were a couple. Mom gasped and covered her mouth with one hand, a deliciously scandalized expression on her face. She didn\u2019t really know what to make of it, but I don\u2019t think she\u2019s upset. More amused than anything else. Fu Xi, on the other hand, tried to speak but couldn\u2019t really find any words for a few moments until he finally just said, \u201cI see.\u201d Wow. I\u2019ve never seen my father flustered like that. Pipa thought it was incredibly entertaining, and she made a show of the fact that we are a couple, wrapping her arms around me from behind and resting her chin on my shoulder.<br /> <br /> Once he was over the surprise of learning who I\u2019m dating, Fu Xi opened a portal to Tian and summoned a lean, distinguished looking young immortal. He was handsome but way too severe for my tastes, and was dressed in Bureaucracy secretarial robes. He bowed and introduced himself as Lu Yisheng, my secretary in the Ministry of Virtuous Behavior and Righteous Action, otherwise known as the Peach Garden Ministry because it also oversees oaths and peach gardens.<br /> <br /> It was MY turn to be flustered. All the sudden I have a job in the Bureaucracy? An office? Paperwork and responsibilities? I didn\u2019t sign up for that. And how the hell did I get put in the Ministry of Boring Prudes? Well, as my father explained, it turns out I inherited my brother\u2019s job when I stole his divine legacy. I started to panic, because I am not, and probably never will be, ready for that kind of painfully colorless drudgery. So I was relieved when my mother told me that I didn\u2019t even have to go into the office. She says she doesn\u2019t even remember where hers is. That\u2019s what I have a secretary for. I can just let Yisheng handle everything.<br /> <br /> Smiling, I turned to Yisheng and asked if that was true. He said, \u201cI\u2019m at your service, my lady.\u201d I think Fu Xi might have been a little irritated by the obvious elation I felt when I learned that I could blow off my Bureaucracy job. But only a little. He explained that my services would be more important in the World, doing the sort of things I\u2019ve BEEN doing, which I gather means foiling the titans\u2019 plots, not clubbing, sipping absinthe, and crashing with artist friends across Europe.<br /> <br /> Yisheng gave me a special ink brush and explained that if I needed to contact him, I could write him a message using the brush, and it will appear in my office in Tian. Very convenient. He told me he might need to send me messages as well, and asked where I wished them to appear in my home. I cleaned out a decorative wicker basket I had lying around and told him that they should appear there.<br /> <br /> Now that I think about it, though, I\u2019m pretty sure I gave him that same basket to carry a bunch of my things to my office so that it will feel comfortable and familiar whenever I get around to visiting it. I kinda miss the comfy spread I sent with him, though\u2014the one I took from my friend Rien\u2019s place in Amsterdam when Zane and I stayed there a few months ago. Maybe I should write a message to Yisheng and ask him to bring it back.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I don\u2019t think Yisheng cared for me very much. He\u2019s way too serious. And I might have been making fun of him a little. And he probably thought the way Pipa was lightly kissing the back of my neck was inappropriate. Still, I should try to be nice to him. I\u2019m relying on him to do my job for me, so I should DEFINITELY keep him happy. I\u2019ll find a way to send him some Berliner pfannkuchen.<br /> <br /> After Yisheng left, I offered absinthe to everyone, and Pipa took me up on it. Mom said she wasn\u2019t going to be the only lady not imbibing, and we sat around talking while we leisurely prepared and sipped absinthe. Fu Xi decided to remain aloof from the drinking, but he continued to grace us with his sagely presence, and pretty soon, with my mind opened by the absinthe, he and I entered a deep and very enlightening discussion about the interpretations of several Yi Jing hexagrams. I performed a divination to seek insight on the path that lies before me.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> On my fate as a demigod - Kui (Diversity/Opposition) transforming into Ding (Cosmic Order)<br /> The oracle advises that my immediate path as a demigod will be fraught with misunderstanding and opposition, but that\u2019s not necessarily a bad thing. It implies diversity. It might seem that things are going against me, when in fact they aren\u2019t. Fu Xi pointed out the symbolic qualities of the hexagrams: fire and water don\u2019t mix, just like enlightenment and worry. I should let go of my restless fears if I want to find clarity. I think, among other things, that means I should try to overcome my fear of responsibility while continuing to identify with freedom. Fu Xi suggested that freedom is an important part of my divine character, so my challenge as I grow into godhood is balancing that with my responsibilities to the Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, I should not struggle to find the right path, but I should instead let myself flow with my fate. As my previous prophecy indicated, I should follow my intuition and let it guide me. If I do, I will find my place in the cosmic order by developing my character in whatever manner Heaven has decreed. I\u2019m just not sure the rest of the Bureaucracy is going to see it that way. Especially not Xiwangmu, who I\u2019m sure still has it out for me.<br /> <br /> My father and I were fairly deep in our discussion of the nuances of my prophecy when Pipa began to grow impatient. She began nibbling on my earlobe to indicate that mom and dad should leave because she was ready to take me to bed, and I was in complete agreement. I saw Fu Xi and Chang\u2019e out, and then Pipa and I broke in my new bed.<br /> <br /> When we made our way out of the bedroom a few hours later, we found that someone had been in the kitchen drinking my wine. Not my absinthe, fortunately, but pretty much all of my wine was gone. Edward stopped by after all! He even left a note thanking me for the wine. You wouldn\u2019t think it, but sometimes he can be very thoughtful.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <b>Berlin</b><br /> <br /> You know, it doesn\u2019t really feel that different being a demigod, except that I\u2019m more in tune with the cosmos and my mind is more open to all the intricacies of experience around me. Which I suppose is quite a difference, but I\u2019m kinda used to it, mostly because of the absinthe. That said, the omens I see are even more common and more obvious now. I can\u2019t really ignore the signature of fate can I?<br /> <br /> Anyway, a day or two (or maybe three; I can\u2019t really remember because it\u2019s all been a blur of absinthe, art, music and lovemaking) after mom and dad awakened me to my new status, Pipa was helping me learn how to play the pipa when there was another knock on my door. It was Daji! I was more than a little star struck again. Daji is gorgeous, and she\u2019s so famous that I felt a little out of my league. As she wandered around my apartment, absently examining my art while throwing enticing little glances my way, she explained that Nuwa had taken an interest in me. More importantly, Daji herself was VERY interested in me. I was considering whether that was a good thing or a bad thing (and ultimately deciding it sounded like a lot of trouble but also a lot of fun) when Pipa said, \u201cI\u2019m in LOVE with her, Daji.\u201d The sincerity really got to me. Lots of people have told me they love me, but not like THAT. Not like they really KNOW what that means and still mean it. It was also clear that she was telling Daji to keep her paws off me, but it didn\u2019t exactly work out that way. I\u2019m not really sure how it happened, but somehow Daji seduced BOTH of us and we all ended up in bed together. It was a pretty amazing afternoon.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t ALL sex. There was also some nice pillow talk, so I got to know Daji a little better. In the end, she gave me a present too, a fine ink brush with bristles fashioned from the fur of a fox-spirit\u2019s tail. It always flows with ink whenever I need it and it\u2019s imbued with a healthy dose of disorder. Daji said that I needed something to help me channel the chaos of my life more productively, and I suppose she\u2019s right.<br /> <br /> After Daji left, I felt guilty. I apologized for giving in to Daji\u2019s wiles and asked Pipa if she was mad. She was annoyed with Daji, but she wasn\u2019t upset at me at all. I mean, Daji seduced her too, so it\u2019s not like she can blame me. And besides, it really WAS a fun afternoon. Still, once Daji was gone, I couldn\u2019t help looking at Pipa and smiling when I realized how much I love her.<br /> <br /> Later that evening, I felt inspired and wrote a traditional Chinese poem about Daji and Pipa.<br /> <br /> The rapturous beauty of her pale, radiant face<br /> is like the cloud-enshrouded moon<br /> gliding mysteriously across the black satin sky.<br /> Silken caresses touch me with the warmth of a breeze<br /> borne upon the cusp of a storm that echoes with a fox\u2019s barking laugh.<br /> But I prefer the daring, fragrant peony<br /> with dangerous lips soft like peach blossoms,<br /> skin smooth like priceless jade,<br /> eyes dark and shining as though the night sky<br /> were reflected in a gentle spring.<br /> The storm passes, leaving the chords of her voice<br /> to strum me gently to sleep.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t notice until after I had finished the poem that I was using the brush Yisheng gave me to scribe the calligraphy, so I guess his first message from me was a little racy. Oh well. I hope he enjoyed it. Pipa certainly did. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve seen her so charmed as she was after she read it. And I like seeing her softer side.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <b><br /> Berlin - On Daji and Nuwa\u2019s interest in me - Tong Ren (Fellowship) transforming into Qian (Creation)</b><br /> <br /> I performed another divination to find out what I can expect from Daji and Nuwa\u2019s interest in me, and it only piqued my curiosity more. It seems that while seeking fellowship with them could be the right path, it\u2019s also going to cause problems, and it\u2019s probably going to lead me astray from the virtuous way of the sage. I can\u2019t follow my curiosity in this regard without getting into trouble, and it\u2019s DEFINITELY going to lead to more of that misunderstanding and opposition my earlier prophecy predicted. Oh well. I guess I\u2019m going to fuck this up, because getting involved with Daji, Pipa and Nuwa is way more interesting than toeing the Bureaucracy party line. Curiosity killed the cat, but cat\u2019s have nine lives, right?<br /> <br /> Yeah . . . that\u2019s EXACTLY the sort of thinking the Yi Jing is warning me to avoid. Oh well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> <b>Interlude:</b><br /> <br /> Gracious lady, I know you and come before you as your servant. Your presence in my heart and home are welcome, as always. I have some hopes of seeing you in person soon. Our daughter is here with me, and according to her seer friend, she is to find her fate here, in the next few weeks. Knowing the dangers of being the father of a scion of the gods, I hope this means you will be visiting as well.<br /> <br /> Our daughter is quite the troublemaker and certainly something of a trial for my wife. Violette has always been supportive and understanding of my past and my duties to you, but I believe she was expecting a refined 23 year old woman, not a mischievous rapscallion who appears to be of age with our son. I had read her some of Zane\u2019s letters, but still, we all have our ideas of what the gods\u2019 children will be like. Speaking of Mathieu, he too has made note of her apparent age, and her beauty. She has grown up quite beautifully, if I may speak biasedly for a moment, quite in the image of her mother. Thankfully, Zane has so far been quite oblivious to his attention. Her friend Ji-Woo\u2019s presence helped that somewhat - he was rather star struck, as it were, while she was around. Mathieu does know of Zane\u2019s relationship to him and would do nothing inappropriate, of course, but he is still a young man, and from her letters, I doubt the attention would please Zane.<br /> <br /> Does she know we named her Suzanne? I\u2019ve slipped up, once or twice, but she hasn\u2019t seemed to notice.<br /> <br /> Regardless, it has been adorable watching our daughter learn how to deal with having siblings all of the sudden. She arrived with a bag full of presents, fully intending to buy her way into their hearts. My wife was enchanted by the wide variety of art supplies, if a bit bemused by the reading levels of the novels she brought. The shoes were strange enough I believe she simply ignored them. Her assurances to Violette and I that she had neither stolen them, nor paid for them with stolen goods was possibly when my wife took against her somewhat. She says I spoil the girl, which, to be fair, is probably true. She deserves a little spoiling, I think, even if that does mean turning a blind eye to her staying up to all hours to practice wrestling with her friend in the back yard, or allowing her full run of the kitchen and pantry. And her rat friends are at least well behaved around her...<br /> <br /> The children are all quite taken with her, odd presents notwithstanding. Mathieu I mentioned, and the girls, Jeanne and Gabrielle, adore her. Even shy little Timothe lights up when he sees her and is constantly calling for her to \u2018frow me again!\u2019 She has read to them every night, for all that the 7 and 10 year old grew out of that, according to them, some time ago. I would wager the readings will continue when Zane leaves us again, at least until we finish off Oliver Twist, though I doubt I could make it half as interesting as she does somehow. Though I have been getting practice - Zane mentioned her friend Andy had been teaching her about \u2018superhero things\u2019, so I offered to tell her some of her pantheon\u2019s stories. I do believe my favorite part of these last few weeks have been when I told our daughter stories of her heritage, while she interjects every so often with something to make it \u2018more interesting\u2019 or with a thoughtful question about a small detail, \u2018so\u2019s I can see it in my head better, yeah?\u2019<br /> <br /> I do hope this has been a restful time for her and that she feels this can be a home for her, that she is always welcome. I have caught her looking wistfully at our pictures, especially of the children but occasionally of Violette and I. I have tried to be good, and not blame myself for her disappearance, but in the brief moment before she notices my presence, it is very difficult to keep from regretting not having any pictures of her.<br /> <br /> She will have to leave soon, I am sure, to go be a superhero somewhere else. Take care of her please, our lost forever-child, our bull-headed rapscallion. Help her find a place she feels safe and comfortable, where she won\u2019t want for anything, especially not love and friendship. Hold her in your sun-warmed hands, and let her know peace.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------<br /> William\u2019s search for his daughter was a quick one, having begun with checking the roof, and then moving on to the kitchen, where he found her eating from a jar of pickled onions. She looked up when he walked in. \u201c\u2018lo Dad. Want some?\u201d She held out the jar to him.<br /> <br /> He wrinkled his nose. \u201cNo thanks, sweetheart. I\u2019m still not sure how you can eat those things like that.\u201d He did a double take. \u201cAlso, I thought we were out of them.\u201d<br /> <br /> Zane nodded. \u201cI thought you or Violette had gotten more. I weren\u2019t going to eat them all this time.\u201d<br /> <br /> He smiled and ruffled her hair. \u201cYou have as many as you like. They were mostly for you in the first place, and I have a feeling this jar is from your mother.\u201d<br /> <br /> She grinned at that and hugged the jar close for a moment. All of a sudden she looked apologetically over at him. \u201cHow\u2019d you know she was here? Did I wake you or summat? I tried to be all quiet-like, but some of the stories had explosions in them...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you tried to be quiet, ma petite, I am sure not even the mice noticed, explosions notwithstanding. No, she paid me a visit as well.\u201d William began making cheese toast and pouring drinks for the two of them, juice for Zane and water for himself.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt were nice, yeah? It\u2019s right strange, thinking about it. Being around Mum... it\u2019s different than anything else. Like being safe and warm and full, all at once. I guess that\u2019s what being a mum is and all - the whore was never a proper mum, even when I thought she was mine.\u201d William put a plate of cheese toast in front of Zane and looked on bemusedly as she bit three onions in half, placing one of the halves from each on the toast. \u201cWell, it\u2019d roll off otherwise, wouldn\u2019t it?\u201d she said defensively.<br /> <br /> \u201cI suppose they would, at that. And I suppose you\u2019re right about your mother as well. She is very good at being motherly.\u201d<br /> <br /> Zane nodded sagely. \u201cIt\u2019s just different, is all. Not like being here. I thought here would be different too, but having brothers and sisters is like having littles in the gang, and I\u2019d got used to sleeping inside and all already. And you telling stories is a lot like Jester did.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJester? The young man who visited earlier? I may be a little jealous.\u201d She gave him a sharp look, freezing in her seat. His eyes widened and a note of panic reached his voice. \u201cNot like that, not like that at all, Zane. Just that you had a father figure that wasn\u2019t me. Which is good! That you had someone to look out for you, it\u2019s good.\u201d<br /> <br /> Zane relaxed and patted William\u2019s hand. \u201cS\u2019ok Dad. I just weren\u2019t thinking... I know you\u2019re a good bloke and all, s\u2019alright.\u201d They say quietly together for a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, what did your mother have to say? That is, if you don\u2019t mind...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNah. She said I was a demigod now, and gave me presents! A scarf-belt thing what makes it so I can\u2019t get cold, and a necklace that helps it so I don\u2019t need any posh book learning to use my healthy type superpowers and all. And I asked her if boyfriends and girlfriends could be mates too, cause in gangs, see, it were supposed to work that way, but it never did. But Ji-Woo and Pipa and well, you and Violette, you\u2019re mates proper, seems like, and that seems weird but Mum said it weren\u2019t.\u201d Zane looked significantly at him and he nodded in confirmation. \u201cShe said too I oughtn\u2019t be held back by my femininity.\u201d She carefully pronounced the unfamiliar word. \u201cI think she meant I should be a boy if I wanted to, but not just \u2018cause girls aren\u2019t strong, \u2018cause they are. She\u2019s got a point, I guess. I mean, Ji-Woo is, and Rajani and Phaedra are, and Pipa and Laughing Carp and Mum. Still and all, now I can be a strong girl and a boy sometimes, so it\u2019s alright.\u201d She nodded so emphatically that William had to stop himself from laughing, despite not being certain either he or Zane understood what she had just said.<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds like a good conversation.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYup. After all that, I told her stories, on account of I hadn\u2019t been writing her letters or nothing. She\u2019s really good to tell stories to, she always laughed and clapped at all the proper places.\u201d<br /> <br /> William did laugh at that. \u201cThat is an important skill for \u2018mums\u2019. And this Jester fellow - did he come by because you are now a demigod as well?\u201d<br /> <br /> Zane nodded. \u201cHe said I might have to do politics things now, and that I could come ask him things, which he probably wouldn\u2019t know about, so\u2019s we could not know together.\u201d She paused and looked up at him. \u201cMum doesn\u2019t hate the Greek... Roman... whatever gang, does she?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPantheon,\u201d he said distractedly, trying to figure out how to answer.<br /> <br /> \u201cHuh?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh sorry. It\u2019s just that the word for a gang of gods is pantheon. But as to your question, that\u2019s... really more of a question for your mother, but she doesn\u2019t hate easily. Most of the rest of your pantheon is... somewhat better at holding a grudge.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, that\u2019s what Jester said. I like Ned though, he\u2019s alright.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen I like him too and the rest of your pantheon can get over it.\u201d William managed to hold onto a mock stern face as Zane looked at him wide-eyed for a few moments before both of them collapsed laughing.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey sound proper fierce, dad, you probably don\u2019t want to get them mad at you or nothing,\u201d Zane managed, between giggles.<br /> <br /> \u201cThen it will have to be our secret.\u201d He gave her a broad smile and a wink, inexplicably inciting another round of laughter.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh! Jester also magicked up my flute. Well, his flute, but he gave it to me back when I first became a superhero. Now I can use it to protect littles so they don\u2019t get hurt just \u2018cause superher- demigods is fighting nearby. He used to be the Pied Piper, you know...\u201d<br /> <br /> Another voice piped up from the door. \u201cThe Pied Piper?\u201d But he\u2019s a fairy tale.\u201d Mathieu looked a bit embarrassed when they both turned to look at him.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, sure,\u201d Zane responded. \u201cSo are gods and superheros and things too.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mathieu paused, unsure how to respond until Zane offered him the jar. He shrugged and got a fork to spear one with. \u201cSo, son, what are you doing home?\u201d I thought you were at Etienne\u2019s.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI, uh, overheard you telling Mom Zane was leaving soon and I didn\u2019t want to miss seeing her...\u201d Mathieu scratched his head, avoiding looking at either of them.<br /> <br /> William turned to Zane, somewhat stricken. \u201cIt\u2019s not that any of us want you to go, sweetheart. It\u2019s just that your mother did tell me you had become a demigod, and reminded me you couldn\u2019t stay at home - here - forever.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cS\u2019alright, dad. I probably do need to be moving again. I gotta visit Londontown and maybe stop by Paris and Amsterdam and see the littles there and then check up on Ji-Woo in Berlin.\u201d She rolled her eyes at Mathieu. \u201cNot that I\u2019d have left without saying bye, any road. I was thinking I might mark everybody, so\u2019s I\u2019d know if you were in trouble or summat.\u201d She stood up, after collecting all the crumbs from the tabletop.<br /> <br /> WIlliam stood up with her and pulled her into a hug. \u201cThat would be lovely, ma petite. And you know... you know you are always welcome here, whenever you need, or want, to drop by.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know, dad. I know.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXII</i><br /> <br /> Everyone basically got two part visitations except Edmond, who was a special case. Rajani was visited by Kali first then later Hermione, and Magnus was visited by Bragi and Idun then his half-giant brother Kjell.<br /> <br /> Edmond was a special case. I ran a series of 8 very short vignettes basically as he stumbled from one event to another. He wound up goading a teenager to attack a clown, landing a plane, breaking into Ji-Woo\u2019s apartment, having a baby, teaching a high school class, running a bicycle directly into a running of the bulls, fought himself, and ended up in Ten Forward. How much of this was real, how much was in his head, and how much was him interacting with the real world via a dream world was never set in stone, but other people\u2019s visitations had snippets of his activities.<br /> <br /> We start \u201cRock it for Me\u201d next time. Join us won\u2019t you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T02:39:45-07:00","id":127334,"title":"","content":"OK Demigod time. Group is back together. Let\u2019s go. Rock it for me.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXIII</i><br /> <br /> <u>Rock it for Me Part I</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Berlin - Da Guo (Great Excess) transforming into Dui (Joy)</b><br /> <br /> So we\u2019re all back together in Berlin! Granted, it seems a little weird that I\u2019m the one who has a place here and was already in town, waiting for the others to arrive instead of the other way around. Of course, Magnus also has his warehouse studio here in Berlin, but we really haven\u2019t seen much of each other since I returned to town. Anyway, I somehow just knew that everyone was gathering again, so I started calling people and insisted we all get together for an awesome night of clubbing at Berghain. Also, it would let us compare notes on our recent transcendence into demigods.<br /> <br /> Before the others arrived, though, Zane showed up at my new place! When I opened the door and saw it was her, I was so happy that I immediately threw my arms around her in a big hug. And then I noticed that something was different. Zane was a guy! She had actually turned herself into a he, and darn cute one too. He still had the same mischievous eyes and adorable freckles, but they were set in a boyishly handsome face. He was still the Zane I know and love, though, and I was thrilled to see him again. He\u2019s going to be staying with Pipa and me at the apartment while we\u2019re in Berlin. There\u2019s not a lot of extra room, but I\u2019m sure Zane can make himself comfy in the studio or something. And least he\u2019s getting along fine with Pipa now.<br /> <br /> Anyway, everyone met up at the Panorama Bar in Berghain. Rajani strutted in looking gorgeous and dressed to kill. Her mother, Kali, visited her and requested a tattoo! That\u2019s a serious honor. Rajani was practically gushing with pride, except that she doesn\u2019t really gush, so it was more like she was glowing with pride. Actually, since I\u2019d already had a glass of absinthe by the time she arrived, she was LITERALLY glowing with pride. Also, she has a second sword tattoo on her back, and like her other one, it can turn into a real sword when she fights.<br /> <br /> Magnus was pretty nonchalant about his visitation. I gather that he and his father got a little competitive but were able to bond a bit. Magnus seems to have some abandonment issues with his father, though. I guess he\u2019ll have to work those out as he fulfills his fate. He also hung out with his frost giant brother, with whom he gets along with much better than he does with Bragi.<br /> <br /> Edward was already there when we arrived, and he seemed confused about the details of his visitation. There was something about a son who might be a centaur and might be a vampire, and there was a plane crash and it all revolved around a horse somehow. He may or may not be married; he seems confused about that too. Also, he might have killed Santa Claus, and I\u2019ll be really pissed off if that turns out to be true. I\u2019m not sure how much of it was a drug-induced hallucination and how much was for real, but with Edward it\u2019s impossible to tell. Oddly, Edward kept speaking Spanish without realizing he even knew the language, but I discovered that I could make him switch back to English by tugging his earlobe. I tried doing the same thing to Zane, but he didn\u2019t turn back into a girl. It did make his eyes sparkle in a really beautiful, dreamy way, though. I love how absinthe lets me see things even more clearly as the really are.<br /> <br /> Andy didn\u2019t say much about his visitation, but I asked how his old man was doing. Mannanan mac Lir IS sort of one of my mentors, after all. It\u2019s how Andy and I knew each other before we met up in Berlin. Andy said Mannanan asked about me. He also said his father was an terrible lecher. Clearly, the two statements were related. I always knew the old man wanted to get in my pants.<br /> <br /> We hung out at Berghain for awhile, and then decided to go see the sisters. I wanted Pipa and Edward to meet them. But we had to stop by my apartment first. I wanted to show it off, and I needed to get something to give to Aoide to make up for taking Mr. Duck back. Speaking of Mr. Duck, I puppeted him having a short conversation with Edward, and Edward seemed vaguely terrified. How can anyone be scared of Mr. Duck? He\u2019s adorable! Except to his enemies. Don\u2019t mess with Mr. Duck! He\u2019ll fuck you up.<br /> <br /> Anyway, everyone complimented my apartment, though it was kinda crowded with all seven of us in there. Magnus said it suited me perfectly. I appreciated that. He\u2019s got an eye for these things, being a fellow artist. I especially enjoyed showing everyone the rooftop terrace. I mean, that\u2019s MY favorite part of the apartment. We sort of hung out there for awhile and I collapsed into a deck chair and started gazing at the stars, and suddenly I saw patterns of fate forming in the constellations. I tranced out and just lay there, languidly staring at the stars until Pipa took my hand and pulled me out of the lawn chair, saying, \u201cAlright, sweetie, you\u2019ve had enough absinthe for the time being.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I explained that I\u2019d just had a prophecy. It came to me like a poem written in starlight on the aurora borealis:<br /> <br /> Where is she, the woman of oak?<br /> Hiding in forests, deeper than the sea, beyond a path walked by the Bard<br /> Where is she, the woman of apple?<br /> Hidden behind the trickster\u2019s eye, Lost to those who seek answers over wisdom<br /> <br /> Where is she, the woman of ice?<br /> Standing in the swamp, surrounded by earth of man<br /> Where is she, the woman of death?<br /> Surrounded by puppets, knowing not what aligns against her<br /> <br /> Where is she, the woman of war?<br /> Surrounded by her betters, stewing in hate<br /> Where is she, the woman of peace?<br /> Separated by guile, lost to vice.<br /> <br /> Where are they, of fire and ice?<br /> Hiding in the skies, two skies, hearts over lands distant<br /> Where is he, the instigator?<br /> Waiting, watching, changing the play<br /> <br /> Who are his tools?<br /> The Warrior Bard, The Woman of Apple, The Woman of Oak<br /> Who are her tools?<br /> The Woman of Apples, The Woman of Ice, The One who keeps his Kenning<br /> <br /> Why does he betray?<br /> Because it is not the time\u2026<br /> <br /> I told the others that I didn\u2019t really understand it all right now, but I knew it would become clear whenever we needed it to. Magnus told us that when he met his father, he also met his stepmother Idunn, the keeper of the Apples of Immortality. For some reason that resonates with me, so I\u2019m pretty sure she\u2019s the Woman of Apple. The Bard is either Magnus or Bragi, probably Magnus. And if that\u2019s the case, then we are about to get involved in some sort of trouble with the Norse pantheon.<br /> <br /> The last line of the prophecy left me feeling insatiably curious, though. It\u2019s not the time for what? Probably Ragnarok. After all, this IS the Aesir we\u2019re talking about, and Ragnarok is pretty much all they think about. I started rambling on about that and Magnus told me I shouldn\u2019t make prophecies. He said that as soon as the prophecy is spoken, it limits our options. I don\u2019t see it that way at all. We always have options. Omens and prophecies just provide guidance. Magnus should be more grateful. I mean, how often have my insights given us the answers we needed to defeat the titanspawn? Besides, fate is fate. It doesn\u2019t matter whether a prophecy is stated or remains unsaid, the river of fate is going to flow its course anyway. We can accept it or deny it, and our choices will shape the way it flows, but we can\u2019t stop it.<br /> <br /> With those thoughts in mind, I disappeared into the kitchen to fetch the nice vintage coffee maker I got from Edward a year or two ago. And while I was there, I tossed the coins to consult to Yijing on my prophecy. The advice was pretty awesome. Our upcoming trials are defined by the hexagram Da Guo (Great Excess), which means that we are approaching a powerful moment in which we will have opportunities to shape the fate of the Aesir, and maybe other pantheons, in important ways. Our recent transcendence has prepared us for this, and the challenge might seem too much for us right now, but if we focus on the right path, we can win the help we need to overcome it. We run the risk of losing our inner equilibrium, though, especially Magnus. He will be challenged in ways he has not faced before, and will have to make choices that might cause serious conflict within the Aesir. He should be cautious, but he should also seize opportunities when they arise.<br /> <br /> If we are mindful of these things and are willing to accept and overcome the conflict, then the outcome will be true joy and inner stability. I guess we will learn and grow from this, especially Magnus.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> After leaving my apartment, we went to see the sisters. Edward had a bit of trouble getting out of my apartment. He doesn\u2019t seem to be able to find the door. And Andy was really mean to him. He pushed him down the stairs from the rooftop terrace! Edward didn\u2019t seem hurt, but it was still really mean. Normally, Pipa doesn\u2019t care much for Andy\u2019s antics, but she also has a malicious streak a mile wide, and I caught her smirking at Edward\u2019s misfortune. Poor Edward.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Magnus told us on the way that he needed to meet with Idunn to discuss the shrikes. Apparently, there\u2019s some question among the Aesir as to who is responsible for them and what to do with them, and since Magnus has dealt with them more closely than anyone else recently, they want his insight. Magnus was pretty eager to go meet with Idunn. I think he\u2019s got the hots for her, but he was trying not to let it show, which is understandable since she\u2019s his stepmother. I guess I could have convinced the others to hang out more with the sisters and let Magnus go see Idunn on his own, but I was WAY too curious to pass up the chance to meet this goddess that has our heavy metal skald all hot and bothered.<br /> <br /> But before we headed off to meet Idunn, we visited the sisters. Their mansion is finished, and Anemone really did install some indoor slides and other fun things, so Zane ran off to play for awhile and didn\u2019t rejoin us until later. Apparently Bori and Sari live there now too. Bori was the first person we met, and he\u2019s a little grumpy because his sister has fallen head over heels in lust with Jean. However, the REALLY juicy news is that Kalypso has a thing for Jean too. Ooh la la! She tried to hide it, but I could tell. That IS interesting.<br /> <br /> I introduced Pipa and Edward to everyone. I tried to get Edward and Iris talking since I think they might enjoy each other\u2019s company, and he\u2019s arguably better for her than Caoimhe. But Edward was weird and confused as usual, and I\u2019m not sure Iris knew what to make of him. She\u2019s still kinda cold to me, but I don\u2019t think she\u2019s really angry anymore. She didn\u2019t seem upset when I introduced Pipa as my girlfriend, anyway. Well, maybe a little. Chloris was really nice to Pipa, though. Hermione was friendly enough, but as soon as she saw Rajani, she was pretty distracted. I guess Hermione likes the strong, silent type.<br /> <br /> Of course, most of my time was spent with Aoide. I\u2019d already told Pipa pretty openly that I had a crush on Aoide but that Aoide was a bit too flighty to really get it. Maybe that wasn\u2019t the best thing to tell my girlfriend, but I think Pipa knows I love her, and she also knows who I am, and she\u2019s REALLY only jealous of Daji (I think), and I prefer to be pretty open about these things. Still, I know she was watching when I apologized to Aoide for taking Mr. Duck away and then used the transformative arts of Taiyi to turn Edward\u2019s vintage coffee maker into a big, fluffy plush cloud pillow with an adorable little face and a pink bow. Oh my god, it was SO huggable. When I gave it to Aoide, her eyes lit up and she smiled brightly, like the sun breaking through clouds. Then were shared some new trance tracks and started dancing with each other and the cloud pillow. Pipa watched us with some amusement and then finally joined in when I shoved the cloud pillow into her arms and pulled her close. I think sometimes I test the limits of her dignity. Still, she was definitely trying to figure out what to with Aoide. I hope that\u2019s a good thing. But I\u2019m not sure . . .<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Magnus drove us all to a large, posh rental house on the edge of town. Two women greeted us. One was a scary-hot heavy metal blonde wearing leather and fishnet. That was Idunn. In contrast, the other was a pretty redhead who was dressed like an American housewife from the 50\u2019s. That was Hestia, the Dodekatheon goddess of hearth and home. She certainly acted the part of the innocent domestic goddess too, offering us brownies and milk as she guided us into a living room like something out of an American sitcom. I don\u2019t know if Hestia\u2019s really all that innocent, though. Edward definitely recognized her. He called her an insatiable tigress and seemed awfully uncomfortable around her, which made the \u201cseparated by guile, lost to vice\u201d line of my prophecy come to mind. I think Hestia is the Woman of Peace.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Hestia played the gracious hostess while Idunn explained the situation. The Aesir are trying to find out more about the shrikes, but Odin and Loki are being awfully cagey about them. Idunn wants to know who made the shrikes in the first place. She thinks Loki was responsible, and wants proof. If she\u2019s right, then maybe Loki is the \u201cinstigator\u201d I prophesied. But if not, then there might be someone else involved.<br /> <br /> Idunn also told us that Hel has a daughter in the area. She might be looking for other bunkers with surviving groups of shrikes, or she might be up to something else. I suppose I should consult the Yijing to find out. I wonder if she is the Woman of Death? Or is that referring to Hel herself?<br /> <br /> Magnus told Idunn all he knew about the shrikes. He was pretty positive about them. I mean, sure, they have some serious problems, being Nazis and all, but he\u2019s been reforming them, so there\u2019s hope for them yet. We decided that we needed to learn more about what the daughter of Hel is up to, so we\u2019re going to track her down tomorrow. Probably not until later, though. Idunn says she needs Magnus for something else in the afternoon. Ooh la la. I elbowed Magnus and gave him an encouraging look, kinda like he did to me when Pipa asked me to dance that first time.<br /> <br /> We hung out with Idunn and Hestia a little while longer after than, and Magnus told some awesome stories about our exploits. I was actually THERE when those stories happened, and it still sounded a lot cooler when Magnus told it! When we eventually left, Idunn asked Magnus to linger a moment so that she could have a word in private. By the time Magnus joined the rest of us outside a minute or two later, I had already done a quick Yijing reading on whether or not he should woo Idunn. I shared the Yijing\u2019s advice with him. If he wants Idunn, then now is the time to act. But he should be warned that if he follows his heart, it might be awesome, but it\u2019s also going to cause him some serious trouble. Andy took note of this and started muttering something about leaving his fancy pen somewhere inside the house.<br /> <br /> Magnus glared at me and Andy for a moment before saying, \u201cSo your omens are basically just telling me what I ALREADY knew.\u201d But even though he said that, he still went back inside to . . . find Andy\u2019s pen . . . yeah. See? Sometimes\u2014a lot of the time\u2014the oracle just helps you better understand what you already know.<br /> <br /> We then split up for the night. Edward begged off and hailed a cab as quickly as he could. He seemed really eager to get somewhere fast. I wonder if it has anything to do with Hestia? I started to suggest that we head to Weekend and hang out in the rooftop lounge, but Pipa insisted on going home. She\u2019s going to have to leave to go back to work for Daji and Nuwa soon, and she wanted to monopolize my time as much as possible before that happens. I\u2019m sad that she has to go. I don\u2019t WANT her to go. But I understand.<br /> <br /> At least Zane will be sticking around.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <b>Berlin</b><br /> <br /> Zane woke me up super early this morning. It was awful. It was exactly 8:42. I know that because I have an absolutely perfect sense of time thanks to my kinship with the stars, and I was just annoyed enough to make special note of the time. Still, boy Zane is super cute, and that took some of the edge off. When he said that Hestia had called because she and Idunn were in trouble, I got up as quickly as I could and used my powers to clean up and dress in the blink of an eye. I summoned my ink wings and Pipa transformed into her demon form so that we could fly like the wind to Hestia\u2019s house, and Zane leapt from rooftop to rooftop in great bounds, easily keeping pace with us. On the way, Zane shouted that there was a really big white wolf thing waiting hungrily outside Hestia\u2019s house, and that Hestia had been out that morning and didn\u2019t know if Idunn was okay or not. Hestia\u2019s not exactly a warrior, so she called us in as reinforcements.<br /> <br /> (to be continued . . .)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> In case you were wondering, my mates is just as barmy as when I left then, for all they\u2019re demigods and such now too. Ned even had a kid - they had to cut it out, on account of him not having the plumbing for the proper way, yeah? Also, it was a horse. Or maybe a centaur, he weren\u2019t sure. He called him Dnumde, in case he were a vampire. The \u2018d\u2019 is silent though. Course, it being Ned, it might or might not been real. Same for him killing Santa too, but Santa\u2019s a tosser anyway, so that\u2019s alright.<br /> <br /> Any road, I got a call from Ji-Woo inviting me to come stay at her place and all while I was looking in on Jester and the gang in Londontown. It were right nice seeing her again. She\u2019s so good at seeing what things are proper, she didn\u2019t even notice I were a boy at first. She did say I was fit as a boy though, when she finally did. I decided to try it out for a bit, being a boy, and see what all the fuss was about, yeah? It did Andy\u2019s head in, and Ned was proper confused, but Ned\u2019s always confused. It didn\u2019t bother Rajani none, or Mags really, though I forgot I looked different at first when I said hullo so <u>I</u> was confused when he didn\u2019t know it were me. He\u2019d had a bet on with Andy on whether I\u2019d be a boy or not too. He lost.<br /> <br /> We\u2019d met up at Berghain, the club what was full of zombies last time we was there. Rajani was looking well hard, with a new sword tattoo and everything. Rajani had gotten to tattoo her mum, the one what was a god and all, which is right ace. Mags had some new tattoos too. Rajani hadn\u2019t done Mags\u2019s, but he said maybe she\u2019d do one later, seeing as he\u2019d left room and all. Andy was dressed up proper posh, when he weren\u2019t turning into a girl to wink at me. It were well strange, since he never came on to me when I was a girl or nothing, and more, right after that he\u2019d go on complaining on account of me not having any tits, not that I\u2019d had much when I was a girl neither. Ned was, well, Ned right enough. He kept complaining about how dark it were, while he was wearing some posh bint\u2019s sunglasses. Speaking of (the sunglasses, not the posh bint part, Ji-Woo\u2019s brill), Ji-Woo got some sunglasses from her god mum and dad, and a bunch of other presents, like a makeup thing, and a new dangly bit for her bracelet. Pipa\u2019s friend Da Ji got her a fancy brush that Ji-Woo used to write a poem on the wall without even using any ink first. She\u2019s also got some kind of posh job now, but she has a secretary or summat like that to do it for her and all.<br /> <br /> Any road, Ned kept talking funny, that Ji-Woo said were Spanish, but Ned said he didn\u2019t know Spanish. Worst, Ji-Woo\u2019d start talking Spanish or whatever when he did. It were easy for her to switch back at least, but Ned looked like he were going to choke trying, until Ji-Woo figured out she could make him switch by tugging on his ear. It worked for anybody even - Andy kept switching him but I\u2019d just switch him back, cause it\u2019s funnier when I can understand the bollocks he\u2019s saying. Ji-Woo tried to see if it would work to switch me to a girl. It didn\u2019t, but it did make sparkles come out of my eyes. That might have been the absinthe though.<br /> <br /> Ned did make Ji-Woo sad, a bit, when he got ice cream and poured absinthe for a topping. I kinda thought it were a brill idea, but I didn\u2019t want to make Ji-Woo <u>more</u> sad, so I just had ice cream. She got distracted though and started telling crazy stories about her mum and dad\u2019s gang pantheon after she used their special magic to turn a glass into a flower for me. Mags was acting all superior on account of the stories being about right strange blokes, until he remembered a bloke named Loki from his dad\u2019s pantheon. He got knocked up by a horse! That\u2019s when Ned told us about his maybe-son and about crashing a plane and teaching somebody art by breaking a wall down. Ji-Woo thinks Ned would be a good teacher. I think she\u2019s a bit off her trolley.<br /> <br /> After ice cream and drinks, Ji-Woo showed off her place to everybody. It\u2019s got this ace open space so\u2019s you can look up at the sky and all, it\u2019s like it were made just for her. I\u2019ve been spending lots of time there, cause it\u2019s nice and cool and Pipa is here, and they can get kinda loud when they go to bed and it\u2019s kinda uncomfortable. Different now that I\u2019m a boy, but, I dunno... strange.<br /> <br /> Any road, Andy kept going into the closet and coming out of the bedroom. Also, he was wearing pajamas with horse heads and dead Santa\u2019s on them. When we were all out on the terrace, Ji-Woo had a prophecy thing, something about fire and ice and wooden women or summat like that. She\u2019d just said it had Mags in it, all important, when his phone rang! It were his god dad\u2019s wife, Idun, who\u2019s well fit, for certain, saying she and somebody from Ned\u2019s dad\u2019s pantheon, Hestia, were about to look in on the Nazi ladies and wanted to talk with everybody. Ji-Woo scared Ned and Andy by saying \u201cIt\u2019s begun\u201d all spooky-like, but we still decided to go see the ladies underground first.<br /> <br /> Ned had some problems leaving though. First, he said he couldn\u2019t use the door, but then he let Andy guide him out blindfolded. Then Andy pushed him down the stairs and said I did it! He didn\u2019t get hurt or nothing, seeing as he\u2019s well tough, but he did go back upstairs and went out through the window. He was upset there weren\u2019t a jungle no more, I guess.<br /> <br /> We headed over to the ladies\u2019 cave, and it were ace, on account of the house being all finished! WIth slides and elevators and tubes and everything! I went down and up all of them. The others went on downstairs, to introduce Pipa and Ned all round. Ji-Woo was also going to give Aoide a new stuffed thing, since she took Mr. Duck back and all. She didn\u2019t bring one, but she did bring a coffee maker and Aoide had a stuffed cloud when I come down, so Ji-Woo probably magiced it up. Sari weren\u2019t around, seeing as she was out with Jean, according to Bori, but Anemone was. She was talking about her next big project, since the house were finished and all. She\u2019s going to make a flying bus, with 2 steering wheels, the usual one and one up top, so you can be riding and driving up on the roof! She were worried about what if both steering wheels was turned different at the same time, so I told her there ought be a button that said which was driving it proper.<br /> <br /> By the way, Ned\u2019s very bad at talking with girls. Ji-Woo introduced him to Iris special, seeing as they\u2019re both artists, but he kept talking about Caoimhe and making her upset. All the girls were paying him some attention when they learned about his dad though. I guess he\u2019s famous and all. We didn\u2019t get to stay too long though, cause Mags\u2019s step-mum wanted to talk with us.<br /> <br /> When we got there, Ned finally noticed it were dark on account of the sunglasses he were wearing. So he ate them. He ate lots of weird things - a tape and the blindfold and a drink glass - that were a sight for certain. Andy were a sight too, going to meet the two lady gods. He was wearing a long fur vest thing and tight pants with more fur. He asked me what I thought, since I\u2019m French and all, so I told him he were fucking weird looking. He kept wearing it though.<br /> <br /> The lady gods were right nice. Mags\u2019s stepmum Idun was well fit, like I said, and Hestia was ace. She made brownies and brought us ice cream in chocolate, vanilla <u>and</u> strawberry. She brought me milk too, cause that goes good with brownies. They were about cause some of Idun\u2019s pantheon was worried about the Nazi ladies. [Ji-Woo?] called them the third shrike, cause shrike\u2019s what the Nazi ladies are called proper. I was right confused, cause I thought she was making a cricket joke, and nobody makes cricket jokes. Also, it weren\u2019t a very funny cricket joke. But it were a Nazi thing, Ji-Woo explained.<br /> <br /> But we talked about that for a long bit. I had 6 brownies, and I weren\u2019t even eating fast or nothing. Odin and Loki and Hel from Idun\u2019s pantheon were acting all cagey about the shrikes. There was also another superhero in town, Hel\u2019s daughter, so that might be trouble, what with the cageyness and everything. Ji-Woo says she\u2019s in a puppet theatre though. We all said nice things about the Nazi ladies. They were nice enough, after all, and well hard, even if only me and Ji-Woo can see the pointy teeth. After that, Mags told some bloody brill stories about us and how ace we are.<br /> <br /> When we left, Ji-Woo did a prophecy about Mags and Idun. She said it said to follow his heart, but not right now, but the time were right. Sometimes prophecy is as confused as Ned. Mags said he knew all that already, but he did go back in to get the pen Andy left. He didn\u2019t do nothing else though, or else he\u2019s right quick. Any road, Ned had somewhere else to go, so he got a taxi and Mags dropped the rest of us off. Andy got off with Ji-Woo and Pipa and me, but then he flew home with his umbrella.<br /> <br /> It were right nice, being with everybody, being a gang again, even if they are all nutters.<br /> <br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not every day that starts by getting a message that your god-friends are being attacked by a big stonking wolf. It gets things moving fast for certain, even Ji-Woo early in the morning. Even just getting there was exciting. We didn\u2019t have a car or nothing there at Ji-Woo\u2019s, so she and Pipa flew, and I jumped rooftops. That were proper ace. Ned nicked a cab, I guess, seeing as we caught him crawling out of a crashed one right nearby.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXIII</i><br /> <br /> Zane decided to be a boy this session. Her player got Zane the Appearance knacks to shift at will. Andy has that power too, but he was using Illusion.<br /> <br /> Not much else specifically to report. Hestia was played as the sort of ideal 50s housewife, but the shift in culture has lead to her having a decidedly kinky side. She is also the bored housewife who dallies with the mailman, and she took a shine to the always-confused Edmond. Of course, no one actually believed he was tied to a bed in a hotel room by the sweet lady giving them all cookies, but that is how it goes.<br /> <br /> This was cleared with his player first, of course.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo made a fair amount of use of her new Taiyi Boon.<br /> <br /> Anyway, actual combat and such next time. Join us then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-07-2014, 05:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T01:55:16-07:00","id":145417,"title":"","content":"t\u2019s time to continue the Rock it For Me storyline. This session was nearly all combat, so easy to cover.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXIV</i><br /> <br /> <u>Rock it for Me Part II</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Berlin</b><br /> <br /> So we arrived at Hestia\u2019s house and found Hestia hiding nearby. Magnus, Rajani, Andy and Edward joined Pipa, Zane and me around Hestia and we considered our options. The huge white wolf that was guarding the doorway sort of sauntered inside at that point, like it was luring us in, so I knew this was a trap. I wanted to have a look inside, and was suggesting that I use my clairvoyance to have a glance, but I was a bit hesitant because it takes a lot out of me to do that. My hesitation was all Edward needed to go crazy again, and he went running inside the house screaming something about how he\u2019d scout it out.<br /> <br /> Naturally, Magnus and Rajani followed, with me, Zane, Andy and Pipa close behind. Then there was fighting. It was pretty crazy. I kicked a table over into a wolf\u2019s face to distract it while I shot another full of holes. Magnus and Edward demolished the rest of the wolves, and Zane and Rajani slaughtered this creepy ice serpent thing that was coiled within Hestia\u2019s living room. We destroyed a lot of stuff, but later, Edward managed to rescue the rugs because Hestia was concerned about them. I\u2019m not sure whether he was being considerate or was simply frightened that she would be angry.<br /> <br /> As we finished the monsters in the house, I heard the distinctive beating of huge, leathery wings from outside, so I warned the others that a couple of dragons had arrived to cover the exits. I also heard the depressing shuffle of zombie feet, so we were also surrounded. That didn\u2019t stop Edward, though, and he scrambled up into the house\u2019s attic and burst through the roof to jump onto a dragon. He took a blast of frosty dragon\u2019s breath to the face and sort of missed the dragon and almost bounced off, but managed to latch on with his claw hammer, and after that he and Rajani made short work of the beast. Then Edward threw it into a cluster of zombies, messily crushing them into oblivion. He\u2019s surprisingly strong for such a scrawny guy!<br /> <br /> I followed Edward outside through the hole he had made, waiting long enough to avoid the dragon\u2019s frosty breath, and then launched myself high into the air. From there, I could see the small horde of zombies, which were led by an aptrgangr. I hate those guys. He noticed me too, and tried cripple me with illness, but thanks to Zane, I was able to shrug off the worst of it and keep fighting. Then I unleashed the power of the sky on our foes and tore several of the zombies and the aptrgangr from the ground, trapping them in fierce whirlwinds. Because I wove a bit of chaos into my whirlwinds, it looked like spectral fox spirits were swirling within them, biting and clawing at the undead. Unfortunately, zombies are pretty resistant to being knocked around, and the aptrgangr tore free of the whirlwinds pretty quickly. So I ended up dropping most of the zombies after crushing one and flinging him into some power lines. Then I opened up on them with my guns. Normally, my guns don\u2019t do much to the undead either, but this time I imbued my bullets with the essence of the heavens so that they burned with starlight. As I shot the zombie,s it looked like shooting starts were raining down on them. That did the trick.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Zane was running interference and punching the hell out of things as usual. He was kinda pissed off at the aptrgangr because it attacked me, so he went after him. Pipa helped clean up the zombies, and Andy was stumbling around like he was drunk, using his antics to bless our efforts and curse the enemy.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve saved the best for last, though. Magnus he went completely berserk! I mean, he grew a couple of feet and all of his muscles were straining like they were trying to escape his skin! He screamed incoherently (kinda like a death metal singer, actually) as he thundered out and took on one of the dragons by himself. His axe hammered the beast over and over until it lay dead, and by then, Magnus had expended his fury and was more or less back to normal. Still, scary.<br /> <br /> I landed as Zane and Edward were finishing the last of the zombies. Looking around and seeing my friends covered in blood and gore, I made a smug comment about how I was glad I had been up in the air and out of the mess on the ground. Then Zane punched the head off the last of the zombies and splattered me with blood. In the strobing lights of a club, zombie blood can be beautiful and evocative. But splattered across my face, the only thing it was evoking was vomit. I glared at Zane, because I\u2019m pretty sure he did it on purpose. No harm done, though. I used my divine powers to clean up in an instant.<br /> <br /> There was no sign of Idunn, so tracking her down was our first priority. Zane could sense that she was in danger, but not imminent danger. Magnus sighed and observed that we had forgotten to leave anyone alive to question. Again. That seems to be pretty habitual for us. Are we really that bloodthirsty? I mean, I know Rajani is. It\u2019s kinda her thing. But you\u2019d think the rest of us would show a little more restraint.<br /> <br /> Then I noticed the crows that were settling on the corpses surrounding the house. Omens seemed to cluster around scenes of death, especially where the Norse are concerned, and I became entranced by the patterns in the crows\u2019 staccato movements. My prophecy, the one I had while gazing at the stars last night, began to come into focus, and I suddenly knew who most of the players were.<br /> <br /> The woman of oak is the troll wife Ulfa, as if the aptrgangr and zombies weren\u2019t enough of a clue. I knew she would come back to haunt us. The woman of apple is Idunn, of course. And the woman of peace, as I\u2019d already suspected, is Hestia. The woman of ice is Sigrid. The woman of war is Hriki. And the \u201cOne who keeps his Kenning\u201d is Utgard-Loki, though that seems odd. Something doesn\u2019t quite measure up there, because if that\u2019s true, the Utgard-Loki is being used in some else\u2019s schemes, and isn\u2019t he normally the schemer? I asked Magnus about that, and he thought the elderly goddess Elli might be pulling Utgard-Loki\u2019s strings, but I\u2019m not so sure.<br /> <br /> I might have been able to learn more, but then two of the crows started acting strangely and talking to one another, and the only insight I got from them was how many licks it takes to get to the center of a Tootsie Roll pop (it\u2019s a very profound truth, and I dare not reveal it here). Andy was fucking with my omens, using his illusion powers to mess with the crows. I was very cross with him, since it screwed up my insights. I kinda yelled at him. So I\u2019m still not sure who the instigator is, or where the ones \u201cof fire and ice\u201d are. At least I was able to glean that Idunn is in the same place as the mysterious daughter of Hel we\u2019ve heard about, which means both of them are probably at the address we got before. So I guess that\u2019s where we\u2019re heading now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> (cont.)<br /> We found Hestia hiding just outside. It was her what called Mags, seeing as she knew Idun were in some trouble, even if nobody were trying to kill her or nothing. She were worried about the carpet too, on account of the big stonking wolf what was breathing out cold. It fucked off inside right as soon as we got close and all, so Hestia thought maybe it\u2019d mess on the carpet or something. She hadn\u2019t even been making wolf treats - Ji-Woo asked.<br /> <br /> Once we\u2019d all got there and everything, we was gonna plan out things. Ji-Woo had some posh new power for seeing through walls and shit, cause she sees things, yeah? It were gonna be a bit rough and all, so she tossed it about just long enough for Ned to run off in by himself. Not that that were very long any road. Andy jumped in right after, saying something about being mannish and all. I got barely time to boost up Ji-Woo and nobbut her, which were good. Well, it were good I got her, cause the big zombie wanker tried making her sick and all. I wish I coulda gotten Mags too - the dragon gnawed on him a bit. But he charged straight in the window. The door was too far away and all, yeah?<br /> <br /> I charged in too, but I used the door, on account of only being a little crazy. I weren\u2019t wearing a shirt neither, so the glass woulda bit a little. Mighta made me look well hard though, cause it\u2019s not like it would have hurt or nothing, just maybe bled a bit. Ji-Woo said next time she\u2019d have blue paints and shit, so I\u2019d look well hard like those pictures you showed me of Mum\u2019s people in the old times. Any road, inside there was 4 ice wolf things, and an ice snake. They was all big fuckers, but I jumped right in a yanked one of them\u2019s tail to make it be off-balance and everything.<br /> <br /> We did for them but good. Rajani had her two swords out now and she was spinning about, cutting the shit out of the wolves. Mags was tossing couches at them, then using his axe to shop them in half, and Ji-Woo were throwing tables around, before shooting them a whole bunch. I mostly ran about, knocking the buggers off-balance. I did get to go a round with the snake bloke, before grabbing ahold of him so\u2019s Rajani could slice him into pieces. Ned had picked up a swing-y type trash can lid, and were pretending to use it like a shield kinda. Also, he were howling like he were a wolf too. I almost didn\u2019t hear the mess of zombie fuckers coming up outside.<br /> <br /> We did though, me and Ji-Woo at least and probably everybody. They weren't being too quiet or nothing. Also, Mags heard the dragon what were waiting at the doors, even though they was proper quiet. While we were doing for all the wolves and the snake inside, Mags went a bit off his trolley, what with them setting us up in a trap and all, and when we was done, his eyes got all crazy, and he were foaming at the mouth like a mad dog and all. I waited until he jumped on out through the roof and everything, then I ducked down into a shadow and popped out another to give the big zombie wanker a bit of aggro.<br /> <br /> There were not the best idea I\u2019d ever had. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ll do it again. I hurt him a bit, sure, but then he hit me back well hard. I\u2019m alright, yeah, nothing hurt or anything, but I had to swap with my shadow to make sure, specially since Ned hadn\u2019t gotten to boost me or nothing.<br /> <br /> Any road, it were just me and Mags on that side of the house. The others ran through the attic, like Mags but less jumping through the roof and more ladders, yeah? They went out the back to get the dragon there, though Ji-Woo got right high up first thing to shoot at everybody. She had a new trick she learned that I helped with. She sent out like whirl-y wind things to wrestke with 4 of the medium sized zombies and the big one, the aptrganger, to hold them still and all, yeah? I were right up close, so I could see there was little foxes running about in the wind-y things, helping out. The aptrganger berk got out right quick, which were a bit bad cause it were right when I was thumbing my nose at it and all.<br /> <br /> While Ji-Woo were helping out with the zombies, Ned and Rajani did for the dragon over there. Mags got our dragon, almost cutting his wing clear off! I don\u2019t think he liked being bit and all. Andy was being well odd the whole time. He got a new boosting kinda power, what makes me stronger and faster and gives me power back and clears my head. But he were acting like a proper piss-artist to do it, nutting Mags, telling me I was the one what was drunk, complaining to Rajani about my tits again, and grabbing onto Ji-Woo\u2019s shoes while she were flying. He kept changing what he looked like, sometimes like Ned, sometimes like some bint and at the end, like some really funny looking blighter, with even crazier eyes than Mags.<br /> <br /> What with Ji-Woo shooting falling stars at them, and me knocking them around, and Raj and Mags and Ned joining up (Ned were even dressed up like a zombie, after a bit. I dunno if I ever wanna go to a fancy dress party with him, since he just picked up a zombie what had had a dragon thrown at it and put it on his head), we\u2019d almost done for the undead fuckers when another 2 ice wolves showed up. That weren\u2019t enough to slow us down none though and we finished up right quick. It were great though, at the end - Ji-Woo didn\u2019t see the last little zombie plonker and was just talking about how she were glad she didn\u2019t get any muck on her, being up high and all, when I splattered him all over her. She glared at me, but I don\u2019t think she were really mad at me. She just dinged clean any road.<br /> <br /> So, the house was proper wrecked. Hestia weren\u2019t too happy about that, even though Ned did save the rugs for her. Mags weren\u2019t too happy that we forgot to leave one of the buggers alive to ask him where Idun were. Good thing we had Ji-Woo though, on account of her knowing everything anyways. There were crowds and crowds of crows about, and Ji-Woo stared at them for a bit. Right off, she was annoyed that Ulfa, the troll bint, were back. She probably sent the aptrganger and all, and Ji-Woo doesn\u2019t like them none at all, on account of her getting sick easy and all. She and Mags talked some about a bloke called Utgard-Loki and a bint named Elli, who are probably important or summat. I dunno whether they\u2019re good guys or bad guys though. Ji-Woo did figure out Idun was with Hel\u2019s daughter, so we decided to go visit her place. Ji-Woo even decided to go without absinthe, she was proper serious.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXIV</i><br /> <br /> So big combat.<br /> <br /> Thje Dragon, Wolves, and snake all were immune to ice but had half soak against fire. Anyone with Frost 1 was immune to the snake\u2019s venom and Dragon\u2019s breath. I swear I thought Rajani had Fire 4 but she did not\u2026my original notes said Rajani had fire, and her player wound up not taking it when she created the character, and somehow I kept forgetting. It did not matter, ultimately. The group did extremely well against the creatures, due in part to the fact that most of them are immune to Frost at this point.<br /> <br /> Next time our heroes stage an impromptu rock concert outside a high school to give a teenage virgin a tattoo. Why? Find out in two weeks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main