":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T21:29:36-07:00","id":159725,"title":"","content":"These are PC journals of actual play with a 6 person group. It is table top, so we are all in the same room. Unless otherwise noted, everything described actually happens in game.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the slow journals for this next game, I should have them up within the next 24 hours. Just got the second journal for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T22:06:16-07:00","id":159743,"title":"","content":"awesome, I enjoy following your adventurers. Reminds me of larp, the sheer depth of the game content","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1584-oberon","name":"Oberon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T16:00:24-07:00","id":160336,"title":"","content":"Glad you are enjoying. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My group tends to have strong characters and a lot of IC interaction throughout games...this is true of all the APs in my sig. I've been asked more than once if eveything happened in game especially on the Geist one.<br /> <br /> So sorry about the delay\u2026we had a journal come late and I am still getting back on an even keel and recovering sleep. The story continues unabated however, as it shall for you\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXV</i><br /> <br /> <u>Rock it for Me Part III</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Berlin</b><br /> <br /> After dealing with things at Hestia\u2019s house, we made our way to an isolated little house on the outskirts of Berlin, where Hel\u2019s daughter and Idunn were supposed to be. Magnus pounded on the door until the butler opened up, and by butler I mean a zombie in a tuxedo. The butler went to fetch his mistress, but Magnus got impatient and barged in, making his way to the house\u2019s basement, where there was a mad science laboratory in which a young woman who looked very much like a teenage Madeline Usher was bolting steel plates to a zombie\u2019s head. Her name was Hert, and it turns out she knows Magnus\u2019 brother, Kjell. In fact, she seems a bit obsessed with him. Hearing her talk about him made me feel claustrophobic. Poor Kjell. I commented that she sounded awfully clingy, and she reacted EXACTLY like Iris did when I suggested the same to her, down to the same tone of voice. Apparently clingy people don\u2019t like being told they are clingy.<br /> <br /> The omens said Idunn would be with Hert, but she wasn\u2019t, and Hert didn\u2019t know anything about her. Sadly, that means someone is fucking with my visions. I should have seen it coming. My prophecy even warned me about it: \u201cWhere is she, the woman of apple? Hidden behind the trickster\u2019s eye, lost to those who seek answers over wisdom.\u201d So it looks like my divinations aren\u2019t exactly reliable right now, and in fact, whoever is doing this was probably trying to get us to attack Hert. That said, my prophecy is spot on, so at least we have something to go by. And now I know that the puppets surrounding the woman of death\u2014Hert\u2014are zombies. I should have seen that coming.<br /> <br /> Hert came to Berlin because Kjell asked her to meet him there. But Magnus called his brother and Kjell says he did no such thing, which means that Hert is being manipulated too. Whoever the trickster from my prophecy is, he\u2019s weaving a pretty complex scheme here, and we\u2019re caught up in it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Hert\u2019s zombies were missing, and we wondered briefly if they hadn\u2019t been stolen by Ulfa for the attack on Hestia\u2019s house. But I argued that Ulfa was perfectly capable of making her own zombies. Something else had probably happened to Hert\u2019s puppets, and after Hert explained that she employed the ghost of an Anglican priest to herd her zombies around, Rajani decided to cut to the chase and just summon the ghost. It\u2019s good to know she can do that.<br /> <br /> The ghost, whom Hert calls \u201cPreacher Bob,\u201d was a tall, gaunt, creepy-looking guy in a priest\u2019s cassock. He spoke in a hoarse whisper of voice that carried the hint of menace. He told us that he had been captured by a frost giantess and her minions and imprisoned in a magical icicle until Rajani\u2019s summons broke him free. Based on his description, it didn\u2019t take long figure out that he had been captured by Hriki, the woman of war from my prophecy, who was serving Sigrid, the woman of ice. We believe that Sigrid is searching for the shrikes, so Magnus called them and told them to remain alert and on standby.<br /> <br /> So, everyone is looking for the shrikes, but we\u2019re not sure what Ulfa\u2019s game is yet, though it\u2019s possible she\u2019s trying to manipulate Magnus into killing Sigrid for some reason. We also don\u2019t know who the trickster is (though my guess is Loki) or what he\u2019s after. And I don\u2019t even think we should necessarily be looking for all the answers, not if my prophecy is to be believed. We should be looking for wisdom instead. That being the case, maybe the trickster is trying to teach us something. I suppose we\u2019ll just keep following the clues and see where they lead us.<br /> <br /> Preacher Bob agreed to take us to the place where he was imprisoned, but he gets a little a crazy when he hasn\u2019t had his fix. He\u2019s hooked on blood, specifically innocent blood from someone who has never had sex, never killed, and never told a lie with the intent to hurt someone else. There was a brief moment where we all looked at each other, wondering if any of us qualified, and then I burst out laughing. All of us have done at least ONE of those things, and I\u201dm guilty of all three. So we had to figure out how to get some blood that would suit Preacher Bob\u2019s needs without actually harming anyone.<br /> <br /> We left Hestia at Hert\u2019s place, where we hope she will be safe. As we were leaving, I drew Pipa aside and told her that if she had work to do elsewhere, this would probably be a good time. Of course I like having her around, but it looked like things were getting pretty complicated, and we might be busy for awhile, so it was probably a good time for us to go our separate ways. She kinda frowned and said that she didn\u2019t like leaving me in a dangerous situation without her, but then she admitted that she might as well get used to that. We made out a bit until Andy started making fun of us, and then she flew off. Unlike some women, Pipa is not clingy.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I spent a few hours this afternoon decorating an abandoned storefront with Edward. We had to turn it into a tattoo parlor. I transformed Mr. Duck and a few other odds and ends into a set of high quality tattoo equipment using the Taoist wonders of Taiyi, and Edward gave the place the right amount of artistic clutter. I even painted a beautiful, hand-hand lettered sign on the front window. It read \u201cHerr Enten Tatowierung,\u201d (Mr. Duck\u2019s Tattoos). After that, I was bored with painting, so I retired to the back of the shop to sip absinthe and read while Edward stood outside and tried to drum up business.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Magnus, Zane, Rajani, and Andy invaded a local high school and held an impromptu heavy metal concert. Magnus can make ANYONE rock out, so by the time they were done, they had even had the principal headbanging, which gives new meaning to the term \u201cheadmaster.\u201d Under the cover of the concert, Zane, Andy and Rajani managed to find a virginal high school outcast and convinced him that a badass tattoo would turn his social life around. Then they brought him back to Herr Enten Tatowierung so that Rajani could work her magic on him.<br /> <br /> While Rajani was giving the kid a tattoo, she used her powers of entrancement to keep him focused on her, which wasn\u2019t very difficult since she\u2019s so hot. While the kid was entranced, Preacher Bob manifested and lapped up the blood beading up from the his skin as the tattoo needles worked across it. And THAT was the point of all this\u2014to get Preacher Bob his fix. And to make a poor high school kid\u2019s life more awesome.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Once we fed Preacher Bob, he was more than willing to lead us to Hriki\u2019s lair, so that\u2019s where we headed next. She was working out of the Berlin Geological Society building, which was closed for renovation. It used to be an old bank but was converted into a museum, and the interior is spacious enough for giants and very secure since it still holds many of the bank\u2019s security measures, including the main vault. I visited it once when I was reading up on geology, but my boyfriend at the time was bored and hurried me through it so we could go back to his place and have sex. I think I left him the next day and went to Istanbul.<br /> <br /> Edward was ready to go charging in like he did at Hestia\u2019s house, but Magnus stopped him and we sent Zane in first to scout the place out while the rest of us waited nearby. When he returned, he reported that Hriki had been talking to Sigrid via Skype on a laptop. Sigrid was ordering Hriki to withdraw her forces, but she also mentioned an experiment. We don\u2019t know exactly what the experiment is all about, but Sigrid arrogantly suggested that Hriki might benefit from it, which really pissed Hriki off. It sounds like the experiments have to do with enhancing giants or something, though I\u2019m not sure why they would need the shrikes for that. After Sigrid terminated their Skype session, Hriki totally lost her temper and smashed the laptop to pieces with her sword. Looks like my prophecy was right, and Hriki really DOES hate Sigrid. We decided to use that if we could.<br /> <br /> Zane also said that Hriki was hot. Ooh la la. Zane is a lot more rakish as a boy. I don\u2019t know how he\u2019d handle a frost giantess, though, so I\u2019m not worried that he might hook up with her or anything. Besides, frost giantesses are more Magnus\u2019 speed.<br /> <br /> After Zane returned and reported what he had seen, Magnus decided to march right in and demand to speak to Hriki. Zane warned us that there were several giants, some gigantic wolves, and a couple of dragons inside, so we knew we were walking into a fight. But I guess Magnus figured that after we had slaughtered a bunch of her minions, Hriki would be more willing to talk.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s pretty much how it went down. We marched in and Magnus demanded to speak to Hriki. That didn\u2019t go over well, so we had to fight some giants and their wolves. Magnus and I fought back to back for bit, which was pretty awesome. Also, Andy has this new trick that lets him awaken the fullest potential of our virtues, and it is AMAZING. Once he blessed me with that, I my aim was truer and it seemed like every shot I made hit something vital. I tore through the giants, and when Hriki\u2019s red hot dragon of pure fire burned its way into the room, I unloaded on it with my starlight flare shots and plugged it right through both eyes. It dropped like a sack of potatoes. And then Edward fell on it with his hammer, or rather THROUGH it since its body was incorporeal and it was burning away to nothing at that point anyway.<br /> <br /> Once the dragon died, Hriki appeared and Magnus shouted that he just wanted to talk. She called off her minions and we had a nice chat. Zane was right, she WAS pretty hot, even though she looked like a twelve-foot tall KISS groupie. She was eying Magnus with a smoldering look of desire, though, so I don\u2019t think Zane has much of a chance with her. I need to paint one of these Norse women to see if I can capture that look. It\u2019s very evocative, and I\u2019m sure it would create a compelling portrait.<br /> <br /> Magnus managed to work out a deal. Hriki is going to try and arrange a peaceful, honorable meeting with Sigrid at Hestia and Idunn\u2019s house. Hriki insisted that if she can\u2019t make that deal, then we will meet up to finish our fight with her later, because she didn\u2019t admit defeat, and she certainly wasn\u2019t surrendering. So, right now we\u2019re off to check on Hert and Hestia again, and then we\u2019re going to relax until we hear from Hriki.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> (cont.)<br /> Well, we went over to Hel\u2019s daughter\u2019s place seeing as we thought Idun was there. Only it turns out, Ji-Woo was wrong! I didn\u2019t think that could happen, leastwise not about god things. I were a little worried Ji-Woo\u2019d be sad about it, specially since Pipa had to go back home too. But it turns out her prophecy said she\u2019d be wrong, so that\u2019s alright and all.<br /> <br /> We was thinking at first we might have to fight Hert - that\u2019s Hel\u2019s daughter - so I held tight to Ned\u2019s shoulder so\u2019s he didn\u2019t go running off again or something. But she were nice, even if she were all... clingy and shit. See, she fancies Mag\u2019s brother Kel, even though he don\u2019t fancy her back. Summat had told her that he were in trouble in Berlin, even though he hadn\u2019t been about since Mags got all demigodded. Mags called him to check, and he were fine, yeah? But Hert had got all worried and brought all her zombies to come find him.<br /> <br /> Her zombies are proper ace! She even had a butler kinda zombie. He were moving all slow though, to go get her, so Mags picked him up and carried him with. It were right funny looking. She was putting metal plates in one when we got there, to make him well tough. She were a bit worried, see, on account of her other zombies getting stoled. Plus her ghost got stoled too. His name is Preacher Bob.<br /> <br /> Turns out we could get him right back though, seeing as Rajani can make ghosts show up! She can\u2019t make zombies do that, so they were still stoled, but Ji-Woo did a bang up job on a poster like for a lost dog, but for lost zombies instead. Preacher Bob were right glad to be called up, on account of him getting trapped in a stonking icicle thing by one of the giants. She\u2019s called Hriki - she is well fit and taller than two of me. She were working for another giant lady called Sigrid - she\u2019s got massive tits - and Sigrid\u2019s working for summat else who wanted Hert\u2019s zombies.<br /> <br /> Even though we didn\u2019t get the zombies back right off, Preacher Bob knew where he\u2019d been, so he took us there after we\u2019d got him some medicine. First, I marked Hert so\u2019s I\u2019d know if she were in trouble, and checked with Hestia to make sure Idun weren\u2019t in more trouble. She weren\u2019t, and Hestia decided to stay with Hert and give her summat to talk with. I guess, on account of Norse people being right strange, it\u2019s really hard for Idun to not get kidnapped or to escape without getting rescued, but it\u2019s really hard for anybody to kill her either. I\u2019m really glad I\u2019m not Idun, cause that shit is not on - it sounds proper boring, being captured and all that bollocks all the time.<br /> <br /> Any road, Bob\u2019s \u2018medicine\u2019. See, he has to have a little bit of blood from summat who\u2019s never fucked or killed anybody or lied to try and hurt somebody. We thought a lot about how to get it - Hert usually uses her superpowers to make nuns and things give him blood. Kids are the other likely go, but I weren\u2019t too ok with hurting a kid, even some posh swot. But then we had a bloody brill idea - we\u2019d give the kid a tattoo! Rajani could do it and mesmerize him during it, so Bob could get his medicine from the blood that comes up when you get a tattoo.<br /> <br /> It worked perfect! Mags gave a concert at some college nearby. The German word sounded like gymnasium, which were a bit odd, but that's where a lot of the swots what were old enough that Rajani were ok with giving them a tattoo were at. Andy picked a kid that looked like he\u2019d work, I got us into a empty shop and then Ned cleaned up, while Ji-Woo painted a sign and turned Mr. Duck into tattoo stuff. That kid got a well ace tattoo too. And when Ji-Woo turned Mr. Duck back, she gave him one made of stitches that matched.<br /> <br /> So then Preacher Bob took us to where the giant lady were. It were some place about rocks, like a museum for them or summat, but it used to be a bank, so it had big vaults and things for giants and even dragons, though the big white one were still cramped and all. While we was planning, I held Ned\u2019s scruff again, least until I went invisible to look around. Then I handed him off to Ji-Woo, even though she handed him right off to Mags, seeing as Ned were a bit stronger than her and all. Andy and Ned and Mags all boosted me, even though I was just going to sneak in and have a butcher\u2019s - Andy\u2019s boost does make me even sneakier, and it\u2019s always nice to be well tough any road. None of the 8 giant wankers saw me, and they weren\u2019t even as tall as two of me either, like Hriki is. There was also 2 wolves, and 2 dragons, the big one like the one we fought before, and a smaller one that was made of fire-y, lava-y light stuff. Ned went right through it when he landed on it later!<br /> <br /> Hriki was arguing with Sigrid on the computer when I found her. Sigrid is a real bitch. We\u2019re not supposed to kill her though, Sigrid, on account of maybe that\u2019s what Ulfa wants us to do, so that all the giants will hate us and our god parents. But she were going off on Hriki about the ghost disappearing and saying Hriki needed to run away now, and talking some bollocks about an experiment. I think it has something to do with making people prettier, cause Sigrid said Hriki needed it most of all, and Ji-Woo said her prophecy said all the people Hriki were working with were prettier than her. But that\u2019s a load of cobblers. Hriki is well fit and well hard. She\u2019s got these spiky wrist band things and big fuck-off boots and all kinds of ink. We didn\u2019t actually get to fight her this time, but I bet she can kick all kinds of ass.<br /> <br /> Any road, I went back out right quick after I heard them, seeing as they were talking about leaving soon. We decided to talk and see if maybe Hriki would be on our side, on account of us being much better than that bint Sigrid, but we figured we\u2019d be fighting anyway, so we got all boosted. It were good too, cause the two wolves and two giants right inside didn\u2019t want to talk any.<br /> <br /> It turns out one of the wolves were a fancy kind of wolf what\u2019s called a fenrir. Mags handled him, specially after Andy boosted him and I tugged on his tail. The fenrir\u2019s tail, not Mags\u2019. Rajani got the other wolf, taking his head off schnik! all in one go. Ji-Woo and Ned got one of the giants, and Rajani started in on the other when the fire-y dragon plus four more giants showed up. The dragon breathed fire right off, which didn\u2019t hurt me none. I got proper worried though, on account of Ji-Woo screaming something serious, even though fire can\u2019t hurt her none anymore. Even Andy were alright mostly, with my boost and all, though his clothes were all burned, showing his Batman pants. Mags was bloody brill too - when the dragon spit a fireball at him, he split it right in two pieces with his ice axe.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo did for the dragon right after, tearing it to pieces with her starlight bullets after I knocked it off balance a bit. Then Mags called for Hriki to stop fighting. I were just getting into it proper, but I guess it were good we stopped before I had to maybe hurt her. She said she\u2019d try and get Sigrid to meet us at Idun\u2019s house to talk, with no tricks. If Sigrid said no, she even said she\u2019d work it out so we\u2019d pick up the fight where we left off! It seems proper strange, but I think it\u2019s a Norse thing again.<br /> <br /> I were a bit put out, on account of Hriki didn\u2019t even notice me until I said I\u2019d been thinking about unplugging her computer when Sigrid were being such a bitch. She really liked Mags though. Probably cause he\u2019s tall like her. I asked Ji-Woo if she thought Hriki would like me more if I was tall. She said maybe, but that she liked me better like I am. So I\u2019ll just have to come up with some other way to get Hriki\u2019s attention.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXV</i><br /> <br /> I\u2019m going to need to end there, but comments and questions are welcome and I will answer as best I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T02:21:53-07:00","id":172560,"title":"","content":"Ok time to check on our new Demigods as they continue rocking across the Berlin area<br /> <i><br /> Session XXVI</i><br /> <u><br /> Rock it for Me Part IV</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions<br /> <br /> Berlin</b><br /> <br /> Well, the afternoon was relaxing, which was nice, since Zane woke me up super early this morning. We went back to my apartment to wait until Hriki contacted us. Rajani kept to herself, and Magnus went out to get a lot of liquor, which I suppose he wanted to use to get into Hriki\u2019s good graces, and maybe her pants. Andy and Edward rummaged around in my kitchen and made a mess of my cleaning supplies.<br /> <br /> Zane and I went up to the rooftop terrace to hang out. I took a sketchbook with me and doodled a bit while we talked. I asked Zane if it was different being a boy. He didn\u2019t seem to think so until I pointed out that he had been acting a little differently than he did when he was girl. He\u2019s more interested in girls for the right reasons, for one thing, not just because he thinks it\u2019s his duty as a boyfriend to look out for a girl. In fact, he\u2019s a bit of a rakish scoundrel, and I approve. I guess I have a weakness for guys like that, and Zane is definitely cute. I love his bright eyes and the sprinkle of freckles over his nose and cheeks and the way his hair is always tousled in flagrant disregard for his boyish good looks.<br /> <br /> Anyway, not long after Magnus returned, Hriki called him. It turns out Sigrid wanted to meet with us to do honorable battle. That wasn\u2019t exactly the plan as I understood it; I thought we were supposed to meet and talk things out or something, but I was only paying so much attention to all of this honorable meeting stuff, so I might\u2019ve missed something. Unfortunately, the trollwife Ulfa is calling the shots, and she forbade Sigrid from confronting us, so that plan\u2019s a bust. Still, Hriki wanted to keep her end of the bargain, so she demanded that we meet her to finish our fight. Of course, Magnus told us all of this and then said he\u2019d be back later after he had met with Hriki. I was happy to let him go settle things on his own, because I was three glasses into my absinthe by then and ready to start painting or zoning out to music or something, but Zane insisted we go with him to make sure nothing bad happened.<br /> <br /> So we all followed Magnus out to the Glienicke Bridge in the middle of Berlin, where Hriki was waiting for us, standing firm in the middle of the road and causing quite a traffic problem. On the way, Edward said he wanted pompoms so that he could cheer for Magnus like a sassy American cheerleader, so I tried to use Taiyi to turn a pair of pigeons into pompoms, but it didn\u2019t work, so I had to settle for transforming a couple loaves of bread I bought from a bakery near the bridge instead. Then I summoned my ink wings and flew up onto the bridge girders to watch the show. Rajani stood coolly below and Andy loitered around like a drug dealer, but Zane jumped up to sit next to me. He was still eying Hriki with a look that said he wanted her bad, but I told him that I didn\u2019t think she was interested in him. She only seemed to have eyes for Magnus, and I predicted that if Magnus beat her in a fight, she would only want him more. After I said that, I could tell Zane kinda wished HE was the one down there facing off against the giantess, if only to prove himself to her.<br /> <br /> But much to my delight, Magnus didn\u2019t want to fight! Instead, he talked to Hriki. First, he offered her some of the booze he\u2019d bought earlier and told her that the debt of honor was settled between them. She\u2019d showed up alone to finish that fight, and that was enough as far he was concerned. Then he got her talking about Sigrid and Idunn. Sigrid\u2019s being manipulated by Ulfa and doesn\u2019t even realize it! To make matters worse, Ulfa has Idunn, which fits perfectly with my prophecy. Now we just have to find Ulfa so we can rescue Idunn. Hriki also asked Magnus to promise to slay Ulfa, particularly if we ended up having to kill both Sigrid and Hriki before this is all over. She must really hate the trollwife. Then again, hate and vengeance seem to come really easily to the Norse.<br /> <br /> Hriki left after that, but not before Magnus grabbed and kissed her. It was one of those movie moments where the cameras spin around and the music swells, but it wasn\u2019t the sweet orchestral music of a romantic comedy. Maybe it was the remnants of the absinthe in me, but I distinctly heard squealing, electric guitar chords crescendoing to the chorus of a soulful metal ballad as the two stood there locked in a warrior\u2019s kiss. When Hriki pulled sharply away, she looked furious, but the fire in her eyes smoldered with something other than anger.<br /> <br /> Then I noticed a sly man in a black leather jacket and cap slink away from the fight. He had shockingly red hair, and he was trying to be VERY sneaky. I almost lost him as he slipped away through the clogged traffic to the nearest subway terminal. Zane saw him too, and we took off after him. The others never saw him but they figured that if Zane and I were chasing someone, it must be important, so they rushed after us. As we descended into the subway and then followed the man into the subway tunnels, I noticed that the lights seemed a little brighter around us and the crowds parted to make way. Even though we were underground, I felt like there was plenty of space, so I didn\u2019t start to feel claustrophobic even when we were forced to follow him into tight maintenance hallways. Intellectually, I knew I was getting in over my head, but my curiosity got the best of me, as it always does, so like Alice I kept following the white rabbit until he disappeared down the rabbit hole. Or, through a wall in this case.<br /> <br /> The problem was that there were a couple of trolls guarding the wall, or maybe just the thick steel door bolted into it. They were as surprised to see us as we were to see them. More so, really, since we were expecting an ambush and they were just minding their own business until we happened along. I shot one and Rajani sliced up the other one, injuring him badly enough that he didn\u2019t feel much like fighting when Magnus grabbed him and asked where the hell Ulfa was. The troll didn\u2019t know, but suggested that his friends inside might, so Magnus kicked in the big metal door and we made our way inside. And by that point, the effect the red-haired man had used to lure us in was gone and my claustrophobia came crashing down on me. My fingers strayed to the Courage tattoo Rajani gave me, and then I reached out and grabbed Zane\u2019s hand for support before following Magnus and Edward into the enemy hideout.<br /> <br /> As usual, things became a little chaotic at that point. We found ourself in a cavernous pump room. The noise of our entry warned the trolls inside that we were coming, so we ended up in a one-sided stand off with a bunch of wizened old trolls and a few horribly mutated shrikes. The trolls said that the hideout was a place of learning\u2014a laboratory\u2014and they knew they were no match for us, but before Magnus could intimidate them into telling us where Ulfa was, several massive fire giants and a couple of flaming dragons came crashing through one of the concrete walls in a wave of red hot flame. As the fire engulfed me, I screamed in terror until I remembered that I\u2019m immune to flames thanks to my mastery of elemental fire, all thanks to the sunglasses my father gave me a few weeks ago. Fu Xi\u2019s gift could not have come at a better time!<br /> <br /> Rajani and Andy dove out of the pump room to avoid the flames that kept swirling through it. Zane bolstered me, and it\u2019s a good thing he did, because when the fire giants attacked, they were empowered with the raging force of a fiery furnace and the speed of an explosion. I couldn\u2019t quite avoid getting hit, and a forge-hot blow from one giant\u2019s hammer sent me flying across the room. Zane got hit too, but he just disappeared into his shadow and then appeared from mine, catching me as I slammed into the wall. He may be a rapscallion, but he\u2019s a chivalrous rapscallion! And if he hadn\u2019t bolstered me against harm in the first place, I might have died! As it was, I was still injured a bit, but not badly.<br /> <br /> It was a really tough fight, but thanks to Andy\u2019s magic and Zane\u2019s distractions, Magnus, Edward and I were able to defeat the fire giants and their pet dragons. I didn\u2019t have nearly enough room to move around in the pump room, though, and I was fighting against my claustrophobia the whole time. Magnus didn\u2019t care about any of that, and he tore big chunks out of the walls and machinery as he swung his axe around. Edward struggled to hurt the giants, but he was able to keep the dragons occupied long enough for us to finish the giants and help out. Edward and Magnus killed one dragon, and Zane caved in the other dragon\u2019s skull after I shot it.<br /> <br /> Fire was still raging through the room, and by the time the fight was over, it had burned the trolls and shrikes to cinders. I whipped out one of my Yi Jing coins and tried to dispel the fire effect with Taiyi so that Andy and Rajani could enter the room again. I didn\u2019t know if it would work, but with a bit of concentration, I was able to cancel the flames. The room was still unpleasantly hot, but at least it was bearable again. The heat didn\u2019t do a thing for my claustrophobia, though, so I grabbed Zane\u2019s hand again. It helped calm my nerves a bit. I wanted to leave right then, but Magnus wanted answers, so he pounded deeper into the hideout and the rest of us had no choice but to follow.<br /> <br /> We found a sort of research center and lab. The search for clues was . . . destructive. I was distracted anyway, but then Edward went around smashing things up and turning over file cabinets and tables. I was going through a file of papers when he snatched it from me, tore it in two, and tossed the shreds into the air. I think he got \u201cransack\u201d and \u201csearch\u201d confused in his drug-addled brain. Oh well, that\u2019s Edward for you.<br /> <br /> Magnus soon found something good in some of the lab\u2019s records, though. Ulfa has a few lairs. We already ruined one a few months ago when we foiled her plans the first time. The other one is a fortress somewhere else in the swamp, which is more-or-less what my prophecy predicted. There was also the National Geological Association building, but that\u2019s been cleared out by now. So Ulfa must be in the swamp fortress. Unfortunately, the standing orders we found say that if we get too close to her swamp fortress, she going to dispatch fire giants to cause a distraction, probably sending them to kill Hert.<br /> <br /> We also found out more about the mutated shrikes. They were seriously messed up and gross-looking. Apparently, the trolls were injecting them with troll blood in an attempt to mutate them into something more powerful. I wonder if it also made them more vulnerable to sunlight? We kept the experiment records, so I should look them over later to see if they have any data on that. It might be useless information now, though. For all we know, the shrikes in the lab were the only ones they had mutated. At the time, though, I just wanted to get out of the tight, subterranean tunnels. At the very least, I wanted to gt back out onto the subway platform, because that\u2019s spacious and familiar enough that it doesn\u2019t bother me. Since we had learned all we could in the lab, Magnus agreed that we should get out of there, and so now we are thankfully back under the fresh air of an open sky!<br /> <br /> One thing\u2019s for sure, though. The redhead who led us to the enemy hideout had to be Loki, which means he probably IS the trickster from my prophecy, which is what I suspected all along. I still can\u2019t figure out what his game is, but he doesn\u2019t seem to be antagonizing us, so that\u2019s good, right?<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> Does it make a person bad if they kinda liked it when a girl gets all spooked? Not mean, like being proper happy over it or nothing, not like the German schadenfreude thing. But just kinda feeling nice, a warm fuzzy kinda nice? Like when Ji-Woo grabbed my hand cause we was in another of them nazi lady bunker things. It were all close and tight and underground, yeah? So Ji-Woo got all crowded. And she went for my hand every time she weren\u2019t doing summat else, like shooting giants and stopping fire magic shit. It made me feel proper growed up, and just like Jester said, I think I\u2019ve an idea why summat would want a girlfriend, yeah?<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo asked me about that earlier. Well, about how it were different being a boy. It\u2019s not really, it\u2019s just me with danglies and no tits, but I do feel a little more growed up. She said I was more rakish, which is kinda the same thing, least the way she said it. Hearing her and Pipa from the other room, then Hriki being all fit and well hard and then my fit, well hard mate feeling all safe on account of touching me, it\u2019s proper nice. Ji-Woo has been acting a bit different now I\u2019m a boy. I wonder if she\u2019d be up for a shag with Pipa gone and all.<br /> <br /> Any road, Hriki still likes Mags more than me, though. He\u2019d gone off for a booze run, while me and Ji-Woo were talking and Andy and Ned were snorting and drinking Ji-Woo\u2019s cleaning shit. When he\u2019d got back, he said he had to go fight a giant and was all set to go by hisself, but everyone started in with questions. Sigurd wanted to talk with us, Hriki said, but whoever was the big gang boss said no. Probably Ulfa, seeing as she\u2019s such a berk. But she maybe wants us to kill Sigurd, to make the giants go off on us, so maybe it\u2019s one of the other wankers in Ji-Woo\u2019s prophecy. Hriki did promise to fight if Sigurd wouldn\u2019t talk and all, but she didn\u2019t have any giants no more, so Mags were gonna fight her by hisself.<br /> <br /> It were a Norse thing and all, so I didn\u2019t tell him he was being a bit of a divvy or nothing. But I did say we ought go with, in case it were a trap. Hriki was proper Norse honorable and everything, so she probably weren\u2019t meaning to trick him or nothing, but if summat was making it so Sigurd couldn\u2019t talk and Hriki couldn\u2019t have no giants, they might be wankers enough to pull tricks like that.<br /> <br /> So we all went. Andy were leaning up against a post, trying to look like a dealer or summat. Ned were pretending to be a cheerleader, with pompoms Ji-Woo made out of some bread sticks. She tried to make them out of pigeons, but they just got some paint on them and didn\u2019t change. Me and her sat way up high on the slanty beams on the bridge where they was supposed to fight. There weren\u2019t no fighting though. Mags shared his bevvies with Hriki and told her he didn\u2019t really want bloodshed or nothing, that since she showed up, the honor stuff were good and all. She said some stuff about Idun, that the big gang boss had her and that Sigurd didn\u2019t know she were being played so bad. She asked a right strange question too. If Mags killed her and Sigurd, would he kill the troll wife? Cause Mags said yes, she said she\u2019d leave off fighting. I dunno whether that meant she wanted or didn\u2019t want Mags to do for Ulfa, bit I guess that\u2019s for him and all.<br /> <br /> He kissed her too, before he let her leave. Ji-Woo said Hriki would like him a lot when he won, but I guess she likes him alright even with just the talking. She didn\u2019t fight or nothing anyways. I weren\u2019t bothered or nothing, I\u2019ll just have to fight proper ace next time we mix it up with her. Like I did today when I killed a dragon! Ji-Woo helped, but I did for it, and it were well tough.<br /> <br /> The dragons were at the new nazi lady bunker. See, while Mags kissed Hriki and all, me and Ji-Woo noticed a bloke loitering about, watching and he buggered off as soon as she did, but loads faster than a proper human could. So we followed him, down to the Underground. It weren\u2019t too hard keeping track of him - Ji-Woo even said she weren\u2019t as crowded feeling following him. But then there were trolls! And the red-haired bloke disappeared into a wall.<br /> <br /> There was only two trolls, and Ji-Woo and Rajani did for one but good. I just barely had time to boost Ji-Woo, just in case. Andy and Ned both boosted me - Ned kissed the back of my head and said he liked me even though I weren\u2019t a girl, then beat his chest like a monkey. Andy took a word from his shirt (it were really long and went all the way around his shirt when it were there) and put it above my head like a halo thing or summat. I like Andy\u2019s new boost thing. It makes me more tough and strong, and gives me loads of energy and all.<br /> <br /> The other troll Mags was good and remembered not to kill. So he could ask questions and all, yeah? Ned named him Cecil. Cecil didn\u2019t know anything about where Ulfa was, but said maybe people inside did, so Mags busted the wall down, after Ned walked through it. He noticed some trolls waiting the way Cecil told us to go, Mags did, so he yelled at them that they couldn\u2019t ambush us or nothing. Which is kinda funny, thinking about it, on account of that\u2019s what the giants and dragons did, from the other way. They cheated though, and broke through a wall after lighting the whole room on fire.<br /> <br /> First though, we talked with the trolls and the funny-looking new shrike ladies. The trolls had fucked with them, putting branches and extra shit all over them. But they all died in the fire. It stung me a bit, but I mostly forgot cause Ji-Woo went off screaming again, even though fire can\u2019t hurt her none and all. When it cleared, there was seven fire giant wankers and two fire dragons. The giants had murder eyes and were all boosted up. With Ji-Woo and Mags though, three of them were done for before they got their heads from their ass. That still meant four went for us and it were a good thing I boosted Ji-Woo, cause she got proper tore up and were mostly just alright cause of the boost. I got hit hard enough I had to find a different bit of shadow to be in, so I went fwoosh to Ji-Woo\u2019s shadow and got to catch her before she hit the wall and all. Even Mags got scratched a bit, and Ned left a splatch of red paint behind when he went for the dragons after that.<br /> <br /> After I set Ji-Woo up right again, I went charging back in, seeing as not everything were off balance yet. Fire kept filling up the room, but it didn\u2019t hurt me none except for that first time, a little. Andy would bugger off when the dragons was about to do their fire thing, but the magic-y one he could ignore too, like Ji-Woo. It weren\u2019t too long before we did for the giants, though one of them got Ned but good. Ji-Woo told that giants to pick on someone his own size, like Mags, after that. I healed Ned up after though, so it were all ok.<br /> <br /> The dragons did keep trying to chew on Ned, when they weren\u2019t breathing fire and all, but they couldn\u2019t hurt him none. I went and roughed them up a bit, once everything was off-balance and all. Like I said, I even did for one of them, after Ji-Woo shot it up a bunch. Mags got the other one, making its head go all icy.<br /> <br /> Then we went investigating. First, Ji-Woo sucked all the fire that were going off in the room by magic into her coin with a hole in it. Mags started off by making another hole in the wall that the giants had already busted through once, so Ned decided that\u2019s what investigating meant, so he spent the whole time busting shit up and knocking it over. Andy even joined in, but he hurt his foot kicking a fountain thing. It looked like proper fun any road, but I stuck close to Ji-Woo instead and helped search proper, cause she really wanted to not be underground anymore, but we needed to find stuff. Mags found the good shit right quick though, in the first place he looked! It said kinda where Ulfa\u2019s other hidey-hole was, and had all sorts of plans written out, like that the new shrikes were weird looking on account of something to do with troll blood, and we were supposed to kill Hert and the giants were going to if we didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> But now we know sorta where Ulfa is, so that\u2019s where we\u2019re going. Time to bust up some more trolls! And get Idun back of course.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXVI</i><br /> <br /> The Fire Giant fight was laid out as a difficult fight for the PCs, and they were warned of this when it started. The Fire Giants had used Fury of War at the start, so the PCs job was initially to whittle their numbers down as much as possible so that once per scene defenses could be used to survive the initial onslaught. Overall it went well. There was one minor mix up but it was not a huge deal.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve had a lot going on and circumstances conspire against me having a great deal of info this time, sadly. I\u2019ll try to make a longer post next time, but any comments or questions you have are always welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T13:24:32-07:00","id":186470,"title":"","content":"Okay Scion time. At the last minute, Magnus\u2019s player could not make (he emailed to say he would be late just before game, and emailed again during to say he could not make it) so we had to adjust to no Magnus. I had a side plot for pacing anyway, and worked that in stronger. But the session went well despite no Magnus, so here we go.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXVII</i><br /> <br /> <u>Rock it for Me Part V</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo's Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Berlin</b><br /> <br /> It is exhausting trying to keep us on task. I don\u2019t normally have to worry about it. I mean, I guess Magnus usually picks a direction, often based on my insight, and the rest of us follow along. Except Edward, who wanders off in some other direction before finally arriving at a destination all his own. But since Magnus left to get his van and check on the shrikes after we left the troll lab, I ended up responsible for keeping Zane, Andy and Edward heading in the right direction. Why? I guess because . . . I don\u2019t know . . . I tend to know things? Anyway, it was way more responsibility than I cared for, but I guess Fu Xi would be proud that I\u2019m at least making an effort.<br /> <br /> Based on the intelligence we unearthed at the lab, we decided that Hert might be in danger, so we should move her somewhere safer. Everyone threw out all manner of suggestions about how to go about that and how we might find Ulfa\u2019s swamp fortress, everything from moon-gazing to Edward offering to dress up like Hert to fool the enemy. In the end, Edward got confused about what fortress we were talking about and was ready to go assault a German military base, so we had to reign him in. Meanwhile, Rajani got a call and said something important had come up in India, so she had to leave for home. I have no idea when or if we\u2019ll see her again.<br /> <br /> Without really deciding anything except that we were going to move Hert to the shrike\u2019s bunker to keep her safe, we headed back to her house in a taxi Edward commandeered. Hestia made us all lemonade and cupcakes while I went down to fetch Hert. Hestia always makes me feel like I\u2019m in 1950\u2019s America, not Europe. I\u2019ve always kinda wanted to go to a sock hop and drink a root beer float while listening to Chuck Berry on a vintage jukebox and gazing into my boyfriend\u2019s dreamy eyes, but I imagine I would grow bored with it pretty quickly, and besides, I don\u2019t have a boyfriend right now, only a girlfriend. And I can\u2019t really imagine Pipa dancing to \u201cJohnny B. Goode.\u201d Maybe \u201cLittle Darlin\u2019,\u201d but that was by The Diamonds. Why do I even know that? And who am I kidding? Pipa doesn\u2019t even LIKE root beer floats! Or so I assume, given her lack of a sweet tooth.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I explained to Hert that she was in danger and that we were going to move her somewhere safer. She wanted to take all of her zombies, but I didn\u2019t like the look of her American cheerleader zombies, which had bladed pompoms for hands and rag-doll hair made of entrails. I know Hert\u2019s just expressing herself artistically, but I felt it was a little much, especially if we were going to be moving across town. She did insist on taking her butler zombie though. I think he hates me because I\u2019m impatient with him. Hert should make a faster butler.<br /> <br /> About then, Magnus called and told us that Hriki had contacted him with a warning, a little bit of rebellion on Sigrid\u2019s part. She warned us that Ulfa had sent a small task force to take out Magnus\u2019 shrikes. The task force included some sort of undying beast. To make matters worse, a bomb was on its way to the nymphs\u2019 cave! Fuck that. The only good news was that Sigrid refused to send any frost giants to help\u2014more thumbing her nose at Ulfa.<br /> <br /> Magnus assured us that he was moving the shrikes to safety, so without a moment\u2019s hesitation, the rest of us hurried to the cave. Edward, Andy, Hestia, Hert and the butler sped to the caves in Edward\u2019s stolen cab, while I darted through the open freedom of the skies with Zane bounding along below. While I soared with the winds, I rummaged around in my bag until I found my French cartomancy deck. I was going to do a quick divination to find out more about the bomb and the enemies attacking the shrike bunker, but the winds caught a few of the cards and tore them from my grasp. Fortunately, even that was an omen, and each card stolen by the winds was a symbol that made me realize a few things. In the end, I just let go and the whole deck burst into the air. It was beautiful, all the cards fluttering through the sky as the winds caught and played with them like dandelion seeds blown from the stem.<br /> <br /> The burst of fluttering cards was not just beautiful, but insightful. The first card torn from my hand showed me that the bomb was still some distance from the cave. We would have no trouble intercepting it before it got close. It was carried by some sort of human-sized homunculus made of sticks and branches, and the cards even showed me exactly where we could find it. The wayward flip of a Jack of Clubs told me that the undying beast was a sea creature spawned from the offal of the Drowned Road, and a spiraling Ace of Spades revealed that we did not have the means to kill the it since the beast could only be slain by a special weapon. Still, the beast was virtually unintelligent and someone like Edward probably wouldn\u2019t have any trouble redirecting it with a little chaos.<br /> <br /> Of course, I also got flashes of insight on other matters, too. Aoide slept with the cloud pillow I gave her last night, And there is definitely something romantic going on between Iris and Caoimhe. I hope Iris knows what she\u2019s doing. Pipa is bored performing her duties for Daji, and just knowing that made me miss her. I tried to glean the location of Ulfa\u2019s fortress from the cascade of raining cards, but it\u2019s hidden behind her illusions, and all I saw was Hert\u2019s house. It does appear that Ulfa\u2019s favorite TV show is Desperate Housewives, though. Wow. I don\u2019t really watch TV, so I haven\u2019t seen that show, but I\u2019ve heard of it. It\u2019s pretty sordid, right? Can you imagine a show called Desperate Trollwives? Or a Desperate Housewives: Overworld? Starring Hera, Persephone, Sif, and, what the hell, my mom? That would be awful. But maybe also hilarious. And scary. Or maybe I have the wrong idea of what the show is about.<br /> <br /> So, I called Zane and Andy and told them where the bomb was, and we went there directly. Zane and I arrived on the street first and found the stick man wrapped in a burqa, riding a bike. Edward\u2019s cab swerved onto the scene moments later, blocking traffic and pissing off a lot of innocent drivers. Without wasting a moment, Zane jumped onto the stick man, grabbed it and heaved it high into the air, where I placed one clean shot right through the thing\u2019s chest. The bomb exploded safely, showering bits of smoldering debris harmlessly onto the city below. One problem down.<br /> <br /> We all headed back to the cave to check on the sisters and let them know they were safe. Jean was there, ready to defend them. Handsome, rakish AND chivalrous. He really is the whole package, isn\u2019t\u2019 he? As far as I can tell, though, Sari has barely left him alone since he showed up. Kalypso is still a bit smitten too, though she won\u2019t admit it. I flirted with Jean a little bit. He really is my type, and oddly, the other girls don\u2019t seem to be that jealous of him. But there is the thing about siring the leader of a new pantheon . . . no thank you. There\u2019s also my girlfriend, of course.<br /> <br /> Mainly, though, I just wanted to see Aoide. I still totally have a crush on her, and knowing she liked the pillow I gave her enough to sleep with it last night meant something. But she\u2019s so hard to read, and usually seems either distant or confused when I flirt with her, so I guess it\u2019s never going to go anywhere. Still, it felt nice to give her and the pillow a hug. I asked for a kiss for good luck before we left to intercept the trolls at the shrike\u2019s bunker, and she looked puzzled, but gave me a peck on the cheek anyway. That\u2019s all I really wanted, though in retrospect, I feel kind of foolish about that, like a blushing schoolgirl. Oh well, I guess a crush will do that to you. Which is weird, because I\u2019m totally in love with Pipa.<br /> <br /> Magnus arrived before too long, and then we all drove to the shrike bunker in his van. Once there, it didn\u2019t take us long to find the trolls. They were, in fact, accompanied by a hulking beast that looked like a pile of kelp and sea floor detritus that had been vomited out of a sea serpent\u2019s maw, and I suspect that\u2019s more or less how the thing came to be. Fortunately, it was so stupid that all it did was stand around drooling while we made short work of its troll escort. We have Andy to thank for that; he manipulated the air so that the enemy couldn\u2019t hear each other, so the trolls couldn\u2019t command their immortal beast!<br /> <br /> The beast is still standing around, but Edward is distracting it. The next stop is Ulfa\u2019s lair, if we can find it. Edward hopes that he can confuse the undying beast so that it attacks the lair with us, but since we don\u2019t even know where the fortress is, I\u2019m not sure whether that will work or not. It WOULD be fun, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> So let\u2019s see. Things we didn\u2019t do while Mags was off getting his van again: We didn\u2019t dress Ned up in a posh frock so\u2019s Ulfa would think he were Hert. Hert\u2019s house never got blowed up. Ned didn\u2019t go after some army base in lederhosen, screaming about Hert being dead. He really wanted to though. We didn\u2019t even hide Hert with the shrikes, even though we were going to, seeing as it was the best option out of all the bollocks Andy and Ned came up with. She\u2019s with the ladies in the mansion cave now.<br /> <br /> See, we had got the plans and all, at the fucked up shrikes place, saying Ulfa were going to try and kill Hert if it turned out we didn\u2019t, and if we got too close to her base in the swamp. So we buggered off over there, quick as could be, and Hestia had made cupcakes! And lemonade! It were proper ace. Ji-Woo had rough time keeping us all on track with all that - she was zonked before we even left Hert\u2019s - but she did get Hert to come up, carrying her stonking huge zombie butler bloke. Hert\u2019s well strong. Ji-Woo did say the cheerleader zombies with knife-pompoms sticking from her hands had to stay at the house though. I were a bit sad at that, on account of them looking proper fierce, even if their hair were guts.<br /> <br /> Any road, we\u2019d called a cab and all when Mags rang up and said Ulfa had sent trolls and some wanker what couldn\u2019t die to go for the shrikes! Worse, she\u2019d sent a bomb for the ladies at the cave! It were supposed to be tricky, like we\u2019d have to choose or summat, but Hriki\u2019d rung up Mags to let him know ahead of time, seeing as Ulfa had told Sigurd not to tell us but hadn\u2019t told her not to tell Hriki to tell us. Sigurd might be a bitch, but that were right tricksy. In a good way, though, on account of it helping us and all, yeah?<br /> <br /> So Mags just told the shrikes to fuck off, so the trolls and the weird sea monster blobby tendrily thing just fannied around a bit til we got there later. First though, there was the bomb and all. Ji-Woo started flying right off, going proper fast so\u2019s I could hardly keep up with her, even roof hopping. Andy started flying too, not so fast though. Ned took that cab we\u2019d called for. Least, that\u2019s what he showed up in, missing a door and with a hole in the roof for the zombie butler\u2019s head.<br /> <br /> It weren\u2019t too hard, dealing with the bomb, seeing as we had warning and everything. Ji-Woo figured right where it were by tossing a deck of cards about. I dived on it, pow, and knocked it clean off its bike, kinda. It wouldn\u2019t let go of the bloody thing, even when I tossed it up into the air so Ji-Woo could shoot it and make it explode where it wouldn\u2019t hurt nothing.<br /> <br /> We decided to have Hert stay with the ladies then, since it didn\u2019t make them more in trouble, seeing as Ulfa already sent a bomb after them, and Hert weren\u2019t even there. Ned were going to steal another car, to get to the caves - he tore the door of a new one off and everything! - but Ji-Woo said no, so he gave the door back. Jean was there, just inside the caves, standing guard, without a shirt on. Made me think he might not have been there for guarding right at first. Specially not with the way Sari were looking at him. He really is well fit though. Ji-Woo really wants to shag him, except for the god-kid thing. Maybe I should ask him for tips in sexing birds up. After we get Idun back though. We\u2019ve got a mission on, yeah? It\u2019s important not to get distracted, much. Not by sex stuff, or by Hestia making more cupcakes.<br /> <br /> Any road, other than a maybe-bomb, the ladies were mostly alright, so we didn\u2019t stay long. Aoide and Saorse was worried that Iris weren\u2019t there, on account of her being with Caoimhe and the soul eating thing, so Ji-Woo gave Aoide a kiss on the cheek before we fucked off so Jean and Sari could get back to snogging.<br /> <br /> I had a nice ride on the top of the busted up cab while Andy were in Ned\u2019s lap even though there weren\u2019t nobody else inside anymore. It\u2019s almost like flying, a little bit. Ji-Woo rode with Mags, cause the cab were too small and she didn\u2019t wanna get too zonked before we even got there, so she didn\u2019t go flying, even if her wings proper ace. We got all boosted, once we was there, since we weren\u2019t getting jumped or following some red-headed bloke or nothing. I pulled a pair of sunglasses I\u2019d stoled off some bird a while back from behind Ned\u2019s ear to give him a boost. They didn\u2019t properly fit him, but maybe now he won\u2019t worry so much about the ones he ate before. Or maybe he\u2019ll eat them. He chest bumped me to get me all boosted, and I gave Ji-Woo a high-five.<br /> <br /> There was only 5 trolls and the bugger what couldn\u2019t die, seeing as Sigurd said Ulfa couldn\u2019t have any giants. The bugger was proper daft and unless the trolls told it what to do, it might just fuck off anytime. Which it did, since Andy did a right loud guitar thing that made it so the trolls couldn\u2019t make no noise, and the lights all sparked. Ji-Woo used the sparks to make her bullets all star-glowy and killed 3 of the trolls right off, bam bam bam!<br /> <br /> Ned and I worked on one, after I\u2019d knocked them all off balance. I got a good knee in there, then Ned, from down on the ground, used his feet to smash him in the goolies with his hammer. Then he died. The troll, yeah? The last troll, after Andy sent frowny faces to it from his nipples, tried to go after Ji-Woo, but she shot his axe so that it dropped on his head and then <u><u>he</u></u> died, and that were that. We was going to try to lead the tendrily sea monster to Ulfa\u2019s place, so we didn't kill it right off or nothing.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXVII</i><br /> <br /> In addition to Magnus being missing that session, Rajani was not there either. However, in her case, her player needed to drop the game. It was unfortunate, but I don\u2019t expect Rajani will be back. The plan right now is we are going to go with four. We will hopefully have Leo and/or Suleiman guest star again. I know both players would like to, it is mostly a matter of time to do it. I am sure at least one and maybe both will (possibly separately) so we can look forward to that. I think we all hope Phaedra will be back, but with her new baby it may be awhile\u2026over a year, at least. We will see how things go.<br /> <br /> This session I had a side plot which I had set aside for pacing and implemented it to buy time for Magnus\u2019s player to arrive. Since he could not, we went ahead and made a session of it, and it went pretty well\u2026the Hert thing was all the PCs plans.<br /> <br /> We will have more next time. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-ea