e":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T02:45:42-07:00","id":191268,"title":"","content":"A worthy pursuit! I just had no below 55 alts atm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T14:21:51-07:00","id":202367,"title":"","content":"I say this a lot, but apologies for the delay. This one was on me, not the players. Been very unproductive lately. But game went well, and we finished <u>Rock it for Me</u>. Let\u2019s have a peek at how that story ended.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <u>Rock it for Me Part VI</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Berlin</b><br /> <br /> So, since I\u2019m journaling anyway, I\u2019ve decided to write all my journals with my official minister\u2019s brush, so all my journals will go straight to my office in Tian, where my secretary, Lu Yisheng, will do whatever he does with them. This way, I\u2019m actually filing reports without any extra work on my part!<br /> <br /> Edward has a way with barely intelligent monsters. He managed to get the undying beast to lead us to Ulfa\u2019s swamp fortress. I\u2019m not really sure how he did it, but somehow he managed to communicate with the beast. He asked for some Reese\u2019s Pieces to help get it headed in the right direction, which I guess is an E.T. thing. We didn\u2019t have any Reese\u2019s Pieces, but Edward had some pot, and I turned it into candy with the endlessly versatile magic of Taiyi. I guess if I did that in reverse I could get drugs on the cheap, but I can\u2019t remember the last time I\u2019ve paid for my own drugs. Except for absinthe, of course, but that doesn\u2019t count. Anyway, the beast almost went down a toilet, but Magnus stopped it, so then it headed into the streets of Berlin, and once it got its bearings, it starting bounding along in great leaps, leaving a trail of bent lampposts and broken fire hydrants. Edward grabbed onto its slime-drowned hide and rode it like a camel, and eventually Zane joined him. I don\u2019t really like being covered with slime, though, so I just flew after them, kind of meandering a bit. I caught sight of the East Side Gallery\u2014you know, the collection of political murals painted on the remnants of the Berlin Wall\u2014and started flying off to have a look at it. Not that I haven\u2019t been there many times in the past. I even took Iris there on a not-date shortly after I met her. But, you know, good art is always compelling, and it certainly compelled me until Zane whistled to remind me what we were doing.<br /> <br /> By then, the police were following at a safe distance, and a paramilitary helicopter with a police strike team were hovering overhead to keep an eye on things. Magnus was skating along after Ed, Zane and the monster on a self-made sheet of ice, so I swooped down and asked for some alcohol and he tossed up a bottle of whiskey. Then I flew up to the helicopter and signaled that I\u2019d like to come aboard. I don\u2019t think the SWAT team inside quite knew what to think when a hot girl flew up and offered them a drink, but one of them shrugged and waved me aboard. I spent most of the rest of the trip out of Berlin hanging out with the SWAT team. They weren\u2019t supposed to drink on duty, but given the circumstances, even the sergeant made an exception. And they were surprised that a Korean girl could speak flawless German. The guy who waved me aboard, Hans, was really hot. Gorgeous green eyes (I love green eyes; they remind me of absinthe), handsome jawline with just the right amount of stubble, and a devil-may-care twist to his smile. We exchanged numbers, and apparently he\u2019s quite the ladies man, because his teammates gave him a hard time about the weird places he picks up girls. I bet it\u2019s never happened in flight on a mission before, though. Anyway, it wasn\u2019t until I left the chopper that I remembered I\u2019m dating Pipa. I don\u2019t really know how jealous she is. I mean, she SAYS she expects us to fool around outside of our relationship, but I don\u2019t know how she\u2019ll actually react until it happens. And even if Hans and I go out, it\u2019s not going to be serious. Not like it is with Pipa. Maybe I should strum her a message on my pipa to let her know.<br /> <br /> See? I\u2019m totally becoming more responsible.<br /> <br /> One we arrived over the marsh, I bid my police friends goodbye and dove out of the helicopter. I landed with my friends at a huge, gnarled tree that loomed from the swamp like a corpse rising from its grave. A narrow crack split the trunk, and the beast contorted its way through the crack and into the space beyond. I was really anxious about going into yet another dark, tight passage, but Zane reminded me that Ulfa\u2019s other lair was really big on the inside. Hoping that this would be the same, I let Zane pull me through.<br /> <br /> And she was right! The inside was another realm with stormy skies that stretched as far as I could fly! On an island in the center was a castle of stone and ice. A bitter chill hung in the air, and frost clutched at everything it could reach. I really wasn\u2019t dressed for the weather, but thanks to mom\u2019s Ice Cream Cone Charm, the cold doesn\u2019t really bother me, so I was fine.<br /> <br /> Hriki stood like a sentinel at the castle gates, flanked by a few frost giants and trolls. Magnus stepped forward and told her we were there to respond to the insult of Ulfa\u2019s cowardly bombing attempt and demanded to see Ulfa. Hriki told us that Ulfa was too cowardly, and that she and Sigrid had nothing to do with the bombing. She felt that Ulfa\u2019s people deserved whatever was coming to them, so she withdrew her giants and left the trolls to deal with us on their own. The trolls didn\u2019t fare so well. Edward even got Sigmund (that\u2019s what he named the undying beast) to eat one of the trolls. It was absolutely disgusting.<br /> <br /> Hriki was ready to escort us in to face Sigrid then, but Sigrid\u2019s face appeared in swirls of frost on the glassy ice of the castle walls. She offered a deal. If Magnus could impress Hriki with his sexual prowess, then Sigrid would withdraw her support of Ulfa. Of course, Magnus would still have to face Sigrid himself, which seemed kinda counterproductive to me. But you know, honor and all. It\u2019s so weird. Magnus didn\u2019t exactly need a lot of encouragement to agree to the plan, so he and Hriki disappeared inside the castle while the rest of us waited outside. Andy and Edward entertained Sigmund while Zane and I talked about sex.<br /> <br /> See, Zane didn\u2019t understand why Hriki would willingly agree to something like this. He still has this misunderstanding about what sex means. So I tried to explain to him that sex isn\u2019t just something women give to men in exchange for gifts and protection. A lot of women, myself included, really like sex. And so does Hriki. She\u2019d been craving a good romp with Magnus ever since they first laid eyes on one another. Zane seemed dubious, so I started to wax poetic as I explained exactly what I liked about sex, like how much I enjoy it when my partner and I explore each other\u2019s bodies with kisses and caresses. I got a bit more explicit than that, of course, and I may have given Zane a little too much detail, but he was a captive audience and I could see him taking mental notes. In fact, for the first time, I noticed the way he looks at me sometimes. I think he wants me. To be honest, I kinda want him too. Zane\u2019s super cute as a guy, and there\u2019s something about his cocky, rakish side that turns me on. He\u2019s still Zane, but very different. Girl Zane is kind of childish and innocent. Boy Zane is anything but innocent, and he\u2019s more grown-up, but still mired in a charming sort of masculine immaturity that I find quite endearing. He\u2019s not relationship material, but then again, neither am I.<br /> <br /> Anyway, after an hour or so, Magnus emerged, disheveled but no worse for the wear. He had that cocky, self-satisfied grin that guys have when they\u2019ve scored with a hot girl and want their friends to know it. Andy tossed the rest of the bottle of whiskey. Apparently, Magnus he earned Hriki\u2019s approval because Sigrid invited us all inside to face her then.<br /> <br /> Hriki escorted us into a throne room. Sigrid stood in the center with a confident smirk on her face, and Idunn was bound to one of the thrones with shackles of ice. An honor guard of ten frost giants stood like stone pillars in a semicircle around Sigrid. Magnus clutched his axe and started to prepare himself for the fight as Sigrid challenged him to battle. She said that she had come to face Magnus and determine whose fate would continue and whose would be snuffed out like an ember in snow. That was the only reason she kidnapped Idunn: to force a confrontation with Magnus. Win or lose, she would release her captive now that Idunn had served her purpose, so Magnus could die knowing that his death had at least saved the goddess. But of course, dying was not on Magnus\u2019 agenda for the day. Not that he keeps a day planner or anything.<br /> <br /> The duel between Magnus and Sigrid was legendary. Neither of them gave ground as they hammered one another with blows that would have cleaved any mortal man in two. Magnus spent his fury in the first half of the fight, then became a more calculating warrior. Andy\u2019s magic bolstered his abilities, but still he needed all the skill and power her could muster to defeat Sigrid.<br /> <br /> The frost giants charged the rest of us. Empowered by their own war fury, there were pretty scary. I shot one dead right off. I even tossed our last bottle of liquor into the air and shot through it so that my blazing bullets turned the spray of alcohol into an explosive burst of flame. It was really pretty, so much so that I was momentarily distracted and almost got hit by one of the giants. Then Zane pounced on him and started beating the hell out of him, shouting that he DID NOT get to attack me. It\u2019s so awesome that Zane looks out for me like he does. If we end up sleeping together, will that just reinforce his belief that women give sex for protection?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Edward led Sigmund to the thrones and got the beast to gnaw through Idunn\u2019s bonds until she was free. The beast then continued to eat the thrones, while Edward turned his attention to the frost giants. Andy used his storm powers to briefly trap one of the giants in winds, long enough to keep it from unleashing the power of its war fury on us. I thought that was a great idea, and I sensed that Magnus had a plan that involved sparing Sigrid. In the interest of creating harmony with potential future allies, I decided to try and immobilize the giants instead of killing them. It\u2019s not like they weren\u2019t ready and willing to die in honorable battle, and I don\u2019t think anyone would have cared if we had slaughtered them all. But it seemed like such a waste, so I followed Andy\u2019s example and tore five raging whirlwinds from the frosty air of the castle, wrapping one giant in each. I ordered the spectral fox spirits that swirl through my whirlwinds not to claw and bite, but they may have tickled a little bit. If so, then the giants are either not ticklish, or they are very good at hiding it. Mostly, they just seemed angry. But most Norse I\u2019ve encountered seem vaguely angry most of the time. I\u2019m sure that\u2019s in the Bureaucracy records already, though. Hou Yi would make a good Aesir.<br /> <br /> Eventually the frost giants burst free of our whirlwinds, and by that time Zane and Edward had taken down the one giant that escaped our clutches. More importantly, the duel came to a dramatic end when Magnus found an opening in Hriki\u2019s defense and landed a powerful blow that caused even the giantess to stagger and fall to one knee. Knowing that she was finished, Sigrid looked squarely at Magnus and invited him to give her an honorable death. But Magnus did not kill her. He told her that the debt of honor had been paid. I didn\u2019t really get all the posturing, but Sigrid seemed satisfied, and the giants stood down.<br /> <br /> Sigrid offered Hriki to Magnus as his own personal bodyguard. Magnus told Hriki that she wasn\u2019t indentured to him and could do what she liked, but he did invite her to stay with him for awhile. I imagine he will have to prove his sexual prowess to her a few more times before she heads back to Sigrid. Of course, Idunn also ran up to give Magnus a huge hug, and did I mention the \u201ckiss-me-now\u201d look Sigrid gave Magnus when he honorably spared her life? I didn\u2019t think frost giants could smolder.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s worth noting that Edward and Zane managed to patch up the giant they knocked out, so he\u2019ll be okay. Zane gave him a stern lecture about messing with me. In short, don\u2019t do it, or Zane will kick your ass. Sadly, the giant I shot was beyond help. I feel a little guilty about that, and wish I had thought of the whirlwinds sooner.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s that. Ulfa\u2019s gone, again, but that\u2019s hardly surprising. We foiled her plans again, and that\u2019s what counts. She\u2019ll no doubt be a thorn in our side for some time, but that\u2019s okay. It\u2019s fate.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a couple of weeks since my last entry. All is well in Berlin, though I\u2019m surprised I\u2019m still here. I\u2019m thinking about heading to Moscow or Athens or Rio for awhile.<br /> <br /> Edward painted an amazing mural on the wall of Magnus\u2019 warehouse studio. It\u2019s a heavy metal nude of Hriki in a scene of battlefield bloodshed, and it\u2019s pretty amazing. Glykeria told Iris about it, and she went to see. I think she was impressed. Hermione\u2019s been kinda grumpy lately, what with Rajani gone, and Aoide is . . . well . . . Aoide.<br /> <br /> Zane has been staying with me, and it wasn\u2019t long after our battle with Sigrid that he put the moves on me. He really WAS taking notes on what I like, because he knew exactly how to please me. It was nice. Zane is my best friend, and there was something special about connecting physically like that. We\u2019re not in a relationship or anything, though. Just friends with benefits. And unlike Iris, Zane seems to be on the same page as me about that. Magnus dropped by the day after, and Zane had that self-satisfied smile I mentioned previously, so I couldn\u2019t stop laughing when the big guy said, \u201cAw yeah!\u201d, grabbed Zane and started knuckling his head with good-natured abandon.<br /> <br /> <b>Berlin - Xian (Attraction) transforming into Ge (Revolution)</b><br /> <br /> I was a little worried about how Pipa would react to the news that Zane and I had slept together, so I strummed her a message on my pipa. She wasn\u2019t happy when she called me back. She seems to think that Zane will eventually make a play for me and that the friends with benefits thing is just an easy in. I don\u2019t know about THAT. I don\u2019t think Zane is that calculating, but he and Pipa don\u2019t get along, so I suppose I should respect Pipa\u2019s wishes and maybe not sleep with Zane again. Besides, Pipa was pretty clear that if Zane did make a play for me, it would NOT be pretty. The LAST thing I want is for my girlfriend and my best friend to got to war over me.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m a little tense because the situation is making me feel trapped, but I really love Pipa and I don\u2019t want to lose her, but I also like what I have with Zane. So I turned to the Yi Jing for advice. It suggested that I acknowledge my desires and remain steadfast in my attitudes. Steadfast isn\u2019t exactly a word I would use to describe myself, but I understand what the oracle is telling me. I can\u2019t let doubt and fear force me out of balance. I know I love Pipa, and I\u2019m content to sacrifice some of my freedom for her. But Zane\u2019s important to me, and his feelings matter too. Ultimately, if I remain true to myself and the path I\u2019ve chosen, namely my commitment to Pipa, then everything will fall into place. It\u2019s just difficult for me right now because I have to change my attitude toward some things like personal freedom. And that means I probably shouldn\u2019t sleep with Zane again, but I shouldn\u2019t deny how much closer we\u2019ve become either. If I were to do that, it would throw me out of balance and probably damage my relationship with Pipa too.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I\u2019m going to make it up to Pipa. She\u2019s done with work for the time being, so the two of us are going to hang out in Rio de Janeiro for awhile. There are some great clubs there, or so I\u2019ve heard. Espaco Acustica is supposed to have a great rooftop dance floor and bar, and you know how much I love that! It will be nice to get out of Europe for a change!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> (cont.)<br /> Turns out things worked a bit backwards from that. Instead of us leading the sea monster to Ulfa, it led us to her! See, Ned tried hypnotizing the thing, and it just gnawed on him a bit. He did figure out its name were Sigmond and it did drawings though. Also, that it\u2019d had been hurt when it were a little and couldn\u2019t read on account of not having bootstraps and it were sad cause people were scared of it all the time. That last bit were for the coppers what started following us, so they wouldn\u2019t be so upset. I\u2019m not sure it worked.<br /> <br /> Before all that though, we had to get it outside, yeah? Ned got Ji-Woo to make him a bag of Reese\u2019s Pieces out of his bag of green, since he didn\u2019t have any peas. Me and her were sharing them, but then Ned took them back. He saved some for me for later though. It were all part of a big Ned-type plan what had cycling to the moon, talking dogs and Pizza huts in it. Andy helped too, taking Ned into a room where there was lots of barking and licking noises until Ned said stop. It must have helped, seeing as after that Ned got the tendrily monster to dance and fuck off into the loo.<br /> <br /> Mags didn\u2019t like thinking about it hanging about in the pipes and all, so he drug it up and got it out into the street. Then he talked to it in Norse talk, but it still didn\u2019t know what \u2018Ulfa\u2019 meant, yeah? So Ned drew a picture, since Sigmond did drawings, but it were of Sigurd, on account of he\u2019d never seen the trollwife before. So he put a bossy angry face on the picture too and pointed to it and Sigmund understood!<br /> <br /> He started florping off to Ulfa\u2019s place, and we followed on behind, sharing Mags\u2019 booze. But then I got bored and decided to ride up on Siggy\u2019s head. It were tough to stay up there, seeing as the sea monster were all slimy and shit, and Ji-Woo didn\u2019t want to give me high fives anymore cause I got slime and ick all over. I tried wiping my hand off on my trousers first, but that didn\u2019t help none, on account of them being slimy too. Andy gave me a high five though, cause he had gloves and all.<br /> <br /> Any road, it were a good thing I hopped up there, since it climbed up a lamp post and jumped like a sea-monster sized flea thing! I got it to wait up on its friend Ned so he could climb up with me. Ji-Woo and Andy could fly and all, so they could keep up with the jumping and everything. Mags were on the ground, but he made a bloody brill ice path thing, so\u2019s he could ice skate super fast, jumping over and swooshing down the other side of cars. It were proper ace.<br /> <br /> Andy and Ned kept singing pirate songs for a bit, but then the plods showed up so Ned started explaining things using Andy\u2019s bullhorn. If you ever meet Ned, Dad, don\u2019t ever ask him to explain things. They was just following us though, even when the helicopter showed up. Ji-Woo took a break from flying by talking with the helicopter blokes. She got one of them\u2019s number even. Which seems fair since she gave them some of Mags\u2019 rum.<br /> <br /> I think they was following us cause Siggy kept eating fire hydrants, seeing as once we got to the swamp, they left off. After a bit, Siggy found a tree with a biggish crack in it. Biggish just means human-sized though, so it had to squish and squeeze into it. Ji-Woo weren\u2019t too happy about going into it, but I told her it was probably bigger inside and all, on account of it being a home for giants and everything. Plus, I held her hand again, after I dinged and got all clean.<br /> <br /> It were loads bigger inside, so I was right and all. It had open sky and everything, so Ji-Woo were fine. She even went flying some while Mags and Hriki were shagging, and she couldn\u2019t find an end to it. Or the helicopter. There was a stonking huge castle too, made of logs what were whole trees and ice! Ned said it were called Fantasy Island. It was on a bit of an island thing in the swamp, so that worked and all. Sigmond lives there now.<br /> <br /> When we got there though, there was frost giants with Hriki plus some trolls lurking about. Since Mags said we was there to talk about the bombing and shit, Hriki said we could fight the trolls by themselves. They weren\u2019t nothing at all really. Ji-Woo flew way up high and exploded two of them right off. Mags did for two too and I even got one. Ned tried to teach Siggy to fight trolls by gnawing on their heads. Siggy\u2019s a little slow though, so it didn\u2019t get to practice none on an alive troll.<br /> <br /> Then things got weird. Hriki was going to fight us, since we\u2019d gotten all interrupted last time, but then Sigurd\u2019s face showed up in the ice wall and interrupted again. She said that if Mags had sex with Hriki, she\u2019d tell her not to fight and then we\u2019d just have to fight Sigurd to get Idun back. That didn\u2019t make no sense to me. Nobody says \u2018if you take this tenner I\u2019ve got, I won\u2019t beat you up\u2019. But then Ji-Woo said that sometimes girls like sex! Well, first she said it were like fighting, but Mags wouldn\u2019t do that, so I think she meant something else. She said the whore probably didn\u2019t like it on account of her not getting to choose her johns proper. And the ganger\u2019s girlfriends mostly chose who\u2019d be able to protect them best, when they got to choose, not who\u2019d care about them or nothing. Any road, Ji-Woo talked a lot about what she liked about sex, while we was waiting, so I won\u2019t have to ask Jean or nothing.<br /> <br /> Mags looked right knackered when he got back, but happy, so he must have had a proper good time and Hriki too, since she didn\u2019t come fight us or nothing. He finished off the last of the whiskey and he were all good to find Sigurd. It weren\u2019t hard or nothing, cause she really wanted to fight us, so the giants led us right there. She weren\u2019t near as much a bitch this time, just all frothy and angry and shit. See, Ulfa had told her she\u2019d get to fight some Norse and that\u2019s why she was working with her, but she\u2019d still not got to. She was even going to let Idun go if we\u2019d lost, since we\u2019d come to fight and everything and she don\u2019t like Ulfa no more.<br /> <br /> It were a bang-up fight too, bloody ace. Mags and Sigurd took turns hitting each other in the middle fight circle. Mags got some proper good hits in, and Sigurd kept talking about how he\u2019d make a good husband. Norse are right strange. The rest of us played with the giants. I started out hopping back and forth over the circle, wooshing past Mags\u2019 axe and knocking giants off balance. Ji-Woo exploded her bottle of rum to do for one, but then Andy had the brill idea to keep them busy and all by tornadoing them. He got one in a proper tornado, and then Ji-Woo helped and tied up 5 of them with her little dancing wind foxes! She\u2019s been practising a lot and kept them tied up for a long time. Andy\u2019s kept breaking out, but he\u2019d just grab it up again.<br /> <br /> I went for the other one, on account of him going after Ji-Woo, which were not on, but he ignored me! So I stomped his foot and pulled his head down by his hair so\u2019s I could reach and ruined his nose proper. He were paying attention to me after that for certain, at least until Ned left off gnawing on Idun\u2019s chair and slammed his hammer into the giant\u2019s busted nose and he passed out. It were alright, cause Siggy had started copying Ned and it kept on gnawing until Idun were free and all, and never gnawed on her, even a little.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo and Andy couldn\u2019t keep them all tied up forever though, but right when Ji-Woo lost her grip, Mags won! Sigurd kept acting like Mags were going to kill her, but he decided not to. She did say Mags could have Hriki, but first Hriki wanted to take Sigurd to a safe place, and Mags said that were alright. The giants went too. They weren\u2019t too mad, cause we only killed the one, that Ji-Woo exploded. The one me and Ned hit were ok after a bit, so I told it off for going after Ji-Woo.<br /> <br /> Then we got to head off home, leaving Siggy to guard the ice castle, like we did with the dragon before. We should take Ned to meet the dragon so he can give it a name. He\u2019s good at that.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> No new missions since we busted up Ulfa\u2019s new place, but it\u2019s been a right fun time. Idun was around for another week or so. She kept Mags pretty close so she wouldn\u2019t get kidnapped no more. And probably cause she thinks he\u2019s well fit and all. Then Hriki came back after about a month and is guarding Mags, so it got all switched up a bit. Ned started up a proper ace painting at the warehouse, of a nude Hriki all covered in loads of blood. It\u2019s bloody brill.<br /> <br /> She still likes Mags more than me, but that\u2019s ok, cause I got to be with Ji-Woo, so I win. That was pretty fucking amazing and I must have paid good enough attention at Fantasy Island cause she said we should do it again sometime. Mags ruffled my hair for it the next day, even though I didn\u2019t tell him or nothing. He just knew. And Jester were right, I for certain understand why blokes do stupid shit for a shag, now that I\u2019m all growed up, yeah?<br /> <br /> Even so, I think I\u2019m gonna be a girl again, just for a bit, yeah? It\u2019s different than I thought, being all growed up. It\u2019s a good thing and all, I think, but still different. Sides, it'll make Andy and Ned happy if I got tits again.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXVIII</i><br /> <br /> Oh Zane, You don\u2019t know Andy or Edmond well if you think they care.<br /> <br /> So the story finished up, and all\u2019s well that ends well right? Magnus wound up sleeping with Idun, which will no doubt have repercussions later, as well has Hriki (a lot). I don\u2019t normally call for any sort of rolls for sex, but as he had to please Hriki to avoid fighting her, there was actually a roll involved there.<br /> <br /> A little IC in group Drama, but nothing major. Still works out.<br /> <br /> 3 months of downtime, then we look ahead to next story, which session 1 was Wednesday; I just did not get up journals as I am useless these days. Our next story is set in Greece and Turkey, and involves insane Maenads, handsome Daemons, including some minor Greek Deities, a missing Goddess, a meddling Goddess, and a whole bunch of people that have not slept in days. <u>Sweet Dreams (Are Made of This)</u> part 1 should be up in less than two weeks. In the meantime Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T15:39:23-07:00","id":202443,"title":"","content":"Considering the trends of mythology, particularly Greek and Norse, I wait to see how Magnus' romping will come back to bite him and that's not counting his romp with his Dad's wife. Days of Our Lives: Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T17:40:50-07:00","id":202507,"title":"","content":"Heh yeah, that works. Most of my games are like that...Geist has the nickname &quot;The Real World: Death&quot; when we discuss it sometimes. This may as well be days of our lives Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T02:09:18-07:00","id":213286,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time for a new story. It had a few rewrites (see below) but I managed to bang it into runnable shape for session 1. Here we go.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXIX</i><br /> <br /> <u>Sweet Dreams (Are Made of This) Part I</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b><b>Rio de Janeiro</b></b><br /> <br /> The past couple months in Rio with Pipa have been great. About half the time, we\u2019re staying in a classy hotel Pipa found for us, but the rest of the time we\u2019re crashing with the new artist friends I\u2019ve made here. I\u2019ve painted a huge art nouveau wall mural on a brick building in the arts district, a faux absinthe ad featuring a portrait of Pipa decked out in her flowing Chinese robes and a lot of jade. The color of jade reminds me of absinthe. Well, pale jade, anyway. Darker jade doesn\u2019t, but it\u2019s still green, and I love green. It\u2019s such a fresh and invigorating color, though not as refreshing as a light sky blue. I guess I like cool colors more than warm ones.<br /> <br /> Over the past few days, we\u2019ve been staying with a DJ friend named Vitor Soares. He sometimes mixes at the club I mentioned before, Espaco Acustica, which is just as fun as I\u2019d imagined it would be. Well, maybe not quite THAT fun. My imagination is pretty crazy. But it\u2019s still fun, especially with Pipa here. The music is pretty different from the trance and house you hear in Europe, but it\u2019s energetic and carefree and blends perfectly with the tropical heat.<br /> <br /> The big Christ the Redeemer statue kinda creeps me out, though. First off, it\u2019s art deco, which has always felt overbearing and oppressive to me. Way too geometric and rigid. Second, I keep feeling like it\u2019s about to pitch forward to crowd-surf over the city. But I suppose Jesus couldn\u2019t possibly have been serious all the time. I wouldn\u2019t blame him if he decided to let loose like that, though I imagine it would cause a lot of property damage.<br /> <br /> Aside from all the art and clubbing and making out with Pipa, I\u2019ve been reading and studying a lot. I\u2019ve decided that since I can turn things into other things with Taiyi, it\u2019s a good idea to learn as much about machines as I can. I never thought I\u2019d know so much about engineering or architecture, but I really think bridges are fascinating now. It\u2019s kinda amazing how much ingenuity goes into making hundreds of tons of metal and stone defy gravity like that.<br /> <br /> Andy called today and said that Caoimhe wants to meet with everyone. She has a line on another of their missing Weise Handschuhe troupe members. Edward, Zane and Magnus are all in Berlin, so Pipa suggested we Skype in for the meeting. No sense leaving Rio just yet. I mean, whatever is going on, I haven\u2019t had any visions about it yet, so it can\u2019t be all that important.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> So, neither Pipa nor I have a computer, but Vitor had a laptop I could borrow, and we took it back to the hotel for the meeting. Skyping sucks. You aren\u2019t really there, and you feel like an outsider even if you aren\u2019t. And you can\u2019t hug or poke or punch anyone. Not that I\u2019m prone to punching people for real, but Edward and Andy frequently deserve play punches. Fortunately, Zane knows me well enough that she punched Edward in the shoulder at all the appropriate moments. She punches a lot harder than I do, though. Edward didn\u2019t seem to mind. And in case it isn\u2019t obvious from my use of pronouns, Zane is girl Zane again. It\u2019s nice to have her back, though I did like guy Zane. Maybe a little too much. Ooh la la.<br /> <br /> The only thing that made the Skyping bearable was Pipa sitting on the bed behind me, gently strumming the Pipa she gave me. The chords fell like raindrops around me as I stared at the computer screen, and gave the whole experience a really surreal but comforting quality. I was two glasses deep in absinthe by then, and the image of my friends on the computer screen felt like a window into another space, but I didn\u2019t dare try to enter that space no matter how much I wanted to because it seemed so small and suffocating! The rain of pipa notes helped brighten my mood and keep me, if not focused, then at least energetic and cheerful. Also, despite the remote circumstances, I was really glad to see Andy, Magnus, Edward and Zane again. Especially Zane.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Iris is fine, and Caoimhe hasn\u2019t eaten her soul yet. So that\u2019s good. Also, I discovered during the conversation that Saorise really likes Andy. He should pay attention. She\u2019s a sweet girl. But Andy is oddly chivalrous when it comes to matters of romance. It\u2019s like he spends so much of his life swimming through lies and absurdity that he\u2019s uncomfortable dealing openly with really serious things.<br /> <br /> As for the purpose of the meeting, though, Caoimhe has located Constancia (Connie), the maenad member of the troupe. She\u2019s somewhere in Thessalon\u00edki with over a dozen other maenads, which can only mean trouble. Unfortunately, there\u2019s something bigger going on in that area. The whole Thrace, Macedonia and Thessaly region is closed off by the authorities, but there\u2019s very little news about what\u2019s really going on there. We don\u2019t THINK Connie is responsible, but she\u2019s definitely caught up in it, whatever it is, so we\u2019re going to rescue her. And of course, in the meantime, we\u2019re going to try find out what\u2019s going on and put a stop to it. I love enticing mysteries like this, so by the end of the Skype session, my curiosity was piqued and I was ready to leave Rio as soon as possible!<br /> <br /> But I still haven\u2019t had a vision or a prophecy or anything about all this. Which is weird. Honestly, it makes me a little uneasy.<br /> <br /> After I closed the Skype connection, I crawled onto the bed with a pout and asked Pipa if she was coming with me or not. I hoped she would, but I expected her to say it was a good time to go back to work. Instead she said she\u2019d come along and look after the Weise Handschuhe people. That turned my pout into a big smile. But for some reason I was feeling a little insecure.<br /> <br /> \u201cI kinda thought you\u2019d seize this opportunity to get away from me for awhile,\u201d I said. \u201cI guess I thought \u2018going back to work\u2019 was a convenient excuse for you to take a break when you were getting a little fed up with me. I know I can be a little trying at times . . .\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t be ridiculous,\u201d Pipa responded, silencing me with a finger on my lips. \u201cI\u2019ve been alive for centuries and I\u2019ve seen too much to become fed up with you so easily. I LIKE your energy and chaos. We might be very different, but that\u2019s what makes us a great couple. Warm and cool, bright and dark, motion and stillness, yin and yang. I\u2019m not one of the cardboard cut-out pretty boys you\u2019ve dated in the past who becomes bored with a toy that outgrows him too quickly.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wow. I really love Pipa. It\u2019s weird. I\u2019ve always become bored with other people so easily that I guess I just assumed the same would be true in reverse, but I suppose that\u2019s not true. Things are changing. I\u2019M changing, forging strong, stable relationships that aren\u2019t to be cast aside on a whim. It\u2019s . . . nice.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <b><b>Thessalon\u00edki</b></b><br /> <br /> Pipa and I flew to the Greek city of Larissa to meet up with the others before heading into Thessalon\u00edki. The landing was a bit alarming, as a charter jet nearly collided with our flight as we approached the airport. I learned later that the jet was flown by Edward\u2019s father, Dionysus. Edward said he briefly ran into his father at the airport. Dionysus seemed to be fleeing the city, so it\u2019s likely he had something to do with whatever\u2019s going on. But of course Edward was too addled to ask about it, so we still know very little. That\u2019s okay, though. It\u2019s more interesting to find out on our own.<br /> <br /> I still haven\u2019t had a vision, which bothers me a little. But since we\u2019ve arrived, I\u2019ve been sensing a strange pull on me. Andy senses it too. The strands of fate are stretched taut here, like the strands of a spider\u2019s web registering every little caress. I suspect that there are lots of people tugging on them and probably watching them closely. Well, I\u2019m about the join in. I just hope I\u2019m not playing out of my league. This does, however, explain why I haven\u2019t had any prophecies yet. I suspect that now that I\u2019m in the thick of it, insight will come calling soon enough.<br /> <br /> Jean, Saorise and Caoimhe came along, all very eager to be reunited with Connie. Andy arranged a limousine for us, and while Edward drove us toward Thessalon\u00edki, I was able to catch up with everyone. I\u2019m not sure why we let Edward drive, since he has managed to destroy or lose almost every vehicle he\u2019s ever driven, but it seems right, so that\u2019s how it is. Fate, I suppose. Anyway, it was nice to see my friends again. Zane and Edward have spent much of the last month with the sisters in the cave-mansion. Magnus has been working on his music, but I could tell something was weighing on him. Magnus is pretty moody. He tends to have his ups and downs. But there\u2019s always a reason for his mood swings. So after we stopped to pick up a couple cases of wine for the maenads and a fresh bottle of absinthe for me, I asked Magnus what was on his mind.<br /> <br /> He confessed that he\u2019s been seeing Idunn. A lot. And he feels anxious and guilty about the fact that he\u2019s been shagging his father\u2019s wife, even though she is seriously into him. He\u2019s worried about what it means for him and how it will reflect on him as a demigod. He doesn\u2019t know if he\u2019s doing the right thing or not. I mean, objectively, sleeping with someone else\u2019s wife if definitely not the right thing to do, but things aren\u2019t always so clear cut for demigods like us.<br /> <br /> We all listened sympathetically to Magnus\u2019 woes, and then I told him we\u2019d sort it out. I whipped out my Yi Jing coins and consulted the oracle.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Magnus and Idunn - Shi (Collective Force) maintaining</b></b><br /> <br /> The Yi Jing\u2019s answer was pretty clear. Essentially, Magnus is warring with himself. On the one hand there is his ego, that part of him that considers his father a rival, but is also concerned about his own personal honor over that of others. On the other, there is his heart, the part of him that powers his art and that has drawn him to Idunn in the first place. As long as Magnus is seeing Idunn for the right reasons\u2014following his heart, not his ego\u2014then he is doing the right thing and good will come of it. In other words, if he\u2019s with Idunn just to prove his worth against that of his father, or because banging a goddess makes him seem like more of a man, then he\u2019s making a big mistake. And let\u2019s face it, Magnus is already man enough. But if he\u2019s with Idunn because she is where his heart truly lies, then the romance will bring unity, not harm. No matter what happens, by following his heart, Magnus will have a sword and shield against any trials that come his way because of the romance.<br /> <br /> Magnus was encouraged by the Yi Jing\u2019s advice, and I was glad to see his spirits lift a bit. Sometimes, you just have to have things put in the proper perspective for everything to make sense. The Yi Jing\u2019s good for that. And I\u2019m just glad to see Magnus a little less mopey.<br /> <br /> We avoided the police checkpoint controlling traffic into Thessalon\u00edki, and shortly after entering the outskirts of the city, we saw four spectral, skeletal Roman legionnaires marching along the road. Of course we stopped to talk to them, and when they realized we were demigods there to help, they were quite friendly and explained the situation as far as they understood it.<br /> <br /> Basically, Dionysus kidnapped Persephone from the Underworld. Hades, being a possessive tyrant, is furious and sent his dead legions out to find and recover her along with Dionysus. Thanatos is commanding the operation. However, that\u2019s just one part of the problem. The legionnaires weren\u2019t very clear about the rest, but it seems that the dreams of the locals were giving birth to chimerical monsters, things straight from Greek legends. In fact, a monstrous cockatrice was prowling nearby, and legionnaires were at a loss for how to stop it. Obviously we offered to take care of it for them.<br /> <br /> In order to stop the dream creatures from spawning, Hypnos came along and did something to prevent everyone in the area from sleeping, or at least dreaming. That stopped new monsters from showing up, but did nothing about the ones that were already rampaging around. Somehow, a bunch of succubi and incubi are tied up in this, and the legionnaires have been hunting them down and killing them. I suppose they might be part of the reason monsters are spawning from people\u2019s dreams. To make things even more interesting, Hecate\u2019s empusa and hell hounds have been lurking about, and somehow the Greek vrykolakas vampires are involved, but the legionnaires didn\u2019t know exactly what they were up to.<br /> <br /> So things in Thessalon\u00edki are even more curious that I was hoping they would be! I guess it\u2019s time to force a prophecy in order to learn what I can from it. Also, the legionnaires told us that Thanatos and Hypnos have joined forces and are staying at the local Hilton, room 328. So we\u2019re going to go see them next.<br /> <br /> But first, we have to go kill a cockatrice.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Well, the cockatrice is dead. It was a dragon-like thing with a deformed rooster\u2019s head and black, oily feathers spewing choking vapor from its grotesque beak. It was stalking prey along the coast, right where the legionnaires said it would be. Predictably, Edward gunned the engine when he saw it and rammed the limousine right into the beast\u2019s scaled flank. Fortunately, the rest of us abandoned ship before the crash. Jean, Caoimhe and Saorise rolled out well before the collision, and I grabbed Pipa and flew out the car\u2019s wide open sun roof. Magnus and Zane rode the car\u2019s momentum right up to the monster and Zane tried to tear the beast apart with her bare hands. I flew up high, well out of the range of its petrifying breath, but my shots didn\u2019t do much to its iron-hard scales until I unleashed the full power of my starlit bullets. It was a grueling fight, and Magnus and Zane both suffered from the cockatrice\u2019s vapors. Their muscles and flesh started to stiffen as they began to turn to stone, but it didn\u2019t take hold and they should be fine in a few hours.<br /> <br /> In the end, Magnus ended the beast by severing its head with his axe. Then Edward slammed the wrecked limo onto its body and I shot the car\u2019s fuel tank, destroying both car and beast in a fiery explosion. In retrospect, the car was probably salvageable if I hadn\u2019t done that. Everyone else thought it was totally metal, though and that made it okay. Speaking of which, I guess I don\u2019t throw the horns properly, because Magnus always winces when I try.<br /> <br /> The head shriveled down into a normal-sized rooster skull, though it looks like it\u2019s made of some sort of dirty gray stone. It should help protect us from the petrifying breath of other cockatrices.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I flew back into town to steal a van for us. We\u2019re off to see Hypnos and Thanatos next.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a bit since I\u2019ve written and all. I haven\u2019t been paying much mind to the day or nothing, but now we got ourselves a new mission! We get to go to Greece this time, Thesaloniky or summat. One of the White Gloves ladies is there, yeah? See, Andy sent us all messages saying we should meet and all. First I thought it\u2019d be about Iris and Caoimhe on account of that making the cave ladies proper upset, but it weren\u2019t. Caoimhe\u2019d found Connie, is all.<br /> <br /> Everybody showed up for the meeting - Jean and Gia and Saorse and Caoimhe and Ned and Mags and Andy and Ji-Woo and Pipa. Ji-Woo (and Pipa) were there on the TV, on account of them being in Rio de Janeiro. She'd been there a while, since before I was a girl again, I just kinda forgot to mention. Not that it bothered me or nothing - I've disappeared with her loads of time and she always comes back so far. I was maybe a little worried, cause mates is supposed to watch each others backs, and I don't even know where Rio de Janeiro is. But she had Pipa there and Pipa's well hard and Ji-Woo is really good at shooting, so I weren't too worried. She even left me a note, and she don't usually, yeah? Any road, it meant I got to piss around with the street littles more. I can't really be like Jester were for us, but I can badger the bigger ones into looking out for the littler ones more.<br /> <br /> But I was talking about the meeting, yeah? Like I said, everybody were there. Jean was in a bathrobe, on account of that being what you were supposed to wear when summat was there on the TV. Ned were wearing his apron what said houseboy on it, even though he didn\u2019t bring any more cupcakes. And Mags were proper sloshed. He\u2019s been full of beans and a titch grumpy since Hriki left. Probably he misses her. That\u2019s why Ned keeps coming to the caves to make brownies and cupcakes. He makes them really good, like Hestia did.<br /> <br /> Any road, Caiomhe\u2019d found Constancia, but they call her Connie. She\u2019s a Maynad, which sounds right strange, very bitey. She is pretty though, even if she does have weird yellow glowy eyes. Caiomhe saw her and her friends with yellow eyes on TV, not like Ji-Woo was, but like the news or summat. Then the Thesaloniky place they\u2019d been got shut down. Nobody\u2019s allowed to fly in, so Andy\u2019s going to get us a plane and we\u2019re going to meet Ji-Woo and Pipa at some place called Larissa, that\u2019s nearby.<br /> <br /> Caoimhe and Jean are coming too and Gia and Saorse, to help and cause Caoimhe wants to be turned into a Maynad too. It don\u2019t last forever and only girls can be turned into them, excepting Ned on account of his dad. I might have to me a boy again later, I dunno if I want to get turned into some kind of bitey slag. Or I\u2019ll just make sure to get some wine, Caoimhe said that will distract them.<br /> <br /> It were good seeing Ji-Woo again. She kept trying to punch Ned, on account of him being silly, even though she were on the TV. So I matched up with her arm and hit him for her. Not hard or nothing, seeing as I was pretending to be Ji-Woo and all. She were a bit confused, since she hadn\u2019t had a vision or nothing yet, but maybe she\u2019ll have one when we\u2019ve got the whole gang in one place in Greece.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> Turns out I were wrong - Mags weren\u2019t in a nark on account of missing Hriki, he were upset he shagged Idun. She is his stepmum and all, so it\u2019s a little weird and all, but it\u2019s not like she\u2019s old or nothing. He were worried about his dad being brassed off mostly. But Ji-Woo did her coin-flipping thing and said some cobblers about following his heart and not his ego, or summat like that. It made him feel better, which were good. It did make Saorse sad though, so I gave her a hug.<br /> <br /> That were after we got to Greece, yeah? Getting there weren\u2019t too hard. Andy got us a plane in no time, then Ned gave it to his dad, but that was after he flew us in it to Larissa. It were before anybody\u2019s got their stuff off but me though, on account of I keep everything in my clothes, yeah? So Mags weren\u2019t too happy about that either. I got lots of little bottles of booze though, so I could keep giving him presents, cause everybody likes presents.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo got there right after us - Ned\u2019s dad almost hit her plane with ours! - but she were alright. We got her some absinthe, since she hadn\u2019t had any the whole plane ride, on account of she gave her posh spoon and stuff away and she forgot to make a new one. She used my canteen to make some in the super posh car Andy got for us that Ned crashed. Well, Ji-Woo helped with the crashing bit.<br /> <br /> Really though Ned was driving right careful, until we heard about the cockatrice. See, there was a bunch of glowy, see-through soldiers in old timey armor with shiny red eyes and no skin what told us to stop. Ned though maybe they needed a ride, but really they needed us to deal with a cockatrice. That\u2019s a proper ace dragon chicken thing that turns you to stone and makes you chunder. The soldiers were supposed to, cause their bosses Thanatos and Hipnos said to, but they were scared of it, yeah? They was here to look for Persephony really, seeing as Ned\u2019s dad Dionisis took her, but then when they got here, everything was in shambles. Nobody is sleeping, even non-ghosts and superheroes what usually need to sleep, and when they do cause Hipnos makes them, weird animal mixups show up. Plus there was inkubuses and suckubusses and something called vricolas. It sounds like proper fun.<br /> <br /> The boss soldier bloke told us where Thanatos and Hipnos were and where the cockatrice were. Then Ned went driving off his trolley again and smashed right into the chicken-dragon, bam! We got all boosted and out of the car first though. It were a right brill fight. The cockatrice was well tough, so I were gonna squeeze it dead, but then it got me with its beak! It were a bad time, and I could feel I was turning to stone, so I decided I\u2019d be under the sideways car instead. I was still turning to stone, but it didn\u2019t hurt me or nothing. It got Mags too, but he\u2019s more tough. It did make his hand go all to stone doing the horns sign. Ji-Woo says we\u2019ll stop being part stone in a few hours.<br /> <br /> The car were still alright after Ned rammed it, but then he decided to pick it up and hit the cockatrice with it, after Mags punched it dead. Then Ji-Woo shot the car to make it explode on it! It were proper ace, even if it did mean we didn\u2019t have a car no more. But it were alright, since Ji-Woo can fly like a bomb, she got us a new one and picked us up before we even walked very far.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXIX</i><br /> <br /> When <u>Sweet Dreams</u> was originally written, I had Ji-Woo, Zane, Rajani, and Phaedra expected to return, and just two guys (Saltmarsh Andy and Magnus). The original story involved the women having the option to become Maenads (temporarily) to do the heavy lifting in a place that would drive mad anyone who was not mad already, while Andy and Magnus do something more minor in the world. Magnus could be second fiddle as he was the major focus for <u>Rock it for Me</u>, and each female would have the option of having lingering Maenad effects they could call on at the price of lack of control when they did (and a chance to have it happen when they got too excited/upset).<br /> <br /> Of course, things changed. Phaedra could not return for the foreseeable, and Rajani needed to drop. Zane is somewhat different than she was at Hero, both in terms of gender shifting and how she portrays her female aspect, so it would essentially become the Ji-Woo show, which as not really what I wanted. So I had to do a lot of rewriting. Especially given Phaedra\u2019s lack of returning I tweaked it to apply more to Rajani (including some Indian stuff put in). This game got hit with an unusual amount of life stuff; I expected to lose Nemi, but not Phaedra (long term at least) or Rajani. Of course, not all bad, Edmond adds an interesting dynamic to the party.<br /> <br /> However, I think I have a pretty good rewrite. A variation of the ending will happen, on a much more even level (and not requiring Ji-Woo or Zane either one to become a Maenad, nor Edmond, who actually can due to his parentage and the fact Edmond is weird). The Indian stuff I took back out, and put back in some of the Greek stuff I had in mind for Phaedra, and swapped Hermes from the original version for Dionysus (who actually worked slightly better) since Edmond is there.<br /> <br /> The Manes they ran into were essentially more powerful ghosts (in that they could manifest). The Cockatrice was a Dragon (using Demigod rules) with a nausea inducing Breath Weapon (think a stronger version of the Harpies smell but as a directed weapon\u2026have you been in a chicken coop?) and the ability to peck people into stone\u2026each peck lowers their Epic Dex by 1 dot, and turns them to stone when out of dots. Earth 6 can change them back, but obviously none of us have that.<br /> <br /> OOC, the players have dealt with Hypnos and Thanatos before in other <b>Scion</b> games. I tend to play them as rather wisecracking young men (Hypnos especially, Thanatos is more serious by comparison) so at least some of them are looking forward to seeing them again.<br /> <br /> I should mention most point Ji-Woo and Zane disagree (Gia coming, the fact Hypnos did not cause the sleeplessness) Zane is correct. Ji-Woo is right about Andy, though. It's also worth noting it is kinda hilarious that Saltmarsh Andy kept going out of his way to get the group nice vehicles Edmond would lose or destroy.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wrote out a vision for Ji-Woo, which she will get the upcoming session. I suspect it is a bit long for her journal, so it may be going up on this or another off week\u2026we will see. In the meantime comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 07-30-2014, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T16:30:02-07:00","id":235856,"title":"","content":"It's the off-week, and I am still sort of swamped with just being back from Gen Con and moving. But since you all have had to wait I wanted to give you a little something. The below is the vision I gave to Ji-Woo's player this time. They were amused with it, amused enough to print out copies for everyone and have us read the play IC at the table, most reading it for the first time then. While Magnus and Zane do not appear, we had those players do &quot;A Vampire&quot; and &quot;A Second Vampire&quot; respectively as well as both reading the part for &quot;The Frogs&quot;. You will note some inspiration, and some lines are lifted from<i> The Frogs</i>, among other plays, but I tend to have references, some more subtle than others, to <i>The Frogs</i> in my games now and again, because it amuses me to do so. Don't judge me.<br /> <br /> Anyway, enjoy, imagine the PCs actually performing the play IC and their players reading it around the table. In a week we should have journals from that session as well, I have one from Zane's player and Ji-Woo should have one by then.<br /> <br /> A VISION<br /> <br /> DRAMATIS PERSONAE:<br /> JI-WOO<br /> XANTHIAS (who looks suspiciously similar to Saltmarsh Andy)<br /> A VAMPIRE (monstrous looking)<br /> A SECOND VAMPIRE (Maenad looking)<br /> DIONYSIUS (who looks suspiciously similar to Edmond)<br /> FROGS<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Scene:<br /> JI-WOO and XANTHIAS are on a Dock, on the Aegean Sea:<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: The night is dark, and yet there is threat within and without.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Within and Without, My lady?<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: This land is full of vampires, fearsome, and yet they block my visions.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Do they, My Lady?<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Of course! Who else would be blocking my visions?<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Pluto, perhaps?<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Why?<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: His daughter is missing.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: His daughter? Persephone is his wife.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: His wife? Oh dear.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: What?<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Nothing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>A VAMPIRE approaches</i></span><br /> <br /> VAMPIRE: Sup?<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: You block my visions, why?<br /> <br /> VAMPIRE: You wound me my lady! I was merely here to bite you.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Bite me?<br /> <br /> VAMPIRE: Don\u2019t mind if I do!<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Wait, before you bite me. I seek answers to the problems of my visions. Also, I at least expect dinner.<br /> <br /> VAMPIRE: What if you were dinner?<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: No.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Who is your master?<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Pipa Jing, at least some of the time\u2026<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: No, you.<br /> <br /> VAMPIRE: Me?<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Yes.<br /> <br /> VAMPIRE: Nikolas.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Nikolas the Vrykolakas?<br /> <br /> VAMPIRE: I guess it seems strange when you say it that way.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Is he blocking my visions?<br /> <br /> VAMPIRE: No.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: You are wasting my time And-I mean Xanthias.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><i>A SECOND VAMPIRE arrives</i></span></span><br /> <br /> SECOND VAMPIRE: Hi!<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Well this is getting better. I am having trouble with my visions.<br /> <br /> SECOND VAMPIRE: I think my biting you would help.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: You vampires have one track minds.<br /> <br /> SECOND VAMPIRE: And?<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: No.<br /> <br /> Xanthas: Who is your Master?<br /> <br /> VAMPIRE: I told you.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Shut up. You, the one taking their clothes off.<br /> <br /> SECOND VAMPIRE: Oh, Sybil.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Sybil?<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Is she blocking the visions?<br /> <br /> SECOND VAMPIRE: No.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: I see.<br /> <br /> SECOND VAMPIRE: Can we have sex now?<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: No.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Scene:<br /> Later, JI-WOO and XANTHIAS are on a boat<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: An\u2026Xanthias\u2026can I call you Anthias?<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: No, my lady.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Cut the \u201cMy lady\u201d crap, I am pretty sure you are making fun of me. Anthias, I am upset. I have not had a vision and not managed to find out why.<br /> <br /> <i>A boat passes close. DIONYSIUS is on it</i><br /> <br /> DIONYSIUS: Sup.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Edward, what are you doing in the play, Dionysius is supposed to show up here.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Um, Ji-Woo.,,<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Oh, right. Edward, can you tell me how I can get a vision?<br /> <br /> DIONYSIUS: MDA?<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Not helping.<br /> <br /> DIONYSIUS: Honestly, I am sort of confused how I got here. Am I in a vision or a play?<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Both.<br /> <br /> DIONYSIUS: Do I need a costume?<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: No.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: EDWARD! Over here. Need a vision!<br /> <br /> DIONYSIUS: LSD?<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Here you go.<br /> <br /> DIONYSIUS: Thanks. I meant for her vision.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Oh well give me some then Xanthdy.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Xanthdy, really? And that was my last.<br /> <br /> DIONYSIUS: Oh wow.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: I am getting upset Edward. Here I am in the second scene and no closer to finding out why I haven\u2019t had a vision. All I met is two Vampires who tried to bite me, and one humped my leg.<br /> <br /> DIONYSIUS: Like Andy is now?<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Xandy, stop that!<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Sorry.<br /> <br /> DIONYSIUS: Do you think the fact I am supposed to be Dionysius might help?<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Probably not.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Actually he may be onto something.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Are you blocking my vision? Bad Edward! (knocks DIONYSIUS off his boat)<br /> <br /> <i>Exit DIONYSUS. He looks confused.</i><br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Well, I think you killed Dionysius, he sank like a rock.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: He will be fine. I wonder if I can have a vision now.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: You are welcome to try.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Scene:<br /> Hours later, the boat with JI-WOO and XANTHIAS drifts along a swampy river<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: I am really starting to get upset. I have not had a vision, and this play is stupid.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: (to audience) She said it before you did!<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: No really Xandrew, try and help me here, you have visions, suggest something?<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: I think you should have shagged the hot female vampire back there.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Probably.<br /> <br /> FROGS: (Offstage) Brekekekex, ko-ax, ko-ax, Brekekekex, ko-ax, ko-ax, We are the children of fountain and lake, let us wake.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Ummmmmmmmm?<br /> <br /> FROGS: Visions come but not when called, a lady appalled. She should look to a lady of many dark odes, a lady of crossroads.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Phaedra?<br /> <br /> FROGS: \u2026.What?<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Just hoping.<br /> <br /> FROGS: But it is not she who holds the key, but when you open your eyes, yea down from the skies, she looks upon you. Brekekekex, ko-ax, ko-ax<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: That does not help.<br /> <br /> FROGS: Brekekekex, ko-ax, ko-ax,<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: At all.<br /> <br /> FROGS: Brekekekex, ko-ax, ko-ax,<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: I hate you all.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Scene:<br /> A bedroom in a Greek villa. It is empty, save a NOTE<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: (enters) An\u2014er Xanthias, I had a vision. Andy? Where did he go?<br /> <br /> (JI-WOO looks around, finds NOTE: \u201cOff partying with Vampires\u201d)<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Damnit Andy, I finally had a vision, and it was just a stupid play. It did not even mention Hyponos and Thanatos till the final act, and they are pretty important. It was like one of those dreams where you keep doing something without purpose. I hate those. I don\u2019t even like working hard for a purpose.<br /> <br /> <i>JI-WOO sits down on the bed</i><br /> <br /> JI-WOO: And now that I have had a vision, I don\u2019t feel any closer to solving this then before. I don\u2019t know where Connie is or what\u2019s going on. Worse, I am pretty sure I am still in the play, and that sucks.<br /> <br /> <i>XANTHIAS and DIONYSUS enter the room, their faces covered with lipstick and wearing women\u2019s clothes, for some reason</i><br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Edward! I knew you did not drown. Listen, I had my vision, and now I need help getting out of this stupid play. Can you help?<br /> <br /> DIONYSUS: \u2026What?<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: We are stuck in a play Edward. After you left, I was mocked by a bunch of frogs. It was awful. Why did you leave me Edward?<br /> <br /> DIONYSUS: Sorry.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Where have you been?<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: It certainly did not involve Persephone.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Were you messing with Hades\u2019 wife? We are supposed to find her, well, I think we should find her.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: Are you sure she is not his daughter? She looks pretty young.<br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Creepy. Also, yes. I am sure. As are you, I am pretty sure.<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: I should probably leave then.<br /> <br /> DIONYSUS: How about this? (DIONYSUS takes hammer, mimes bashing away part of the wall toward the audience.)<br /> <br /> XANTHIAS: That will do. (He runs out and offstage toward audience.)<br /> <br /> <i>Exit XANTHIAS.</i><br /> <br /> JI-WOO: Edward, you made a hole in the play, thanks. (She flies out toward audience.)<br /> <br /> <i>Exit JI-WOO.</i><br /> <br /> (DIONYSUS shrugs, puts down hammer, lays on couch and goes to sleep.)<br /> <br /> <i>Curtain.</i><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome, otherwise see you in a week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 08-20-2014, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T12:45:06-07:00","id":241617,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check in on our Scions. If you have not seen it, I put the vision/play up last week to enjoy, so check it out before reading if you did not before.<br /> <br /> Okay, let\u2019s get rolling.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXX</i><br /> <br /> <u>Sweet Dreams (Are Made of This) Part II</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <b><br /> Thessaloniki</b><br /> <br /> Dear Yisheng, I wonder if you have ever been stuck in a play that\u2019s really a prophetic vision. No, probably not. You don\u2019t have visions, do you? You should. I\u2019m sure Edward can provide something that might help with that. Anyway, I got stuck in a vision while we were driving from the place we fought the cockatrice to the hotel where Hypnos and Thanatos were staying. It snuck up on me. One moment I was listening to Andy spinning entertaining lies while Zane listened with child-like fascination, and the next I was standing on a dock on the Aegean Sea, or at least a theatrical set that was supposed to represent a dock. At the time, I didn\u2019t realize anything was wrong. It seemed quite natural, until later in the play when I became frustrated with it.<br /> <br /> The play revolved around my attempts to find out why I hadn\u2019t had a vision yet. Andy, as the comic hero Xanthias, was with me, and we encountered vampires, maenads, Dionysus (played by Edward) and a chorus of annoying frogs who pretty much convinced me that Hecate really is involved in whatever is going on, even if she isn\u2019t the cause of it. There was also confusion over whether Persephone was Hades\u2019 daughter or his wife, but everyone knows she\u2019s his wife, and I still don\u2019t know what THAT was all about. It might\u2019ve just been Andy messing with me.<br /> <br /> Anyway, in the end, Edward made a hole in the play with his hammer, and I was able to fly out. When I emerged from my vision, I realized that I was the one holding Edward\u2019s hammer, and I had just smashed one of the windows out of the van with it. No worries, though. It worked to get me out of that stupid play, and besides, we were under attack by vampires. A group of vrykolakas bloodsuckers had ambushed our vehicle, and everyone was clambering out to fight them. Edward thought he was on a crashing plane, and somehow became obsessed with the idea that throwing a vampire through a nearby shop window was the only way out. Honestly, I have no idea what\u2019s going on in his mind most of the time, but he seems to muddle through, so I guess it\u2019s okay.<br /> <br /> Pipa and I jumped clear of the van, and Pipa sort of herded Caoimhe, Jean and the Saorise to a safer spot. I flew to the top of a nearby building and started raining fire down on the vampires while Magnus mowed through them with his axe. Zane decided to humor Edward, so she grabbed one of the bestial vampires and threw him through a shop window. In response, several angry serpent-women came swarming out. Obviously, they were Hecate\u2019s empusa, but I have no idea what they were doing in that jewelry store after hours. They certainly seemed happy enough to loot the place when they got a chance.<br /> <br /> It was about then that I noticed that the moon was looking at me. It didn\u2019t have eyes or anything, but I could tell that it was staring right through me. And I started to glow with a soft, silvery aura. It felt . . . weird. But not bad. I think it was Hecate. I suspect my prophecy drew her attention, so I stared back, and lost several moments gazing into the pale disk of the moon, which reminded me of how beautiful Pipa\u2019s face is in the moonlight. Then I peered deeper, so deeply that I could see the world reflected in the moon, and that\u2019s when I realized that we were in trouble. More and more vampires were converging on our location, so if we didn\u2019t escape soon, we could easily be overwhelmed.<br /> <br /> The empusa just seemed confused. They didn\u2019t want to attack the vampires, so they are probably allied, at least loosely. But after I started glowing in the moonlight, they didn\u2019t seem eager to attack US either. And when one of the vampires tried to mesmerize me, they jumped on him and tore him to shreds. I think Hecate must have marked me, but I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s a good thing. She is notoriously fickle.<br /> <br /> We managed to kill most of the vampires that ambushed us, and while we had a brief respite, we piled back into the van and sped off to the hotel. On the way, I scribbled down the lines of my vision-play in my sketch book. I thought we could act it out once we got to the hotel. Maybe then it would all make more sense. Unfortunately, we had more work to do before we could get to the play, because the hotel was under attack by some of the chimera beasts that were spawning from people\u2019s dreams. There were two of the, horrible goat-headed, lion-bodied, scorpion-tailed things that stank of fetid meat and halitosis. They were just padding about near the elevators, looking for a way to get to the upper floors. They couldn\u2019t take the stairs, because the stairwell was blocked with a wall of leering, staring skulls. Thanatos\u2019 work, no doubt.<br /> <br /> The chimeras were tough, but Magnus managed to slay both of them with Edward and Andy\u2019s help. Meanwhile, Zane and I were distracted by a shadow-black hound with eyes that reflected silver in the light. The beast pounced on Zane from the darkness, and would have torn her open if she hadn\u2019t dropped into a shadow to escape. I couldn\u2019t see what happened to her next because she became invisible. So did the hound, but I managed to peer through its veil and keep track of it as it prowled around the combat, intent on hunting Zane. The beast must have been sent by Hecate, so I guess she\u2019s taken an interest in Zane too. Either that or she\u2019s just fucking with our mission, but I really think she just decided on a whim to hunt Zane and help me. The scary thing is that she could change her mind at any time, so next time I play with fate and mystery, I should definitely try to manipulate things so I stay on her good side.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Zane is always protecting me, but this time it was my turn to protect her. Since I was the only one who could still see the hound, I took care of it with a few shots. I guess that makes it sound pretty easy, but it was actually pretty tough. I probably would have had a hard time if it had decided to attack me back, but fortunately it seemed reluctant to do that.<br /> <br /> By the time I\u2019d killed the hound, the others were done with the chimeras. Magnus and Edward dragged the chimera bodies outside, and Zane, Andy and I arranged the lobby into a rudimentary set by shoving some of the furniture around. Then I shared my scribbled notes on the vision-play with everyone and we all acted it out. Andy and I played ourselves (though Andy went by Xanthias, or Xandy for short). Obviously, Edward played Dionysus. Magnus and Zane weren\u2019t actually in the play, so they played the parts of the vampire, maenad, and frog chorus.<br /> <br /> Actually, acting out the play was a lot of fun. And it did help us sort some things out. Hecate is definitely involved in what\u2019s going on, but she isn\u2019t responsible for it. Actually, the presence of the maenads implies that Cybele has a hand in this as well. I suppose she and Hecate both caught wind of things and decided to meddle. It was Persephone\u2019s disappearance from the Underworld that triggered everything else. I\u2019m not sure why Dionysus kidnapped Persephone, or even if that\u2019s really what happened. Still, Dionysus might be part of the reason I\u2019ve been having trouble with my visions, though. In fact, I\u2019m pretty sure he\u2019s somehow responsible for drawing Hecate and Cybele into things as a smokescreen to cover his actions.<br /> <br /> Oh well, I suppose the smoke will clear in time.<br /> <br /> Also, Magnus sounds really funny when he tries to do the Greek frog sound. Don\u2019t tell him I said that, though.<br /> <br /> After giving up on the play, we headed upstairs. Thanatos\u2019 skulls were happy to roll aside to let us pass, and Thanatos and Hypnos welcomed us into their suite. They were both super hot, shirtless men with sunglasses. They actually looked a lot alike, but the shadows seemed to cling to Thanatos like a lover, which was very sexy. Between the two of them, they filled us in on what they knew.<br /> <br /> Dionysus visited Persephone in the Underworld, and then both of them left and fled to the World. After that, something blotted out the moon in parts of the Underworld. Hypnos and Thanatos were sent to figure out what\u2019s going on, and that\u2019s when they discovered the problem in Thessaloniki: chimera spawning from dreams and people being unable to sleep. I thought Hypnos was keeping them from sleeping to stop the monsters from spawning, but in fact the opposite is true. He doesn\u2019t know why they can\u2019t sleep any more than we do, and when he tried to force people into gentle slumber, a flood of monsters emerged from their dreams.<br /> <br /> It seems like Hecate took offense to Hypnos and Thanatos trying to divine what\u2019s wrong. It\u2019s weird that she suddenly decided to show up and stir things up a bit since she\u2019s been out of touch for a long time. Still, she\u2019s always been adversarial. She\u2019s not exactly a titan, but sometimes she might as well be. And she\u2019s probably working with the vampires. Maybe. My insight tells me that the leader of the vrykolakas worships her, but that doesn\u2019t mean she\u2019s showing him any favor. Can you believe that the vrykolakas leader is named Nikolas? No really! How funny is that? Oh yeah, I forgot. You don\u2019t have a sense of humor do you, Yisheng? I\u2019d like to hear you laugh some time. Are you ticklish? Pipa isn\u2019t. Trust me. I\u2019ve tried.<br /> <br /> I was still wondering about the wife/daughter confusion over Persephone in my play, so I asked Thanatos if Hades had any scions in the area. As far as he knew, there were none, so that\u2019s one theory blown. On the other hand, Thanatos does know Constancia and thought she might be roaming around. I stepped out on the balcony to see if I could find the maenads reflected in the moon, and sure enough, there they were, heading east toward Anatolia. That\u2019s very curious, since that part of Turkey is Cybele\u2019s home territory. And then I noticed that the vrykolakas seemed to be gathering to follow them, so we decided to go find Connie and the maenads next. They are obviously up to something, so they might know more about what\u2019s going on. However, the chimera are much stronger at night, and the vrykolakas can\u2019t emerge during the day, so we decided to wait until morning before heading out. It\u2019s safer that way.<br /> <br /> Of course, that meant we had to find a way to entertain ourselves for the rest of the night. Thanatos was flirting pretty heavily with me and Pipa. He suggested that we might be able to find something to do to while away the time, so I glanced at Pipa to see what she thought. Her sly, sultry (and mildly predatory) grin convinced me she was interested, so Thanatos, Pipa and I retired to another room to enjoy some absinthe and a menage a trois. I think Pipa got more of a thrill out of sleeping with a sexy death god than I did, but that\u2019s not to say I didn\u2019t enjoy myself. When it comes to death, Thanatos is as skilled with la petite mort as he is the normal kind.<br /> <br /> Is that too much information, Yisheng? If so, let me know. But I\u2019m not in Berlin, so I probably won\u2019t get your message until I go back and check the basket in my apartment. If I remember.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Once Ji-Woo had gotten back with the car, we headed off to the hotel where Thanatos and Hypnos were. Ned got to telling Ji-Woo about us flying in, except he were lying, or maybe just pretending, about loads of it, including some cobblers about it being the wrong week to quit anything, and Ji-Woo weren\u2019t listening. She weren\u2019t asleep or nothing, she batted my hand off when I waved it in her face, she were just staring out the window, all fixed-like.<br /> <br /> After, she said she were having a vision, or watching a play, or both. It were a proper strange play too. I weren\u2019t in it, but Ji-Woo told me to be the Maenad vampire lady what humped her leg, in the play. But that were later. Her vision-play-thing got broken up when she busted a window in the van with Ned\u2019s hammer, or maybe when the 2 rat-faced fucks landed on the bonnet of the van Ned was driving. They was vrykolakas and there was 50 bazillion of them. We killed loads and there was loads more that kept coming for us.<br /> <br /> I got Ji-Woo all boosted before she jumped out the busted up window, saying something about dinner first. She and Mags busted up the vrykolakas but good, with Andy helping. I helped Ned out, even though he was acting like he was right off his trolley, even more than usual. He thought the van were a plane, and the spare tyre a parachute and the window were an escape hatch. But he said it were important that one of the vrykolakas blokes got throwed into a shop window. So I did and snake ladies came out! I tried to knock another one into a different window, but Mags killed him first. He did throw the dead vrykolakas into a window with his axe, but it didn\u2019t work that time.<br /> <br /> The ladies were bloody brill, with claws and snake bits and grenades. They didn\u2019t really like us, except for Mags, they wanted to have a go with him. They couldn\u2019t hurt Ji-Woo neither, on account of she went all glowy. They wanted to kill me, which weren\u2019t really all that brill, but they decided nicking some swag were better, so they buggered off. Except one came back to give Ned his flask and wink at him, so maybe she wanted a go with Ned. Ji-Woo didn\u2019t say so though.<br /> <br /> Since there was 100 gajillion of the vrykolakas wankers, we decided to bugger off too, once we\u2019d killed a couple or a dozen. Ji-Woo really, really wanted to do her play-vision-thing in real life, but the only proper safe place were the hotel with the in-charge blokes, on account of some magic stuff they did. So we decided to go there and just do the play downstairs before we talked with them. There was even a proper ace pile of skulls what blocked off the stairs until we asked them to move and watched our play. But first there was two monster things, with lion bodies and snake necks and scorpion tails and creepy goat heads. I never liked goats and their heads is the worst part, with the eyes and all, yeah?<br /> <br /> So we started busting them up and things went proper backwards. See, I started knocking the buggers off balance and standing between them and Ji-Woo, since she couldn\u2019t fly up or nothing. But then, a stonking black dog with silver glowy eyes came from bloody nowhere and just about bit me in half! I fell down into its shadow though and popped back up behind Ji-Woo. Then it disappeared and I couldn\u2019t even hear where it was, seeing as its noises all sounded like they was coming from the moon. So I disappeared so good it couldn\u2019t find me. Course, I couldn\u2019t find it neither, but Ji-Woo could and couldn\u2019t find me, so I was better at sneaking. Ned boosted me after I jumped on his shoulder, by throwing a bit of coke at me, but then Ji-Woo did for the dog but good, since it wouldn\u2019t listen when she told it to go back to its mum.<br /> <br /> She said its mum was a god-lady called Heckaty (its probably not spelled like that, cause Greeks spell things weird, but that\u2019s what it sounds like and she weren\u2019t written in the play with her name or nothing). She\u2019s probably who made Ji-Woo all glowy. See, the snake ladies are part of Heckaty\u2019s gang. She\u2019s the one what keeps looking at me when I boost people too, on account of she doesn\u2019t like mum\u2019s pantheon and the powers and things I got from mum make my boosting better. I didn\u2019t think nothing of it the first time, but it keep happening and it happened just before the bloody dog showed up, so it\u2019s probably all her fault.<br /> <br /> Any road, after we\u2019d done for the weird monster things and the dog, we did the play. It were proper silly, with biting and frogs and clothes taking off and and Ned drowning and sex stuff, but it were just for pretend, so it were alright. I got to be one of the frogs too, with Mags, and make proper strange sounds, mostly on account of them being hard to sound out, yeah? Mags and Ned explained it after and it sounded more like frog noises, I just read it funny. Lots of it didn\u2019t make sense, except for Heckaty\u2019s messing around with things but doesn\u2019t have the key, and Hades has a kid what is important, probably.<br /> <br /> We talked some about the leader bloke of the Greek pantheon. I don\u2019t like him very much. Ned and Phaedra are alright and all, yeah, but I think I\u2019m more ok with mum\u2019s pantheon not liking their dads\u2019 pantheons. As long as they don\u2019t mess with Ned or Phaedra. Heckaty don\u2019t like the Greek pantheon neither, on account of Zeus the leader bloke taking advantage and Dionysus (Ned\u2019s dad) is Persephone's kid by Zeus, on account of him taking advantage again. We think maybe Dionysus is protecting Persephone from summat, seeing as it\u2019s his mum and all.<br /> <br /> After the play, we went to go talk with Thanatos and Hypnos, who only showed up in the play when Ji-Woo were complaining that they never showed up in the play. They don\u2019t like shirts. Jean likes that they don\u2019t like shirts. They were fit and all, and their sunglasses were proper ace. They said that Hades didn\u2019t have any superhero or demigod type kids here, so maybe Xanthdy were just being silly? Nicolas (a vrykolakas what was talked about in the play) is some special boss kind of vrykolakas, on account of him being the first. Sybil from the play is probably the boss lady of the maenads, seeing as they are right powerful and she can make special ones. She and Heckaty don\u2019t like each other much, but we don\u2019t know which got here first, and which was just following the other. Sybil does like Dionysus, so maybe she\u2019s protecting him too.<br /> <br /> For now we\u2019re just waiting til daytime, seeing as the weird monster things aren\u2019t all chaosy in the day, and maenads aren\u2019t as strong and vrykolakas explode in the sun. When it\u2019s day, we\u2019re going to follow everyone east. I\u2019m going to hang out with Mags and see if I can shoot any vrykolakas from inside the place, on account of everyone else being off shagging or talking with skulls or summat.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXX</i><br /> <br /> Ji-Woo did get one detail wrong, Hypnos was sent to see why people were not dreaming and ran into his brother there. Otherwise she is on task.<br /> <br /> Session was some time ago, so not much to add. Between moving and Gen Con seems like forever. I will answer any questions/comments folks have, though. Should be back on track next session and moving on with the story. See you then!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/