OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T16:27:51-07:00","id":255652,"title":"","content":"We are overdue, it seems for a journal for Scion. I got my timing thrown off as we had the game Monday not the usual Wednesday to accommodate schedules, then I got busy. Still, all is well, and here is the journals<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXI</i><br /> <u><br /> Sweet Dreams (Are Made of This) Part III</u><br /> <b><br /> Ji-Woo's Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Greece</b><br /> <br /> The morning dawned bright and early. I\u2019m not normally awake to see the morning sunlight slowly flood into the room, but since I couldn\u2019t sleep, I didn\u2019t have much choice. It was a nice opportunity. Pipa and I were still in bed with Thanatos, so I had to stop the romping so that I could watch the light creep through the windows. I really wanted to enjoy the dawn with my senses keyed up, but I didn\u2019t have any absinthe left, so I whipped out my Bureaucracy brush and wrote a message to Yisheng (requesting absinthe) on Thanatos\u2019 chest. Thanatos didn\u2019t seem to mind.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, no absinthe showed up. I was pretty cross with Yisheng. What the hell was he doing, and why didn\u2019t he deliver my absinthe immediately? Still, I can never stay mad for long, so when Saorise came floating in to tell us that everyone was gathering downstairs, I was already over it. In fact, without even thinking, I waved Saorise over and told her she should join us in bed. In retrospect, that was not the smartest thing I could do, but at the time, Saorise just fled in embarrassment.<br /> <br /> Eventually we got up, got dressed, and went downstairs. Magnus had been sitting at the bar all night with his guitar, and was just coming out of a sort of focused meditation on his music, so he was only dimly aware of what was going on around him. Fortunately, the hotel bar was well stocked and had a couple brands of absinthe, so I slowly prepared glasses for myself, Thanatos and Pipa. While I sat there and sipped mine, letting the familiar sensations sweep over me, I toyed with my Yi Jing coins. Somehow they fell in just such a way that they seemed meaningful, and suddenly I knew exactly where Connie and her maenads had gone, or at least which town were in. It was a small place near the Turkish border. I also realized that Yisheng wasn\u2019t slacking off at all. In fact, he had filed the proper paperwork for my absinthe order immediately. The paperwork was caught up in Bureaucracy red tape, though, so who knows when it will arrive. When it does, it had better show up where I am, and not in that hotel room. Unfortunately, I also felt the taut strings of fate shift in an ominous way when I read the coins. Hecate noticed me again. That\u2019s probably not a good thing.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Zane and Edward arranged transportation. We knew it was time to go when Edward drove a Hummer through the front of the hotel. There\u2019s a lot more property destruction in my life these days. I blame Edward. And Magnus.<br /> <br /> We spent most of the rest of the day driving east toward Turkey. Fortunately, the vampires weren\u2019t out during the day, but there were still plenty of chimeric beasts for us to fight or avoid. At one point, we drove by a Greek military base. There were these horrid, long-necked buffalo-warthog things roaming inside the base. I recognized them as creatures called catoblepas. I warned everyone that if you met their gaze, they could instantly kill you, but Edward either didn\u2019t hear or didn\u2019t care, and went driving straight toward the base. There was no way the car was going to smash through the gate, though, and with Andy and Mags help, I eventually got him to stop just before we crashed.<br /> <br /> Instead of going through the military base, we took a detour around it, which led us through a little town that was being systematically flattened by huge skeletal rhinoceros. Even though it was much bigger, it didn\u2019t seem as dangerous as the catoblepas, so we parked the Hummer and went to fight it while Pipa kept Jean, Caoimhe, Saorise and Gia safe. The rhino was pretty tough, but between Edward attacking its legs, Zane tearing it apart from the inside, me raining fire down on it from above, and Magnus going head to head with it, the beast eventually fell. I did get distracted when Magnus set his frost axe aflame in the jetting fires of a gas main I\u2019d shot up. The mixture of fire and ice was fascinating, and it left a little rainbow in the wake of his axe swing. It was beautiful, but I don\u2019t think rainbows are very metal, so I think I\u2019ll keep that little detail to myself. That goes for you too, Yisheng. I order you not to embarrass Magnus by spreading rumors that his axe leaves rainbows in its wake.<br /> <br /> Once the fight was over, Magnus, Zane and Edward mounted the beast\u2019s head on the Hummer\u2019s chassis so that we were driving around a truck-sized rhino skull for the rest of the day. As Magnus put it, it doesn\u2019t get much more metal than that. I\u2019m pretty sure it made up for the rainbows. I kinda hope that when we\u2019re done with the skull, we can grind the horn down into powder. My intuition tells me that if I were to sprinkle the powder on any undead, it would help weaken their supernatural toughness. It sounds like something to hold onto for when we REALLY need it.<br /> <br /> At this point, I should note that Saorise was furtively making eyes at me all day, and it didn\u2019t take me long to figure out that she was smitten. I really shouldn\u2019t have invited her to join us in bed this morning. I\u2019m not really interested in the lovestruck ghost girl. I mean, sure, she\u2019s adorable, and I\u2019ve never made out with a ghost before. I AM terribly curious about it, so I wouldn\u2019t mind giving it try. Saorise\u2019s a sweet girl, and I don\u2019t want to hurt her feelings. But Pipa\u2019s my girlfriend, and for the first time in my life, I\u2019m serious about that. Besides, I can\u2019t really give Saorise what she really wants: a child.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t get a chance to talk to Pipa about it until after we smashed through an empusa roadblock and entered the town where Connie and the maenads were supposed to be. We stopped for a rest and to wait until night so that we could check the town\u2019s reflection in the moon for any signs of maenad activity. Pipa and I went off for some alone time and found a nice place to view them moon. It was very romantic until I told her about Saorise. I was worried she\u2019d be mad, but I should have known better. She actually thought it was kinda funny, but she also told me it was entirely my fault. She told me I should be more careful with what I say and do. I guess she\u2019s right. Still, she doesn\u2019t have a problem with me fooling around with Saorise, if only to satisfy Saorise\u2019s curiosity (and my own). She\u2019s not worried that anything serious will come out of it like she is with boy Zane.<br /> <br /> Anyway, once the moon appeared in the dusk sky, I peered at it, wondering if it would look back at me again this time. It didn\u2019t, and I was able to pinpoint the maenad\u2019s location. They were apparently partying at a local bathhouse, so that\u2019s where we headed next, but not before Zane, Magnus and Edward welded crude metal spikes to the hummer\u2019s wheels. That vehicle was looking more and more dangerous by the moment.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not hard to tell where maenads have been. Just look for lots of empty wine bottles. The streets around the bathhouse was littered with them. Also, talking to maenads is weird. They are really distracted because all they want to do is have sex with you (if you are a woman) or eat you (if you are a man) or do both (if you are Edward). In fact, while we were chatting, Edward ended up making out with one of the maenads, and by the time we pulled him out of the bathhouse, he was missing a couple of bite-sized chunks of flesh. Oh Edward, what are we going to do with you? Of course, the maenads kept coming on to me too, but they were way too aggressive about it, and it made me uncomfortable. I\u2019m glad they didn\u2019t pressure Zane. She\u2019s so innocent as a girl, I didn\u2019t want her getting involved. I tried to shield her eyes from maenad orgy, but she was invisible, so I couldn\u2019t really make it work.<br /> <br /> Still, Magnus and Andy did a good job questioning the maenads, even with all the distractions. It turns out Connie left the bathhouse earlier in the day, and she\u2019s now headed into the mountains with Persephone. So now we know where Persephone is. Apparently, Connie has some plan to use Persephone to make herself and her maenads more powerful. The maenads at the bathhouse didn\u2019t say whether Persephone was complicit in this plan or not, but my guess is that Connie can\u2019t make the goddess do anything she doesn\u2019t want to do. Unless she somehow managed to make Persephone into a maenad too, which would be fascinating but would probably piss off Hades. Then again, who knows. Maybe it would spice up their relationship.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <b>Turkey<br /> </b><br /> So, we\u2019ve crossed the border into Turkey. The border guards tried to stop us, but once Magnus explained that we had killed the rhino whose skull now adorned our Hummer, the long-suffering guards just waved us through.<br /> <br /> Saorise managed to drum up the courage to talk to me during a quiet moment. She asked if my offer from the morning still stood, and said she\u2019d like to make out. I told her that it probably wasn\u2019t a good idea, even though I WAS curious about what sex with a ghost would be like. That sent her into paroxysms of embarrassment, and she insisted that she just wanted to make out a little, nothing more. So I shrugged and said sure. We could give it a try sometime. Saorise went floating off, giddy as a goat. This is going to end badly.<br /> <br /> Deep in the night, we finally reached a large town where we thought Connie might be stopping over on her way to Turkey. There was a large hotel there, and it was under siege by a bunch of vampires and a huge hound with a flaming mane and scorpion tail. Zane, Edward and I took care of the vampires, tout de suite. Magnus slew the hound, but it gave as good as it took. One swipe of its paw shattered Magnus into a million shards of brilliant ice, but then new ice crystals grew from the remnants of his legs to form a new Magnus. Like Zane\u2019s shadow trick and my ink splatters, it let Magnus survive an otherwise grievous hit unscathed!<br /> <br /> I got distracted by something then, so even though I could clearly hear more fighting going on inside the hotel, I ignored it until we made our way inside and found even more vampires. I was honestly surprised, so I was a little slow to react, and by the time I did, the others had killed most of the handful of vampires in the lobby. I helped finish the last few, and that was that!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> Something proper odd\u2019s happening with Saorse and Ji-Woo. They\u2019ve been whispering a bunch and I can hear really good, so I know what they were saying, about snogging and stuff. Probably had summat to do with this morning, on account of when Saorse went in to get Ji-Woo and Pipa and Thanatos to come on out, she went flying back out again, even more all pale-like, which is right impressive, her being a ghost and all. I didn\u2019t think much of it then though, seeing as Ji-Woo came down in a bit any road, looking for absinthe and all. The others came with her. Thanatos had Ji-Woo writing all over his chest (he weren\u2019t wearing a shirt still, yeah?). I don\u2019t remember that being a sex thing, seems like it\u2019d be to tickle-y.<br /> <br /> Once Ji-Woo\u2019d come down, Ned remembered we was supposed to go driving, and stopped playing with the skulls to go get the Hummer I\u2019d nicked and drive it into the hotel proper. Me and him had been playing with the skulls, but I was invisible and all, so when he made the skulls hands, he thought they was voting about who should be Yorick. It were harder to make them fight with toothpicks all sneaky though. Mags were playing his guitar, kinda asleep-like, but not really, seeing as there weren\u2019t no monsters coming out. He woked up proper when Ned brought the car into the front room though.<br /> <br /> After Mags threw his bottle at the sun for being all bright, and we\u2019d got tons more full bottles for the car, Ned started us out going east. Ji-Woo tossed her coins about for a bit and then started telling Ned where to go proper. She also said something about her secretary or summat, I think he did some paperwork saying she should get some more absinthe? So she told him to do some paperwork saying he did a good job. Ji-Woo\u2019s mum and dad\u2019s pantheon is well strange.<br /> <br /> The ride to the city with the maenads in it was proper fun. First we saw a whole bunch of small planes, with some catableepus guards. Ji-Woo bricked it a bit, on account of they would kill you if they only looked at you proper. They were right daft looking, eating concrete with a fuzzy humpy bit and a long long neck. There was a stonking fuck off rhino skeleton too, just smashing the shit out of a whole load of houses. Ned really wanted to ride a plane, even though he were the only one what could drive one, and they was too small for everybody to be in the one. Even if I rode on the wing, which would have been proper fun.<br /> <br /> Any road, we went after the skeleton instead. We thought maybe we could ride him around a bit, but he weren\u2019t very nice and didn\u2019t want to talk none. He were well tough though, but Mags and Ji-Woo and Ned did for him but good. Xanthdy had us all well boosted too. I were about to bust up his skull proper by squeezing through his eye holes, but they finished him off first, after Mags froze his axe up out of a fire hydrant and sharpened it up, and Ji-Woo helped me break its ribs up and Ned went for his hooves things. It were a good thing I didn\u2019t, on account of then we put the entire stonking skull right down over our car, so it looked like we was just sitting inside a moving skull, with wheels and everything. It were probably the most well hard thing ever, specially with Mags and his ice axe standing up through the hole in the roof.<br /> <br /> Mags made it even better when we got to the maenad city. He put a bunch of metal spiky bits and swords on the wheels! Like poking out so they spinned and cut things up that we go past, yeah? It were proper ace. I had to go find the tools and things, but it were worth it, specially since Jean kept talking about wanting a bang.<br /> <br /> When I got back, Ji-Woo were talking about going to a bath house, which seemed daft, on account of I just had a bath and all at the hotel, but really it were because that\u2019s where the maenads were and she knew all the time and was being all secret-y. She did say I needed a bath though, on account of all the fighting, yeah? Mags got proper upset cause they was playing One Direction, on account of he don\u2019t like them much. He made them stop with his super powers, so it were alright though. I went all invisible and sneaky, seeing as I didn\u2019t want any of them to turn me into a maenad too. Yuck.<br /> <br /> I forgot a couple of times and talked while I was invisible, but it were alright, seeing as there weren\u2019t no big dog statues looking out for me this time. They mostly just started snogging after they talked with us for a bit, one of them with Ned and two with each other after they got in a fight about praying mantises. The one with Ned really want to have his arm off, but he didn\u2019t let her take the whole thing, just little bites. Any road, Connie weren\u2019t there no more, she buggered off to Turkey to get Persephone, on account of the maenads get well strong if they drink her blood.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo kept trying to cover my eyes up, but I were too sneaky. Not like I was watching them having goes at it with each other, or like I hadn\u2019t seen loads of times before. It still don\u2019t look like much any road, specially when the maenad were talking about having a nosh while giving Ned a nosh. I\u2019m glad I\u2019m not grown up no more, for now.<br /> <br /> We ran into the other ladies too, the snaky kind what work for Heckaty. We scared them off though, with our bloody brill skull. They wanted to eat us too, both times! Greece is well strange. After them though, it got boring for a bit, so Ned started doing coke while he was driving. He\u2019s really good at it, ti were kinda hard to stop watching. Then he started telling stories about driving for a band when he were in college, on account of Mags getting us into Turkey by saying we had a music gig. I don\u2019t think Ned realized he were pretending.<br /> <br /> We caught up with the vrykolakas, going to where the other maenads said Connie was. THere was another stonking chaos wanker too, a huge dog thing with a neck what was on fire and a scorpion tail. I liked it better than the goat head any road. Xanthdy and Mags went for the dog, leaving the vrykolakas for me and Ji-Woo and Ned. We didn\u2019t have any problems or nothing, though one of them did try to hurt Ji-Woo while she were hanging upside down, but she\u2019s proper fast, so he missed. Then Ned did for him, so we all helped Mags and Xanthdy, seeing as the dog just shattered Mags like he were ice! He were ok though, on account of he\u2019s well hard. He just got all misty and froze up again.<br /> <br /> They were attacking another posh hotel, so we decided to see why and inside there was more vrykolakas fighting some maenad ladies. They weren\u2019t nothing though. I threw one of them posh chandelier things at them, and Ji-Woo knocked a couple down the elevators, and then the box on top of them, and Mags ran through walls with them. Ned kept flirting with the ladies while he were beating up the vrykolakas, even though they probably wanted to eat him too and Andy kept us all boosted so it were proper lemon.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXI</i><br /> <br /> Not much in the way of new enemies or such to discuss this time. Was a fun session all around.<br /> <br /> Last session went well too, so look for that journal hopefully closer to usual time. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T01:13:23-07:00","id":267256,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay, it has been a crazy week and I am still behind. But we have Scion Journals to put up!<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXII</i><br /> <br /> <u>Sweet Dreams Are Made of This Part IV</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo's Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Turkey</b><br /> <br /> Maenads are awful. All they want to do is fuck and drink and bite, and while I confess that I have a healthy appetite for two of those activities, the third is just too much. And these aren\u2019t sexy little love bites like the ones Pipa likes to give me. These are full on \u201cOMG you\u2019re delicious I\u2019m going to eat you!\u201d bites. Or maybe \u201cOMG being a maenad is great I\u2019m gonna make you into one too!\u201d bites. Either way, it\u2019s not good. I always thought my first meeting with Persephone would be more enjoyable too. I mean, she gets along with my mom just fine, so I thought she would be fun. I did NOT foresee that she would immediately pounce on me and start biting. But perhaps I should have foreseen it, given the circumstances.<br /> <br /> I suppose a bit explanation is in order.<br /> <br /> We loitered around the hotel lobby a bit after clearing it out. There was more fighting going on upstairs, but as usual we got distracted. Edward thought we were at a concert and started rocking out on a sofa, and Magnus didn\u2019t need an excuse to join in with his guitar. Of course, Andy got involved. Meanwhile, as Zane and I examined the rest of the lobby, I started to notice patterns in the discarded wine bottles the maenads had left scattered about. Some of the labels seemed particularly significant. They told me that Connie and Persephone were hiding out on the 14th floor of the hotel, and that Persephone had willingly become a maenad, at least for as long as it takes to deal with whatever they\u2019re after in Anatolia. Other labels showed me that the vampires are after Persephone, but they also have some other agenda. Most disappointingly, though, my absinthe order is sitting on the desk of the minister of Wine and Spirits, waiting for his stamp before it\u2019s sent for distribution. OH MY GOD! I\u2019m never going to get that absinthe! It had better be damn good absinthe, made from anise and wormwood grown in Tian itself.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the hotel lobby was open all the way up to the top floors, the halls and rooms sort of ringing the wide open space. So I shouted to the rock stars that Connie was on the 14th floor and flew on up. Andy flew up with me. I\u2019m pretty sure he was looking up my skirt, but if I cared about that, I wouldn\u2019t wear skirts, not with the amount of flying I do. Magnus and Zane jumped from one landing to the next until they arrived at the fighting, but Edward disappeared to take the stairs, and didn\u2019t show up until later.<br /> <br /> There were a bunch of vampires fighting maenads throughout the 14th floor. I could see most of the fight from where I was flying in the open lobby, so that\u2019s where I stayed. That didn\u2019t stop a couple of vampires from jumping out after me, but Zane took care of them. She even grabbed one right out of the air and rode him down to the floor 14 stories down! He didn\u2019t survive the impact. Magnus took on a creepy-looking lion-headed spider beast and made short work of it. I think he went out of his way to destroy as much of the hotel as possible during the fight. Meanwhile, I fought a huge stone bust that hopped around on its pedestal and lashed out with a whip-like barbed tongue that sent paroxysms of confusion surging through anyone it touched. I managed to dodge it, and it STILL muddled my mind a bit. Not enough to throw me off my game, though, so I shot off the tongue and then shattered the statue with a couple more bullets. Edward seemed fascinated by the tongue when he finally showed up. He grabbed it and used it as a weapon for awhile, and then after the fight started licking it even though it obviously tasted awful. I worry about him.<br /> <br /> Once the coast was clear, I led the others right to Connie\u2019s room since I just sort of knew where it was. Connie thought I was room service at first, but I\u2019m not sure whether that meant she thought I was a call girl or a meal. Probably both. I pushed my way into the room, explaining that I was neither, and told her we\u2019d come to find her on behalf of the White Gloves troupe. That\u2019s when Persephone jumped on me and started biting. I squealed and tried to beat her off, and Zane came to my rescue. Connie managed to calm Persephone down enough to lock her in an adjoining room, and it was really disturbing to see Persephone obey Connie like a loyal dog.<br /> <br /> Once THAT was settled, Connie explained to us what she knew, and everything started to make more sense, particularly in conjunction with my prophecy-play. Connie is on assignment from Cybele. There is a powerful chaos entity affecting people\u2019s dreams. This entity started out as a lost child who somehow fell into Hundun\u2019s clutches. I mean, Hundun is all about rampant chaos, so that makes sense. I should report this to the Bureaucracy, because if I can help strike a blow to my pantheon\u2019s titan, it will probably look pretty good on my permanent record. Not that I especially care about that, but I suspect that I have a lot to make up for, and besides, it might help expedite future absinthe requisitions.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the child was corrupted with Chaos and turned into a powerful entity that exists simultaneously in dream and reality. It\u2019s the one causing dreams to spawn monsters. Also, this Dreamer might have Morpheus. Or maybe not. All we know is that Morpheus is missing. He\u2019s probably the one keeping people awake to mitigate damage the Dreamer can do.<br /> <br /> Cybele ordered Connie to find the Dreamer\u2019s corporeal form. She disguised herself as Dionysus and kidnapped Persephone from the Underworld. Hades till thinks Dionysus is responsible, which is probably serving as a fantastic distraction right now! Persephone was complicit in everything, of course, and Cybele gave Connie the one-time power to turn Persephone into a maenad so that the other maenads could drink Persephone\u2019s blood and gain strength from it. That\u2019s the only way they were going to be able to fight off the vampires and other monsters long enough to complete their journey into Anatolia and find the Dreamer.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Persephone\u2019s maenad mind becomes more feral when she\u2019s lost a lot of blood. That\u2019s why she was acting so strange when we found her. Once she\u2019s managed to rest and recover a bit, she should be more like her normal self, which is good, since I\u2019d rather she not bite me again.<br /> <br /> Also, Connie thinks I\u2019m a total prude because I refused to sleep with her (even though she\u2019s very attractive) and I didn\u2019t want Persephone biting/fucking me. I\u2019m sorry, but maenad sex is just too wild and weird and dangerous for me. Not for Edward, though. He\u2019s been making out with one maenad or another since we arrived here.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> We needed to let Persephone recover a bit, so we took a bit of a break. It gave Caoimhe and Jean a chance to catch up with Connie. They were all pretty happy to see one another again. Andy has been acting the gentleman and even donned a suit of elegant-looking Unseelie armor in order to present the right impression the Persephone. Edward went off to bang a maenad who had been fondling him all night. Magnus was playing music and breaking things upstairs, and I think Zane hung out with him for awhile.<br /> <br /> Pipa and I headed down to the bar, where we just sat and talked. I drank a lot of absinthe, which always puts me in a better mood and opens my mind to all sorts of things that I wouldn\u2019t see otherwise. Saorise hung out with us too, but she was pretty quiet. I think she liked the absinthe, though. Insight came to me during the early hours of morning. I still have no idea where the Dreamer\u2019s corporeal form is, but I do know that my absinthe requisition has been stamped and is at the Divine Boxing and Bottling Bureau to be prepared for shipment. Unfortunately, it\u2019s going to be delivered to the hotel in Greece where I ordered it. Sigh. No wonder the Bureaucracy has so many problems. It can\u2019t even get an absinthe order right. I wrote a message to Yisheng ordering him to pick up the absinthe order and deliver it to me directly no matter where I am.<br /> <br /> I also realized that one of Yisheng\u2019s favorite things is fresh chrysanthemum tea. So don\u2019t worry, Yisheng, I\u2019m going to order you a huge supply as thanks for all the trouble you\u2019re going through for my absinthe.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Magnus and Zane wandered down to join Pipa, Saorise and me. I started going on about how kissing Pipa was like kissing music itself, and Magnus understood exactly what I meant. I don\u2019t know if you have ever kissed music before, but it is one of the most amazing things you\u2019ll ever experience, like becoming one with the wind as it flows through you or allowing the brush strokes of a beautiful painting to embrace you with caresses of pure color. That\u2019s what kissing Pipa is like. Gods, I love her. I even love her serious and slightly disapproving frowns, but I love her sly smiles more. Both are equally musical, just different.<br /> <br /> It was after dawn when Connie, Persephone and the others came down to find us. Persephone was in her right mind again, and told us a little more about what we\u2019re facing. Defeating the Dreamer will be difficult, because in order to do so, we have to defeat his dreaming self. But in the realm of dreams, he is essentially omnipotent, and we wouldn\u2019t stand a chance against him. If we can attack his corporeal form at the same time, though, it will distract him enough to weaken him in dreams. This means we\u2019re going to have to split up. One group will go into dream to attack the Dreamer there, and the rest will attack his corporeal form once we find it.<br /> <br /> In order to get into the realm of dreams, Connie has to drink an elixir that Dionysus gave her. It will help her become a sort of conduit, a portal of madness leading into dream. That sounds so cool. I can\u2019t wait to try it! I need to drink a bunch of absinthe before we go in to make it even more amazing! Unfortunately, the realm of dreams will drive even the strongest mind mad unless it\u2019s already insane. That means that whoever goes into the realm of dreams is going to have to become a maenad, at least temporarily. And only women can become maenads. So I\u2019m going to have to let Connie bite me and change me. I\u2019m not looking forward to it, but at least being insane can lead to more potent visions. Edward is going in too. I\u2019m not sure why, but when he showed up this morning, he was a woman. I guess he isn\u2019t that different from his father. He was already wearing the clothes of the maenad he slept with last night, and he didn\u2019t look too bad after we got him all made up.<br /> <br /> So Edward, Connie and I are going into dream, and the others are going to assault the corporeal Dreamer. Zane\u2019s a girl, but her female aspect is innocent and pure, more or less, so I won\u2019t let her become a maenad, and she doesn\u2019t want to be one anyway. So she\u2019ll be sticking with Magnus and Andy. She\u2019s not happy that we will be separated. She protects me, and I think she\u2019s worried that I won\u2019t be safe without her. Honestly, so am I. But hopefully things will be okay.<br /> <br /> Anyway, now we\u2019re on the road again. I transformed a bus into a nice luxury RV by painting a flowing dragon on its side. We needed something that big so that everyone could travel in comfort. I mean, there\u2019s like a hundred of us now: Magnus, Andy, Zane, Edward, me, Caoimhe, Saorise, Gia, Jean, Hypnos, Thanatos, Connie and Persephone. Okay, there\u2019s thirteen of us. Thirteen is kind of like a hundred, if you\u2019re a rabbit and numbers greater than five don\u2019t mean anything. Some of us stayed behind, though. Pipa\u2019s looking after Jean, Caoimhe, Gia and Saorise while the rest of us continue onward.<br /> <br /> I made sure the RV had a hot tub, and that\u2019s where I\u2019m relaxing right now along with some of the others. We should always travel in this kind of style. I\u2019ve been chatting with Persephone about my mom. They\u2019re pretty good friends, and it\u2019s fun gossiping about her. Also, Persephone is super hot. Unfortunately, she isn\u2019t very fond of Pipa because Pipa ate one of her scions once. Awkward.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> After that we\u2019d done for all the vrykolakas downstairs, so we decided to take ourselves a break. Ji-Woo started up poking about at all the broked wine bottles the maenads had left about and found one what said Connie were on the 14th floor and one what said Persephone were a maenad now, for a bit. Then she got all sad on account of she found one what said her absinthe were waiting for a stamp or summat. Later she figured out it were going to the hotel back in Greece any road, so she sent Yishing after it.<br /> <br /> Ned still thought it were a gig, so he built himself a stage from cushions and started up singing Mags\u2019s songs. Mags started playing guitar with him too, but he kept his shirt on. Ned and the yellow eyed lady what were playing with his nipples didn\u2019t. Neither did Xanthdy - he were playing drums with bottles and pillows. Ned were pretty good at singing Mags\u2019s songs, even though he didn\u2019t know German or nothing. I turned him to Spanish halfway through, but it didn\u2019t help. Ji-Woo wound up going to the bar to make absinthe and all, so I got beers for everybody, once they\u2019d stopped having a gig. Ned had traded shirts with the maenad bint sometime, after paying her back massages, yeah? He looked like a proper tart.<br /> <br /> Once we\u2019d had beers all around, cept for Ji-Woo\u2019s absinthe, we went up to find Connie and all. Ji-Woo flied up, with Xanthdy holding on to her ankle. I climbed the walls and Mags just jumped, pew! right up the balconies. Ned took the stairs. Right near where she was, there was a big stonking spider, like car sized or summat, what had a lion\u2019s head, more vrykolakas wankers, and a posh lady statue what was just a head and some shoulders and a long sharp tongue. The chaosy things were proper hard to hit, so I started out knocking them off balance by jumping on the statue\u2019s head and getting all tangled up in spider legs. Mags used his axe like a flyswatter thing and smashed the lion-spider into the wall, splat! after I got out of its legs and Xanthdy shook an icicle from his pants onto Mags\u2019s head. The statue kept sticking her tongue out at Ji-Woo, so she shot it off and killed the stone bint. Then Ned started licking the tongue! He\u2019s a right nutter.<br /> <br /> Then there was just vrykolakas. One of them tried to go for Ji-Woo, so I tossed him off the side and rode on his back down so\u2019s he fell on the chandelier. Mags killed one with the ice making machine, then another with the ice scooper, that were well hard. They got the others while I got back upstairs, hopping this time, on account of it was faster.<br /> <br /> When we finally got to Connie\u2019s room, she thought Ji-Woo was room service and were going to try and eat her! That were not on, so I grabbed Ji-Woo\u2019s shirt and didn\u2019t let Connie drag her inside and all. I had to pull Persephone off Ji-Woo too, on account of she\u2019s a maenad now and lost lots of blood, so she\u2019d lost the plot with it and weren\u2019t talking none. She did bite Ji-Woo proper good, so\u2019s that she were bleeding alot, but I had stuff to fix her up with and all. Connie were being a right berk about it though, taking the mick out of Ji-Woo about not wanting to be bit up.<br /> <br /> She did explain things though, and then Persephone some more later when she got her blood back and everything. See, there were some big fuck off chaos wanker, that were a little what got lost in a bad Chinese place full of chaosy things and came back all bad, and he were building a chaos army. Plus, he\u2019s in two places at once, in the regular world and some dream world place. Sybil got Connie to come deal with it, and so the chaos bugger got his friend Nicolas the vrykolakas to send other vrykolakas to come protect him, so Sybil got Dionysis to make Connie look like him so she could get Persephone, on account of she makes maenads stronger when they get her blood. That\u2019s the complicated part.<br /> <br /> Then there was the bad part. On account of the chaos wanker being in two places, we\u2019ve gotta do for both at the same time or it can\u2019t be done for none. So Connie\u2019s going to drink some posh Dionysis drink thing and become a portal or summat like that so we can attack it in the dreamworld and all. But the dreamworld does bad things to you if you\u2019re not barmy already, like the maenads and Ned is. But only me, Ji-Woo and Ned can be maenads and I can\u2019t. Maybe boy me could go all crazy with the biting and the sex stuff, but boys can\u2019t be maenads, cept for Ned, cause of his dad, yeah? Summat wouldn\u2019t be right, me being a maenad, so that means I won\u2019t be able to protect Ji-Woo or nothing. I told Ned he better be careful of her, but it\u2019s not the same. Me and Xanthdy and Mags will be doing important things, on account of if the chaos bugger isn\u2019t distracted, he can just kill them dead right off, but it\u2019s not the same still.<br /> <br /> Any road, once we\u2019d figured out what were going on, Mags went to get the White Gloves people and Saorse and Pipa and the Greek blokes from across the street. Then there was more waiting, on account of wanting to let Persephone get her blood back. Plus everybody had to have another bang, I guess. Ned went off with Diamond, the maenad bint who liked his nipplies and Connie jumped on Caoimhe right off and Jean got a room with Hypnos and Thanatos. Mags went off to play music though, so I went with him to play some on my pipes. The maenads played drums with us too, banging on other maenads\u2019s heads for it.<br /> <br /> After a bit, Mags started busting shit up, on account of it being a hotel and all, but I were getting hungry, so I went to the bar, seeing as they have pickled onions sometimes. They did this time too, and Ji-Woo and Saorse and Pipe were there! I thought they\u2019d gone off for a snog, but Ji-Woo was proper absinthe-floaty and had lots of saucers, so she\u2019d been at it awhile. She weren\u2019t calling anyone who they was, just calling Sarose the wind and talking cobblers about kissing music. But she\u2019s fun to listen to when she gets all floaty, so it didn\u2019t feel too long until everybody else were done.<br /> <br /> When it were time to go, Ned was proper bit up and had his hair all spiky, which was proper ace, the hair bit at least, and he were wearing Diamond\u2019s clothes. I fixed up the bit parts and the ouchies he\u2019s got fighting yesterday. Ji-Woo switched her shirt so\u2019s it matched with Ned\u2019s, which were right funny, since he looked like a proper scrubber. Persephone were better now, and said she were sorry for yesterday. She ate a fish dog! She weren\u2019t really sorry to us for that, mostly just sorry for herself, but she were sorry about the biting. We did introductions all around then. Mum doesn\u2019t like her much, I guess - she said she made a bad first impression on her, or summat. Or maybe she was afraid I were going to grass on her trying to bite Ji-Woo to Mum. It\u2019s all complicated. Also Persephone don\u2019t like Pipa much, seeing as Pipa ate one of her scions before. Pipa wound up staying to watch over the others though, Saorse and the White Gloves people, so that\u2019s alright.<br /> <br /> Xanthdy were acting right strange with Persephone there, all posh and proper and polite, on account of him being a Knight of the Unseelie Court. He were talking like a bloke from a book and everything, He even did his clothes all dark and somber and posh. I told him he ought look like one of them beefeaters from London town, but only when he were helping Ned shave up and put on make up. I weren\u2019t going to take the mick out of him in front of Persephone or nothing.<br /> <br /> Connie knew kinda where to go next, on account of Sybil telling her with a tuna fish sandwich, Persephone got proper giggly thinking of other foods Sybil might talk to us with, like alphabet soup or summat. But there still was a ways to go, so Ji-Woo magiced us up a stonking motorhome, seeing as the proper ace skull car got all smashed up. And she didn\u2019t even put spiky bits on the wheels! She did put in a hole in the roof though, so I hung upside down and made Ned scared that he were. There was also a hot tub and a bloody brill painting of a snaky dragon flying through fire clouds with lots of Ji-Woo writing all around it. Mags did right for the skull car, getting the horn off first, and then lighting it on fire and having it explode and everything. And then we was off!<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been listening to Ji-Woo talk about her mum with Persephone, seeing as they\u2019re friends and all. But things are getting a bit bumpy, I better keep look out for Ned.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXII</i><br /> <br /> So who thinks the RV won\u2019t survive the next session? Show of hands?<br /> <br /> Next time our heroes meet Hecate and fight more nightmare critters. Also, some planning. Hope you enjoyed. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T02:12:31-07:00","id":276140,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check on the Scion team, lets see what they are up to. Things get stranger in\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXIII</i><br /> <br /> <u>Sweet Dreams (Are Made of This) Part V</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <b><br /> Turkey<br /> </b><br /> Okay, this is just getting ridiculous. We\u2019ve been driving . . . somewhere . . . for hours, but I have no idea where we\u2019re going. All I DO know is what the Yi Jing has shown me: the Dreamer does NOT have Morpheus, Morpheus is NOT responsible for the curse of sleeplessness, Persephone is NOT a natural blonde, and Yisheng has finally picked up the absinthe I ordered from Tian. I hope he arrives with it soon. I need it. Badly. You\u2019re getting this, right Yisheng?<br /> <br /> Still, I don\u2019t really mind not knowing where we\u2019re going. That\u2019s pretty much normal for me. I\u2019m just tired of all the weird stuff that keeps happening along the way, and the fact that Edward keeps making it worse. I\u2019m tired of crashing into invisible nightmare beasts that practically explode with gore when the RV hits them. I\u2019m tired of having the remake the RV. And no one else seems keen on taking responsibility for things, so I\u2019ve had to step up and keep Edward in check, and I\u2019m terrible at it, because all I want to do is ignore his drug-addled antics and find my zen place. Right now, I just want to lose myself in the mellow rapture of some deep chill trance, preferably wrapped in Pipa\u2019s arms or hanging out with Zane while relaxing in a nice, cool place with dim, colorful lighting. And there needs to be absinthe.<br /> <br /> Responsibility sucks, and it\u2019s also futile.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Edward is going to get me killed.<br /> <br /> He just drove right through a minefield. If I hadn\u2019t been in the passenger\u2019s seat so that I could shoot a path through the mines, we would have lost the RV again, and I probably would have died from the explosions.<br /> <br /> The minefield covered the road running in front and a secluded mountain monastery. The monastery seemed important somehow, but Edward didn\u2019t stop, and I was too busy shooting mines to worry about it, so we passed it by. I have a feeling that was a mistake, but right now I don\u2019t really care.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> After night had fallen, we stopped in a small Turkish town. Unlike most places we\u2019ve been since this madcap quest began, the town was full of activity. People were celebrating, and even the police and militia were joining in the festivities. Magnus stopped a militiaman and asked what was going on. The soldier said they were planning to secede from Turkey, and that some snake-women had been in the town and were staging something. Apparently, Hecate\u2019s empusa were up to no good there. We wandered through the town and saw people setting up some sort of stage in the town center. There was a burning tank in one intersection, and everyone seemed a bit insane, which is only natural since none of them have been able to sleep for four or five days. It was kinda sad, really.<br /> <br /> Magnus, Zane and Andy tried talking to some of the half-crazed townsfolk, and Edward sort of got lost in the chaos for awhile. But I couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that something big was happening in the town, so I gazed up at the moon, wondering if it would gaze back at me. It didn\u2019t, but I could see in the town\u2019s reflection, that the people were slowly but surely moving burning cars into a big circular pattern several blocks in diameter. I know a summoning circle when I see one, and it was pretty clear to me that they were trying to summon Hecate. I imagine the empusa had a lot to do with it.<br /> <br /> Once I told the others about it, they leapt into action. Magnus started yelling at the townsfolk, ordering them to start dismantling the summoning circle. It didn\u2019t take long before Magnus had a big group of them all working hard to undo what they had already done. Zane jumped in to help too. She threw cars around like they weighed nothing. I think Edward spent the time looking for the empusa, but he didn\u2019t find any. They must have already left.<br /> <br /> We couldn\u2019t afford to spend any more time helping the townsfolk. As Magnus put it, their situation wasn\u2019t going to get any better until we had resolved the curse that was keeping them from sleeping. So we drove on into the night. Still, something about the monastery still bothered me, especially after the summoning circle thing in town. I focused on my memory of the place, and was able to shift my consciousness so that I could see it again.<br /> <br /> What I saw was shocking. The monastery was bathed in moonlight, and vrykolakas vampires were crawling all over the place. One of them was carefully moving mines around to cover the path I shot through the minefield earlier. Others were drawing another summoning circle in the monastery\u2019s vast, open courtyard. And one of the vampires, a tall, monstrous thing dressed in something that resembled a Greek Orthodox bishop\u2019s robes, seemed to be presiding over the preparations for a ceremony. I\u2019m certain that was Nikolas, the vrykolakas leader. And I think he and his followers were preparing to summon Hecate, probably to ask for her help dealing with us and the maenads. Connie agreed with me.<br /> <br /> Once I\u2019d explained what I saw to the others, we decided to stop. I suggested that we summon Hecate on our own. If we could do so before Nikolas did, we might be able to make a deal or otherwise convince her not to help the vampires, and to help us instead. I came up with a quick ritual. Magnus found an abandoned car, which I transformed into a big hound effigy using Taiyi. Zane and Edward drew a summoning circle under Andy\u2019s supervision. Then we burned the effigy, and Hecate rose from the shadows cast by the flames like viscous ink dripping upward from the ground.<br /> <br /> She was sort of intimidating, dressed in a long, elegant black dress with a huge, fan-like collar. She had three faces, just like the legends said, and fortunately for us, all three surveyed the scene with aloof curiosity rather than rage or malice. She asked what we wanted, so I asked if she knew where we could find the Dreamer\u2019s corporeal form. She didn\u2019t, but she knew where we could find out. She promised to tell us, and to remove her guardian servants from the place, in exchange for Persephone. She\u2019s curious about Persephone\u2019s connection to both life and death, and wants to experiment on her to find out how it all works. It sounds unpleasant.<br /> <br /> Obviously, we weren\u2019t going to agree to that. So she offered another price. I could promise to perform some sort of service for her for a whole year, or I could promise to help push one of her requests through the Celestial Bureaucracy in the future. Neither option sounded very good to me. I wouldn\u2019t even consider giving up my freedom by agreeing to the former, but I guess I did consider helping her out with the Bureaucracy, once she assured me that the request would neither harm the Bureaucracy nor empower Hundun in any way.<br /> <br /> I called Pipa to get her advice. She knows a lot more about this sort of tricky maneuvering than I do. She wisely told me not to take the deal. It would only end badly. If I was open about what I was trying to do, the Bureaucracy would stonewall Hecate\u2019s request because she isn\u2019t one of us. And if I tried to hide it, then I\u2019d probably get in trouble for treason. So that was right out. I might break the rules, and I might shirk my responsibilities, but I\u2019m not going to commit treason against my pantheon. Not even Da Ji or Pipa would go that far. I think.<br /> <br /> It looked like were at an impasse, and I probably should have let it go at that point. Magnus sure wanted to drop the whole thing and figure it all out on our own, but he tends to get pretty impatient about this sort of thing. Personally, I\u2019m tired of all the crazy chaos. From the start, I\u2019ve felt confused by this whole ordeal. I didn\u2019t foresee it coming until we were already embroiled in it, and then I ended up in a stupid play. On top of that, so many of fate\u2019s threads are hidden from me that it makes me feel a bit lost. On top of all that, Edward has been getting crazier and more ridiculous the longer this goes on. I blame the maenads, and I hope he\u2019s back to his normal self when this is all over.<br /> <br /> So, with all of that weighing on me, I wanted some answers. I asked Hecate if she couldn\u2019t just promise not to help the vampires. She said sure, but only if we would lend her Persephone for a day or two, after which she promised to return Persephone unharmed. Persephone was hesitant, but she agreed to Hecate\u2019s terms. It sounded to me like Hecate was getting a lot more out of the deal than we were, though, so I argued that she should really be a good sport and tell us where to find the info on the Dreamer. She didn\u2019t have to withdraw her servants, she just had to let us know where to go. Fortunately, she agreed.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s how things came full circle. It seems the Dreamer consulted the library at the vampires\u2019 monastery, and we can find what we\u2019re looking for by consulting the tomes stored there. Of course, we will probably have to fight our way through a horde of vampires unless we show up during the day. And if we DO show up when the sun is out, who knows what other defenses they have? Whatever. I\u2019m sure we can handle it.<br /> <br /> Magnus seems unhappy with the deal. I think it\u2019s because he\u2019s worried about how angry Hades will be when he finds out we pimped out his wife. I guess that\u2019s a legitimate concern. Maybe once all this is over Persephone can go back to the Underworld all safe and sound and he\u2019ll never find out. You should probably strike this part from the official record, Yisheng.<br /> <br /> That reminds me, where are you with my absinthe? This is like the worst room service EVER!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> It were a proper good thing I were keeping a look out for Ned. Otherwise we might never have got the camelion off the roof and Ned might have got us namastayed to death with the antlions. Ji-Woo helped too, even though it were her fault he went all namastayey anyway. She blowed up all the explodey bits in the road, when Ned weren\u2019t listening.<br /> <br /> See, it\u2019d got all bumpy on account of Ned seeing an invisible camel, honking at it, then running into it. It got all sorts of blood and guts all over the windshield, then got up on the car! Ji-Woo said so, and that it weren\u2019t Morfeus and that it were ok that Persephone colored her hair. So Ned asked the invisible camel on the roof if it were dead and it weren\u2019t, so I told him to go proper fast round the corner, zoom!, so\u2019s it would fall off, yeah? It were bloody brill, and it worked, or at least we got lighter right after. And there were a big dent down the cliff a bit. Ned wanted to run into it again, seeing as it weren\u2019t dead, but me and Ji-Woo said no, on account of it being at the bottom of the cliff.<br /> <br /> Then the antlion wankers showed up. They was about as big as a regular car, and Ned were getting all worried, on account of there being 8 of them. So Ji-Woo told him to calm down, cause her coins said to, and he closed his eyes and started praying or summat, folding his hands up in front of him. So I had to hold on to the wheel and when Ned finally stopped the RV, the antlions started noshing on it! I dunno what it is with Greek people and eating stuff what shouldn\u2019t be eaten. It\u2019s probably the sleep crazies. Any road, that were not on, the antlions eating our RV, so I told them so, and busted them up good, in their stonking lion faces.<br /> <br /> Xanthdy kept fussing at people, for swearing and all, on account of Persephone being there and being a princess and everything. He buffed me up cause I weren\u2019t swearing or dressed up like a slag. Ji-Woo weren\u2019t dressed like a slag no more either, but she were swearing, and Ned were still done up like a tart and Connie only had the top half of her cozzy on, and Mags were just in a Speedo thing. Mags got proper upset when the antlions finished breaking the car, even though he\u2019d been right calm up til then. I guess he traded off with Ji-Woo, cause she were proper angry at first, on account of them trying to eat the car, but then when the car broke, she were calm again, all namastay like Ned kept saying.<br /> <br /> It were all ok in the end though, cause Ji-Woo could fix the RV! She needed rocks and things to fill in the holes with. She couldn\u2019t use the antlions cause they was living, even though they weren\u2019t no more. But it were easy to get rocks, specially when Mags started busting up the cliff.<br /> <br /> After that Ji-Woo were in the passenger seat to help Ned, even though she kept trying to ignore him talking cobblers to me about all kinds of movies. Mags went back to the hot tub, but it weren\u2019t as comfy no more or summat, so he was still cranky. We got to kill some more antlions though, in just a bit, and Ned ran into another invisible camel, after Xanthdy bit his head. Ji-Woo saw the camel too this time, and said it were actually a camelion, one of them lizards what changes colors, but with crab claws. She were sitting on the window edge so she could shoot when Ned hit it, so she got proper soaked with blood and guts and all. She jumped in the hot tub to clean off, but I think she actually did the ding! thing, cause there weren\u2019t no guts in the hot tub.<br /> <br /> Then Ned went off his trolley again, cause he tried to bandage a tree with paper towels, and wanted to take it to the hospital. Me and Mags said no, but he pulled it out of the ground anyway. So Mags pretended to be a tree doctor and checked it over and said it didn\u2019t make it, so he shoved it off the cliff. Ned were proper sad, but he had a leaf left and he gave it over to Ji-Woo to keep.<br /> <br /> Ned were quiet after that, on account of he was trying to remember what he\u2019d been talking about before, then he got distracted and were trying to remember what he\u2019d been trying to remember. But that meant he weren\u2019t listening when we came up on a monastery what had bombs in the road around it and nooses in the trees, so he didn\u2019t go around or nothing. So Ji-Woo got to be proper ace and shoot up all the explodey bits, pow boom!, before we got there.<br /> <br /> Then we drove some more and some more and some more. It weren\u2019t boring or nothing, not really - my mates know lots of stuff, like about moving islands and lemmings and lady camels, though Mags fussed at Ned when he started talking about lady camels\u2019s humps. Ned started singing like Mags to make up for it. He also talked a lot about a different Greece, what was in France, where there was camel vampires what did politics, but I think he were talking bollocks again. Ji-Woo said that some islands moved too though, and Xanthdy, so that part\u2019s probably true.<br /> <br /> Mags were really wanting a drink, but all we had were the small bottles I can fit in my pockets. I had to stop from laughing too much - it looks right silly when littles drink from those tiny bottles, and even more when it\u2019s stonking big Mags drinking from them. He found some proper bottles when we got to the next town though. They was having a big party, cause the snake ladies told them to and making some kind of circle out of burning cars to get Heckaty to come over. Ji-Woo thought that were bad, so I tossed cars away and Mags got all the regular humans to stop doing stupid stuff, like shagging and eating bottles and setting houses on fire. Ned kept thinking it were another gig and tried to bribe the soldier by pulling his shirt up. The soldier said he\u2019d throw a grenade if Ned did it again, but he let us through and all, so it worked.<br /> <br /> The snake ladies weren\u2019t about and Mags figured we needed to do for the dreamer right quick, so we got back to driving pretty quick. Ji-Wo figured out the vrykolakas were trying to summon up Heckaty too, at the monastery with the bombs, so we decided to summon her instead. Ji-Woo set everything up, turning a car into a big fake black dog like what attacked me all invisible, by putting Greek writing on it. She told Ned and me to make a circle, so Ned told me to spin him around on a rope and it actually worked! The ritual bit worked too, Heckaty came right off.<br /> <br /> She were a very pretty lady in a posh dress with a tall spiky black collar thing behind her three heads. All three of them talked together too. She didn\u2019t know where the dreamer were either, but she knew somewhere we might could find out, but she had people guarding it. She were going to let us in it if we gave her Persephone, which were not on. Ned offered to go instead and wear a black dress and dye his hair blonde, but that were not on either and besides, one of Heckaty\u2019s heads made a yech face. She said she\u2019d do it too if Ji-Woo promised to make sure her pantheon did something later and if they didn\u2019t, Ji-Woo had to go with her or the same but without the going with part if she just told us where it was and didn\u2019t make the guardian go away. Or Ji-Woo could do whatever Heckaty said for a year. But the first ones would be really bad, and she didn\u2019t want to give up all her freedom or nothing, so that didn\u2019t work out. Ned tried doing a strip tease, but Heckaty didn\u2019t want a ride or nothing, even though she did like boys, so he had a go with Connie instead.<br /> <br /> I thought about trading for Ji-Woo for the second kind of the first thing, and ask Mum to help me do a favor, but then I\u2019d have had to make Mum or some of Mum\u2019s gang help, and she wouldn\u2019t say what she wanted for a favor, so that might be bad. When we asked about her just not helping the vampires, cause they wanted an even specialler dog that the one what attacked me already, she said she would if she could have Persephone for just a day. It were still not on, but Heckaty said she weren\u2019t going to kill her, or get her up the duff or nothing and Persephone were kinda ok with it? On account of finding the dreamer being proper important, yeah? Ji-Woo said that were a big deal though, so she got Heckaty to tell us where the place we could find stuff about the dreamer at.<br /> <br /> Turns out, he used the library at the explodey monastery place for summat, so there might be a clue there. Mags were right upset on account of he had wanted to go mash up the Nicolas bloke (he moves super fast, like a red blue, Ji-Woo said) any road and not make deals with Heckaty, but we probably wouldn\u2019t have looked in the library or nothing elsewise. Well, I might have, but only for books that would be fun to read, yeah?<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXIII</i><br /> <br /> Well things are getting weirder. As events get more bizarre the whole thing takes on a dreamlike quality.<br /> <br /> Next time come for the Ant Lion with a little girl voice, stay for the Castlevania Homage. See you then, Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T05:08:16-07:00","id":289447,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check on the Bohemian Front. This time they battle Vampires in an\u2026oddly familiar scenario. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXIV</i><br /> <br /> <u>Sweet Dreams (Are Made of This) Part VI</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Turkey</b><br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t had any absinthe in over a day now, and the world is starting to turn bland and gray. I mean, it\u2019s literally starting to turn gray, like the Wizard of Oz in reverse. The change was so gradual that I didn\u2019t really pick up on it until after I\u2019d finished discussing politics with Zane as we drove back to the vampire monastery. She wanted to know why the Bureaucracy wouldn\u2019t help out Hecate, since we\u2019re all on the same side against the titans. She likened the situation to gangs (the pantheons) helping each other out against the coppers (the titans). I tried to explain that the members of the Bureaucracy think they are better than everyone else and therefore don\u2019t play well with others. Andy pitched in and explained that Hecate is actually a titan. But even if she was a normal member of the Dodekatheon, I\u2019m pretty sure the Bureaucracy wouldn\u2019t cooperate with her very easily.<br /> <br /> Eventually we arrived at the monastery again. It looked like Hecate had honored our wishes and refused to help the vrykolakas. The land mines were almost all exploded, and it appeared that one of her hounds and a few vrykolakas had been caught up in the blasts. There was also a gigantic ant lion creature half buried in its pit traps. We took care of it after Magnus tore it from the ground. It looked like a normal ant lion (the insect, not the things we fought before), but it had a little girl\u2019s head, and it kept inviting us to come play in a delightfully innocent little girl\u2019s voice. When we attacked it, it started screaming, so Andy used the powers of silence to shut it up. It occurred to me that the thing\u2019s severed tongue would let someone speak like a little girl, and I made the mistake of mentioning it to Edward. He spent much of the rest of the excursion talking like a girl, or pretending like other things were talking that way, like a gas mask he acquired somewhere. Since Edward is a woman right now, it wasn\u2019t actually as weird as you might imagine.<br /> <br /> The monastery itself was spacious, and the architecture was beautiful. It seemed deserted, but we assumed that was because all the vampires were sleeping in the catacombs below, safely hidden from the daylight. We didn\u2019t have any trouble finding the library, which is what we were really after. The only problem was that the library was filled with some sort of mustard gas. Zane and I could sense traces of it as soon as we stepped into the monastery. Magnus, Edward and Zane might be able to shrug off the gas, but Andy and I couldn\u2019t, and we were the ones who needed to get into library to look for the tomes the Dreamer must have consulted.<br /> <br /> So Edward and Zane sneaked into the gas-filled library. It was a bit dangerous, but they were both too tough to succumb to the toxic gas. They searched until they found a caged, three-foot-long caterpillar-like nightmare creature that was emitting the caustic vapor from the large pores across its body. Zane smashed it into a puddle of greenish ichor, and once the source of the gas was gone we just had to wait for it to clear out. Magnus opened up the library, and I summoned some whirlwinds to clear the air. I made sure to stay well out of the way. Poison gas is awful.<br /> <br /> Once things had cleared out, Andy and I got to work while Zane and Edward played hopscotch and Magnus kept an eye out for enemies. We found a lot of occult books containing rites dedicated to Hecate. Most of the rites were intended to despoil the temples of other gods in order to give Hecate an advantage there, which really isn\u2019t playing fair. The library had tomes filled with other ancient occult knowledge too. I could have stayed there for days just reading, though I would need some absinthe and I\u2019d probably get bored and have to go out and do something more active periodically.<br /> <br /> Anyway, judging from the amount of dust on most of the books, the vrykolakas didn\u2019t use the library very often. I eventually found several tomes that weren\u2019t as dusty and seemed to have been consulted fairly recently. My divine intuition told me that those were the books the Dreamer read, so Andy and I cracked them open to see what they had to say.<br /> <br /> The books mostly referred to a hidden temple of Cybele in the Anatolian mountains. Inside the temple, there is a room where worshipers could commune with Cybele. The room is perfectly attuned to dreaming, so I\u2019m positive that\u2019s where the Dreamer\u2019s corporeal body is resting right now. Connie agreed, and I think she was eager to remove this trespasser from her matron\u2019s temple. The tomes did not show exactly where the temple is, but there were enough clues that I\u2019m pretty sure Andy and I will be able to find the place once we make our way to the region.<br /> <br /> This monochromatic world is really starting to mess with me. I wonder how long it will take for ALL the color to leach away. I asked the others if they had noticed it, but they said things looked normal to them. I guess it\u2019s just my mind playing tricks on me. I wonder if the world is really monochrome, and I just see it differently? I can\u2019t believe that\u2019s true. I remember everything being in color when I was younger, before I discovered my favorite drink. I guess I just need more absinthe. That\u2019s a hint, Yisheng. Where ARE you?<br /> <br /> Anyway, we had what we came for, so we could have left the monastery then. But we decided we should deal with the vampires first, if only to keep Nikolas and his followers from ambushing us later. They were almost certainly in the catacombs below, but the catacombs were really dark and cramped, so I was far from eager to go looking.<br /> <br /> Then Edward suggested that we use the land mines to blow up the cliff side. The monastery sat on a cliff, and the catacombs were presumably adjacent to the cliff face. If we could blow it up, it would let sunlight in, so any vampires that weren\u2019t killed in the explosion would be exposed to the light of day. Best of all, I wouldn\u2019t have to go into those tight, dark crypts. The only problem was that there weren\u2019t enough land mines left to do any real damage to the cliff face.<br /> <br /> So I suggested that I could make some explosives out of a couple of small boulders using Taiyi. Taiyi is very versatile, especially if you\u2019ve studied physics, chemistry, and engineering, which I have. Magnus and Zane found a couple of good boulders, and I spent some time brushing a complex arrangement of Chinese characters and illustrations onto them. I LOVE the fox-tail brush Daji gave me. It makes the Eight Trigram Transformation SO MUCH easier. When I was done with my brush work, we had two lumps of plastic explosives, which Zane and I broke up into smaller chunks and positioned carefully across the cliff face. Even with the amount of explosives we were using, there was no guarantee that we would be able to crack open the cliff, but Edward assured us it would work as long as he was at ground zero. He might be addled and insane, but I have a knack for telling when he\u2019s right and when he\u2019s crazy, and this time he was right. So I turned another rock into a bungee cord, which Edward tied around Magnus.<br /> <br /> When everything was ready to go, Magnus struck a power chord on his guitar and then started playing a heavy metal version of the 1812 Overture, and Edward dove off the cliff face, anchored only by the bungee cord. I soared into the air a safe distance from the explosives, and let the electricity arcing from Magnus\u2019 guitar empower my guns with the fury of a storm. Just as Edward reached the bottom of his dive and was right in the middle of the explosives, I fired, and the electricity sparking across my bullets ignited the demolitions. Edward rode the bungee cord back up the cliff mere meters ahead of the explosive chain reaction, and the cliff burst open with a fiery boom. One wing of the monastery toppled from the cliff, and the catacombs were almost completely obliterated! As the echoes of the explosion faded, the only sound was the wail of Magnus\u2019 guitar.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, we didn\u2019t get the vampires. They were lurking behind a black, magical door that remained floating in mid air above the ruins of the cliff. It was probably anchored in the catacombs\u2019 masonry before we blew everything up. The good news, though, was that the explosion cleared out all the chlorine gas that had filled the catacombs.<br /> <br /> Zane jumped through the floating doorway to have a look. It led to some sort of terra incognita that was a perfect mirror image of the monastery, only upside down. Sadly, that meant I had to go through the catacombs after all. Zane took my hand and helped give me the courage to go in. Fortunately, we didn\u2019t have to stay in the catacombs long, though. They quickly opened up into the main part of the monastery, which was much more spacious. Once we were out of the catacombs, I was able to enjoy the place. The upside-down architecture was fascinating and fun. It was so dream-like\u2014we were walking on the ceiling with everything hanging in reverse, even the candle flames! And the world in the terra incognita didn\u2019t seem as gray, which was a relief.<br /> <br /> We made a lot of noise on our way, especially when we took out a couple of vrykolakas guards, so as we emerged into the monastery\u2019s main hall, several vrykolakas crawled from darkened doorways and shadowed ledges to ambush us. They were led by Nikolas, a monstrous-looking vampire clad in Orthodox robes. He carried a staff that burned with an unholy bluish light. There was also a huge, creepy-looking porcelain mask that cried tears of blood and screamed with a piercing cry that threatened to shatter my soul. It was awful, so I opened up on it while the others started taking out the vrykolakas. Unfortunately, the mask was really fast, so I missed with my first couple of shots. And then when I DID hit it, my bullets just glanced off its blood-streaked cheeks. Zane had things well in hand, though. Her punches easily cracked the thing\u2019s face, and before long, she brought it down, but not before it unleashed a final scream that nearly destroyed us all. As it was, every time the mask screamed, she broke more of the monastery\u2019s windows, which let the nighttime storm raging outside lash us with bolts of fierce lightning. I managed to avoid the worst of it, but not all the vrykolakas we so lucky.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Nikolas awakened several of the stone angel statues scatter throughout the hall, and they launched themselves in the air and fired arrows at us. Zane was hit and began to turn to stone, but she was able to shrug off the worst of it, and Andy helped her destroy the mask with his magic. Edward tore through the vampires, and Magnus smashed the angels. He even tore the chandelier out of the floor (ceiling?) and used it to crush our enemies!<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I turned my attention to Nikolas. He was awakening angels and blasting Zane with searing blue flame, and that had to stop. So I jumped around the room, looking for the best angles to fire. I unleashed a torrent of starfire bullets on him. He was fast, and he tried to flicker away from my shots, but I was faster. He didn\u2019t survive long. Unfortunately, his power must have been maintaining the terra incognita, though, because as soon as he shrieked his last breath and burst into blue flames, the whole mirror monastery started to break apart and collapse. The ceiling cracked and chunks of ancient masonry fell upward toward the floor.<br /> <br /> We fled, jumping from one piece of falling debris to the next until we entered the catacombs. The whole subterranean crypt was falling in on itself, and it threatened to crush us before we could make it out. To make matters worse, a massive serpent had crawled out of some hole somewhere (or maybe just appeared, like in a dream) and was blocking the exit. I mean, WTF? I wasn\u2019t interested in tangling with the beast, so I dodged past it. Then Magnus slammed into it like a bulldozer and pushed it right through the door to the real world. The snake fell a long way down the cliff, and everyone else jumped clear onto solid ground.<br /> <br /> Well, that was exciting, don\u2019t you think, Yisheng? Make sure it sounds exciting when you tell your friends how awesome your boss is, okay? You do have friends, right? I mean, aside from me?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> Politics is proper confusing and so is Greek explodey monastery libraries. Especially when they\u2019re full of garlic-y mustard gas from a caterpillar. But Ji-Woo helped me out and Xanthdy did too, with the politics things. I were trying to figure it out, yeah, about why Ji-Woo\u2019s pantheon wouldn\u2019t like her doing a favor for Hecakty so\u2019s she would do a favor for us, tit and tat and all. I was thinking, if the pantheons was like gangs, then the Titans\u2019d be like coppers and since the dreamer bloke was like a snitch or summat, working for the plods, the gangs might do favors to deal with it, even if they didn\u2019t like each other much.<br /> <br /> But Ji-Woo said Heckaty were actually a Titan, so that make sense. And made me feel icky about thinking she were pretty. Coppers is even more dangerous if you think they\u2019re pretty, even if Xanthdy did go on talking cobblers about lady cops and spankings. But most of what Xanthdy said made sense. Ji-Woo were talking about her da\u2019s gang specifically, cause they don\u2019t like anybody else\u2019s gang, like the Frenchies don\u2019t. I mean, like them what\u2019s in Londontown. Not like you and Mum and the littles. Any road, she said they\u2019d be upset even if Heckaty weren\u2019t a Titan, on account of them having sticks up their bums. Like popsicles! So we stopped for ice cream.<br /> <br /> There was lots of different kinds of ice cream at the place Connie threw a hydrant in the window of. Ned had a pushup thing and Mags got himself a whole Mags-sized bucket of ice cream and were pouring whisky into it, like a float. I had chocolate, on account of it being my favorite. I mixed it with whisky too and made one for Ji-Woo. She were cross and sad, seeing as Yisheng weren\u2019t here yet with her absinthe. She were all out, and so things were looking all gray. Later I gave her a cup of pretend absinthe, what said absinthe on the side, that I made all proper, just with water from my canteen instead of real absinthe. It helped her a little, cause she was all worn out from making explosives and I gave her some of my power for a bit with it, but I guess things were still gray.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Ned\u2019s a girl now. Mags thought maybe it were like being sick and she caught it from me. But it were cause Connie bit her too much, I think. Maybe had a bit of a nosh, like the other maenad bint wanted to. She didn\u2019t look proper hurt though. It\u2019s alright though, she\u2019s still Ned and not at all right in the head - she threw a rock at the antlion with the girl little\u2019s head like it were a grenade, but it didn\u2019t blow up. Mags and Ji-Woo did for it though, after Xanthdy made the little\u2019s head stop carrying on. Mags ripped the whole big thing out of the ground and then pulled the girl head off and crushed the antlion brain after Ji-Woo shot it up a bunch. It bit Mags a little, but he\u2019s well hard, so he were alright.<br /> <br /> Then, on account of Ned liking tongues and Ji-Woo going barmy for a bit, Ji-Woo told her that the girl little\u2019s tongue would make her sound like she were a little, if she put it in her mouth, unless someone were listening with magic, then she\u2019d sound like a stonking antlion thing. Then when we found the little caterpillar gasmask, she put the mask on her hand and made it talk like a little. She gave it back though, the mask, on account of it kept cursing at her. Plus, people kept threatening to bite her hand off. Not just Connie either, Mags did too! Xanthdy looked like a girl little for a bit, but he stopped when Ned made it not cool no more.<br /> <br /> But that were after we got to the explodey monastery, and we had to get the motorhome past the hole the antlion\u2019d dug. So I picked it up and jumped, whoosh! right over it. Ji-Woo helped some, but said I were real strong. Cause I am. Ned kept trying to make a bridge, but she came across after a bit cause it kept not working.<br /> <br /> At the monastery, there were lots of blown up land mine things and bits of bloke and some dog bits too. So Heckaty did do like Ji-Woo said, and sent one of her dogs after the vrykolakas what were putting out bombs before. Inside, there were a pet antlion in a cage and it smelled like swimming pools and garlic. The whole place, not the antlion. Ji-Woo said it were chlorine and mustard gas, so Ned held her breath, even though mustard gas don\u2019t care about being breathed. Ji-Woo said so. It weren\u2019t that bad - the library were full of it and I didn\u2019t get dicky at all. Ji-Woo isn\u2019t so tough as me though, so me and Ned went first to find the caterpillar what were making the gas. Usually caterpillars don\u2019t make mustard gas, or icky green spit up stuff, but this one did, so I squished it. I had to ding to get clean and all and Ji-Woo used her whirlwindy stuff to get rid of all the gas left.<br /> <br /> I played hopscotch with Ned for a bit, but then he got distracted by the girl little gas mask, so I looked for books to read. I didn\u2019t find any, since all the signs and most of the books weren\u2019t in English or French or German. Ji-Woo found some for me later though. First, she had to find stuff about the dreamer with Xanthdy. They found a bunch of books with no dust what were talking about a secrety temple of Sybil up in the mountains, with a special dreaming room. So we are going to go there now, cause Ji-Woo can follow the clues, but we wanted to bust the vrykolakas up first, so they wouldn\u2019t follow or nothing.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why Ji-Woo made bunches of explody stuff and a stretchy bouncing cord. We was trying to make it so we opened up the catacombs bits where the vrykolakas was hiding, and let the sun in some, so Ji-Woo and Xanthdy got the explodey stuff set up perfect, and Ned and Mags went to the top of the cliff. He started playing proper exciting music, with the bouncy cord in his teeth. Ned held onto the cord and jumped right in between the explosions that Ji-Woo made by shooting the bomb stuff with lightning bullets. It were bloody brill! The lightning part came from Mags\u2019s guitar and everything!<br /> <br /> But the vrykolakas were tricky buggers and had a special upside down monastery what didn\u2019t get blowed up! Instead, there were a floating door left. I snuck in all invisible and figured out it weren\u2019t all catacombs and it were night and stormy on the other side, so we all went in to bust up the vrykolakas, seeing as they was awake and all. Ji-Woo weren\u2019t too happy about it, on account of the catacombs being all close and tight in (even though they\u2019re an ace place to sleep if no one finds you), so I held her hand until we got to the big part and got to sneak up on the vrykolakas guards. We got those two right off, then Mags put his axe down so we could get to the main room with the chandelier, seeing as the door were way up high on account of the ceiling being like the floor cause we was all upside down.<br /> <br /> We made lots of noise getting the guards though, so then we were fighting loads of wankers. Nicolas were all dressed up like a priest, like Ji-Woo said, and there were a whole bunch of vrykolakas and a giant face like a posh doll\u2019s, but crying blood. She kept shrieking, and first it woke the angel statues up, but then Mags smashed all the angels, so her shrieking just busted windows up, letting the lightning in. That were good for us though, seeing as the lightning killed one of the vrykolakas buggers. I did for the doll face almost by myself, cause it had to be punched and I\u2019m the best ever at punching. She tried to confuse me and almost got me, but I focussed real hard and wound up smacking my head into the wall, and I weren\u2019t confused. I\u2019d almost did for it, breaking off sharp pieces so that the heart underneath it were showing, when it started screaming loud enough to hurt. Mags made everything go quiet though, and then she shattered to bits.<br /> <br /> The other wankers didn\u2019t like me busting the face up, so one of the angels shot me before Mags broke it and made me start going stiff. Mags had the horn from before though, so I\u2019m getting better. Nicolas shot me too, with blue fire instead of a stone arrow, and I got a little singed, but just a little. I dodged after that! Ji-Woo did for him but good, and looked proper ace doing it, standing in front of the window when it shattered, and all the colored glass went flying everywhere around her. After that, the whole place started to fall down! Well, up really, on account of the place being upside down, yeah? Ji-Woo grabbed my not-stone hand and pulled me out, almost right into a giant snake what were trying to get out too. Mags charged it like he were a knight or summat, and his axe were a lance thing and we pushed all the way out before everything fell up on us.<br /> <br /> Mags got a right ace thing from the doll face, an eyeball-looking thing, shaped like a heart, all over with blood. It makes his sound powers even more good at breaking things and he can put the blood under his eyes and look well metal. Ji-Woo grabbed Nicolas\u2019s stick, the one what had blue fire on top before, and gave it to Xanthdy, on account of him being a mage. For once, our car didn\u2019t get broked, so now we\u2019ve got right off to the mountains to look for the temple for Sybil where the dreamer is.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXIV</i><br /> <br /> Obviously, the monastery took some inspiration from <i>Castlevania: Symphony of the Night</i>.<br /> <br /> So we entered this story with some discussion about how turning into a Maenad affects a PC. Obviously most Maenads can\u2019t turn a Demigod but Constancia can, and that was decided as a facet of the adventure back when I was planning for Phaedra and Rajani as well as Ji-Woo to be part of the posse. Edmond\u2019s player and I discussed if, given Dionysus, Edmond may be able to be turned, becoming a female while under the effects of it. So we ran with that. Edmond will no doubt be back to his old self again after the story but may\u2026relapse\u2026at times, if the player is interested in that happening.<br /> <br /> Next session will probably be the last of the story, unless we just get really bogged down. Also will bump us up to Legend 6, so all new powers and such after. See you then, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T02:31:31-08:00","id":303136,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to cover (most of) the end of the story, we ran over so had to put off the d\u00e9nouement, but this covers the climax. Enjoy.<br /> <i><br /> Session XXXV</i><br /> <br /> <u>Sweet Dreams (Are Made of This) Part VII</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Turkey</b><br /> <br /> As we drove deeper into the Anatolian mountains, following the clues that would lead us to Cybele\u2019s hidden temple, I couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that we were missing something, and my feelings are usually right. So I kept my eyes open for more omens, but this time, I was the only one who DIDN\u2019T see the omen. Well, I don\u2019t think Magnus, Andy or Persephone did either, but Zane, Connie and Edward saw the talking frogs from my play vision!<br /> <br /> Before that happened, though, we almost ran over Persephone. Fortunately, Edward stopped in time, and we picked her up. Hecate had released her, and I gather nothing terrible happened to her. She says that she was able to distract Persephone with her feminine charms. So that\u2019s good.<br /> <br /> No long after that, we ran across a fallen bridge. The chasm it was supposed to span wasn\u2019t too wide, so Magnus and Zane were able to carry the RV safely across. But first we had to defeat a gigantic frog beast. Edward tried to talk it into jumping the RV across the chasm for us, which was completely idiotic. I was grumpy because I still haven\u2019t had any absinthe going on two days now, and when the frog attacked the RV, I punched Edward in the arm out of frustration. Not hard, mind you, and I couldn\u2019t hurt Edward with a punch even if I tried. Anyway, we attacked the frog beast after that. I stayed as far away as possible, but Zane, Edward, Connie and Magnus attacked up close, so they got a dose of the frog\u2019s psychotropic slime. That\u2019s when they saw all the rocks around us turn into smaller frogs that told them Cybele\u2019s temple could only be seen in the light of the moon. That was the missing piece and the final element of my prophecy! Yay!<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Yisheng, you should know that being a maenad is a wild ride. The ecstasy of madness is extremely enticing, if only because of the prophetic insight that comes with the insanity. It was like the floodgates of rational thought were blown open and a river of insight swept through me. Still, I didn\u2019t like the way I lost my mind. Sure, it was liberating, but also terrifying, and I\u2019m not sure I liked myself as a maenad. It was all sex and alcohol and prophecy and violence!<br /> <br /> Actually, now that I put it that way, it sounds like being a maenad is kinda like being me normally, only turned up to eleven. Except for the violence part. I\u2019m not really bloodthirsty. I do shoot things a lot these days, though. Anyway, I\u2019m glad I\u2019m not a maenad anymore. It\u2019s just too much.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t let Connie turn me into a maenad until we found Cybele\u2019s temple though. We waited until night and then Andy and I were able to zero in on its likely location. The moon shone through a break in the mountains and illuminated the ghostly temple. It was quite beautiful, and I would have liked to paint it, but we didn\u2019t have time for that. Maybe later.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Andy, he is being very noble toward Persephone. He totally wants her, and she\u2019s totally into him. But he shut his desires behind walls of chivalry and acted the perfect gentleman. It was admirable, really. Andy is so much more impressive when he\u2019s playing the wise trickster or the noble Unseelie Knight than we he\u2019s up to his usual cartoonish antics.<br /> <br /> Once we were in the temple, we pinpointed the dreaming room, but it was sealed behind a stone wall. A little thing like that wasn\u2019t going to slow Magnus down, but we decided to wait until daytime so that if there were any nightmare beasts lying in wait for us, they would be weaker. In the meantime, Connie dragged me off to another room and bit me. That\u2019s when I turned into a maenad. It was ecstatic, and Connie and I spent the rest of the night having wild sex. I\u2019m sure Pipa will understand.<br /> <br /> It was at the height of all that sex that I had the most intense prophecy I\u2019ve ever had. I gotta tell you, Yisheng, orgasmic prophecy is something you should absolutely experience. It was fucking amazing! Literally! Hmmm. I guess that was TMI, huh?<br /> <br /> And the prophecy was . . . eye-opening. Life-changing, in a way. It was . . .but no. I shouldn\u2019t say anything else about it. Not for now, anyway. For the time being, it\u2019s just for me. Maybe someday I\u2019ll share it with you, Yisheng, but not yet. Besides, it might not go over well with the Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> So when morning arrived, we all got together and prepared to fight the dreamer. Being a maenad, I was a still a bit frisky, so I think I said some things to Zane that I probably shouldn\u2019t have, not while she\u2019s in her innocent girl aspect. If she had been the rakish young man, though, I might have gotten even friskier, which would have been really embarrassing, so I\u2019m glad that didn\u2019t happen. As it was, Zane wasn\u2019t happy about us being separated for this fight. She looks out for me, and didn\u2019t like the idea that she wouldn\u2019t be there to protect me. But I had Edward with me, so I assured her I would be okay.<br /> <br /> Anyway, once everyone was ready, Connie drank Dionysus\u2019 elixir and a sort of wine-colored aura surrounded her, then she stepped into the aura-portal and disappeared. Edward and I joined hands and jumped through the portal after her just as Magnus raised his axe to smash through the wall separating him from the Dreamer\u2019s corporeal form.<br /> <br /> And then I was floating in a psychedelic dream world where everything was spinning colors and boundless possibility. The monochrome grays of my absinthe-dry world were replaced with colors I\u2019ve only imagined, and that was when I realized the world had been filled with color again ever since Connie turned me into a maenad. I could have pulled every picture I\u2019ve ever painted and every sculpture I have yet to sculpt from the polychromatic void, and there would still be more to explore. That\u2019s why I like sleeping so much\u2014my dreams are like a transcendent canvas upon which my art is born. Apparently the same is true of the dreamer, though he looked surprisingly . . . banal. He was just a man dressed in a tailored suit standing impassively in the color-filled void, and the only remarkable thing about him was his glowing red eyes. At first, his seemed omnipotent, but as the others attacked his body in the real world, his control over the dream realm wavered. Of course, he wasn\u2019t alone. He was surrounded by creatures of the Dreamlands: ghasts and nightgaunts. Edward, who was also a maenad, of course, shrieked and started swatting nightgaunts and ghasts with his hammer. He made pretty short work of them. Connie jumped on the dreamer and took a big bite our of him, but then he focused his power on her and hurled her far, far away into the shifting void, and it took her awhile to run back to us.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I flitted around the dreamer, blasting him with starfire shots. I was in tune with the dream realm, and in a potent moment of insightful clarity, I realized that the entire realm was illusion, and all points were the same. After that, my shots couldn\u2019t miss and bullets that I\u2019d already fired struck him multiple times because he was always in their path. I even drew the colors of the realm into my guns and unleashed their wrath upon the dreamer, staggering him.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s when he summoned the gugs, massive, shaggy giants with arms that split into multiple forelimbs. The gugs grabbed Edward and he couldn\u2019t escape, so I diverted my attacks from the Dreamer to help him out. Then the gugs came after me! They were surprisingly quick, and I only narrowly escaped their clutches.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s when Connie returned and jumped on the Dreamer from behind. She bit into his neck and tore out his throat, and with a tortured, gurgling scream he imploded! The center of the dream realm became a black hole, pulling us all in toward oblivion. I didn\u2019t have the strength to resist, and for a moment I thought I was lost, but then Edward came to my rescue. He grabbed me and pulled me through Connie\u2019s portal just in time. He always comes through in a pinch.<br /> <br /> We fell back into the real world, and the others were standing around the Dreamer\u2019s corpse and the carcasses of several nightmare beasts. The dreaming room was cavernous, and the fight there must have been epic. Magnus took care of the nightmare beasts, and Zane beat the Dreamer to a bloody pulp despite being partially turned to stone by a cockatrice\u2019s breath. I always knew Zane was a badass, but I\u2019m still impressed!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m just glad we all came through it in one piece. Now I REALLY need to go find some absinthe. Or, you know, my loyal secretary could show up with the stuff I ordered DAYS ago. It\u2019s okay Yisheng. I don\u2019t really blame you. We both know it\u2019s the Bureaucracy\u2019s fault. Uh oh. I can sense you frowning at me. But I\u2019m right, aren\u2019t I?<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> It were totally not fair, Da, Ji-Woo wouldn\u2019t let me drive, even when it got dark, on account of I\u2019m too little and I don\u2019t got a license. There weren\u2019t even any baddies for a long time, cause we was mostly just driving through places we\u2019d been on the way to the Antalion Mountains. And it didn\u2019t make sense, cause Ji-Woo didn\u2019t have a license neither and I\u2019ve driven when I was loads littler. I mean, it didn\u2019t wind up mattering, on account of Ji-Woo convinced Ned to turn on the lights, so it weren\u2019t a problem that she couldn\u2019t see in the dark like me, but even Ned doesn\u2019t have a license and she\u2019s good at driving! She did pull summat out of her all over diamonds purse what I though said something about Clyve, but then it said something about her being able to drive, but only MANNISHLY. All big letters like that too. I think Xanthdy did it.<br /> <br /> Any road, we found Persephone again right after it got dark and all. She were in the middle of the road, so Ned slammed on the brakes, even though we was blocks and blocks away. She were alright and everything - Heckaty wanted to look at her heart for summat, but Persephone distracted her. Probably with sex, on account of her being a maenad. It makes you proper dirty and all.<br /> <br /> It turns out Ned\u2019s not very good at listening, specially when she\u2019s talking about how good she is at listening. Ji-Woo had to poke her a bunch to make her go to the right part of the Antalion Mountains. And then there were the frog. See, there were a bridge what were broken, on account of a house-sized frog with long sharp teeth and a beaver tail were chewing on it. Ned did listen when Ji-Woo said not to try and make the motorhome jump over the hole by itself. But then she got it in her head that we ought get the frog to carry the motorhome on its back, yeah?<br /> <br /> The frog just wanted to eat the motorhome though, so Mags chopped its tongue off and Ji-Woo punched Ned. She kept trying to talk at it, Ned did, mostly talking gibberish and sometimes hitting it with her hammer and then biting it some, which don\u2019t sound like a good way of talking to me. I gave it a good one in the eye anyway, but I weren\u2019t trying to talk at it. I didn\u2019t bother to knock it off balance or nothing, on account of it being stonking huge. I just got in the one good thump, seeing as it were right slimy and I almost falled off, but Mags and Ji-Woo mashed it up proper. Ji-Woo knocked a whole bunch of rocks onto it, and finished taking the eye out I punched. Mags busted its teeth up and cut its tail off, chop!, all yelling in some other language.<br /> <br /> That made things even more confusing cause I was already hearing the frog faces on all the rocks, and the moon, and the leaves, and the shadows talking some cobblers about only seeing Sybil\u2019s temple in the moonlight, and making that silly sound like in the play, brekekekex koax koax. They were talking Greek, so I just understood them cause of some kind superpower or summat, or maybe cause I were high from touching frog slime. But it were just like in Ji-Woo\u2019s play, so she started feeling better, even though she were still grumpy, on account of not having any absinthe still.<br /> <br /> After the dead frog put on a hat and danced off the cliff, and Mags broke the moon on account of Ned trying to pick it up, me and him picked up the motorhome and jumped it over that way. Ji-Woo and Xanthdy found the best place to look for the temple, Ji-Woo looking up at the moon and Xanthdy watching the road. It were a big stonking thing, all made of stone, with lots of statues of a lady with lots of tits. Not like, big ones or nothing, just like 20 of them. Sybil is right strange.<br /> <br /> It were still nighttime, which were good, seeing as we needed moonlight and all. But once we got inside and everything, we decided to wait until it were daytime again, so\u2019s any guards the Dreamer bloke had wouldn\u2019t be so hard to hit and all. So Connie and Ji-Woo got a room and had a bite-y kinda shag, what turned Ji-Woo into a maenad. I tried to read the book Ji-Woo found for me, but the ones in any proper language were a \u2018Janet and John\u2019 kinda thing. The others had right pretty pictures though, all posh like a fancy bible, and then Ned started making up stories for them, doing all sorts of different voices and everything. It were nice and relaxing, yeah, as much as it could be.<br /> <br /> It were frustrating for Mags though. See, first Persephone were being all flirty with Xanthdy, looking for a bang, but Xanthdy were being well dense, on account of him protecting her, which seems right backwards, but then he told Mags a story about some bloke he knew what had been protecting some bird and then she got killed while they were having a go. So I guess it makes sense, yeah? Then Ji-Woo came back and were acting like a proper slag, growling and carrying on, saying she wanted to bite me and blowing me a kiss. If I\u2019d been all growed up again, I might have forgot Andy\u2019s story for at least a little bit, but mostly it just made me feel proper queer. I did give her a hug, to boost her up, before she went into the glowy yellow Connie shaped portal thing.<br /> <br /> So Mags went all yell-y about the sexual tension or some cobblers, and he busted down the wall but good. Inside the room Connie showed us were one of them cockatrice wankers, a lion thing with bat wings, a scorpion tail and a human head, and some toff in a suit, lying down sleeping.<br /> <br /> I knocked the others off balance as soon as I could, but mostly left them and the big shadowy dogs like we saw in China what showed up later for Mags. They were well hard wankers, but Mags busted them up good, even if the cockatrice made him shatter like ice. He wound up pulling that bugger\u2019s head clean off, with his hands, and threw it at the lion thing.<br /> <br /> I got beat up a lot by the lion thing\u2019s quills it shot from the scorpion tail. It didn\u2019t help that the Dreamer could knock people off balance like me. Also, the wanker kept shooting me! It were right strange too, on account of whenever he did, it felt like I was almost getting pulled somewhere. It were good I didn\u2019t though - I had to keep the Dreamer distracted, cause Persephone said if we didn\u2019t distract the Dreamer in the proper world, he could kill Ji-Woo, and Ned, and Connie, just by thinking about it. So I made sure to keep at him, even if I had to start disappearing in between punches so the black dogs didn\u2019t hurt me none. Xanthdy helped too. After he gave me his hat, I managed to knock the dreamer clear across the room. Plus, he called the cockatrice a chicken.<br /> <br /> Mags told me not to tell Ji-Woo this next part, but that were cause he wanted me to try and shag her, so it\u2019s alright if I tell you. I thought I were done for, not for good or nothing, the bastards never shot me somewhere serious, but he were a curb away from stomping the shit out of me. I figured I\u2019d get in one more good hit, and Mags\u2019d finish him off, but then Mags grabbed a hold of his gun and then held him still for me. Then, him and me, we taught him a proper lesson. After I\u2019d broked a few of his teeth, he turned into another hole portal kinda thing and started to suck us in! I managed to hold tight, barely, and Mags grabbed hold of Xanthdy.<br /> <br /> Just after, Ji-Woo and Ned and Connie came back! Ned had a stonking big arm in one hand and were pulling Ji-Woo out with the other. Connie had to push her over so\u2019s she could get out too. They was all ok, though Ned said he got pulled apart by the giant what used to have that arm. She were ok now though. Ji-Woo really looked like she were gonna bite me, but she didn\u2019t. That were probably good. She would have felt right awful after, when she\u2019s not a maenad no more. I think she can be not a maenad. If she wants. Persephone started making out with Xanthdy though, and Ned with Connie. I was too tired to even think about being all growed up. That might have made the bite-y thing different. But I were just glad I didn\u2019t pass out or nothing, and that Ji-Woo weren\u2019t hurt. Fights aren\u2019t as much fun without Ji-Woo, and Ned.<br /> <i><br /> End Session XXXV</i><br /> <br /> Went pretty well given we split the party. The earth group fought the usual monsters (minus Vrykolokas, since they took care of them earlier), but I threw Nightgaunts, Gugs, and Ghasts at the dream group, just because it seemed the thing to do at the time. The Dream group automatically resisted somewhere between ten and twelve mental effects as they are Maenads.<br /> <br /> But that is enough madness for now. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T17:40:15-08:00","id":317817,"title":"","content":"Started a new Scion story, let\u2019s look in on our group. Please note, the whole Dark Woods thing was written by the players so not actual play, but of course relevant to game events.<br /> <br /> <i>Episode XXXVI</i><br /> <br /> <i>Six Underground Part I</i><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo's Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Berlin</b><br /> <br /> Dear Yisheng, I\u2019m writing to thank you again for delivering my absinthe. The way you ran in right after we finished defeating the Dreamer, bearing the bottle of absinthe as though it were the Holy Grail, was truly heroic. I must admit, though, that I\u2019m glad that you at least waited until after Cybele showed up to thank us and turn me back into my normal self. Somehow I don\u2019t think being a maenad would go over well with the Bureaucracy. Anyway, you can report to the Ministry of Wine and Spirits that the absinthe of Tian is absolutely exquisite. It restored all the color to my world and opened my mind once again to the beauty of life. I hope you\u2019ve made god progress on submitting the paperwork commending yourself for a job well done, but I\u2019m also glad you were able to sit quietly with me for awhile in Cybele\u2019s temple as you enjoyed a glass of absinthe and rested a bit before heading back to Tian. You need a break from time to time too. In fact, if you haven\u2019t taken a week off yet, you should get on it ASAP! I\u2019m serious. Get on that.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I\u2019m bored and frustrated and restless. Normally, I\u2019d run off to Amsterdam or Ibiza or something, but I don\u2019t really feel like going anywhere else right now. I\u2019m also not feeling very creative. I think it\u2019s because Pipa\u2019s been gone for awhile on some task for Daji. I miss her. It\u2019s weird, though, because I\u2019ve never really MISSED anyone like THIS before. I mean, I\u2019ve never been that attached to anyone except for my father, and I do miss him. But that\u2019s different, and I don\u2019t know how to deal with this. Sure, Hermione and Aoide and Zane and Edward are around, and I can easily distract myself by hanging out with them, but it\u2019s not the same without Pipa. She\u2019s up to something with Daji, and I\u2019m sure it\u2019s important, so I don\u2019t want to bother her. But I hate feeling like this. It\u2019s frustrating and a little scary.<br /> <br /> I have to do something to occupy myself until Pipa comes back. I think I\u2019ll see if Zane wants to go explore the Black Forest through the portal in the dragon cave, the one Ulfa used to escape so long ago. We won\u2019t go in deep; just enough to have a look around for an afternoon and then come right back. Maybe the mystical wonder of the place will brighten my spirits! But first, I have to see if it\u2019s auspicious or not!<br /> <br /> <b>Dun (Retreat) transforming into Guan (Contemplating)</b><br /> <br /> Well, that\u2019s not good. The Yi Jing advises retreat. I should withdraw from the situation, which seems to mean that it is definitely NOT auspicious to go into the Black Forest. I should remain at home, which won\u2019t resolve my current frustrations, but will at least teach me something. That\u2019s just great.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Fuck the Yi Jing. I can\u2019t hang around Berlin anymore. I\u2019m getting Zane and we\u2019re going to the Black Forest, auspicious or not.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I should have listened to the Yi Jing. Now Zane and I are lost. It\u2019s not all bad, though. The Black Forest is amazing, and I\u2019m rationing my absinthe. Everything is . . . epic. It\u2019s like a fairy tale forest, beautiful and terrifying all at once. I\u2019ve been sketching plenty of references for later. Honestly, even though we\u2019re hopelessly lost, this journey has undammed the river of my creativity, and I can\u2019t wait to get back to my flat and start painting.<br /> <br /> Getting back to the flat is turning out to be the problem, though. Yisheng, can you send help? Preferably more quickly than last time, with the absinthe delivery? Thanks!<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Yisheng, we\u2019re still lost, and I haven\u2019t heard from you. We could really use a guide or something, because this forest twists even MY mystical insight. On the other hand, Zane and I managed to outsmart a witch with nothing but our wits, and then Zane outsmarted a big bad wolf with nothing but her fists. So at least being lost has been entertaining. I\u2019m running out of absinthe though. So please hurry.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I just remembered, it\u2019s your week off isn\u2019t it, Yisheng? I guess that explains why you haven\u2019t sent help yet. Oh well. I brought my pipa, so I guess I\u2019ll use it to summon Pipa. She\u2019s been around for centuries, so surely she knows how to navigate this forest.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Pipa doesn\u2019t know the way out of the forest, so now she\u2019s lost too. She was very cross with me for awhile, but she\u2019s over it now. And at least she\u2019s here! That makes everything better.<br /> <br /> Since Pipa joined us, we met a gorgeous nixie who was delightful except that she drank the last of my absinthe. And then we saved a fellow traveler from a hideous, mangy, leonine creature that spoke with the voices of its past victims and could shapechange into pleasing forms to catch its prey off guard. I could tell instantly that it was wearing a different shape, though. Still, that was probably the scariest part of the excursion. Unfortunately, the traveler we saved turned out to be a bandit. He tried to rob us and kidnap me, so Zane beat him up and Pipa ate him. It really is like we\u2019re wandering around a Grimm\u2019s fairy tale!<br /> <br /> At last! I\u2019m finally home. All I had to do was retrace our steps through the forest. It wasn\u2019t easy, and I wouldn\u2019t have known what to look for, or even how to look, if Manannan mac Lir hadn\u2019t shown up to help us out. He was charming as always. He asked after Andy, of course, and made sure I still had the absinthe spoon he gave me (it\u2019s one of my priced relics). He also brought a fresh bottle of absinthe, which made the remainder of the trip flow much more smoothly. Honestly, the green fairy really helps open my senses when I need to see beyond what\u2019s in front of my face!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I followed the signs and they led me back to the portal, and then Zane, Pipa and I were back in Berlin! We were gone almost a week, which is way too long to be wandering lost in a forest. But I learned a lot from the experience, including how to survive in such dangerous environments. Looks like the Yi Jing was right about that, at least, even if I didn\u2019t exactly obey its advice.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Pipa\u2019s back in town, so I\u2019m going clubbing.<br /> <br /> Oh, Yisheng, you can ignore all of those requests for help in the Black Forest. Just toss them out if you haven\u2019t already.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ireland - Gou (Temptation) maintaining</b><br /> <br /> Well, the Yi Jing indicates that our current situation is defined by temptation. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s addressing any specific action, but I think it\u2019s making a statement about the theme of our current endeavor. And it seems like it\u2019s a desire for power: mystical, political, and romantic. I hope our patrons in the Unseelie Court really do mean well.<br /> <br /> I should clarify what\u2019s going on though. Andy asked us to join him on a trip to Ireland to meet the Queen of Air and Darkness. She and the Unseelie Court need someone to pull off a heist, and felt that their noble knight, Andy, would be the perfect person for the job, and of course they\u2019re right. Unfortunately, Magnus was asleep and no one wanted to wake him since he\u2019s been in a mood lately, so the rest of us\u2014Edward, Zane, Pipa and me\u2014flew to Ireland on Edward\u2019s plane. It\u2019s the same plane he used to fly us to Greece, but it\u2019s been customized a bit since then. It\u2019s very odd, but perfectly Edward. There\u2019s also a charming nymph flight attendant who seems perfectly capable of handling her employer\u2019s quirky personality.<br /> <br /> Once we arrived in Ireland, Andy led us into the hills to a faerie mound, and we descended into the Dark Court\u2019s subterranean realm. I was anxious about it despite Andy\u2019s assurances that his status among the Unseelie would shelter us from any malicious attempts trick us into some bargain that would leave us trapped in the realm for centuries. After all, the whole realm was underground, and I HATE being underground. But Pipa and Zane were with me, and besides, it turns out I had nothing to worry about. The place was so vast and spacious that it wasn\u2019t like being underground at all. It was like wandering through a realm of eternal twilight. The darkness was lit by the soft blue and purple glow of luminescent plants, and a spooky yet gentle mist coiled around our legs as we walked through a forest of twisting gray trees. In the shadows between the trees, glowing eyes peered hungrily at us. It would have been scary if my friends hadn\u2019t been there, but I knew they would protect me. And besides, the beasties in those woods would never get a chance to eat me because Pipa would eat them first.<br /> <br /> Anyway, eventually a couple of dour Unseelie knights on skeletal steeds came to greet us, and after Andy made courtly introductions, the knights summoned some more skeletal steeds from the bones of the earth, and we all rode off to the Queen\u2019s castle. I\u2019d never ridden a horse before, and didn\u2019t really know how, so I rode with Pipa. Zane chose not to ride. She ran alongside us and kept pace perfectly well. I\u2019m pretty sure the Unseelie knights were impressed, but they were determined to snub all of us but Andy, so they didn\u2019t let it show.<br /> <br /> The Unseelie palace took my breath away! It was a towering cathedral of interwoven gray trees, their branches entwined to form intricate embellishments, majestic windows, and tall, slender doors. The architecture was stunning, and I couldn\u2019t help staring at it as we passed through the entry hall and entered the throne room, where the Queen of Air and Darkness sat upon her ebony throne.<br /> <br /> She was just as majestic as the architecture, and she was attended by a dashing dark fae lord named Yrtalion. He seemed to be an advisor. After more polite introductions, the Queen wasted no time telling us what she needed us to do. To summarize, there is a powerful relic, a Black Cauldron that can summon an army of the dead. If the bodies of fallen warriors are placed inside it, it will produce an elixir that ghosts can drink to become powerful soldiers. The Deathlords of Helheim recently acquired the Cauldron from Crom Cruach, and they are searching for two other relics, both of which are required to make the Cauldron work. One is a magical stirring ladle, but no one knows where it is. And no one knows WHAT the third relic is, but we aren\u2019t the only ones looking for it. The Queen believes it\u2019s dangerous to leave the Cauldron in the hands of the Deathlords. They aren\u2019t exactly good guys, after all, and while the Unseelie aren\u2019t really good guys either, at least they aren\u2019t in league with the titans.<br /> <br /> The Unseelie Court has not informed Hel or the Aesir of the Cauldron\u2019s location because they don\u2019t want Hel taking an interest. So part of our challenge will be retrieving the Cauldron without tipping off Hel. Fortunately, Hel is a bit distracted right now. She has captured a scion of Baldur and is trying to woo her, but the scion is very clever and has some mystical help from her father, so she\u2019s managed to put off Hel\u2019s advances so far. Good thing too. I hate it when the gods get all pushy! Also, Loki gave Hel a torque that is supposedly a powerful relic, but he didn\u2019t tell her, or anyone else for that matter, what it does. This has also caused a great deal of concern among the Aesir, so it can serve as a nice smokescreen for our heist too. Of course, we have to be really careful not to implicate the Unseelie Court in anything we do. They have a rocky past with the Aesir, but right now there\u2019s a bit of a detente, and it would be better for everyone if things didn\u2019t erupt into open hostility between the two again.<br /> <br /> So, we just have to get into Helheim, find the Deathlords\u2019 realm, and steal the Cauldron. The catch is that the Deathlords' realm is bitterly cold, so cold, in fact, that it drains the very life from one\u2019s soul. Even Magnus couldn\u2019t survive there for long, and the fact that he and I are both immune to mundane cold won\u2019t protect us. However, Hel has a relic called the Dark Key that guards against the soul-draining effects of the Deathlord\u2019s realm. So we have to get the key . . . or make a copy.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s the exciting part! Lord Yrtalion is a master of shadow magics, and he knows some deep, dark mystical secrets that will allow me to use my Taiyi to create a copy of the relic from my own shadow. Isn\u2019t that fascinating? I can\u2019t wait to try it, though I have to admit I\u2019m a little nervous. I\u2019ll have to tear away my own shadow, and that\u2019s going to hurt. A lot. But it\u2019s not every day you learn such an amazing trick!<br /> <br /> Anyway, Andy assured the Queen of Air and Darkness that we would take care of things. He is very courtly and noble when he\u2019s among the Unseelie. It\u2019s quite charming. Actually, even Edward was on his best behavior! Which is good, because once we were done at court, Lord Yrtalion escorted us to a teahouse known as the Weeping House. It was wonderful, with platforms suspended on the bowed branched of a huge willow tree. Luminescent white blossoms lit the place with a soft glow, and the atmosphere was both spooky and genteel. Andy recognized a few of the other patrons, and we joined them. It was instantly obvious that the three ladies, two banshees and a sluagh named Madb, Deirdre and Aoibhell, were deeply attracted to Andy, and who can blame them? There was also a brooding fae lord named Fionn, and he seemed to hit it off with Edward.<br /> <br /> Of course, I had to sample the local absinthe, and I found that it was remarkable! Yrtalion warned me that it contained the tears of children, but assured me the Unseelie had not been the cause of those tears. Zane seemed to disapprove, but I was too curious to pass it up, and I\u2019m glad I didn\u2019t. The absinthe was exquisite, and once I felt it open my senses, I decided to read the tea leaves floating in Deirdre\u2019s cup, hoping to gain some insight into our upcoming heist.<br /> <br /> The tea leaves were a bit reluctant, but they offered a few nice revelations. I couldn\u2019t divine what the torque really does, but I figured that information would he hidden behind too many veils of illusion for me to see it. It did become clear to me that Andy had a relationship with Madb, Deirdre and Fionn, though. He had slept with all three and was actively courting Madb and Deirdre, the banshees. He wasn\u2019t involved with Aoibhell, but she certainly wanted to be involved with him. I didn\u2019t need to read tea leaves to see that.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, though, I learned that the stirring ladle is located somewhere in the Underworld, and that there is a detachment of frost and grave giants searching for it and the Cauldron\u2019s other components. I suppose it was futile to hope there wouldn\u2019t be competition, huh? That\u2019s not really how fate works. Also, the tea leaves showed me that Hel\u2019s security is tighter than usual right now, but it\u2019s focused on the torque, of course, so we can use that to our advantage. Also, Helheim\u2019s sentinel, Modgud, is jealous s of the scion of Baldur, so she might not be quite as diligent in her duties as she usually is.<br /> <br /> Of course, during our little tea party, Yrtalion was very charming, and clearly flirting heavily with both me and Pipa. I thought he was very handsome, and so did Pipa. He\u2019s exactly the sort of guy I like sleeping with, because I know it will be a lot of fun, but there won\u2019t be any commitment or attachment. So Pipa and I shared a look and decided that we would hook up with Yrtalion later. But first, he had to show me how to create a duplicate of the Dark Key. So Pipa and I returned with him to his elegant mansion of crystalline shadow while Andy left for some private time with Madb and Deridre. All in all, it seemed we were in for a very romantic evening. Edward, however, was stuck without a date, but he made the best of it by sharing drugs with Fionn and the other patrons of the Weeping House. Zane tells me that things got a little crazy there after the rest of us left.<br /> <br /> The process of transforming my shadow into the relic is fascinating. It involves some very touchy Taiyi techniques that come dangerously close to etching my soul, and the risk of damaging my spirit is very real. It takes a delicate touch but a firm command of Taoist techniques, and I will have to write new symbols with ink made from my shadow itself. In fact, that\u2019s the part that will tear my shadow away from me: it will turn into the Key when the symbols become reality. I think I can handle it, but I guess we won\u2019t know until I try. Still, it\u2019s very exciting! I asked Yrtalion how he knew all of this about Taiyi, and he said he made a point of analyzing his chosen medium in other paradigms. Makes sense to me. I was a bit concerned about losing my shadow, but Yrtalion assures me it will grow back.<br /> <br /> Once the lessons were over, Pipa and Yrtalion and I spent the rest of the evening in his luxurious bedroom, wrapped in each other and in sheets made of pure shadow and startled gasps. It was delightful and dream-like and wonderful, especially since I was still drinking the Weeping Absinthe. Actually, I think I\u2019m becoming addicted to these wonderful mystical absinthes. Between the Tian absinthe, the Weeping Absinthe, and the potent stuff Andy\u2019s father gave me in the Black Forest, I\u2019m becoming a bit bored with mundane absinthes. They don\u2019t have the same impact the mystical liquors do. Yisheng, what would it take to set up regular deliveries of Tian absinthe?<br /> <br /> Anyway, our time with Yrtalion was over too soon, but it\u2019s probably for the best. We have work to do. We\u2019re flying back to Berlin to pick up Magnus. He might be able to get us some more information from Hriki and Sigrid. Then it\u2019s off to Helheim!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Once everyone were done with the kissing stuff, Ned wanted to bust up the temple, on account of that\u2019s what Mags usually does. But Ji-Woo said no, on account of it being her matron\u2019s. Ned thought that was her mum, but that\u2019s a whole different word. Ji-Woo meant Sybil, the maenad gang leader with all the tits. She didn\u2019t have all of them when she showed up to say thanks, or else she were just hiding them better than the statues did. She did have a proper nice cloak thing. I didn\u2019t ask her about her tits. I thought Ji-Woo might have bit me.<br /> <br /> Turns out she\u2019d been the one stopping everybody from having a kip, seeing as people sleeping made more chaos-wankers to fight for the dreamer bloke. But since I punched him and Ji-Woo shot him a lot with green and pointy things, it were all safe, so she were letting people nod off again. She said she was going to help Dionysis too.<br /> <br /> To say thanks proper, she let Ned be a maenad whenever she wants, and she made Ji-Woo get better faster. I were glad when Ji-Woo weren't bite-y no more, even if Sybil were a crazy bint what thought biting were good and all. She teleported us back to Berlin too, with the motorhome, but first Yisheng showed up! He\u2019d run the whole way, and had Ji-Woo\u2019s absinthe! She were well chuffed. She said he deserved a reward so Ned bit him, but Ji-Woo stopped her and told Yisheng to do paperwork to get himself a prize. So he started to leave but then she told him to stop and have some absinthe and then that he should do the paperwork to have a week off but when he stood up to do that she said he should sit and have some more. It were proper confusing, Ned even fell asleep on him. But Ji-Woo were happy, so that were good.<br /> <br /> Xanthdy and Persephone got shoved off by Sybil while Ji-Woo were being confusing, but once she\u2019d got some absinthe, me and her and Mags and the motor home all got shoved off to Berlin. I dunno where Ned went, but she\u2019s probably biting people.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> The Black Forest is bloody brill! I got to beat up a big bad wolf and trick a witch and talk with another pretty water lady. We answered loads of riddles and saved summat else who was lost from some kind of shape shifted monster fucker and only let Pipa eat the monster.<br /> <br /> It started out just me and Ji-Woo, on account of her being bored and missing Pipa, seeing as she had to go back to work. Also, the Troll Mum went that way, so maybe we could have fought her too. I\u2019m not as good at getting around and finding food and things when I\u2019m not in the city, so I brought loads of food, which were good, cause we got proper lost. It were alright at first, cause it were fun and all, and Ji-Woo got pretty good at finding food and places to sleep and things, but then we wanted to start back and everything, and Ji-Woo didn\u2019t know which way it were!<br /> <br /> She summoned up Pipa after that, but Pipa were lost too. She were a bit cross at Ji-Woo for that. She got over it though, and we have more fun any road. I weren\u2019t even all the way out of food when Andy\u2019s dad, the god one, Manannan mac Lir, showed up. He were proper charming, and had on fancy armor stuff. He told us to retrace our steps, which were proper silly, on account of us having been wandering around for days and days, but it made sense to Ji-Woo, so we got out!<br /> <br /> It were fun, and good too, cause now I\u2019ve got more stories to tell the littles. I\u2019ve been checking in on the ladies and the White Gloves people some, and sleeping in the caves when I hafta sleep, but mostly I\u2019ve been watching over the street littles in Berlin, teaching them how to nick things good and where from and where to sleep and things like that. And listening to ace stories is the best way to make things better when you\u2019re a little. I\u2019ve got down to some other cities too, like Paris and Hamburg and Vienna too, to help out the littles there. And Ji-Woo said maybe we\u2019d go to Australia too later. They talk proper funny English there.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> I get to nick a thing, for fairies! Like, fairy tale fairies, and banshees and things. And we get to nick lots of things, cause to get one thing, we have to nick (well, get a sneaky look at) another one, and then the one thing has two other pieces that are lost that we might get to nick. It\u2019s a secret though, so shh!<br /> <br /> I were leaving apples hid for the littles in the sewers when Ji-Woo called and said that Ned were there, and Pipa were smoking hot and Ji-Woo\u2019d got more absinthe and Yisheng didn\u2019t help us in the Black Forest on account of him having the week off like she said to and Andy had a heist for us. So I went to hers, and made sure to ding! first. Ji-Woo don\u2019t like it when I get sewer gunk in her place.<br /> <br /> Mags and Ned weren\u2019t there when I got there, but that were because Ned were in the closet looking for me. Andy threw in two cats smushed into one in with him and leaned on the door. I opened it any road, but Ned were dressed up in everything at all that were in the closet, even though it were mostly too small for him. So I shut it, and moved Andy back to where he were. Sides, Ned were playing with the smushed cats.<br /> <br /> He came out anyways after a bit and Andy said the blokes he were a Knight for, the Veiled Court (Ji-Woo said it were also called the Unsealy court) needed something nicked. He didn\u2019t know much but that, and that politics said they couldn\u2019t just nick it themselves. Ned were worried about eating food there and Ji-Woo said no making deals, but Andy said it\u2019d be alright, on account of him being a Knight and all.<br /> <br /> So we took Ned\u2019s plane to Ireland. Ned\u2019s Dad had got it back to him - Ned had been flying it all around, that\u2019s where he\u2019d been and all, since Greece. It had a motorcycle steering thing and sounded like one, and had massage chairs and an ice bucket for wine that made more everyday. There were a nymph too, what talked Spanish at us until I pulled on her ear. He had all sorts of Spanish things on the inside too.<br /> <br /> Mags still weren\u2019t there, so the music were much quieter. I guess Andy couldn\u2019t find him, or summat. Hopefully we can when we get back, on account of we need to talk to Hriki and go to Helhime. But me and Ji-Woo had fun playing on the plane ride to Ireland.<br /> <br /> Once we got there, Andy said he needed to find a she, except it were a sidhe, instead. Ji-Woo spelled in out for me, just like that. Ned did too, and said it were sidwn, but that\u2019s just silly. Fairy words are weird all around though, like names and all. H makes m sound like v, and make id disappear. It\u2019s all messed up. He found one anyway and we started to go down under a hill. Ji-Woo weren\u2019t chuffed about it, but me and Pipa held her hands, and it were proper big inside.<br /> <br /> It were proper ace inside too. Loads of trees and mists and glowy plants, with floating yellow eyes and skittery-scuttery noises. Pipa showed all her teeth to the eyes and they looked a little scared, I think. It were still all forest-y when we found two blokes in black armor on skeleton horses. They\u2019d only talk to Andy, but I think they liked me better than the others. They were a little toffish anyways. But they did make horses for the others, made of bones and rocks from the ground for armor. I ran instead, cause I\u2019m proper fast. I\u2019m not the bestest at running, but I keep up with Ji-Woo and get less tired. I\u2019m even better at balancing than I were before too, which were good, cause I never saw the ground and we was running proper fast.<br /> <br /> We got to a city kinda thing after we were running a while, but all the buildings was made of trees! Not like, made of wood from trees or summat, but whole trees. It were right brill. The armor blokes brought us to a stonking one and said the Morrigan weren\u2019t there but the Queen of Air and Darkness were and that\u2019s who Andy wanted to talk with any road. There was some bloke called Lord Urtalien, who was all done up in even fancier black armor, and were well flirty. He taught Ji-Woo how to make magic-y things using her shadow. I think they had a shag too. Ned kept bollocksing up everyone\u2019s flirting, though, it were proper funny.<br /> <br /> That were later though. The Queen told us she wanted us to nick a cauldron thing from some death lord blokes in Helhime, something from Crom Cruock. If you put in summat who\u2019d died fighting, and fed it to ghosts, they\u2019d get well hard and and if you got the stirry bit and something else, they\u2019d be as strong as superheroes! The Queen didn\u2019t know where the stirry bit or the something else were though.<br /> <br /> The politics bits was right weird. The death lord blokes were in Hel\u2019s gang - they give tribute and all. But they\u2019re like Titan-y kinda, but Hel\u2019s not, but she\u2019s not really on the gods\u2019 side either. The Aesir (and Hel too) and the Veiled Court don\u2019t like each other very much. But the Queen said something about a daytaunt and Ji-Woo said that meant that things were getting better and they didn\u2019t want to fuck it up or nothing. So, we get to nick it!<br /> <br /> The other bit of nicking is cause the death lords live in a proper cold place. I got the scarf from Mum, but it\u2019s even more cold than all that, and kills everything that\u2019s not dead already. So we got to get a key from Hel, but if Ji-Woo looks at it, she can make it from her shadow, so we\u2019re gonna nick it without taking it. To get there, we\u2019ve got to go past Maudegud, what guards a bridge and is Hel\u2019s daughter and girlfriend, which is right strange. But we figured out later at the Weeping House that Maudegud is upset cause Hel\u2019s been seeing a scion of Balder instead,<br /> <br /> The Weeping House were a pub kinda place, but calmer, yeah? It were proper pretty, even if Ji-Woo wouldn\u2019t stop talking about how ace the tears-of-littles absinthe were. I didn\u2019t have none of that. I had a beer. I thought the Weeping bit were on account of it being in the weeping kinda tree, but I had to tell them not to put widow tears in it, so I guess it were cause of the crying and all. We talked to some banshees there, and a bloke, who told us about the Maudegud thing and that Loki\u2019d given Hel a tork that were magic but nobody knew what it did. Ji-Woo said it didn\u2019t lock the Titans in the kitchen sink forever if you punched Odin in the face and grabbed Frigg\u2019s ass, so there\u2019s that, I guess? They also said there was loads more frost giants and grave giants about and Ji-Woo said that were to find the stirry bit and the other thing.<br /> <br /> Andy\u2019d gone all posh again, and were talking funny and gave me angry looks when I said shit, on account of the lady banshees. Two of the them was flirting with him and the other were all upset over it. After Ji-Woo and Pipa went off with Lord Urtalien, he and the two flirty bints went off for a walk, even though he said before he didn\u2019t know how to bonk a girl. I knew he were lying anyway, on account of Caoimhe. Ned got the bloke what was left to try a little bit of coke, and didn\u2019t even mix it with the tears of mums who\u2019d lost their littles, or some bollocks. He were alright though.<br /> <br /> To get back, we jumped into the fountain. We mostly didn\u2019t get wet, except for our feet, except I maybe splashed a little bit. Andy found his proper voice in his pocket even, and we\u2019re headed back to Berlin to get Mags.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <i>End Episode XXXVI</i><br /> <br /> Mostly Rping, not much action. This time we touched on the Unseelie Court. As noted the earlier adventure in the dark wood was collaborative fiction, which is cool.<br /> <br /> The grave giants were because I was tired and could not remember the name Charnel Giants. Future installments will call them that.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s all for now, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 12-21-2014, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T14:56:52-08:00","id":347011,"title":"","content":"Due to quite a bit going on here in the end of the year, we did not get up a journal for two sessions ago. We have a journal for the past two sessions from Zane, and one from Ji-Woo which covers both, so I am just going to do one combined session report.<br /> <i><br /> Session XXXVII and XXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <u>Six Underground Parts II and III</u><br /> <b><br /> Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Norway</b><br /> <br /> After leaving the Unseelie Realm and fetching Magnus from Berlin, we managed to make it to Norway. Unfortunately, Pipa had to leave work on some plot Daji has cooking, and that\u2019s where she is now. I was sad that she had to leave, but it\u2019s okay. I\u2019m distracted by our mission now anyway! Still, it would have been nice to have someone to cling to during our landing in Norway. It was a close call. I didn\u2019t think Edward could possibly land the plane safely in a snowfield on the edge of a cliff, but somehow he did it. I should have more confidence in him. Still, if the plane hadn\u2019t stopped in time, it would have soared right over the edge, and the chasm beneath the cliff was very deep. I know because I flew down on my own and checked.<br /> <br /> After landing we hiking into the mountains to Jotunheim. Well, I flew, of course. I\u2019m glad I\u2019m immune to cold, or I would have been utterly miserable like Andy, poor guy. Zane looked out for him, though, and gave him a bit of a boost.<br /> <br /> I honestly don\u2019t remember much of what happened in Jotunheim, though. We met up with Magnus\u2019 brother Kjell, and then Magnus left to visit Sigrid and Hriki. The rest of us stayed at Kjell\u2019s place, but I spent most of the time passed out drunk. Kjell had some sort of potent alcohol that knocked me out cold until Zane used her magic to sober me up. Somehow I did manage to receive some insight on our situation, though. Alcohol can be incredibly liberating when it comes to mystic visions. For one thing, I realized that the Dark Key I\u2019m suppose to copy is locked away in Hel\u2019s personal wing of her palace, probably in some sort of treasure room. That will make it much easier to find once we are there. Also, Hel prefers death metal to other kinds of heavy metal, which I\u2019m sure will become important later.<br /> <br /> Divine insight also revealed to me that Baldur\u2019s scion, Gloria Lichtdottir, is NOT Hel\u2019s willing captive. She\u2019d rather not be under Hel\u2019s power at all. But there IS a reason she\u2019s there, and it\u2019s not to seduce Hel. Something\u2019s going on and I\u2019m terribly curious to know what it is. Obviously, Gloria is a huge distraction, but why is someone trying to distract Hel?<br /> <br /> Oh, and Magnus is going to be a father! Hriki is pregnant. It\u2019s exciting, but gods, I don\u2019t know why anyone would want to be a parent. Being pregnant, giving birth, and taking care of screaming children sounds absolutely AWFUL to me. To each his own, I suppose. Actually, I don\u2019t think Magnus told the news to any of us, so I probably shouldn\u2019t say anything to the others until he makes an announcement. That goes for you too, Yisheng. Hush hush!<br /> <br /> Anyway, by the time I was sober again, Zane and Kjell were fast friends because Zane could hold her own drinking with him. She could even handle the hard stuff, some sort of Dragon Brew made from the blood of wyrms from Muspelheim! Meanwhile, Edward built a huge snowman of Magnus. I should also mention that Kjell\u2019s voice resonates with the deep tones of an electric bass guitar, or at least they do when my mind is open from absinthe. I told this to Kjell and he seemed pleased. He also went out while I was drunk to talk to some of his fellow giants and learned that Utgard-Loki is offering a standing reward to anyone who could steal Hel\u2019s mysterious torque. Edward decided he wanted to steal it in that case, since he needed a new car, but I scolded him and told him that no, we mustn\u2019t steal the torque under any circumstances, because it would surely invite way more trouble than we are ready to face. And Hel might just kill us dead.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <b>Helheim</b><br /> <br /> Hel\u2019s palace is kinda dull and unpleasant. It\u2019s full of all sorts of torture machines and other unsettling furnishings, like iron chandeliers that look like they are made of meat hooks. Sure, I guess it\u2019s totally metal, but I\u2019ll be glad to get out of this place.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, we have to wait until after Magnus does an encore performance tonight, and until then, I\u2019ve mostly been wandering the halls with Zane and practicing flapper dancing and flirting heavily (but not seriously) with Andy. When I\u2019m done here, I\u2019m going to help Edward get ready for the show. He\u2019s been sporting Dia de los Muertos make-up since he returned from Mexico, and now he wants to paint his arms and torso that way too. So I\u2019m getting ready to help him with that. I did get bored and painted some cute stars on the door of Magnus\u2019 room. You know, like you see on actors\u2019 dressing room doors in Hollywood. When I was done, I realized they were probably way too girly for Magnus, but I like them, so I left them as is. Magnus isn\u2019t the sort of be unmanned by a few feminine decorations anyway.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Magnus, he\u2019s been locked in his room all day working on something\u2014a new song for the show tonight, I suppose.<br /> <br /> So far, though, aside from today\u2019s boredom, things have been really interesting here! We didn\u2019t have any trouble getting into the realm. When Magnus informed her we were there to pay our respects to Hel with the power of metal, she let us pass. Magnus, Edward, Kjell and Andy spent the rest of the afternoon preparing for the concert. Zane helped, playing the part of a roadie, and I pretended to be a groupie, so I mostly listened to my iPod, drank some absinthe and chatted with people.<br /> <br /> Once the show got underway, the real fun began. Zane and I slipped away with the first thunderous chords of Magnus\u2019 guitar and made our way quietly to Hel\u2019s wing of the palace. There were saucy-looking skeletal maids roaming around, tidying the halls here and there, but we were able to avoid them until we reached the monolithic doors to Hel\u2019s private chambers. An ominous silver skull was set into the wall above the door, and its unrelenting gaze swept the antechamber. It would probably scream an alarm or something if we tried to break in, so I decided to freeze it in time. First, though, we had to lure the maids out of the room, so I knocked over a thorn-filled vase in another hallway using my Qi and they went scurrying out to clean up the mess. Then I channeled the timeless principles of the celestial firmament into the skull, and it was frozen in time for a few minutes, long enough for us to get through the door. And when it succumbed to time again, it was be none the wiser!<br /> <br /> Beyond the doors was a network of treasure rooms and bedchambers. Hell\u2019s room was there, but we didn\u2019t dare go in. Gloria Lichtdottir\u2019s guest room was also there, very near our destination. The scion herself was at the concert with Hel, though. Too bad, really, because I kinda wanted to ask her why she\u2019s really there, and maybe help her escape. Even though Gloria wasn\u2019t there, her magical dolls were hard at work constructing a labyrinthine series of puzzles for Hel to overcome in her quest to steal Gloria\u2019s virtue. The whole place was like an intricate set for a play, layer after layer of mechanical scenery designed to present Hel with one challenge after another. Hel could easily have knock smashed through the puzzles, but that\u2019s not the way these things work. She had to solve them properly.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the dolls were having a hard time of things. Hel had sent her skeletal maids to sabotage their work by moving their building materials and cleaning up their tools. It was obvious that the dolls were losing ground, and even though Zane could slip right through by becoming invisible, I wasn\u2019t going to be able to sneak by all the maids without some help. So I offered to assist the dolls. After all, I\u2019d hate to be Gloria. She\u2019s in an awful situation, and she\u2019s unhappy about it. Even if Hel DOES manage to seduce her somehow, it just wouldn\u2019t be right. So while the dolls moved set pieces around to give me cover and Zane threw things at the maids to keep them distracted, I use my engineering know how and a little Taiyi to magic up a complicated mechanical trap involving a series of levers that will engage gears to open the way past the trap. The gears have to be engaged in just the right way, and to figure it out, you have to have understand how each gear will effect the works of the whole machine. I guarantee that Hel doesn\u2019t have what it takes to solve my puzzle, so it should keep her stalled for one more night at least. I hope she doesn\u2019t get too mad if she figures out who made it, though.<br /> <br /> So, with the doll\u2019s help, Zane and I made it to the treasure room that held the key. Oh, I wish we could have spent all night there, sorting through the chests and wardrobes! There must have been some amazing relics in there, and certainly a thing or two that Hel wouldn\u2019t miss, right? But we only had so much time before the concert was over. Of course I knew exactly which box the key was in: a jewelry box covered in intricately engraved human skin. We opened that one first. But it was locked with a riddle. A small silver skeleton built into the box\u2019s latch asked the riddle, which went something like this:<br /> <br /> \u201cIron gray with flaxen tail and a brass boy driving.\u201d<br /> <br /> Of course I knew the answer instantly. Needle, thread and thimble. And as soon as I said it, the box opened and there was the Dark Key, a key made of iron so black that it seemed like a key-shaped hole more than a physical object that I could reach out and touch.<br /> <br /> Next came the hard part: making a copy. Zane gave me a worried look, then squeezed my hand and bolstered my strength. I used my Celestial Jade compact to reflect light across my shadow, symbolically severing it from my body. It hurt. A lot. I know I screamed and fell but Zane caught me. Thank goodness she bolstered me, or I probably would have passed out! After that, though, crafting the shadow into a copy of the key wasn\u2019t too hard. It was actually really exciting to use Taiyi like that. It was like sculpting with thought and ink and gossamer strands of darkness. I love the possibility embodied in Taiyi. It\u2019s almost addictive!<br /> <br /> Once the key was safely tucked away, Zane and I decided to rummage around the other treasures a little before we left. One box made of hardened coal was locked with another riddle:<br /> <br /> \u201cSea of red heralds death; screams and cries without surprise.\u201d<br /> <br /> Obviously, the answer was birth. Inside the chest was ring. I recognized it from the lore. Anyone wearing it can\u2019t be killed; someone else nearby will die instead. Unfortunately, when that person dies, the person wearing the ring acquires all of their remaining fate. Youch. That sounded completely awful, so Zane and I agreed to leave it be.<br /> <br /> Another box that was decorated with an onyx wolf carving contained something else I recognized from my studies: the key to Garm\u2019s collar. Zane and I agreed that we probably shouldn\u2019t play around with that. Besides, anyone who takes it has to send the wolf\u2019s spirit out to hunt a person of lower virtue within a lunar month, and I don\u2019t want that kind of responsibility.<br /> <br /> We did steal something out of the last thing we searched, though. It was Hel\u2019s wardrobe full of her old clothes. It had fancy clothes dating back hundreds of years! There was a Victorian gown, medieval dress, and even a crisp Nazi SS uniform. I took Hel\u2019s stunning flapper dress for myself, and Zane took a tailed coat and top hat. The magic imbued in the wardrobe demanded that we leave something behind if we took something, so I left my new winter coat and Zane left one of her spare shirts.<br /> <br /> We were running out of time by then, so Zane and I crept out of Hel\u2019s chambers and back to the concert. I had to still the skull again, but aside from that we made it back without a single problem. Then we mingled with the crowd and got to enjoy the stunning conclusion of Magnus\u2019 concert!<br /> <br /> Of course Hel was impressed. So impressed that she asked Magnus to perform again tonight. I suspect she\u2019s up to something involving Gloria. Of course Magnus agreed to stay and put on another show, even though we were all eager to get out of there. And that\u2019s why we\u2019re still in Hel\u2019s palace, effectively trapped unless Magnus impresses her again tonight. It\u2019s enough to make me feel claustrophobic, so I hope we leave soon!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters<br /> </b><br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> I got a new bracelet, on account of being well hard and being able to drink, a lot, and not fall over or get proper drunk like Ji-Woo and Andy. It\u2019s all cold and that, seeing as it came from Mags\u2019 frost giant brother, and it\u2019s made of bone, and it fits perfect! OK, it\u2019s maybe a little bit too big, but it\u2019s proper ace.<br /> <br /> We got to Kel\u2019s (that\u2019s Mags\u2019 brother) by Ned flying us on the plane. Mags had woken up, by the time we got back, and after Ji-Woo explained everything in her floaty kinda way, we decided to go to Jotunhime, on account of them being neighbors with Helhime, even though we\u2019re going to France to get to Helhime and we went to Norway or summat for Jotunhime. Mags and Ji-Woo had to have little\u2019s tears absinthe first though, so I drank all his beers. Ji-Woo tried to put a sign on the absinthe what said it were all right, like Ned did for landing the plane in the woods, but I told her it didn\u2019t work like that.<br /> <br /> Maybe it does though, seeing as Ned did land all right in the woodsy place, right on the edge of a cliff! I boosted Ji-Woo any road, on account of her looking proper scared, even if Ned couldn\u2019t find a scarf to blindfold himself with, cause he were wearing it. She were better after we got out though, and when I dropped a rock off the tall, tall cliff, she went diving down to race it.<br /> <br /> We had to walk the rest of the way to the giant place. It were well cold, but the scarf Mum got me kept me warm so\u2019s I hardly even noticed. Ji-Woo had on a right nice coat, and proper ace arm warmer glove things, but no trousers. She don\u2019t feel the cold neither though, so it were just funny. Andy does feel the cold, and he started getting all frost bit up, so I boosted him by throwing a snowball down his back and giving him a hug, and then Mags made him tougher, so he were all right after that.<br /> <br /> There were guards at the giant place. They didn\u2019t talk English none, so they didn\u2019t notice Ned called them ladies even though they was blokes. They scowled at him though, and Ji-Woo too, when she waved. She scowled back, and it were right adorable. I just flipped them off, on account of they were gonna be pissy any road. Mags talked something funny at them and they let us in, so bollocks to them.<br /> <br /> Kel\u2019s house were proper metal. It were big and posh, with music things all over. He had guitars as big as four mes! At least! Ned tried to pick one up, and Mags smacked him one, on account of him not asking and waiting for an answer. He had food and drink for us, a whole pig, what Mags called a boar on account of its big tusk things, and loads of bread and salty cheese and berries in honey. The mead were proper good too, in cups made of ice that I had to use both hands just to hold and even then my hands weren\u2019t all the way around. It got Andy well bladdered, and Ji-Woo passed right out, right off, talking cobblers about bees. I made a den for her with her extra jacket and my pack and other soft bits and bobs I\u2019ve got.<br /> <br /> She woke up later when Andy shot Ned, and had some absinthe then went back to sleep. I had lots of the mead - it were made of honey and all, so it were nice and sweet and warm making. Kel figured out some things about the charnal giants, that they weren\u2019t crazy like the fomorians but worked for Crom Cruock same as. They was hanging out with the death lords, like the Queen of Air and Darkness said. Kel said the lords was blokes what had sold their souls to Jell, and was ice skeleton things, like the litch guy from Berlin, maybe? Odin said she weren\u2019t allowed to do that no more, so they was hidden away in a fisher, which is the ditch kinda place where we need the key to not die.<br /> <br /> Kel said Sigurd might know more, but she were taking care of Hriki, but then he wouldn\u2019t say what were wrong with Hriki! He talked funny with Mags about it, but then Mags wouldn\u2019t say either. He went to go talk with Sigurd and Hriki all on his own, and didn\u2019t come back til the next morning and still didn\u2019t say! For fair, I forgot about asking til right now. He did say she were all right though, and she weren\u2019t mad at him or nothing, they had a shag and everything.<br /> <br /> Me and Ji-Woo and Andy kept at Kel\u2019s food though. Ned went off to build snowmans, so he didn\u2019t get any dragon booze like me, that were all steamy and lovely warm. Kel thought he were ugly and dumb too, so maybe that\u2019s why. I finished a whole glass of it, and Ji-Woo said I made a blue tada! with yellow sparkles when I did, and that Kel\u2019s voice sounded like a sexy guitar. That\u2019s why Kel gave me the brill bone bracelet. The drinking thing, not the tada! or the sexy guitar thing. He also gave me another blinding drink with the giant pancake breakfast, what tasted of cranberries and lighter fluid. It were ace!<br /> <br /> There was also a stonking big cigar, what made Ji-Woo laugh and laugh until she were crying cause her head hurt from the hangover. I fixed it up with my superpowers though, so she got to laugh at me some more. It were all right - Kel wouldn\u2019t let her have nothing but water to drink, in case the apple juice made her pass out too. He was teasing her and Ned something fierce, and Andy too, so it\u2019s ok that Ji-Woo was laughing at me. The cigar was stonking gigantic too.<br /> <br /> Mags said Sigurd didn\u2019t say much more, except that we shouldn\u2019t go for the torkeven though Utgard-Loki were giving out treasure for it, so Ned really wanted to, in case it were a car. Utgard-Loki were also maybe giving rewards for summat taking a butchers at the charnal giants and snitching to him, but we\u2019re supposed to be all secrety and Utgard-Loki is tricksy, so we\u2019re just going to Helhime without talking with him.<br /> <br /> Kel is coming with us, even though he almost can\u2019t fit on the place. Ned was able to make it fly all right, even if he knocked over some more trees. Ji-Woo said he wouldn\u2019t be able to, on account of it not being magic and there not being enough room, but he did, so maybe the plane is magic.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> Kel has awesome plans. And me too! See, Ji-Woo was all worried about going into the Underworld place, it being maybe like an ant hill thing, and having to climb around inside the roots of the special tree she found in France. So Kel gave her some of the dragon booze and she passed right out! I had to carry her, but that were alright. I\u2019m strong and good at balancing. Once we got to the big wide open bit, I told Andy to shoot Ned, on account of that\u2019s what woke Ji-Woo up last time. Ned decided to shoot himself instead. And Ji-Woo woke up! I had to undrunk her again and Ned had to fix his makeup then we was all good.<br /> <br /> Helhime were a big wide open space, nothing like an ant hill at all, and there were this big stonking bridge what Maudegud were guarding. It were proper dark, so Andy got out a lantern what had a little Peter Pan kinda fairy in it, getting electrocuted. It bothered Ji-Woo at first, then it didn\u2019t, so it were probably alright. She did like that absinthe though...<br /> <br /> We decided to tell Maudegud that Kel were going to visit the frost giants and all, and to be polite and everything, we was gonna put on a rock show for Hel. Ned is going to be the drummer, on account of he likes banging things, on account of him being a bit of a slag, even when he\u2019s not a girl. It\u2019s alright to say, cause he said it first. Andy doesn\u2019t know what he\u2019s gonna be, except proper strange. He put on a right funny outfit, all blue with a pretend chest (a pretend bloke\u2019s chest, not tits or nothing) and fuzzy red hair. He kept scratching his back with a guitar what used to be a drumstick and saying groovy and other cobblers like that. Me and Ji-Woo don\u2019t get to do music with them though, seeing as we\u2019ve got to not nick the key while they\u2019re distracting everybody.<br /> <br /> We did get a little mixed up talking about Balder and fate and things. Balder, he\u2019s the guy what has a kid making time with Hel right now, is a dick and is fated to die, Kel said. So Ji-Woo started up talking about fate things, what makes Mags twitchy and made Kel get all yell-y. He almost made an ice megaphone just to be louder about it. But it all worked out and Maudegud let us cross and everything, after she warned us not to get the tork too.<br /> <br /> <br /> I got to be a roady, on account of being good at carrying things, even though I didn\u2019t get to do any music. And Ji-Woo were a groupy, seeing as she\u2019s good at carrying on and all, even though she\u2019s not strong like me. She did help some, with setting up and everything, when Ned were painting a well hard ice dragon skull thing. She made some fire shooty things too, to go with the blood and the zombies and the chains.<br /> <br /> It were a proper ace show and long. It were long enough we even got to dance some, once we was back from sneaking. Ji-Woo\u2019s good at dancing, even if she\u2019s not very metal. We got to see Hel too and Gloria, that\u2019s Balder\u2019s kid, she was with her. Hel is proper funny looking. Half of her face is all normal and half\u2019s gone zombie! It\u2019s cause she\u2019s a god of death and all, yeah? It were proper spooky.<br /> <br /> It weren\u2019t hard to sneak off, even for Ji-Woo who weren\u2019t invisible like me, cause everybody were looking at Mags and Ned and Andy and Kel. None of the guards had a chance neither until we got to a stonking silver skull thing above the door we needed. It were looking around proper sharp, and probably just wanted to ask us a riddle and maybe couldn\u2019t even see me, but we didn\u2019t check, cause Ji-Woo could use her superpowers to make it go all still by painting on her mirror and then made all the skeleton maids go away by knocking something over from a long way away so she weren\u2019t there.<br /> <br /> We was almost at the place with the key, but Gloria\u2019s room were in the way, and there was loads of me-sized wooden dolls and skeleton maids fucking about there. The dolls was building puzzles that Hel had to solve to get at Gloria while she were having a kip. She weren\u2019t allowed to bust them up or nothing, unless they doubled up or summat. The maids was there to mess things around, moving bits and making it tough for the dolls. Me and Ji-Woo, we decided we\u2019d help the dolls out, cause it weren\u2019t on, messing with summat\u2019s hidey-hole and the maids was something like cheating.<br /> <br /> We was going to after we got the key and all, but then there was too many things for Ji-Woo to sneak past. She\u2019s good at sneaking but still not invisible. So we traded for them to help us and all. I made a snowball out of dark instead of snow and turned it into another eye what could float about. A bunch of maids found butterfly net things and went after it, so they stopped fucking things up. Then Ji-Woo built a puzzle thing, poof! with levers and gears and moving bits, using her paint brush like it were a magic wand and spinning about. It were proper complicated, so Hel didn\u2019t get Gloria tonight for certain!<br /> <br /> After that the dolls helped Ji-Woo stay hid and we found a room full of boxes and boxes of things. Most of them had silvery skulls and skeletons on them, what asked riddles. Ji-Woo knew all the answers and what was in everything, so we found the key right off. It were in a jewelry box all covered in skin. I boosted Ji-Woo before she copied it and all. She still screamed lots when she used her mirror to reflect light and cut her shadow off. But she weren\u2019t hurt really, on account of me.<br /> <br /> There were loads of other brill things, like a clothes holder with all kinds of posh clothes and coppers uniforms and things. It didn\u2019t have a silver riddle skeleton, but we had to trade things or else it would be bad. I traded one of my shirts for a fancy jacket with tails like the Dodger gots, and a sock for a proper top hat thing. I can\u2019t wear them yet though, not til we\u2019re gone, even if I traded for them and didn\u2019t nick them. Hel might not be ok with us trading with her clothes. Ji-Woo traded her jacket for a pretty dress, what she called a flapper dress. It\u2019s for dancing, I know cause she and Andy have been flapper dancing all night, and flirting something fierce.<br /> <br /> There were other things we didn\u2019t take, on account of it being bad, like the wolf one. It had another key, for summat named Gorm\u2019s collar. But if you nicked it, you had to set the wolf spirit thing on summat. There were a stonking big dusty black chest what had a proper fancy ring in it, but it made it so if you died, then summat else did instead and then you traded fates, which is not on.<br /> <br /> So we sneaked back and got to dance some. Hel were well chuffed with Mags and the rest, so we got to stay an extra night so they can play some more. Mags has been writing a song, I think, or else he\u2019s gone to sleep again, which is bad on account of I don\u2019t think Hel\u2019s alright with waiting a week for more songs. Ji-Woo tried to get him out, but then just painted a really girly star thing with his name on it, but spelled like M\u00e4gn\u00fcs, except the dots was more stars. Then she helped Ned get painted up like a skeleton all over, instead of just his face.<br /> <br /> I got Kel to show me how to play the guitar, using a guitar I made from shadows, not my shadow, just regular shadows, seeing as his was too big for me. It were good to have summat to do with my hands. I never snuck around such a posh bint\u2019s house for so long without nicking nothing. Not even the food, on account of I\u2019m spoiled and it were proper off. Some of it even had worms, and the worms was the tastiest bits. I ate some, right enough, it were food, and I\u2019m not that spoiled, but I didn\u2019t want to nick none for laters. It\u2019s enough to make my fingers itch a bit. I don\u2019t got a need for it or nothing. Some buggers need to nick like other bastards need a fix, but not me. It\u2019s just with all the sneaking and that, yeah? Any road, tomorrow we\u2019ll be off and I get to nick a thing from the giants and death lord blokes, and that\u2019ll be fun.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <i><br /> End Session XXXVII and XXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> And everything went fine till Zane took it upon herself to steal the Torc. But more on that is coming up next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T02:46:52-08:00","id":356483,"title":"","content":"So, after being told many times not to steal to Torc, and Ji-Woo stole the Torc. Enjoy the results below.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXIX</i><br /> <br /> <u>Six Underground Part IV</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo's Visions</b><br /> <b><br /> En Route to Malibu, California</b><br /> <br /> Well, Magnus is pretty mad at me right now. He\u2019s not really upset that I was complicit in an improvised plot to steal Hel\u2019s Torque. Or rather he IS, but that\u2019s not the PRIMARY reason he\u2019s angry. Mostly, he\u2019s mad because stealing the Torque distracted Hel and ultimately ruined the end of the amazing song we was performing for her. Really, though, the song is still amazing. Too amazing, in fact. I couldn\u2019t just stand idly by and let Hel have her way because Magnus roofied Gloria with the power of metal!<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, no one can know anything about this, so I\u2019m not writing with my ministry brush. Yisheng and the Bureaucracy can\u2019t find out about this debacle.<br /> <br /> Of course, the fact that Magnus is angry isn\u2019t the biggest problem we\u2019re facing. I was still trying to figure out how I was going to steal the Torque when I suddenly noticed that it had already been stolen and replaced by a shadow replica! I was surprised, but I just HAD to take advantage of the opportunity, so I use a little Taiyi to flick the fake Torque from Hel\u2019s throat, and THAT got her attention. Once she realized the torque was gone, all hell broke loose, and she forgot all about romancing Gloria. Mission accomplished! I tried to get Gloria\u2019s attention and telepathically told her to find and meet me later, but things didn\u2019t work out that way because we decided to leave Hel\u2019s palace as soon as possible. It\u2019s too bad, really, because I wanted to find out why Gloria\u2019s there if she doesn\u2019t want to be.<br /> <br /> We hurried back to our rooms and packed up our stuff as quickly as possible. Of course, no one suspected us of stealing the Torque because we were all occupied with Magnus\u2019 concert at the time. All except for me, and I was pretty visible right in front of the stage. Still, there was no sense in taking chances. Then this mischievous-looking girl showed up out of nowhere and sauntered in like she belonged there. She even tried to take some of Edward\u2019s things, claiming they were hers! None of us had any idea who she was, and Magnus, who was already pretty angry, was not in the mood to put up with some stranger\u2019s shenanigans. But when the newcomer realized that we didn\u2019t recognize her, she became very confused and a little upset. She looked downright heartbroken when I admitted I had no idea who she was.<br /> <br /> The girl said her name was Zane and that she was our friend, and had been for a long time. She claimed that she and I had planned to steal the Torque to stop Hel from seducing Gloria, which made sense to me since I HAD been planning to do just that. She stole it, but then, when she went to hide it somewhere in the palace for Hel to find later, it was gone, vanished like it had never existed! Magnus invoked some magic and told us that something was seriously wrong the mystery girl. She was in some sort of mystic vacuum, completely cut off from fate! I couldn\u2019t divine anything about her fate either, which just proved the point.<br /> <br /> The mystery girl\u2019s story made Magnus even angrier, especially when I admitted that I had in fact been planning to steal the Torque. Sure, I know that just a couple days ago I insisted that we absolutely MUST NOT do that very thing, but despite what the grumpy Aesir think, fate is very fluid and its course constantly changes. But I started putting the pieces together and quickly figured out what had happened. I think that when this girl stole the Torque, it did something to remove her from fate altogether! That sounds awful. My guess is that this is all some experiment of Loki\u2019s. After all, he was the one who gave the Torque to Hel in the first place, and he would certainly be interested in finding a way to cheat fate. It also explains why no one remembers who Zane is. Of course, she might be lying. She might even be Loki in disguise. But she does know an awful lot about our adventures, and I feel like we can trust her.<br /> <br /> We decided to sort things out later and left Hel\u2019s palace as quickly as we could with Zane in tow. Being cut off from fate means Zane is cut off from her divine power, so if she really is our friend, we need to help her find her fate again before we go looking for the Cauldron. We briefly considered summoning Hecate for help. This is all more-or-less my fault, so I was willing to accept some sort of task from Hecate if it would help fix Zane. Magnus and Edward felt that it would be better to go right to the source and track down Loki. I felt that would be a lot harder than calling on Hecate, especially since Loki may not WANT to be found by us, not if Zane is an experiment that he\u2019s trying to observe. Still, I\u2019m not really eager to be locked into some deal with Hecate, so I was more than willing to go looking for Loki instead.<br /> <br /> Of course, Loki is completely hidden from my divinations, so Edward called up his lover, Hestia, and she told us that Idunn, Sif, and some of the other Aesir ladies were enjoying a shopping trip in Malibu. So that\u2019s where we\u2019re headed now. Hopefully, they can give us some idea of where Loki is. Meanwhile, I\u2019m trying to pass the time during the flight. Kjell is still with us, and he disappeared into the back with Edward\u2019s flight attendant nymph, Alodia. Our mystery girl, Zane, seems kind depressed, but I don\u2019t really know what to say to her. She tried playing some music on her flute, but got bored with it, like she was expecting something that didn\u2019t quite happen. Oh well. I guess I\u2019ll zone out with a couple glasses of absinthe and listen to my iPod.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <b>Malibu, California</b><br /> <br /> Believe it or not, I\u2019ve never been to Malibu before. It\u2019s a little gaudy and flashy for my tastes, but Seoul is worse, so I can\u2019t complain. The others followed me and eventually I led them right to Idunn, Sif, Thrud Freya and Skadi, who were laden with shopping bags and having a really good time. We all went to a bar to talk, and Magnus explained that we were looking for Loki. Idunn told us that Heimdall would be able to help, but that he and Tyr were in Antarctica hunting some fearsome dragon. Great. I\u2019d really rather not go to Antarctica.<br /> <br /> I was curious what would happen when Idunn and Magnus met up again. Now that Magnus is going to be a father, things might get a little awkward. I asked if he was going to tell Idunn \u201cthe news,\u201d but he just told me to shut up and keep walking. Oh well. It will probably all end in tears. Trust me, I know. I mean, I\u2019ve never been pregnant, but I have juggled two or three boyfriends simultaneously before, and it never ends well. It\u2019s a hell of a lot of fun while it lasts, but I guess I do feel a little guilty about taking advantage of those poor guys. I would never do something like that to Pipa.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Aesir ladies were very boisterous, and I don\u2019t think I would enjoy hanging out with them. I just like to dance or chill out with some absinthe and good music. It\u2019s been far too long since I\u2019ve just relaxed in a soothing, chill trance lounge and let the essence of the absinthe and the soft beats flow through me like a gentle spring breeze laced with a warm, cleansing rain. I sometimes think the absinthe is at its best then, when every element of my surroundings is in harmony and I enter that dream-like state where I can experience what really lies beyond the illusion of mundane reality. No one else I hang out with really likes those places, though. Aoide and Edward can\u2019t sit still long enough to just enjoy it, and Magnus . . . no. Andy might enjoy it, but I don\u2019t think it\u2019s really his thing. His mind is always active, and I think he has trouble letting go of his thoughts long enough to allow the experience to just wash over him. I\u2019d love to enjoy it with Hermione and Pipa, but they like things a little more edgy and less cerebral. Hmmmm. Hermione and Pipa. I should have those two spend more time together. I bet they would get along.<br /> <br /> What was I talking about? Oh yeah, the Aesir women. They like to fight. And that\u2019s what Sif and her daughter, Thrud, ended up doing. Zane joined in on their bar room brawl and held her own okay. She apparently likes the ladies, so much so, in fact, that SHE turned into a HE just so she could impress Thrud. And mystery man Zane is a pretty handsome guy, with the sort of roguish good looks I like. Meow.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I don\u2019t especially enjoy such raucous behavior, and I was feeling a little bad because Magnus was still quite angry with me, so I stepped outside and gave Pipa a call. She knew instantly that I had done something bad. It\u2019s actually kinda scary that she can tell that just from the way I said, \u201cHi Pipa,\u201d but also kinda nice. I mean, to know and love someone enough to be able to read them like that means something. It makes me feel close to Pipa like I\u2019ve never felt close to anyone else before, and I like it. I hadn\u2019t really intended to tell Pipa everything. I really just wanted to hear her voice. But I ended up telling her all about the Torque and Zane. Of course, she also didn\u2019t know who Zane was. And as soon as I told her what had happened, her voice grew frantic and she started assuring me that she would talk to Daji about a rescue and petition the Bureaucracy to have me released from Hel\u2019s dungeons! Wow! My girlfriend is awesome! But I quickly explained that I wasn\u2019t in any trouble because no one knew we had taken the Torque, and anyway we didn\u2019t have it anymore. The relief in Pipa\u2019s voice was palpable. She scolded me a bit, but mostly she was just glad I was okay.<br /> <br /> By the time I returned, the others were pretty much finished at the bar, so Edward, Andy, Magnus, Zane, Kjell and I headed back to the plane to fly to Antarctica. I guess I\u2019ll spend the rest of the flight finishing a painting for the cover of Magnus\u2019 next album. I tried to make it as metal as I could, and it even has Hel lording her power over a kneeling slave girl that looks a bit like Gloria. Hopefully it will serve as an apology and help to cool Magnus\u2019 rage. I don\u2019t like it when people are mad at me. Especially not big, scary people like Magnus.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <b>Antarctica</b><br /> <br /> We\u2019ve arrived in Antarctica and are about to head into the Underworld to track down Heimdall and Tyr. It never ceases to amaze me just how competent Edward actually is. It defies all expectation and logic. Still, you can\u2019t argue with results, and so far we\u2019ve always managed safe landings, even on the ice fields of Antarctica.<br /> <br /> The trek to the Aesir camp was uneventful, but I\u2019m glad I\u2019m immune to cold. Otherwise I would have been freezing my ass off, like Andy, poor guy. As we neared the camp, I noticed a hidden sniper, a dwarf armed with some sort of high-tech rifle. He didn\u2019t shoot us or anything, and it was clear he was an ally of the Aesir, so I just telepathically told him that we were looking for Heimdall and that I didn\u2019t appreciate having a rifle pointed at me. Then the stubborn bastard aimed right at me and kept me in his sights until we reached the camp! I was a little piqued by that, so I used Taiyi to fling the rifle from his hands, and by the time he retrieved it, we\u2019d arrived.<br /> <br /> The camp was small but filled with all sorts of high-tech machinery. A hologram of the dwarf appeared and challenged us, but Magnus told him why we were there. There was a bowl built into one of the devices, and Magnus cut himself and bled his Aesir blood into it, which activated another hologram, this one of Heimdall. The hologram reported that Heimdall and Tyr had descended into the Underworld to hunt the dragon they were trying to slay. It also said that the keystone to the Underworld gate required the blood of someone who has lost a part of his body.<br /> <br /> I guess all that\u2019s left is for us to open the gate and head into the Underworld. I hope it\u2019s not too tight and close down there. Hel\u2019s place was fine, but I\u2019m worried about going underground again. Being claustrophobic sucks. When can we go to the Overworld instead of the Underworld?!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Mum!<br /> <br /> It\u2019s horrible! It\u2019s all gone wrong, and it\u2019s my fault too. I nicked this necklace, see, from Hel, only I weren\u2019t really nicking it, just borrowing it without asking, and I were gonna give it back, but then it were gone and now nobody remembers me none, not at all! Not even my mates. Not even Ji-Woo! That's why I'm writing to you, not Dad, on account of he\u2019d probably be confused cause of the not remembering thing. My superpowers from you don\u2019t work neither. It\u2019s like being stoled, again, but worse cause I remember things proper. But it\u2019s a little better too, cause this time I\u2019m not a little and I can fix it, maybe. We\u2019re looking for Loki now, on account of he\u2019s the one what did it. My mates is helping too, even though they don\u2019t think I\u2019m their mate no more. Ned keeps calling me Jane. And Mags is proper upset.<br /> <br /> See, Ji-Woo made this puzzle thing, right? It were proper brill, to keep Hel from busting into Gloria\u2019s room and making her do sex stuff. But then Hel were all happy, yeah, cause she\u2019d got a new plan, to get Mags to write an ace song and do all the work for her, so she didn\u2019t have to go making nobody. It were bloody great, the song, well hard and proper metal and Ji-Woo weren\u2019t happy, on account of Gloria not wanting to be there any road or summat. So she wanted to distract Hel, so I said I could nick the necklace, yeah? Well, borrow, really. I were gonna put it somewhere else and all, just so\u2019s she\u2019d have to go looking for it and be all distracted.<br /> <br /> But then when I got where I were gonna stash it, I didn\u2019t have it! I checked all my bestest hiding places, and my bags and my pouches and even my regular pockets, where it would have been right silly to put it in. And it weren\u2019t nowhere! So I checked to make sure I actually nicked it, and they was fussing about like it were gone, so I went to our rooms. The rest of the gang were there and Ned were even grabbing up my bit of the stuff. I thought he were just kidding around about not knowing who I were, but then Mags didn\u2019t neither. And Ji-Woo didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Mags looked at me proper fierce, and then just said I were fucked and started fucking off. He keeps calling me kid. Ji-Woo got him to explain a bit and then knew all the rest. Something cut off all my fates! I can\u2019t use Deuogdonio cause of all the fate stuff, and Andy and Ji-Woo can\u2019t use magics or prophecy or mystery things on me. Plus I can\u2019t get my superpower back after I use it no more. Plus even more, Ned keeps forgetting me again, cause he\u2019s not as smart as Ji-Woo and Andy and Mags and keeps wandering off too. I got them to believe me, kinda, by showing my bracelet Kel gave me and telling stories and things. Ned told me stories too, while we was climbing the tree and all, but they was all wrong, seeing as I weren\u2019t in none of them.<br /> <br /> The gang\u2019s all proper good superheroes though, seeing as they said they\u2019d help me even though they don\u2019t know they\u2019re my mates. They\u2019re even gonna get the cauldron thing later. I said I'd go rough up Loki and make him fix it while they found the cauldron, but that'd probably be right difficult, so I'm glad they're helping. Ji-Woo said Loki and maybe Heckaty could help. She said Loki probably wanted to study what he did so\u2019s he could do it to him and maybe he\u2019d fix it if I let him. I ain't getting my ear pierced like Ned said. I'd maybe go through the maze though, I like cheese. Ji-Woo said we\u2019d have to trade with Heckaty and she\u2019d do what Heckaty said like she wanted before, on account of it being her fault, but it weren\u2019t, I nicked it, so I weren\u2019t gonna let her, but we went looking for Loki instead any road, even if he is a dickhead, but we shouldn\u2019t say that in case he\u2019s watching, but he\u2019s probably not watching what I\u2019m writing, yeah, so it\u2019s ok. We decided on looking for him on account of Ned knew summat to talk with.<br /> <br /> So we climbed back up the tree. Ji-Woo asked Ned for the dragon drink, so I had to tell her Kel had it. And waked her up up top, on account of Ned were on the phone so it wouldn\u2019t be on to shoot him. He were acting proper odd on the phone, but Hestia said Idun and a bunch of other Norse god ladies were at Malibu and they might know where Himedoll is and he might know where Loki\u2019s at.<br /> <br /> So Ned\u2019s flying us in his plane to Malibu. Planes are a lot less fun when Ji-Woo is sitting by herself with earphones on and all. I tried playing my flute some, but it weren\u2019t the same, by myself. I hate this. Your gang\u2019s not supposed to just forget who you are. It\u2019s not right. I bet Jester probably doesn\u2019t even remember me.<br /> <br /> You probably don\u2019t remember me neither.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> Mum -<br /> <br /> I decided to send that last one, and this one, any road, even if you don\u2019t remember me. If this thing with Loki don\u2019t work, maybe you and the rest of the gods in your gang can help? I don\u2019t have any way to prove you\u2019re my mum, it were always just me and you so you probably don\u2019t remember nothing that had me in it. I do got all the presents you gave me, maybe you\u2019ll know those? Any road, we, I mean, you do fate things, so maybe you can help just to be good to summat what\u2019s proper fucked, like my mates are doing.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re off to Antarctica now. That\u2019s where Himedoll and Tear are, getting dragon\u2019s blood for Odin, Idun said. She didn\u2019t recognize me neither. She had a bunch of friends with her, Sif and Frayer and Scoddy and Thrudd. Thrudd is well fit. I\u2019d been thinking about being a boy again, cause the nymph kept ragging me about being a little and in case, maybe, cause I\u2019m a proper berk, Ji-Woo would recognize me that way. That were well daft, but she did say I were handsome a lot, so that felt a little nice. Ellodia (that\u2019s the nymph) tried to get me and Ji-Woo to have a shag before we left, on account of she thought Ji-Woo had chatted me up in Malibu, but Ji-Woo didn\u2019t want to, on account of Pipa.<br /> <br /> But I did turn into a boy, on account of Thrudd being well fit. She\u2019s well hard too, and proper strong. Me and her and her mom Sif had a proper fun row. Sif won. I didn\u2019t want to hurt her or nothing, yeah? Also, she\u2019s well hard too. Thrudd didn\u2019t know me before, so talking with her didn\u2019t make me sad or nothing, not like listening to Mags tell all of our ace stories without me in them. I think Thrudd liked me though. When Mags remembers me again, I\u2019ll have to get him to tell her the stories proper. Ji-Woo called me a tiger and told me to go get it. We were kinda in a hurry though, so I just talked Mags into a couple more drinks.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re almost to Antarctica now. Kel and Ellodia are off making time and Ji-Woo\u2019s all done with her painting. It\u2019s for Mags\u2019 new album, with Hel and a blonde haired lady and loads and loads of skulls. It looks proper metal. Maybe Mags'll be less angry now.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> Mum -<br /> <br /> I\u2019m proper glad for the scarf you gaved me. Antarctica is proper cold! We found Himedoll and Tear\u2019s camp right quick though. We even met another dwarf, right off. He were right prickly and mouthed off about gods being bullies and all, yeah? He were proper funny, when he weren\u2019t pointing a big fuck off gun right at Ji-Woo. I tried to stand in the way, but I were too short to do it proper. He were well good at hiding too. I didn\u2019t see nothing but the him made of red light until Ji-Woo said he were over there with a gun. That\u2019s why he were pointing it at her. He stopped though when Mags said to, Mags just had to get done with bleeding on a computer first.<br /> <i><br /> End Session XXXIX</i><br /> <br /> So Zane got trapped outside Fate. This made her immune to, but unable to use or benefit from, Magic, Mystery, Prophecy, Samsara, or Deuogdonio. As Deuogdonio is her Pantheon Purview, that is especially rough. Also, unable to regain Legend (from any Source) and people do not remember her outside their presence for longer than minutes=Intelligence + hours=Epic Intelligence. Edmond forgot her a lot.<br /> <br /> Stay tuned for next time, where they fight an Abyssal Dragon and meet Loki. Comments and Questions welcome in the meantime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T13:06:02-08:00","id":371378,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to look in on our group. After the whole Torc fiasco, they need to fix Zane and get back on track.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XL</i><br /> <br /> <u>Six Underground Part V</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Carhenge, America<br /> </b><br /> Well, the cat\u2019s out of the bag now, so I might as well fill you in, Yisheng. To make a long story short, while we were in Helheim, Zane and I decided to steal Hel\u2019s mysterious torque to distract Hel from Gloria Lichtdottir so Gloria wouldn\u2019t succumb to the heart-melting effects of Magnus\u2019 love song. The torque was a trap set by Loki and it cut off Zane from the rest of fate, so none of us remembered her. I still don\u2019t remember her, but I do trust that she is who she says she is, and since she\u2019s apparently one of my best friends, I\u2019m eager to repair her fate. Hel and Loki know all about our hijinks now since we had to track down Loki in order to figure out how to fix things, so there\u2019s no harm in sharing all of this with you.<br /> <br /> Also, Magnus was pretty angry with me for awhile, and he\u2019s still quite annoyed.<br /> <br /> Because of all of this, we\u2019ve been distracted from our original goal of finding the Black Cauldron in order to return Zane\u2019s fate, and so far it has led us into Antarctica and the Underworld, where we had to find Heimdall so that he could tell us where Loki was. Heimdall and Tyr were hunting a dragon of darkness and death, and frankly I was happy to leave them to it once Heimdall pinpointed Loki\u2019s location for us. I don\u2019t like the Underworld anyway, and that particular part of the Underworld was full of desolation and loneliness and hopelessness and it made me feel absolutely miserable, and fighting a dragon wasn\u2019t going to help ANY of that because I don\u2019t like fighting in the first place, even if I do seem to be inexplicably good at it. But everyone else decided they wanted a piece of that action, and they deserve to have some fun too, so I went along with it.<br /> <br /> We ambushed the dragon and had an epic fight. It kept summoning these tough, aggressive zombies, which was okay at first since I was flying around shooting at the dragon. Magnus jumped onto the dragon\u2019s back and tangled with it mid-air, berserking the whole time. Edward and Zane mixed it up with the zombies and helped Tyr protect Heimdall, while Andy helped us with his magic. Everything was going pretty well until some of the zombies decided to use some sort of wind magic to pull me down to the ground where they were able to mob me. I only barely escaped, and then they did it again! They almost overwhelmed me, but Zane and Edward came to the rescue, and then I shot up out of the horde like a firework and plugged the dragon with a few final shots before Magnus finished the beast off and then surfed its crashing corpse to the ground. It was epically metal, I suppose, but I was ready to leave the Underworld, so I might not have appreciated it as much as I could have. Edward got starry-eyed, though, and I suspect he will immortalize the tableau in an awe-inspiring painting soon!<br /> <br /> After harvesting some of the dragon\u2019s teeth and claws to make weapons, we returned to the surface with Heimdall and Tyr. Heimdall pointed us toward a place called Icehenge (well, that\u2019s what we called it, anyway). It\u2019s a place connected to other, similar places across the globe, like Stonehenge and, more importantly, Carhenge, a Stonehenge-like monument in America that\u2019s made of wrecked cars. That\u2019s where Heimdall told us Loki was, so that\u2019s where we went next. Edward wanted to try flying the plane through Icehenge, and I think he really thought it would work. We convinced him otherwise. I love Edward, but he tends to assume that his twisted version of reality will bow to his every whim. Sure, it might do so far more often than it should, but there are limits. In any event, Edward sent the plane back to Berlin with his flight attendant nymph, Alodia.<br /> <br /> I was able to figure out how Icehenge works fairly quickly, and once I did, it was child\u2019s play to open a portal to Carhenge. And there was Loki, looking like Hunter S. Thompson in the film Fear and Loathing in Las Vegas. Magnus took the lead and explained the situation. Loki told us that the torque really was meant to be a gift to his daughter. It was actually some sort of protective ward, but the fate-theft effect was a planned contingency. I\u2019m pretty sure it\u2019s the other way around, though. After all, Loki went through a lot of trouble to make it enticingly mysterious.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t help but pipe up when Loki started talking about some of his theories on fate. I\u2019d actually like to discuss them with him more. Of course, that means spending more time with him, and I\u2019m not really keen on that. He scares me, but I\u2019m willing to put up with it to satisfy my curiosity.<br /> <br /> Edward forgot that Utgard-Loki, not Loki, was the one offering a reward for the torque. For that matter, he forgot that we don\u2019t even have a torque to hand over for the reward, but that didn\u2019t stop him from asking for a new car. So Loki created a hot pink Mazda Miata for him. It was . . . alive, and kept giggling and edging flirtatiously closer and closer to Edward. Unfortunately, I was in no mood to enjoy the absurdity of it because after we explained everything to Loki, Hel appeared. She had been there all along, hidden by Loki\u2019s illusions. I was pretty sure she was going to strike me dead then and there, but she didn\u2019t. She told us she would forgive us for stealing her torque, but only if we offered restitution.<br /> <br /> You know how I said Magnus was still annoyed? Well, he got over most of his anger when we were on our way to Antarctica, but when Hel explained what she wanted from us, all that anger came flooding back, so he\u2019s very cross with me again. And for good reason, I guess. I mean, I AM responsible for all of this, even though Zane is getting most of the blame. And let\u2019s face it, Yisheng, I\u2019m pretty upset about all of this too right now, because Hel wants us to go into yet another Underworld. This time it\u2019s Yomi, and we are supposed to steal some research notes from Izanami\u2019s palace and then go into the Poison Sun Ward to capture and return some sort of undead abomination made from the souls of hundreds of soldiers. Hel and Izanami were collaborating to create this abomination until relations cooled between their pantheons and they had to stop. Izanami kept the results of their experiments, and now Hel wants them back.<br /> <br /> You do realize, Yisheng, that this means I\u2019m going to die, right? I mean, we\u2019re talking about going into the POISON SUN WARD. That place is full of radiation and I\u2019m going to wither away into little more than a shadow-stain. Actually, I won\u2019t even be a shadow-stain, because I don\u2019t have a shadow right now. Andy and Edward assure me that their spirit lanterns will protect me as long as I stay close, but I\u2019m still really nervous. Edward\u2019s spirit lamp looks like a lit marijuana joint. I wonder how potent it is, because I might have to take a few puffs off of it to calm my nerves when we head into the Ward. And there\u2019s also the fact that the Amatsukami don\u2019t really like the Bureaucracy. Izanami might decide to kill me just because she\u2019s petty and it amuses her. Still, if all goes well, maybe she won\u2019t even know we\u2019re there. Is that too much to hope?<br /> <br /> This is going to be bad. I should call Pipa before we head in. It might be the last time I speak to her before I die! I can\u2019t let her know where I\u2019m going, though. She\u2019ll just worry.<br /> <br /> Despite all this, I\u2019m still worried about Gloria. I\u2019m so curious about what she\u2019s up to that I just can\u2019t let it go. So, I consulted the Yi Jing for advice, and here\u2019s what I got.<br /> <br /> Ming Yi (Fading Light ) transforming into Jian (Hardship)<br /> <br /> Both Gloria and my attempts to help her are a fading light, but the Yi Jing encourages me to persevere and not give up. The light can be saved if I keep following the path I\u2019ve begun, and if I do so because it\u2019s the right thing to do (which it is). I have to put aside external distractions and renew my determination, and above all, the transforming lines tell me not to lose hope in the situation just because all my previous efforts have accomplished so little. Well, that\u2019s not exactly true. They\u2019ve actually caused a lot of trouble, but they haven\u2019t really changed Gloria\u2019s situation as much as I\u2019d like, and that\u2019s the problem. Anyway, if I continue to persevere, the Yi Jing says that I should be able to uncover the potential in Gloria and her situation, perhaps saving her from Hel, or perhaps learning more about why she\u2019s really there in the first place.<br /> <br /> So, in accordance with the will of Heaven and the fate revealed to me by the Yi Jing, I have a very serious request, Yisheng. I was wondering if you could find a way to deliver an urgent message to Gloria Lichtdottir as soon and as secretly as possible. I know that you usually have to fill out loads of paperwork for something like this, but I implore you to expedite this request, Yisheng! Even now, Hel could be stealing Gloria\u2019s virtue! And we belong to the Ministry of Virtuous Behavior and Righteous Deeds and Peach Gardens or whatever, so isn\u2019t it our job to protect virtue!? This is very important, Yisheng, but if there\u2019s anything I\u2019ve learned since we started working together, it\u2019s that I can trust and rely on you.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s the message I want you to deliver:<br /> <br /> \u201cDear Gloria, you don\u2019t really know me, but you have seen me. I\u2019m Ji-Woo, daughter of Fu Xi, and I\u2019m the Asian girl who tried to arrange a meeting with you after all hell broke loose at the end of Magnus\u2019 concert the other night. Unfortunately, I had to leave Helheim quickly and wasn\u2019t able to find you because my friends and I were the ones who stole the torque. But don\u2019t worry, Hel knows all about it now, and we\u2019re in the process of smoothing things over.<br /> <br /> I wanted to speak with you because I sensed that you were unhappy being a guest in Hel\u2019s palace. I know you don\u2019t want to succumb to Hel\u2019s advances, and I\u2019ve done what I can to help hinder her attempts to woo you. I also know that at the end of the concert, Magnus\u2019 divine music began to sway your heart, and you felt yourself opening up to Hel\u2019s romantic overtures. It may have been a fleeting moment, but I fear that it might have had an profound effect on you, and I don\u2019t want the power of Magnus\u2019 song to lead you down such a dark path.<br /> <br /> To that end, I beg you to consider this. Where did the emotion that infused that song really come from? It wasn\u2019t Hel. She didn\u2019t write the song. She didn\u2019t perform it. She didn\u2019t pour her heart and soul into it. All she did was make a request. Everything that song made you feel\u2014everything it made you want and desire\u2014all came from Magnus. If your heart is melting, let it melt for him, not for Hel.<br /> <br /> If you are able, and you wish to convey a message to me, you may do so through the Bureaucracy servant who delivers this message. If I can assist you in any way, please let me know how. Also, I\u2019m intensely curious as to why you are REALLY staying with Hel. I know you\u2019re up to something! Maybe I can help. That is, if I don\u2019t die in the next day or so, which is in serious question right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> Got it, Yisheng? It\u2019s all up to you!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> See, Himedoll and Tear were were in the Antarctic underworld place to fight a dragon for its blood and scales. They hadn\u2019t found it yet when Ned found them which were right strange cause Ji-Woo is the one what finds things and Ned\u2019s the one what gets lost. He did find the Norse ladies in Malibu, but I think that were by accident. He still keeps forgetting me. I\u2019ve got a new game for just me - whenever Ned is confused about me being there, I give him a different name what rhymes. We only got to Dane, on account of he wandered off less in Antarctica.<br /> <br /> It were proper empty down there in the Antarctica underworld. The mouthy dwarf had to get the door open for us, but he had to stay at the camp on account of he weren\u2019t allowed to move it. It were big and open at least so Ji-Woo weren\u2019t scared. She didn\u2019t like it none though any road and I didn\u2019t neither. It weren\u2019t empty like a safe place what\u2019s yours and only yours. It were empty like... like not having any mates. Mags is right strange. He liked it a lot, on account of he thought it were proper metal.<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t seem to bother Himedoll or Tear much either way. Tear didn\u2019t like me none at all though. He kept pulling faces at me and talking about me with Mags in giant talk or summat. But he had a big stonking axe and killed loads and loads of zombie blokes, crash! all with one hit, so he\u2019s alright. Maybe he knowed I nicked the necklace. Or maybe he don\u2019t like blokes with no fates. Himedoll didn\u2019t care. He let me look at his blinky thing. It were like a computer or summat with a big globe map on the main bit, with a blinky thing saying where Loki were at. It also had a bit that were flashing through all sorts of different world, like Jotunhime and Helhime and... other himes, I guess? Maybe that\u2019s why he\u2019s called Himedoll. It gaved me a headache, but he could see all the things at once.<br /> <br /> It let him find Loki right quick. He were at Carhenge, which is like Stonehenge, but with cars instead of stones, and even more uglier. There were one in Antarctica too, Icehenge, and Tear said they was all connected, so Himedoll were gonna send us to Icehenge and then we could all go through to where Loki were, but then they said we could fight the dragon too so we did that first! We had to talk Ji-Woo into it, but it made Mags and me happy, so she didn\u2019t need too much talking around. It breathed anti-life! I dunno what that means, unless it means zombies. There were loads of them. I\u2019m well hard, so whatever it were breathing didn\u2019t hurt me none. Andy\u2019s light and Ned\u2019s joint helped too.<br /> <br /> It were bloody brill! Himedoll shot him first, to make him come close, with a big fuck off gun, like a sniper gun thing only he used one hand and it had loads of blinky bits. Himedoll likes blinky lights. Ji-Woo made us all proper fast, so we went off like a bomb. It were ace, being all quick-like. Andy made us better at everything, and Ned boosted me, on account of me being low on superpower and all. I boosted him and Ji-Woo, which were good, cause a zombie what were on fire punched her but good. I were worried all the time, any road, on account of she kept screaming cause they pulled her down from flying. She weren\u2019t proper hurt though, from that or the punching, seeing as she were boosted.<br /> <br /> Mags were well hard! He jumped all the way to where the dragon were flying and wrote a whole new song while he were standing on the dragon\u2019s back chopping his wing off. He even surfed it all the way down bam! when he killed it. He were a little bruised up after, so I fixed him up. He kept the tail what the dragon kept hitting him with. And I got a claw! So did Ji-Woo and Andy. Himedoll and Tear kept the rest, and the eyes, for presents. I should have taked a steak too. Maybe Leo would cook it up for us. When he remembered me.<br /> <br /> Me and Ned helped Tear with the zombies. There were loads and loads and always more, even when Ji-Woo slowed the dragon down by filling him with stars. The dragon were all over black, the blackiest black ever, except where Ji-Woo shot him with stars. She helped with the zombies too, so\u2019s they wouldn\u2019t kill her. I couldn\u2019t hold all of them back, or kill them fast enough. But they all went fwoosh when Mags did for the dragon, so that were good.<br /> <br /> After that, Himedoll did the thing where he took us to Icehenge so we could go to Carhenge but first we went back to the camp place so Ned could tell Ellodia to fly it to meet us. Kell went with her, on account of not wanting to see Loki I think.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> Mum -<br /> <br /> It\u2019s right ace! We found Loki and he said he\u2019d give me my fates back, on account of he learned loads of sciency things by studying me. Only, he don\u2019t know how yet. And Hel is proper angry at me. But Loki said she weren\u2019t allowed to torture me for one thousand years, seeing as he likes your gang (and all the science), so instead I\u2019ve got to nick more things, for a where guilt. I didn\u2019t know what that were, but Loki said it were when a Norse, or a boon companion to a Norse, got caught doing summat bad to summat else and they had to pay up. Mags said Loki were the expert on it, so it all made sense. And it means I\u2019m a boon companion!<br /> <br /> I dunno why Kell didn't want to see Loki, he were nice, even if he didn\u2019t believe I weren\u2019t stealing the necklace, just nicking it to put it somewhere else, to be distracting yeah? He weren\u2019t really ok with it being a distraction though either. That were harder, cause I didn\u2019t know why a song weren\u2019t ok, like chatting summat up, or buying them drinks or summat. But I weren\u2019t going to say it were Ji-Woo\u2019s fault, on account of it weren\u2019t. He said I was cruel to take it, but she\u2019d have it back if he didn\u2019t make it disappear, but he said he didn\u2019t, so I dunno where it is. He said I was brash too, but that\u2019s all right, brash is a good thing. I think.<br /> <br /> Any road, Hel were there at Carhenge invisible the whole time, so that\u2019s why she\u2019s proper narked with me. She made it my where guilt to go to some place called Yomy and the Poison Sun Ward and get a subject and some notes or summat she was making with Izanommy until there were a war said they couldn\u2019t talk no more. The subject were a stonking zombie thing what made up of like a thousand blokes, so it\u2019s proper hard to kill. The the Poison Sun Ward place sounds proper awful. Ji-Woo weren\u2019t happy with it and Mags were well upset again. It didn\u2019t help none that he lost a bet with Ned that I were lying. He ought know by now not to make bets about me. He always loses. And then, Ned said something to Loki about kids being locked up that got Mags in even more in a nark. But mostly I think he didn\u2019t want to go stealing something proper from a different god, but it\u2019s a Norse where guilt thing, so I have to. Loki said, and he\u2019s an expert. I can sneak to the subject bloke and then I have whip thing what lets me talk in German and he\u2019s got to do what I say, so that's alright. The notes will be more harder, on account of they\u2019re probably all sciency and bollocks. But my mates will help and Ji-Woo knows all sorts of sciency things! Plus the notes are in the Yomy place, not the Poison Sun place, so it won't be dangerous for Ji-Woo.<br /> <br /> Loki said he\u2019d come find me next time, when he could fix me. He said my name were Suzanne too. Is that what you and Dad called me before I got stoled? I guess you won\u2019t remember until later. I hope it\u2019s ok if I use Zane still. Suzanne sound like summat who were a little in Dad\u2019s house and had posh dresses and cakes every birthday, and maybe a boyfriend and don\u2019t know how to fight dirty. It don\u2019t sound like me. Sides, loads more things rhyme with Zane and Ned still forgets me.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XL</i><br /> <br /> The Dragon battle was fun. The undead tended to miss a lot, but added successes they missed by from their previous attack to their next, which meant they tended to be really dangerous every other attack. Their damage was midrange, they could not badly hurt Magnus or Edmond. Of course, the Dragon could.<br /> <br /> The next session takes place in the Poison Sun Ward. Do join us.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T14:37:47-08:00","id":371459,"title":"","content":"I'm sure the Poison Sun Ward will be such a thrilling experience that they'll all want to bask in the after glow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T16:30:03-08:00","id":371527,"title":"","content":"LOL. It did prove rather exciting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T02:44:08-08:00","id":384870,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to venture into the Poison Sun Ward. Which, of course, means pissing more goddesses off\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Yomi</b><br /> <br /> I hate the Underworld, Yisheng. It\u2019s awful. And the Poison Sun Ward is the worst! It\u2019s bad enough that it\u2019s in the Underworld, and therefore underground. But sickly green radiation permeates the area, and even though I was protected by Edward and Andy\u2019s spirit lamps, it still made me feel ill. And I couldn\u2019t fly! I mean, I could, but I didn\u2019t want to draw the attention of the leering fighter aircraft that circled above us, just waiting for targets. I don\u2019t like being places where I can\u2019t fly. Even if I DON\u2019T fly, I still like to know I could, if the whim strikes me. You understand, right, Yisheng?<br /> <br /> Anyway, after we arrived in Yomi to get Hel\u2019s abomination and research notes, we had to figure out where exactly we needed to go. So I took a puff off Edward\u2019s spirit lamp and then slowly blew out a stream purplish smoke. I paid attention to the eddies and whirls in the smoke, and they told me everything I needed to know. The abomination was in the center of the Poison Sun Ward, in a place called the House of Pika Don. That was bad news. Pika Don is an aspect of my pantheon\u2019s titan, Hundun, so we decided we would need to be extra careful. Fortunately, the research notes weren\u2019t in the Poison Sun Ward. They were stored in an archive house elsewhere in Yomi. Sadly, the archive house contained a fountain that was crafted to resemble the Jizo, the Buddha of lost children. The fountain filled the archives with the bitter tears of women who had lost their children. These tears were like liquid fire to anyone who had never lost a child, but they would heal and comfort anyone who had.<br /> <br /> Well, none of us have ever lost a child, thank goodness, so I was worried about what we should do. I thought about summoning Pipa, because I\u2019m sure she\u2019s lost children over the ages, but it seemed rather cruel to remind her of her loss. Also, she would probably be very cross with me for calling her to Yomi just in time to visit the Poison Sun Ward. But Edward, Zane and Magnus said they were willing to brave the burning tears to find what we were looking for.<br /> <br /> When we arrived at the archive house, we found a small crowd of grieving women milling around it. It\u2019s a good thing Andy used his illusions to make us look like the rotting dead that inhabit Yomi. Zane even had a worm crawling around his eye socket! It was gross. Edward didn\u2019t really look all that different, though. The house\u2019s courtyard was filled with small Jizo statues of all shapes and sizes. Many of them had small trinkets laid to rest with them: a child\u2019s shoe, a favorite toy, a worn bib. And the whole place rested in a shallow pond filled with the tears of loss. My gods, it was depressing. I was eager to leave as soon as we arrived, but first we had to find the research notes. I described exactly what we were looking for and then Andy and I waited outside while the others waded in to find them.<br /> <br /> It took them awhile, but they didn\u2019t seem any worse for the wear when they emerged. I was worried about Zane, but he seems to be just as tough as Magnus and Edward. Unfortunately, the caustic tears did nothing to improve Magnus\u2019 mood, and he was still really grumpy. He is REALLY moody.<br /> <br /> I must confess, Yisheng, that my responsibility in all of these travails is weighing on me. I\u2019m actually having to deal with the consequences of my actions, and it\u2019s no fun. On top of that, I\u2019m worried about handing over the means to manufacture more of these abominations to Hel. What if she turns against the gods? It could happen. I feel like I should do something about it.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve managed to escape the Poison Sun Ward. I am SO glad that\u2019s over. Edward got us inside using his ability to walk through walls, and like I said before, the spirit lamps kept the radiation at bay. But I couldn\u2019t fly for fear of getting shot down, and even though the blasted city ruins felt empty and abandoned, we occasionally ran across groups of screaming people wreathed in yellowish-green flame. They ran about madly, spreading the flame to others like wildfire. Fortunately, we were stealthy and quiet, and managed to avoid their attention. Zane and I also noticed human-like shadows here and there that only moved when we weren\u2019t looking at them. They were really creepy.<br /> <br /> Every now and then, loud air raid sirens blared across the city. Fortunately, I was able to pinpoint nearby basements or bomb shelters every time that happened, and we took cover from the atomic blasts that seared the ruined cityscape. Of course, for me, the shelters weren\u2019t much better than the bombs. They were tight and dark and they smelled of rotting flesh. As soon as we were closed up inside, my claustrophobia set in and I started to panic. Fortunately, my friends were there to help me. Zane took my hand, and Magnus quieted the roaring bomb blasts outside. Andy did something to make some soothing music and Edward started describing open fields and clear blue skies and brisk winter mornings and soaring birds. There had to be birds. I like birds.<br /> <br /> Speaking of birds, I keep meaning to ask Pipa about Hu Ximei, the nine-headed pheasant who was the third member of the Da Ji trio when they were stirring up all the trouble for the Shang dynasty. Hu Ximei was supposed to be extraordinarily beautiful in her human form, but I\u2019m also curious to see what a real nine-headed pheasant looks like.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, we survived the bombings and the others kept me from completely freaking out. It was a close thing when we had to take shelter a second time, though. There were some mutant radiation zombies hiding in the basement where we took shelter, and they attacked us. I was completely useless because I was already freaking out from the claustrophobia. All I could do was back away from the fight. Andy was right there by my side, though, and he helped keep me from doing something stupid like fleeing the shelter. Damn, claustrophobia sucks. Gods aren\u2019t supposed to have to deal with things like that.<br /> <br /> The others handled the radiation zombies without any trouble, though Edward was hurt a bit, and his wounds sprouted some yellow-black radiation fungus, like the fungus that\u2019s been growing in the Chernobyl reactor. It was repulsive. Edward seemed curious about it and was going to eat some of it to see if it was psychotropic, but fortunately Magnus stopped him and Zane cleaned away the rest of the fungus and healed Edward\u2019s wounds. Edward seemed disappointed, but we convinced him it was for the best.<br /> <br /> After that, it was just a short distance to the House of Pika Don, a deep, crumbling crater in the center of the Poison Sun Ward. Now that we were out in the open again, I wasn\u2019t freaking out, and I was able to pick a safe path for us across the unstable ground into the crater. There wasn\u2019t a lot of cover, though, so when we ran into a herd of the burning people, Magnus decided to cause a distraction so the rest of us could sneak into the crater and get the abomination. He led the burning people on a wild chase around the crater, playing power chords just to taunt them. Of course, all I could imagine was some sort of heavy metal version of Yakety Sax, so that is absolutely what should be in the official report, Yisheng. I\u2019m sure Andy will confirm it if you need a witness.<br /> <br /> Anyway, while Magnus was strumming Yakety Sax on his guitar and skating around with a bunch of burning people in tow, the rest of us clambered down into the crater. We crept through the crumbling pit until we located the abomination. Unfortunately, a couple of the burning people and several of the creepy shadows stood between us and our quarry, but we handled them with ease, especially after Andy used his magic to bless us. The fight caused a bit of a commotion, though, and no sooner had we finished the last of the shadows then the abomination charged us!<br /> <br /> Fortunately, Zane was faster. He dodged under the abomination\u2019s soul-shattering punch and swatted it with Hel\u2019s riding crop. After that, the beast fell right in line, obeying Zane\u2019s every command. He ordered it not to attack any of us and to follow us out of the crater, and we fled as quickly as possible.<br /> <br /> We never actually saw Pika Don, but I suppose that means he never realized we were there, and that\u2019s a good thing. Once we were out of the crater, we signaled Magnus and I used the rune stone Hel gave us to open a portal to Helheim. We escaped through it, and Magnus only barely made it, leaping through just in time before it closed, trapping the burning people on the other side.<br /> <br /> Now I just have to figure out what to do about these research notes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Mum -<br /> <br /> The worst thing about having no fates ain\u2019t that I\u2019m starting to get super-hero tired, like I\u2019m out of juice, yeah? I mean, I am, but the worst bit is the being alone thing. People ain\u2019t supposed to be all alone, nor superheroes nor demigods or nothing neither. Jester told me that, when he first found me. I was on my own then too, after I shoved off from Mum the whore. I thought people weren\u2019t no good, yea, what with the other street littles and adults and coppers roughing me up and taking my things, or the whore using my monies for booze, or the bastards what have a go with littles. But Jester, he were good. He didn\u2019t even push or nothing, he\u2019d just show up and talk, when I were feeling the worst, so\u2019s I weren\u2019t alone along with everything else. I even caught him chasing off some wankers what were trying to mess with me when they thought I were sleeping.<br /> <br /> Then he showed up one day with a little who were sicky and asked if I\u2019d watch over him for a day or two. He were proper little too, and I thought it were crazy to waste time and food on summat who was sick and little and all. But Jester just looked at me and the little were so pathetic I couldn\u2019t say no or nothing, or just leave him there. When Jester got back with special food and medicine and candy, the little were telling me a story. He weren\u2019t very good at it, on account of being little enough he didn\u2019t understand about things being in order and he forgot loads of things but I\u2019d never heard any stories before. The little told Jester that, when he said they had to go so he could have his medicine and all, and he said, Jester did, that maybe I could come with, and he\u2019d finish the story for both of us. So I did, cause people ain\u2019t supposed to be alone. And stories are ace.<br /> <br /> It has been a little better since Carhenge, now that they believe me more, even if Ned and Mags keep calling me kid or the new guy. Ji-Woo is trying proper hard. But it\u2019s just not the same. Something is missing, yeah? She didn\u2019t even know I was well hard, as hard as Mags and Ned no problem! And she thinks maybe I\u2019m one of her boys, on account of Ned said so, which is the worst reason to think something. I mean, he\u2019s right a little, but I were never her boyfriend or nothing. Any road, hopefully we\u2019re done soon and Loki figures out how to fix this so I can be their mate again. And so I can have you and Dad and Jester and everyone back too.<br /> <br /> We got a little distracted going through the portal on account of talking about all the underworld places. Well, Ned were talking about movies. Ji-Woo said he should watch less, cause he were talking bollocks about Japanese and cars or summat. Any road, do we have a special place? Underworld, I mean. Mags said maybe we can go to his, if we die fighting, or bonking summat and we can drink and party forever. But maybe ours is cool too. His does sound much better than Ji-Woo\u2019s, which is loads of hells and hells are bad places, yeah? The Japanese one weren\u2019t so bad, cept for the Poison Sun place. There were loads of zombie blokes all over Yomy, which were good on account of Andy magiced us up to look like them, with maggots and everything. It were proper brill. He said I had one in my eyeball hole what were winking.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo did her thing with the coins to figure out where the notes was. I was right, they was all science-y and stuff and there were a whole bunch of other science-y cobblers there too. Plus it were in Japanese, which has all these weird letters. But Ji-Woo said just what to look for, so me and Ned and Mags didn\u2019t take too long, even if Ned mostly just threw books at Mags. Ji-Woo and Andy couldn\u2019t help, seeing as there were a special fountain of burning water, but only if you\u2019d never had a little what died. None of us even have a little, and songs don\u2019t count even if Ned said they should, so it woulda been ouchy if we weren\u2019t well hard. And I were just as well hard as Mags and Ned, so there.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo weren\u2019t too happy about giving the notes over, nor Mags neither but he got proper brassed off when Ji-Woo said maybe she could make some fakes. I thought that\u2019d be cheating with the where guilt thing, and that\u2019s important so I can be a boon companion so we didn\u2019t. They weren\u2019t too happy about going into the Poison Sun place, or Ned either, but they didn\u2019t think I could sneak by my lonesome neither. So we had to. We got all boosted and Ned and Andy made their lamp things and Ned got us, whump!, through the big metal fuck-off walls.<br /> <br /> Inside it were all exploded and glowy. There were plane noises and shadows what only moved when you wasn\u2019t looking and people on fire and everything were greenish yellow. It thought it were kinda cool, cept I were scared for Ji-Woo. She thought she were gonna die, and said Ned could have her flat if she did, but I told her she weren\u2019t allowed. The part where she couldn\u2019t fly, on account of the planes, were no fun either. And the mushroom thing were just weird.<br /> <br /> See, there was these proper eerie wee-ooooh noises what sounded really bad sometimes. We was sneaking mostly but when those started Ji-Woo pointed at an exploded house\u2019s basement door. I had to get us in, on account of it being locked, but I got it right quick and we got inside, then it were all screaming and lights and badness outside. Mags made it go all quiet the first time and Ned told Ji-Woo a story about horses and birds and open skies and everything so she wouldn\u2019t freak out. The second time there was four stinky blokes with glowy eyes what exploded ick when they got hit. Ji-Woo hid on account of it were all closed up and she\u2019s not well hard and didn\u2019t wanna get icked and then be all sicky. We dealt with them right quick. One of them did plant mushrooms on Ned, but I squished its head and then picked the mushrooms off Ned before he did, and did not give them over, on account of Ned wanted to eat them. I mean, he\u2019d probably be alright, he eats sunglasses, but Mags didn\u2019t even let him eat the small bit he\u2019d broke off, so I kept the big bits away too.<br /> <br /> There was only the two times that happened, and then we got to a big open space around a stonking big hole in the ground where the nuclear explosion had been, Ji-Woo said. That was Peeka Dawn\u2019s house, and that\u2019s where the subject were. Ji-Woo kept leading us, even though we could see it, on account of the ground were all collapse-y and she knows everything like where to step.<br /> <br /> At the edge of the crater there was loads of the people what were on fire and no place to hide or be sneaky. So Mags made them follow him like it were a parade or summat. He were rocking on his guitar and whooshing around on ice. It were bloody ace! Ned said it sounded like angels screaming. Which were right strange, but kinda right too.<br /> <br /> In the middle of the crater were a bright, bright glowy bloke, that were Peeka Dawn, I think, and loads of shadows and two more fire people. Ji-Woo started up on the fire dudes, but their fire went all poof! into ash and they was alright, until she shot them again after they charged and missed her. Then they was dead. The shadow blokes were fast and they hurt my hands to punch, but I\u2019m well hard, so I weren\u2019t proper hurt. We did for all of them right quick, and only Ned got hurt and only a little and he were boosted, so he weren\u2019t really hurt.<br /> <br /> Then the subject started coming for us! I made it so\u2019s I got the jump on it and then tried really hard to hit it with the whip thing so he\u2019d do what I say. I\u2019m not very good at hitting things with sticks or whip things, but I heard Mags\u2019 music and looked at my mates and thought about getting my fates back and tried really hard and hit it whack! right on the knee. Then I told it not to hurt me or Ji-Woo or Andy or Ned or Mags or other people I said later and to let me ride on its shoulders and to go where I said and punch things I said to. We met Mags riding an ice slope down the crater and Ji-Woo used the portal thing and we got right out of there, with me riding up on the big ghost giant zombie subject thing.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLI</i><br /> <br /> So Edmond is crazy. He had this odd thing with his maybe/maybe not existent maybe/maybe not a horse, vampire, or some combination thereof hypothetical child and how the fountain proved Nomde was still alive. Yea.<br /> <br /> The PCs elected to mostly sneak past their enemies in the Poison Sun Ward. They had to go underground when the alarms sounded, and had to fight some monsters in one. Still, it was fairly good work slipping through. Zane of course had constantly lowering Legend.<br /> <br /> But they are back, and Zane gets fixed next time and\u2026wasn\u2019t there something about a Cauldron? Something about that. Comments and Questions Welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T18:10:15-08:00","id":387893,"title":"","content":"well you learn something new every day. I had never heard of radiotrophic fungus before and of course you stir new ideas in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T14:00:26-08:00","id":406092,"title":"","content":"Our Scions have escaped Helhiem. Of course, they have to go back. But first, they need to fix Zane.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLII</i><br /> <br /> <u>Six Underground Part VII</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo's Visions</b><br /> <b><br /> The Dark Forest</b><br /> <br /> After we emerged from the portal from Yomi, I looked around and instantly recognized where we were: the Dark Forest. Last time I was here, I got horribly lost but eventually figured out how to find my way, so I wasn\u2019t worried. Also, we were in an ornate tree house fortress populated by a bunch of distinguished-looking trolls. Well, some of the them looked distinguished. \u201cDistinguished\u201d is actually a very difficult look for trolls to pull off. It\u2019s also difficult for Edward. The trolls with lab coats managed to pull it off better than their more common brethren, though. When one of the lab coat trolls noticed us, he sighed and left to fetch his superiors, and Loki soon came to find us.<br /> <br /> Loki warned us that he had a way to fix Zane quickly but it would rely on the help of a trollwife. At first, I thought he might be talking about Ulfa, but he expressed such contempt at that idea that I realized he must mean Angrboda, THE trollwife and mother of countless monsters, including Jormungandr and Fenris. Hmmm. I guess that should have been my first guess anyway, but I\u2019d rather not get too involved with Angrboda. But we didn\u2019t have much of a choice, not unless we wanted to wait gods know how long for Loki to figure out some other solution. I\u2019ve never been one for waiting, so I was game, and besides, as Edward pointed out, Loki wanted this to happen, so it was in our best interest to play along. Magnus was unhappy about it (big surprise) because Angrboda isn\u2019t exactly a friend of the Aesir, but the choice was really up to Zane, and he decided to go for it.<br /> <br /> Loki took us into the tree house facility\u2019s labs and introduced us to his mistress. Angrboda is a voluptuous Nordic blonde, and she wasn\u2019t really prepared for company, but once she was dressed more appropriately, we discussed the situation with her and she took us to some sort of analysis chamber. I was extremely curious about the process of reversing Zane\u2019s disconnection from fate, so I examined everything she was doing. I think she became a little annoyed at the questions I was asking, but I was curious and they were good questions. Edward was completely confused by the whole experience, but when I tried to explain it to him, he just shrugged and told me that it was okay. I seemed to know what was going on, and he\u2019s confident in my oracular abilities. I didn\u2019t think much of it at the time, Yisheng, but reflecting on it later, Edward\u2019s faith in me means a lot. I haven\u2019t exactly inspired a lot of trust in many of my friends in the past. I guess I\u2019ve moved around too much and left too many people behind. But my scion comrades do seem to trust my insight, and that makes me happy.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Angrboda put Zane on a sort of metal examination table surrounded by all sorts of scientific instruments, some of which were foreign to me. A fascinating holographic display showed Zane\u2019s mystical anatomy, which I examines very closely. Then Angrboda asked which of us had the closest fate connection to Zane, and without skipping a beat, Zane said it was me. We\u2019re supposed to be really close friends. And more than that, we\u2019ve been lovers in the past.<br /> <br /> That was news to me! All this time I\u2019ve been thinking about how roguishly handsome male Zane is, and it turns out Edward was right! Zane IS one of my boys! Not that I get around as much as I used to now that I\u2019m happily involved with Pipa, of course. Or maybe I do? There was that Yrtalion thing in the Unseelie Realm. Hmmm. Still, I was all the more eager to reclaim my memories of Zane after learning we\u2019d had a fling at some point, so when Angrboda said she needed to scan me too, I hopped up on the table without any hesitation.<br /> <br /> After scanning me, Angrboda had a plan to help us. If she could restore Zane\u2019s fatebond to me, it would act as a catalyst to bring all the others back into alignment. She locked the two of us in a weird chamber where she could manipulate our fate strands. We had to remain close and preferably in physical contact for the few hours it took to restore Zane\u2019s fate, and there was a bed in the chamber, so I asked if having sex would interrupt the process. I didn\u2019t think it would. In fact, I suspected it would speed it along. Angrboda seemed fine with the idea, but Magnus got mad again and told us that we could not, under any circumstances, have sex in Angrboda\u2019s labs.<br /> <br /> I should note, at this point, that Magnus was being far more cagey about this whole process than the rest of us. He made Loki promise that Angrboda would not steal any of our genetic material in order to engineer new monsters, and Loki held up his end of the deal, even going so far as to use his flames to incinerate any genetic traces that Angrboda might be able to use. And that\u2019s why Magnus didn\u2019t want us to have sex. It was too risky. After all, it would be awful if Angrboda made some sort of Zanewoogandr to torment us later on.<br /> <br /> So, no sex. Just back rubs and hand-holding. Zane was supposed to focus on an important event from our friendship, so he started telling the story of the one time we made love, which sounded really romantic. And before long, SNAP! Zane doubled over with the pain and shock of having all his fate restored, but the pain only lasted an instant, and after that he was fine. For me, it felt like an electric jolt. And then I remembered everything! I threw my arms around Zane and gave him the biggest hug ever, and several kisses for good measure.<br /> <br /> I am SO GLAD Zane is back! Now things are turned around again in my memory\u2014it\u2019s hard to remember that he was there at all during the past few days\u2019 adventures, but if I really think about it, I can recall a shadow of his presence. It\u2019s a good thing I\u2019ve been filing my journal reports, huh Yisheng?<br /> <br /> Oh, one other thing. It seems my absinthe became radioactive in the Poison Sun War. It was glowing green, and not the sort of green it sometimes glows after I\u2019ve had a few glasses. It was so sad! Sure, it looked pretty, but I can\u2019t drink radioactive absinthe. I\u2019d probably sprout mushrooms or get sick and die. Zane and Edward and Magnus thought it was amazing, though, so they took it and quaffed the whole bottle without mixing it into a louche! Those barbarians have no idea how to enjoy absinthe, and the worst part is that they wanted to see if it made their piss glow.<br /> <br /> Ugh. Boys.<br /> <br /> So anyway, I need to place another order for more Tian absinthe. I\u2019m out. I\u2019d love to have you deliver it to my current location, but we both know how that worked out last time, so I guess you can just deliver it to my home. Also, it\u2019s more important for you to deliver my message to Gloria if you haven\u2019t done so already, so make sure to complete that mission first!<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Well, Yisheng, we dropped off the abomination and research notes with Hel. I hope that doesn\u2019t come back to bite us, but if it does, at least I\u2019ve studied the research. We didn\u2019t stay in Helheim any longer than necessary, though I REALLY wanted to sneak off and find Gloria. I\u2019m am dying to know what she\u2019s up to! Hopefully you\u2019ll be able to dispel the mystery soon, Yisheng. I couldn\u2019t sneak off, though, because Magnus wouldn\u2019t allow it, and I dare not make him any angrier than he already is.<br /> <br /> So now we\u2019re resting in the home of one of Kjell\u2019s acquaintances, a frost giant named Hruk who lives in a village on the edge of the Deathlords\u2019 chasm. Hruk is not happy we\u2019re here, and he\u2019s acting awfully suspiciously. He\u2019s clearly excited about whatever it is the Deathlords are up to, and he\u2019s suspicious of us snooping around. If Magnus and Kjell hadn\u2019t invoked the laws of hospitality, I\u2019m pretty sure Hruk would have tried to kill or capture us by now.<br /> <br /> Also, I don\u2019t like Hruk\u2019s house, because it reminds me of a mausoleum. It\u2019s creepy and it makes me feel like I\u2019m being buried alive, which plucks at my claustrophobia even though the place is spacious enough that I don\u2019t really feel confined.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, Magnus can be pretty manipulative when he wants to be, so he managed to get Hruk to drop his guard and talk about the Deathlords. They were once warriors who would have been worthy of Valhalla except that they were evil and honorless. So when they died, they ended up kind of like powerful Einherjar tied to Death and Frost. Of course, they made a deal with Hel to become what they are now. Currently, they are working with disgusting charnel giants, which means they\u2019ve forged some sort of alliance with Crom Cruach. Andy and I suspect that Crom Cruach is using the Deathlords to acquire the Cauldron, and when we had a spare moment while Hruk was out of the room, we explained as much to Kjell and the others.<br /> <br /> Hruk never mentioned the Cauldron by name, but he did refer to some sort of treasure that lies within the castle at the bottom of the chasm, So at least we know we\u2019re on the right track. Of course, we\u2019ve decided not to stay the night because Hruk is clearly going to betray us, so we\u2019re going to leave at the earliest polite opportunity. Then it\u2019s down into the chasm to find the Cauldron!<br /> <br /> At least Magnus is in a better mod now that we\u2019re back on task. I\u2019ll be better once we\u2019re out of the Underworld entirely.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Well, we\u2019ve made it into the Deathlords\u2019 castle. It just took a bit of creative trickery.<br /> <br /> The depths of the chasm were cloaked in shadow and they were so far away that only Zane and I could make out any details from up above, but the two of use were able to get the lay of the land from the chasm\u2019s edge. A sepulchral castle dominated the chasm floor, and the grounds around it were crawling with patrolling undead vikings and small groups of charnel giants. Standing atop a tall tower of stone and ice near the castle was a sentinel who resembled a skeletal valkyrie clad in icy, bluish armor. Her cold gaze swept the chasm floor, and it was unlikely anyone but Zane would be able to just sneak past her without being noticed. On top of that, a pair of undead dragons soared sluggishly through the darkness in the chasm, ready to pounce on intruders as soon as the Sentinel sensed any trouble.<br /> <br /> Still, we came up with a plan to get into the castle without resorting to violence. I sketched out some drawings of the patrolling undead, and Andy disguised us all with illusion so that we would look just like undead vikings! Then it was a simple matter to climb down into the chasm and make our way to the castle. The only tricky part was that we had to stay fairly close together so that my copy of the Dark Key could protect us all from the soul-chilling cold.<br /> <br /> The rear of the castle was largely hidden from the Sentinel\u2019s piercing gaze, and even Magnus was able to avoid drawing the notice of the guards as we slowly and stealthily scaled the wall to the top of one of the castle\u2019s rear towers. There was a trap door there leading into the castle, but it lay within the Sentinel\u2019s view. Fortunately, she couldn\u2019t watch everything at once, so Andy let us know when her gaze swept away from the tower, and we made a dash for the trapdoor and ducked inside!<br /> <br /> To be continued . . .<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> Hey Dad! I hope you\u2019ve not got worried or nothing, on account of me not writing for a bit. But you didn\u2019t remember me cause Loki put some magic thing on the necklace what I nicked, so I lost my fates. So we went and fought a big fuck off dragon and went to a glowy Japanese Underworld place and got a big fuck off subject zombie to give to Hel to say sorry cause I\u2019m a Norse boon companion. And then we went to a tree hospital! Like, a hospital what\u2019s in a tree, not a hospital for trees, on account of that\u2019s silly.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo\u2019d used the thing Loki gave us to get out of the Poison Sun glowy place, and that\u2019s how we got up in the tree with the giant zombie bloke. It were a tree in the Black Forest place, where we\u2019d got lost before, me and Ji-Woo. Loki got fetched by a troll what was watching for us. He kept calling me Suzanne again, on account of he forgot me too, but his notes and prophecies and things called me Suzanne. He still didn\u2019t know how to fix me then, but he said one of his girlfriends could make it go faster, yeah? Mags looked proper upset, and Ji-Woo too, but Ji-Woo were happier when he said it weren\u2019t Ulfa. Apparently he don\u2019t like Ulfa neither, but he does like troll wives like Ulfa though, cause this bird Angerboda were one, Ji-Woo said.<br /> <br /> First she looked like a well fit regular sized lady in a nightgown thing, but when she saw we was there she left and then came back all giant-sized in a doctor coat, but she were still pretty fit, not like Ulfa at all. Loki were talking her up big time, saying she were good at magic and sex both. I really wanted to be better faster, but I didn\u2019t know nothing about her and Ji-Woo started looking worried again and Mags stopped looking worried right when she walked in and wouldn\u2019t say nothing while she was there. So Loki let me talk with the gang in private before I had to decide.<br /> <br /> They said Angerboda were Hel\u2019s mum, and she had loads of monsters for kids. She\u2019s not really in the Aesir gang though. She even said she were their enemy, but Mags said not always? Politics are confusing. Andy said it\u2019d be alright though, if I got Loki to promise she wouldn\u2019t use my bits or my fates to do nothing bad or make monsters, that she\u2019d just help fix me. He\u2019s sneaky, but if he promises, he\u2019s good. Mags said so too. He had to ask Angerboda proper nice, but he promised.<br /> <br /> So she helped, which meant I laid out on a table with a worn down spot that were person sized. It would make a nice bed. It were even kinda warm, for all it were made of metal and all. It made there be a picture of me, like the dwarf in Antarctica, made of light, except it were flickering a whole bunch cause sometimes it were girl me and sometimes it were boy me. After she looked a the picture a while, and asked Loki what he did (it were from a book he nicked from Odin) she said if she could fix one fate string, they\u2019d all come back. So me and Ji-Woo had to be touching while she did stuff, on account of she\u2019s one of my best mates and Mum couldn\u2019t come down what with the politics and all. Plus, me and Ji-Woo had shagged before (Angerboda were proper confused when I said so) but Mags said we couldn\u2019t have a go there, on account of Angerboda would make us have monsters and Loki said we couldn\u2019t, on account of he couldn\u2019t, even though we had to be touching and everything for hours.<br /> <br /> So I gave her backrubs and held her hand and we talked for about ever then Angerboda told me I needed to think about the first time me and Ji-Woo had a shag, so I started telling the story to Ji-Woo. It stung like a bastard when she did her thing and Ji-Woo got shocked a little bit too but we weren\u2019t proper hurt or nothing. And Ji-Woo remembered me! It were glorious.<br /> <br /> Ned and Mags and Andy remembered me too. Ned didn\u2019t remember that the me without fates were me, but the others did, if they tried. I checked all our fate strings using Mum\u2019s super powers, and they was all right. We have to go get the cauldron now, so I can\u2019t check yours or Mum\u2019s or Jester\u2019s, but hopefully they\u2019re all fixed too, or else you\u2019re very confused.<br /> <br /> Loki offered to take the stonking zombie to Hel for us, but I kicked Ned and said we\u2019d do it, so\u2019s I could say sorry again, but really it were cause the cauldron\u2019s near where Hel is, so if Loki took us there Ji-Woo wouldn\u2019t have to climb down roots and we wouldn\u2019t have to go past Maudegod again. So Loki made us a fire portal and I high five\u2019d him.<br /> <br /> Kell were waiting for us, with loads of empty whiskey bottles. I gave him a hug too, which were almost bad on account of he only kinda remembered me being a bloke, but I had my bracelet, so it were ok. We had some more drinks, me and him and Mags and Ned, of Ji-Woo\u2019s absinthe. It were glowing, on account of her taking it to the Poison Sun place, so she said it were bad. She still got upset at us drinking it from the bottle and not with the water and everything like she does. It did taste kinda funny, but Mags said it might make us have glowy piss!<br /> <br /> Nothing exciting happened at Hel\u2019s. She were still cheesed but I apologized and Mags apologized and I gave her the things and we were set. Ji-Woo were sad cause Gloria weren\u2019t about but Mags were happy about that and said we couldn\u2019t look for her. He did give a well ace talk about being back on the road of destiny that made everything exciting after though.<br /> <br /> Kell had done us good while he were drinking, and took us to talk with his friend Ruck. He were one of the death lords\u2019 gang, but Kell liked him better than the others. He almost made us go away still, on account of the \u2018special\u2019 thing he wouldn\u2019t say what it were, but it were the cauldron down in the pit. Kell got him to talk with Mags though, and Mags is bloody good at buttering people up, so Ruck told us all about the death lords and charnal giants and everything. Not the cauldron though still, just that there was summat what would give the death lords powers.<br /> <br /> Kell thought he were acting right strange, so we left after just a beer. He were proper worried, so he decided to come with and so Mags told Ji-Woo to tell him about the bucket (he meant the cauldron). Kell were ok with the death lords not having that bollocks, so he gets to come be badass with us.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> I think we should take over the death lords\u2019 castle and keep it. After making it so we don\u2019t need the key, yeah? It\u2019s all stonking big, and we had to walk forever down the pit, proper slow, on account of we had to stay close and Andy and Mags is slow, and we had to play pretend like we was dead and all, so I couldn\u2019t even go zooming around them. Any road, there\u2019s skeleton dragons there, and rotting giants and loads of skeletons and some in armor and a lady skeleton what glows blue and is good at seeing, even if she didn\u2019t see me, but I\u2019m the best at sneaking. It were ace!<br /> <br /> On account of having to walk forever, we got Andy to illusion us, seeing as there\u2019s not much to hide behind and the others can\u2019t go invisible. Me and Ji-Woo looked in the pit cause it were too dark for the others to see, and Ji-Woo drew a picture when we decided that the armored skeletons were best. Andy gave me a maggot again, and Ji-Woo looked sassy. Andy said so.<br /> <br /> We decided to walk all the way around the castle, so\u2019s the lady with the glowy blue armor and eyes didn\u2019t see us. I can climb the best too, like one of them little monkeys, and Ji-Woo and Andy can fly, so I made shadowy climbing spikes like you get for second story work on posh houses for Mags and Ned and we didn\u2019t have no trouble, except it were slow. After forever when we got to the top, I got myself to be quick like a rat and went invisible and snuck to unlock the door and Andy peeked out to shoo people in when the glowy lady skeleton weren\u2019t looking.<br /> End Session XLII<br /> <br /> The portrayal of Angrboda was heavily influenced by her portrayal in Scion: Ragnarok. Most of that was actually unplanned; I was asked the day before who would be there when they teleported back by Ji-Woo\u2019s player, and after doing some thinking about twists having Angrboda there seemed like a cooler idea than what I had in mind, so I worked her in.<br /> <br /> The rest was part of the original story plan. You know, the whole main storyline thing. Crazy right?<br /> <br /> Anyway, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T02:01:02-07:00","id":439628,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time for an abbreviated session recap. Inclement weather ended the session early, but we get our heroes out of danger.<br /> <i><br /> Session XLIV</i><br /> <br /> <u>Six Underground Part VIII</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo's Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Helheim</b><br /> <br /> So where was I? Oh yes, escaping from the Deathlords\u2019 castle. Zane and Edward were all set to slide down the spiraling banister to the ground floor, but I said it would be better to emerge on the roof so that we could deal with the undead dragons before we got swarmed by a bunch of charnel giants and undead vikings. So that\u2019s what we did. Zane was disappointed, and Edward wasn\u2019t listening, but since he was riding in the Cauldron and Magnus was carrying him, he didn\u2019t really have any choice in the matter.<br /> <br /> As soon as we arrived on the roof, I dashed to the edge and leapt off, popping my ink wings on the way down so that I swooped right over the heads of the enemy below. That got their attention, especially after I strafed a few charnel giants with my guns. The dragons immediately wheeled about and dove on us. Of course, Andy had a plan. He usually does. He made his zombie giant look really dangerous, with flaming boulders and everything, so the dragons decided to attack it first. Then he told us all to jump onto one of the dragons when it swooped past so we could catch a ride across the chasm. Of course, I was already flying around, so I didn\u2019t jump on, but everyone else did. Then Andy made sure the dragons had bigger problems to worry about, or THOUGHT they did, anyway: he made a huge illusion of an invading Loa force approaching from the chasm\u2019s edge, probably there to punish the Deathlords for attacking them and capturing one of their ghede. The dragons had no choice but to fly up and attack the Loa head on.<br /> <br /> As they ascended toward the lip of the chasm, I ended up dogfighting one of the dragons! It was exciting, and it almost ate me, but I was just a little too fast for it. It\u2019s a good thing I sped up my own time and armored myself with chaos, or I wouldn\u2019t have been quick enough to stay ahead of it. After peppering it with a few well-placed shots, I maneuvered above it and shot its skull to splinters. It went crashing back into the chasm.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, my companions were trying not to get flung from the other dragon\u2019s back. The Sentinel couldn\u2019t get to us, but we were in range for her to fling bolts of enervating darkness and shards of piercing ice. She had it out for Zane, probably because Zane was swinging around the light-eating sword she got from the Deathlord I killed. I guess the Sentinel and that Deathlord were lovers. I feel bad that Zane keeps getting blamed for things that are really my fault. Fortunately, Zane turned invisible to hide while Magnus made sure everyone on the dragon stayed safe using the Cauldron for cover. Kjell went a little crazy, though, and started hacking the beast\u2019s wing off even before they reached the chasm edge.<br /> <br /> Once the remaining dragon crested the lip of the chasm and began breathing fire on the illusory Loa, everyone jumped off, but not before leaving it with a few parting blows to remember them. It didn\u2019t get to remember them for long, though, because they killed it.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Great Power (Da Zhuang) transforming into Persevering (Heng)<br /> <br /> So, I\u2019m going to pause in my recollection of our mad escape from Helheim because I want to say that I\u2019ve had a revelation. Well, maybe not a revelation, but I\u2019ve been thinking about something that\u2019s been at the back of my mind for a long time. Ever since I was awakened to my divine potential and became an adopted daughter of Fu Xi, I\u2019ve been avoiding the responsibilities of my divine heritage. But clearly my companions and I are involved in a heroic journey through the Underworld. And this kind of journey is always a crucible. Magnus may not like it, but we\u2019re invested in our fate now, and since Fate is my sexy sexy mistress, I may as well accept that I\u2019m maturing into godhood. I should be coming out of this with a better sense of who I am. I\u2019d rather keep living the same way I have been since I ran away from home over four years ago, that\u2019s not what Fate has in store for me. Besides, it\u2019s about time I found myself. I\u2019ve been wandering around looking for long enough.<br /> <br /> This means figuring out what\u2019s to become of me as a goddess, and I\u2019m going to try not to grow up to be just like my mother, Chang\u2019e. I love her to death, but I don\u2019t think the Bureaucracy needs two of us.<br /> <br /> I consulted the Yi Jing, of course, and I think it\u2019s been waiting for me to ask about this because it more or less slapped me in the face with the answer. The present hexagram shows that I have great power, and I must persevere in finding the right way to use it. This means I have to look for the right time to act wisely without being anchored to the weight of my own ego or petty desires. I can\u2019t let myself be guided by external distractions. I have to sincerely follow my inner truth: I\u2019m a seer, potentially a very important one.<br /> <br /> If I persevere, I\u2019ll find my path, even though it means I might have to give up some of my freedom. To be honest, a portion of my freedom is an illusion anyway. At least, it is if I really believe in the power of Fate. But knowing that and really accepting it are two different things, and it makes me nervous. I mean, sure, this isn\u2019t the first time I\u2019ve considered this, but these things take time to sink in, you know?<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been feeling guilty about getting Zane to steal the torque, but I\u2019m not sure it was the wrong thing to do, even if Magnus is still grumpy about it. That\u2019s okay, Magnus may be wise, and he may be a great leader, but he doesn\u2019t ALWAYS know best. Sure, I was encouraged to steal the torque by my rampant curiosity, but I really DID want to help Gloria. And I still do. That can\u2019t be bad, can it? If nothing else, it\u2019s not completely selfish, which is more than I can say of most of my actions over the past several years.<br /> <br /> Well, anyway, just knowing I need to take more responsibility and approach things with a bit more wisdom doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s going to happen overnight. I have a lot of bad habits to break, and I don\u2019t actually want to break most of them. There\u2019s no way I\u2019m giving up absinthe, for one thing. Speaking of which, I haven\u2019t had any for at least a few days now, and things are starting to turn gray again. Or maybe that\u2019s just because I\u2019m in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Even if I AM on the path to becoming an inscrutable Taoist immortal, I\u2019m not really sure how I\u2019m going to fit into my pantheon. I bet my brother wouldn\u2019t have this problem. He\u2019d probably know EXACTLY what to do. If I hadn\u2019t stolen his fate, he would probably be an amazing seer. It makes me feel like kind of a loser. But then again, I guess that\u2019s always how my brother makes me feel, no thanks to our mother. And this time I mean my mortal step-mom, NOT Chang\u2019e.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I can\u2019t bear the thought of sitting in an office doing Bureaucracy paperwork, so there must be some other role for me. I confess that I\u2019m intrigued by Da Ji and Pipa and the important, if questionable role they play in the Bureaucracy. I should talk to Pipa about this. I wish she were here, because now that I\u2019ve been thinking about my brother and how awesome he would be at a becoming a god, I feel like a complete fuck up.<br /> <br /> To be continued . . .<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Then I were a little upset cause we\u2019d decided to go out the front door, so I were gonna go down the bannister, but then Ji-Woo said we should go up to the roof instead, so that all the little zombies couldn\u2019t get at us, just the dragons. It woulda been a little fun I guess to jump off, like to the blue lady\u2019s tower and then down again, but Andy had the best idea ever. He thought maybe we should ride the dragons like they was a plane, and he\u2019d make them think loads of blokes was attacking the deathlords\u2019 place from where we was trying to get to, so the dragons\u2019d fly off that ways.<br /> <br /> So I were good and didn\u2019t even complain too much. Ned were still going to go down the bannister and come back up, but Mags held the bucket way up close to the ceiling so\u2019s he bumped his head and couldn\u2019t get out. I might thought about it too for a bit but I didn\u2019t want to make Mags more upset, even though I could get back quick enough I\u2019d pass him anyways. But we had to get all boosted on the way up, so\u2019s we could fight the dragons, yeah, so I didn\u2019t. I gave Ji-Woo piggyback ride up the stairs so there was some fun and all. I guess it were more a rattyback ride, on account of I\u2019m real good at being like a rat now, so I can move well fast and think proper fast too, and I\u2019m good and tough.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo launched off as soon as we got on the tower, and started making a big show, swooping around and shooting at blokes, so\u2019s they send the dragons over. Mags started waving the cauldron around and yelled out that we had the fucker\u2019s bucket. Then he put it down like a big shield or summat. First he had to tell Ned that he\u2019d gone down the bannister already and just didn\u2019t remember, so\u2019s he wouldn\u2019t try to do it again.<br /> <br /> Andy\u2019s zombie giant Reginald were being all tough too, pretending like he had summat big to throw. I bet Andy made it look like he did have summat, on account of the blue lady and the dragons both were after him hard, even after I shot one of thems. I didn\u2019t hurt it too much, but it dented up one of its rotty scales and then Ji-Woo hit right there and blowed a big hole in it. She\u2019d made herself go well fast, and shot up one of the dragons, the one we wasn\u2019t on, right good. She didn\u2019t have to be on a dragon, see, on account of she can fly so she were zooping around a lot. The dragons kept after her, seeing as she were messing one up pretty bad, but they only bit her inky wings a little and it didn\u2019t hurt her none, just got ink black all over their teeths. Then she exploded the other one's skull!<br /> <br /> It were exciting on the dragon too. Mags scooped me up with the pot on account of I weren\u2019t quite ready seeing as I shot at the other dragon, so I had to kinda scramble out to stand proper. Then I decided I were gonna look proper metal so Ned could paint me on one of Mags\u2019 music pictures, so I stood on its head all heroic and everything, with the well dark death sword. I were proper metal - Ji-Woo said so. But then the blue lady got all mad at me. Ji-Woo thinks maybe she were the death lady lord\u2019s girlfriend so she were upset I had the sword even though I didn\u2019t kill her or nothing. I didn\u2019t even steal it, cause she were dead and so it weren\u2019t stealing.<br /> <br /> Any road, she hit me with more shadowy darkness icky stuff kinda like the sword but sorta liquidy and it hurt like hell. I popped up out of Mags\u2019 shadow though, and were alright, and I\u2019m well hard, so the second bit were only a scratch and Ned had boosted me anyways. I went invisible after that, and Ned thought I\u2019d gone away again, so I tugged on his ear and turned him to Spanish. Kel started cutting the wing off on the dragon we was riding, so the dragon started getting a bit wobbly, but we was almost there so it were alright. The blue lady didn\u2019t like that neither, and I were invisible, so she threw her sword at Kel, but Mags batted it away with the pot.<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t take too long before we was at the cliff out, so I guess Andy\u2019s illusion worked. I think he made it so Ned could see it too, on account of he kept going on about summat in Spanish, and pointing. He yelled out a warning right before we jumped off, to the nothing that the dragons were breathing ice at. He didn\u2019t even think about popping the dragon one on account of being worried about our imaginary friends. Me and Kel and Mags did though, and we finished it off. I even pulled one of its teeths out, one what was covered in Ji-Woo\u2019s wing ink. Ned were proper surprised when he landed on the ground and not on whatever he were jumping at, but we was all alright - I were the only one what were even a bit hurt, and that\u2019s on account of the blue lady\u2019s darkness.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLIV</i><br /> <br /> Not much to add. We ended about an hour or two early, as when we started it raining some, but we decided to keep an eye on things. One player happened to, when on a restroom trip, notice the back yard had turned white. Looking out it was snowing and we (very) quickly broke and folks headed out. Everyone made it home okay.<br /> <br /> Saltmarsh Andy created an illusion of Loa forces at the mouth of the ravine (with a bong cannon, because Andy is strange) and while he only needed to affect the enemies, he decided to affect Edmond, because seriously why not?<br /> <br /> Also, Kjell continually attacked the Dragon he was standing on\u2019s wing despite needing it to survive to edge of the valley. That\u2019s Kjell, like a Koala in the rain, no fucks given.<br /> <br /> Full session next time. Carhenge will never be the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T15:52:59-07:00","id":459458,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to look in on our Scions as they escape Helhiem and begin the next phase of their quest.<br /> <i><br /> Session XLV</i><br /> <br /> <u>Six Underground Part IX</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo's Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Guinee</b><br /> <br /> Now we are in Guinee, and I have to say, this is by far the best Underworld I\u2019ve been in. There\u2019s partying and alcohol and everyone is carefree and happy. The whole place sprawls across the sea floor and the cerulean shades of the water reflect off everything with hypnotic patterns that really come alive under when the absinthe is coursing through me! Sure, the murky depths beyond the borders teem with hungry specters and bloated monsters, but the Loa keep those things at bay, so there\u2019s nothing to worry about. At least as long as Mami Wata doesn\u2019t get the upper hand, which I guess is sort of why we\u2019re here.<br /> <br /> Before we arrived in Guinee, though, we had to get out of Helheim. We decided not to pass by Modgud, even though I thought it would be hilarious for Edward to pop out of the Cauldron singing \u201cHappy Birthday Mr. President\u201d like Marilyn Monroe. I\u2019d like to think that Modgud would have been so baffled by it that she would let us pass by, but Magnus didn\u2019t want to risk it, so instead he made an ice raft and we poled our way across the river.<br /> <br /> Then it was back up the ash tree, so of course Zane gave me more of that Dragon Brew to knock me out. When I woke up, we were in Carhenge again. Zane and Edward were both women, which led Kjell to comment that he\u2019s glad that at least I am ALWAYS a woman, though he apparently thinks my breasts should be bigger. Or maybe he was just trying (successfully) to get me to flash him. Whatever. Zane and Edward were ordering pizzas and Alodia was on her way with the plane, so Magnus and I made our way to the closest town to pick up more absinthe and whiskey. I needed my fix. All they had on the shelves was that fake American crap that doesn\u2019t even have real wormwood in it, but the liquor store clerk had some authentic Czech absinthe stashed in the back and was willing to sell it to me for twice what it\u2019s worth. Jerk. Then Magnus convinced him a discount would be better than a markup.<br /> <br /> Anyway, by the time we got back, Alodia had arrived with the plane and we were ready to go, so we flew off to Ireland so that we could stash the Cauldron with the Unseelie and then head out to Guinee. Our stop with the Unseelie was short, but I was able to get some more of the Weeping Absinthe. That stuff is wonderful. Not as good as Tian absinthe, but still, the hint of bitterness really gives it a unique flavor, and the way it opens my mind is very exciting. I think Glykeria would like it. I also got to see Yrtalion again, but sadly, we didn\u2019t have any time to fool around. Besides, I don\u2019t think I would enjoy it as much without Pipa. Also, I might have pimped Yrtalion out to Marissa.<br /> <br /> Anyway, once Yrtalion took possession of the Cauldron, we were off again into the sea and down to Guinee. I would go on about Zane\u2019s paddle boat (which should have been a swan boat), but I was a little distracted because, honestly, my companions have been a storm of distraction since we left Helheim. Keeping us on track is like herding cats, and I have to admit that I\u2019m having a bit of a hard time dealing with it given my new sense of purpose.<br /> <br /> Also, I have discovered that Zane and I have developed a new fatebond. Apparently, Zane gets blamed for some things that are actually my fault. She seems to be okay with this since she\u2019s good at getting out of trouble and she likes to look out for me. I think it\u2019s pretty interesting, personally, though I guess I do feel a little guilty about it. I should probably stop using my divine charisma to keep others from getting mad at me when Zane\u2019s around, but I really can\u2019t help it.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> How the hell did I end up in a tight, stuffy tunnel in the most open, least claustrophobic Underworld there is? I mean, really. I know we\u2019re taking the tunnel to get to the Ladle secretly, but I\u2019d rather risk tangling with Mami Wata\u2019s minions in the reef than crawl through this place. I\u2019m actually dictating this out loud and using my Qi Hand to write while we creep through this awful place. It was Zane\u2019s idea. It keeps me distracted. We\u2019re also swimming circles around Magnus and Kjell, which is fun and helps me feel less constricted in here. The brothers are not amused.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we met Baron Samedi\u2019s wife, Maman Brigitte. She was delightful! Casual, fun, and no-nonsense. I really liked her. And I think I made a good impression when I gave her a bottle of the Weeping Absinthe as a present. We drank some of it while she told us where the Ladle is.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, one of Mami Wata\u2019s sea monsters is lurking around the spot where Marissa buried it. Coincidence? I think not. The charnel giants are a step ahead of us, and they are already moving against the sea monster with the support of some sort of ghost ships they dredged up somewhere. Maybe they\u2019ll wipe each other out so we can swoop in to take the Ladle, but somehow I doubt it.<br /> <br /> Oh, you have got to be kidding me! This tunnel gets even narrower? And they collapsed it? Wait, what? You can\u2019t be serious. There\u2019s no way I can crawl through that tiny little passage! Yes, I know that if Magnus and Kjell can fit through it, so can I. That\u2019s not the point! No, I don\u2019t care how hard those zombies worked to clear it, I\u2019m not going through there! I can\u2019t!<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know how, but somehow Zane got me through the passage. She held my hand and pulled me through. I just let her drag me and kept my eyes closed. I was trembling so bad once we emerged on the other side that by the time I got control of myself again, the others had already killed the giants that were waiting to ambush us.<br /> <br /> Now we just have to go get the Ladle. The sea monster, giants, and ghost ships are still engaged in a battle that would make Hollywood proud, and it looks like there are some carnivorous mermaids trying to dig up the relic while the Deathlords\u2019 forces are distracted. I think Zane and I can handle those while Magnus, Andy and Edward take on the sea monster. . .<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> The undead blokes were proper distracted by whatever Andy\u2019d done, so we got up and over the cliff without no problems. We talked about how to get out to Andy\u2019s Underworld place while we went the long way round the other frost giant town. Ji-Woo kinda wanted to go by Kel\u2019s place, Jotunhime, so\u2019s we didn\u2019t have to climb up the tree what\u2019s all tight, yeah? But then the other Loki, the Utgard one, might want to know about the cauldron, even if I made a shadow blanket to go over it. Same if we went out the tree way, cept with Maudegud. So instead Mags made a boat out of ice and we got over the river that way. Ned wanted to turn the cauldron into a hot air balloon, but it\u2019s far too heavy, so that\u2019s just daft. Instead he hid in the cauldron under the blanket on account of if summat did wanna see, he could bust out and sing them happy birthday and call them president. He\u2019s right strange.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo had more of the good booze what Kel has to pass out for the tree bit. Kel kept teasing her that she didn\u2019t have enough tits and the booze\u2019d give her more. He\u2019s dead wrong about the more tits thing, but he did get Ji-Woo to flash hers at him so maybe he were just being tricksy. She wound up drinking it any road and I carried her up.<br /> <br /> We came out at Carhenge on account of it being the last non-superhero kinda place we was at. Mags knocked on the cauldron to get Ned out so\u2019s he\u2019d call for the plane. He thought it were the signal to sing, so he started taking off his clothes. Kel grabbed his face though, he does that a lot, until Ned called Ellodia. First he were telling her to come to the United States, then Stonehenge, on account of the United States is a big place, then Carhenge, on account of that\u2019s where we was, but for the last two he forgot to dial her again. Then he called the pizza place instead. So I nicked his phone and told her where to come.<br /> <br /> We had to wait though, on account of she lost the plane. Ji-Woo wanted absinthe, so I called the pizza place back too. They didn\u2019t have none though, just coke, so she and Mags fucked off to the town so\u2019s she could get some. They got back with loads of whiskey in a big fuck-off barrel and some absinthe right just before the pizza did and the plane. The plane knocked over some of the stacked up cars, so we got out of there fast, before the coppers could nick us, even though Ned wanted to take pictures with some old bint. Mags and Kel did try to put the cars back.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo\u2019s drinking her absinthe now, and says the colors are coming back. She keeps going on about the blackness in my ace new sword fighting with the blackness in Mags\u2019 heart, specially once Ned started on talking about using the whiskey he brought for the hot air balloon idea. I\u2019m gonna make the balloon part out of shadows, once we\u2019ve got all the bits.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> Well, now we\u2019ve got one of the three bits safe with that Urtalien bloke. He\u2019s got a castle for it, and a right odd bed what makes noise by itself, crying sad kinda noises, Ji-Woo said. She got more of the little\u2019s tears absinthe too,while we was at Andy\u2019s Underworld place. I kept giving her looks about it but in secret I were still happy about getting to play music with her on the plane, so it were ok, I guess. They kept saying they didn\u2019t make the little\u2019s cry or nothing...<br /> <br /> Kel were fun there, in the Underworld place, even if he thinks its weird when I change. I\u2019m a girl again now, on account of Marissa didn\u2019t know I could so I showed her. Ned\u2019s a Maenad bint too, on account of he started wearing Ellodia\u2019s pants and Mags said they was for girls. But Kel didn\u2019t like riding horses neither (he kept calling them ponies too) so me and him ran and played catch with the cauldron. It were proper ace! Cept when it made Ji-Woo\u2019s horse go funny caused Kel throwed it over her head. But she were alright.<br /> <br /> Once we got back out of the she/sidhe thing, we had to go out in the ocean to get to the Genay place. I made us a boat out of shadows, so I made one of the little pedalos like they got on the Thames, but big so\u2019s we could all fit. Me and Ned paddled, on account of us being well hard and Mags rowed the whole time in Helhime. Plus, Ned said he would race me. Ji-Woo were sad it weren\u2019t a swan and Mags were well upset and said we weren\u2019t allowed to be pirates in it. I hadn\u2019t been thinking about being a pirate but then he said we couldn't and it sounded like loads of fun. We had to get to Genay though, so we\u2019ll be pedalo pirates later.<br /> <br /> Once we got far enough, I stopped and let Ned keep racing so\u2019s that we started spinning on account of Andy said we needed a whirlpool. A proper one didn't show up until we\u2019d all jumped in and then we was underwater but could breathe and we could walk like normal or swim and it were like flying. We went to a village place what had fish swimming all around and loads of people with skull-faces like Marissa. There was shark people too, but they was all outside and not invited to the party. We was though, so we danced and had rum and Andy told stories with me in them until Marissa came back.<br /> <br /> She said Maman Bridget wanted to talk with us, and Ji-Woo thought maybe that meant we was in trouble, on account of she\u2019s in charge I think, but Marissa said we wasn\u2019t. Ned were upset she didn\u2019t have no drums, seeing as we was on tour, so I made her some from shadows. The concert were right ace. But first Ji-Woo gave Bridget one of her absinthe\u2019s from the Unseely place, and Bridget told us about the sea monster. I like Bridget. She\u2019s not posh or nothing even though she\u2019s in charge and she talks like a real person.<br /> <br /> She said the sea monster were made of drowned people and didn\u2019t talk, but the people tried to sometimes. It were bigger than her house and her house were well huge. It were guarding the ladle bit, and eating the giants and their ghost ship and skeletons, but Bridget thought it were from Mommy Water. I asked Ji-Woo later, to distract her from the tunnel and she said that Mommy Water were the skull-faced people\u2019s Titan-bottles and that she\u2019d the Queen of the Drowned Roads. So it were bad that it were near the ladle.<br /> <br /> We had to go through some caves to get there. Well, we didn\u2019t have to, but else we\u2019d have had to fight loads of the shark people called specters. Ji-Woo weren\u2019t happy, but they was big caves, so me and her swam in circles around Andy and Mags. But then there was a rockfalled part at the end and a pirate what was holding his head in his hands on account of it had falled off. He said the giants had found the cave so they exploded it shut, but Half Blind Steve, he\u2019s a zombie what only had half a head, and the other zombies what had all of their heads, had carved up a tunnel for us. Griseld, she\u2019s a zombie too, what talked like falling people screaming, said most of the giants was off getting a bigger boat.<br /> <br /> Ned traded a little bit of coke for a map with a big red X on it, so\u2019s we knew right where the ladle were. Then we had to go through the tunnel. I pulled Ji-Woo along on account of her eyes was shut, but it weren\u2019t too long. Then we got to fight some more giant blokes. It were proper fun, on account of the water made it like flying. Mags got to make his axe halfway through swinging it!<br /> <br /> I did for one of them. I punched it and it exploded like stars and Ji-Woo winked at me. Mags did for the other two. They didn\u2019t explode though. One was going for him but missed on account of him singing. The other cut Kel in half! But he were alright and distracted the one by pointing at Ji-Woo so Mags could finish it off.<br /> <br /> After that we had a butcher\u2019s at the monsters. It were a big stonking thing, all over with drowned people like Bridget said. There was a bunch of mermaids too, like the pirate said, so I thought I better plug up my ears. There was 8 giants still, and a death knight, waiting on the big boat. There was a cave fish too, with a little light on its head, what looked like one of them eel things, but big like a bus. A regular one, not a double decker or nothing. It were proper strange looking.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLV</i><br /> <br /> So the next session was a big setpiece fight. As for this one, we finished the last part for Helhiem.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo\u2019s color issues are a character thing. No system for it.<br /> <br /> See you next time, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T01:53:12-07:00","id":472414,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time for a throwdown in Guinee. Here are two accounts of the battle.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLVI</i><br /> <u><br /> Six Underground Part X<br /> </u><br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Guinee</b><br /> <br /> Two down, one to go. Getting the Ladle was no problem at all, except that I had to go through a really tight tunnel, TWICE. And I almost died. It\u2019s a good thing I\u2019m an ace at using Taiyi to block adverse mystical effects, and that I\u2019ve got Zane, Magnus, Andy and Edward here to back me up.<br /> <br /> We split up. Andy kicked things off by summoning an illusion to distract Mami Wata\u2019s sea monster and lure it toward the ghost ships, not that it really needed any encouragement, since they were already shooting at it. Still, it kept the beast from paying any attention to what Zane and I were doing. Edward, Kjell and Magnus charged into the fight and boarded the Deathlords\u2019 ghost ships, the largest of which was captained by the legless Maggot Hag we fought in the Deathlords\u2019 castle. Edward proved to be more clever than usual, and since he knew we couldn\u2019t easily kill the Maggot Hag, he distracted her by doing a Marilyn Monroe \u201cHappy Birthday Mr. President\u201d lap dance routine, which boggled her mind enough to keep her from assisting her crew while Magnus and Kjell plowed through them.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Zane and I sneaked through the coral forest toward the patch of sea floor where Marissa told us she\u2019d hidden the Ladle. There was a coven of flesh-eating mermaids there looking for it, but once Zane was in position to start looking, I summoned several whirlwinds with streamers of fox-spirit ink to trap the mermaids and keep them from interfering with Zane\u2019s search. Unfortunately, the ghost ships noticed, and no sooner had Zane begun burrowing into the sea floor than they started firing on us. I was nowhere close to ground zero, but the blast wiped out all but one of the mermaids. I finished off the last of them by crushing her in the winds, but by then the ghost ships had deployed a team of skeletal divers that descended on us and began their own search for the Ladle.<br /> <br /> I twisted time around Zane to help speed up her search, then started shooting skeleton divers to thin their numbers and slow them down. It was working until a pair of brutal, angry Deathlords came swimming from the ship to protect them, and I ended up in a fight against a pair of undead ladies who REALLY wanted me dead. I started dueling one, and she was a good match for me! She wielded a jagged whip made of spinal vertebrae, and it was all I could do to dodge her lightning fast strikes while trying to pin her down with gunfire. It didn\u2019t help that her heavily-armored friend was harassing me with all sorts of unpleasant magic. First, she made me horribly ill with plague magic, but Zane swam up like a dolphin and healed the sickness before it could slow me down much. Then the Deathlady tried to tear the moisture from my body, but I was able to block the effect with Yin Yang Destruction. Whip Girl also tried to freeze me in a block of ice, but I stopped that effect too. Those ladies ran me ragged deflecting their magic! It\u2019s a good thing I\u2019m awesome. Also, Andy helped me out with his blessings. Go Andy! He\u2019s like the best cheerleader ever. Note that I said \u201clike\u201d the best cheerleader ever. The REAL best cheerleader ever would look better in a cheerleader\u2019s get-up. I mean, Andy\u2019s hot and all, but cross-dressing tends to undermine some of the allure of a real cheerleader. And honestly, I\u2019m not really into cheerleaders anyway. It\u2019s such a hopelessly American thing.<br /> <br /> Anyway, by the time I got the upper hand against Whip Girl and managed to finish her off, Magnus came hurtling toward us and slammed into the other Deathlord like a shark. He made short work of her, finishing her off much more handily than I finished Whip Girl, but the Deathlords had accomplished their goal. I wasn\u2019t able to keep the skeleton divers from finding the Ladle before Zane. Fortunately, Zane is not above a little theft, so she destroyed the diver carrying the Ladle with a single punch (\u2018cause as we all know, she\u2019s the best at punching) and snatched the Ladle right out of the enemies\u2019 hands.<br /> <br /> The skeleton divers are poor losers, though, so they all exploded then. I was far enough away that I wasn\u2019t hit by anything other than a bone-jarring shockwave, but Zane was in the thick of it and almost died. Fortunately, she managed to survive by hiding in her own shadow, but I was worried she\u2019d really get hurt, so I told her to disappear and retreat with the prize! And the I started retreating. I mean, the sea monster was still standing, and one of the ghost ships was still afloat, but I\u2019d had enough fighting for one day. I hesitated only long enough to grab Whip Girl\u2019s bone whip. I\u2019m going to give it to Pipa. It seems like her kind of thing, so I think she\u2019ll really love it! I hope so. I worked hard to get it!<br /> <br /> Anyway, we were beating a retreat, but I was NOT going back into that tiny little tunnel again. I\u2019d already had a hard enough time in the fight and I was tired of almost dying, and I could only imagine the thing collapsing on me because it was weakened by all the explosions from the battle or something. Anyway, I was too afraid to go back in, so I was going to find my way back through open waters. But Fate, my cruel mistress, decided otherwise. Actually, it was Kjell who decided otherwise, but of course he\u2019s Fate\u2019s bitch too.<br /> <br /> See, Kjell set a ghost ship\u2019s powder stores alight, which utterly destroyed the rest of the Deathlords\u2019 ships and sent Kjell shooting through the water, over the coral forest, and right into the entrance to the tunnels. Both Edward and I happened to be swimming away along his path, so he grabbed us both as he flew by. I had no choice but to hold on tight and bury my face in Kjell\u2019s manly chest as we slammed into and then through the tunnel, making it a little bigger and then much smaller as it collapsed behind us. Kjell, being the lovable thug that he is, held me close and protected me from the impact with his body. I think I screamed a lot, but I was nearly senseless with fear and surprise, so I\u2019m not sure.<br /> <br /> Even if Kjell he does pick on me a lot, I like him. I don\u2019t think you\u2019d care for him, though, Yisheng. He\u2019s kind of boorish and crude, and I know you have a thing for propriety. Don\u2019t worry, though. Kjell\u2019s not really the kind of guy I usually hook up with, so I don\u2019t think you have to worry about him becoming \u201cone of my boys,\u201d as Edward likes to put it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> We wound up leaving the cave fish alone, on account of it were the other way from the giants and all. Andy started it all off by making a hairy man monster things, what Ned called a Yeti and a Sasquatch, have a butchers over some rocks, then chuck one at the stonking drowned people monster. We got all boosted up first though. Andy boosted everybody, but Ji-Woo only boosted not me and her, seeing as the monster were gonna be chasing them. But she gave them booze to do it, and that weren\u2019t fair, so I stoled some of Kel\u2019s. Mags said liquor were his mistress and Ji-Woo said it were her muse and then it got weird, cause Ned said it were a miscreant and Andy said it were muskrat love, which sound proper rank. I didn\u2019t know any other m-words cept mum, and liquor\u2019s not my mum, so Ji-Woo decided it were my monkey. My mates is well strange.<br /> <br /> After all that though, it were time to find the ladle. I were invisible, and proper sneaky, so none of the bastards messed with me none, but I were looking by myself, and there was 12 of them skeletons, and then I had to heal Ji-Woo, so it weren\u2019t fair or nothing either, so it don\u2019t count as them beating me, even though they found it first. I took it off them though, and then exploded one by punching it, so there.<br /> <br /> See, the bigger boat showed up right when we\u2019d got to where the red X said to go. Ji-Woo had just got the mermaids tangled up with foxes made of ink when the boat threw bombs at us! I weren\u2019t hurt proper, on account of I\u2019m well hard and Ned boosted me, but most of them mermaids got exploded. Ji-Woo got her foxes to crush the one what were left.<br /> <br /> But then the boat let off like a bazillion Viking digger skeletons and they started looking for the ladle, plus two death ladies lords. One had this ace bone whip thing, Ji-Woo took it for Pipa. I were still faster than the skeleton diggers, but the death lady lord without the whip made her all sicky. If I hadn't done a proper good job of boosting her, she\u2019d have been hurt bad. So I went zoosh! out of the hole like I were one of them dolphins but invisible and got her healed back up.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo did magic with her brush next time they tried to use superpowers on her, so she didn\u2019t get sicky again, or all frozed up neither. She shot right through the ice, and did for the whippy death lady lord. Mags got the other one, after he got the giants. He can run proper fast, when he feels like it. He\u2019s just usually slow. The ice ramp he were skating on helps, yeah? He did get a little hurt, with all that, but it were just bruises and nose bleeds and things. I patched him up right quick once we was done.<br /> <br /> Ned and Kel fucked with the ship instead. Ned made the Captain come out and it were the woman what was just a top half! She decided to start taking off her clothes, Ned did, and started singing Happy Birthday to her. She were upset on account of the old lady didn\u2019t have no lap. So she asked the pilot bloke for his. I think everyone were well confused. Kel busted up the cannon but good, so it didn\u2019t get to throw no more bombs at us, yeah? Then he exploded the ship! He used it to push him to the cave again and grabbed up Ned and Ji-Woo on the way.<br /> <br /> First though, we\u2019d got the ladle. Like I said, the skeleton diggers got it first, but they was cheating, so I busted the one with it up with a big stonking seashell I was wearing on my fist and took it back. Then they exploded, all but one. There was lots of explosions, is what I\u2019m saying. It blew me right away, but I were alright - I popper out of the shadow of one of them coral things. Ji-Woo told me to disappear again, so I got really sneaky, but first, I punched the last skeleton and it exploded too. That didn\u2019t hurt so much though.<br /> <br /> The boat exploding didn\u2019t hurt none either, on account of we was so far away. Kel is well hard though. Ji-Woo still screamed the whole time after Kel grabbed her and in the tunnel, but she were alright really. I got Mags fixed up with a drink from my canteen, even if it started floating and he had to slurp it up from the air-water. He said it were good pirating, on account of there not being any paddle boats, just giants and skeletons and cannons and sea monsters. Plus, we got treasure!<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <i><br /> End Session XLVI</i><br /> <br /> The session was full length, just lotta combat.<br /> <br /> Zane mixed up which Skeleton used Health on Ji-Woo. She was accurate in her\u2019s.<br /> <br /> Edmond\u2019s bizarre \u201cHappy Birthday Mr. President\u201d lapdance/striptease is one of the most disturbing stunts for Paralyzing Confusion I have seen.<br /> <br /> Kjell lit the ship on fire to destroy it because he passed his Courage roll so had to either keep fighting or spend a WP. He elected to finish the fight explosively, and survived only due to Skin Shedding, even if he is a Frost Giant.<br /> <br /> Not much to add past that. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T13:26:04-07:00","id":488634,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check back in with our Heroes, as they heroically get a fairy drunk and shanghai her into joining their mission they sidetracked because \u2026well, it\u2019s complicated.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLVII</i><br /> <br /> <u>Six Underground Part XI</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Unseelie Realm</b><br /> <br /> We\u2019ve dropped the Ladle off with the Unseelie, though in the end, we\u2019ve decided to give it to the Loa for safekeeping. It\u2019s probably best if each piece of the Dark Cauldron set is kept by a different faction. That way no one can use its full power. I\u2019ve also decided that the last piece, the Pestle, needs to go to the Seelie Court. Andy wasn\u2019t happy with that suggestion, but I think the others are warming to it, and we\u2019re planning on rescuing a poor Seelie faerie girl from her boring desk job so that she can help us get the Pestle and then get it back to her people, which will make her a hero, if a very fussy, uptight sort of hero.<br /> <br /> The faerie in question is named Trilla, and she\u2019s the Tinkerbell sort of faerie who flits about on lacy wings and sprinkles faerie dust all over the place. It\u2019s actually quite a spectacle when my mind is opened by absinthe, and I\u2019ve been drinking enough of it since we arrived here to keep things pretty interesting. Anyway, Trilla is a Seelie ambassador, and she\u2019s here to make sure the Unseelie aren\u2019t up to something nefarious with the Cauldron. I don\u2019t know what she did to get sentenced to a stodgy job like that, but we\u2019re planning on liberating her tomorrow, whether she likes it or not.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I\u2019m spending the night with Yrtalion. Kjell and Magnus have been making fun of me a lot because I prefer dashing, handsome, elegant men rather than rugged, boisterous, musclebound men. Kjell in particular has been very dismissive of my views toward romance and lovemaking. I\u2019m not really bothered by it, though. It\u2019s all in good fun, and honestly, Kjell\u2019s only making fun of me because he really likes me. He\u2019s just expressing it by acting like a schoolboy picking on his childhood crush.<br /> <br /> Of course, it doesn\u2019t help that I\u2019m naturally quite flirtatious. Actually, I don\u2019t think I\u2019m being flirtatious, but apparently when you are as open as I am with your observations, people think you\u2019re flirting with them. For instance, when I commented on how enchanting Trilla\u2019s faerie dust looks when it\u2019s dancing around her and singing to the tune of my absinthe, she assumed I was coming on to her, but I wasn\u2019t. I\u2019m not particularly interested in hooking up with a stuffy 10-inch tall faerie whose hair looks like she\u2019s been dancing on a Tesla coil.<br /> <br /> In other news, while we were discussing things with Trilla, Edward wandered off and bit some unseelie ladies and turned back into a guy, so he, at least, is back to normal. Of course, Edward\u2019s changing gender doesn\u2019t bother me any more than Zane\u2019s does, but Kjell is much more comfortable when Edward is a man.<br /> <br /> Anyway, our next stop is Naraka, which is where I suspected the Pestle would be. After a rest here with the Unseelie, we\u2019ll be heading to Yama\u2019s palace. My omens indicate that it might not be the only Underworld we have yet to visit, though . . .<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <b>In-flight to China</b><br /> <br /> It actually takes a lot to really piss me off, but I\u2019m pretty upset right now. I mean, hell, I know Edward\u2019s flight attendant/co-pilot/kept woman is a nymph and therefore prone to sexual encounters, but she has no right to invite a whole fucking football team onto the plane. Fortunately, she kicked most of them off before she picked us up in India, but not all of them. And then she started fucking the three obnoxious players she kept on board right there in the middle of the passage compartment of the plane. What the fuck? I mean, I love sex, but it is something you enjoy with your lover (or lovers, as the case may be) in private, not right there on the floor in front of everyone. Especially not with football players. I fucking HATE football players.<br /> <br /> Magnus was no happier about things than I was, and he browbeat the hell out of the athletes. It was pretty fucking scary! Even Edward was angry with Alodia and her boytoys, and no doubt a bit jealous too. Once Magnus was done with them, Ed kicked them out of the plane (we landed first, so they weren\u2019t hurt, though they ARE stranded naked somewhere in Italy).Still, Alodia fucked up big time, and the whole thing left a bad taste in my mouth. I was already unfavorably disposed toward Alodia because she\u2019s always being reckless with the plane and making us wait while she disentangles herself from her sexual exploits, and this experience has convinced me that I don\u2019t like her at all. And I don\u2019t like the fact that I don\u2019t like her, because I generally like almost everybody unless they are specifically mean to me.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I\u2019m sure you didn\u2019t want to hear all of that, Yisheng, but you\u2019re going to have to deal with it because I needed to vent.<br /> <br /> The good news is that we\u2019re on our way to meet with Pipa, and I\u2019m excited to see my girlfriend again. It\u2019s all because I impulsively extended our Underworld Odyssey by arranging a trip to Diyu. Actually, I don\u2019t really want to go to Diyu. It\u2019s one of the Underworlds I LEAST want to visit. But we\u2019re taking advantage of Pipa and Daji\u2019s mischief to maneuver our way into Yama\u2019s good graces, and my plan is to make a good impression on Nuwa an Daji by taking care of a little problem for them.<br /> <br /> Let me explain. First off, we visited Trilla again before leaving the Unseelie Realm, and I kept sharing absinthe with her until she was completely drunk. She kept doodling on her ledger, and I took the opportunity to embellish her doodles with quick, elegant ink paintings. The absinthe did the rest, and pretty soon, we were enjoying a spectacle of gracefully dancing brush strokes while Zane played her flute and Magnus strummed his guitar. Edward tried to snort some of Trilla\u2019s faerie dust, and before it was all said and done, I used a few crafty strokes of my brush and a bit of Taiyi to transform Trilla\u2019s ratty old dress into something far more stylish.<br /> <br /> Then we took her with us when we left for India to find our way into Naraka. She was happy to get away from her desk job, which is good, because triumphing over the oppressive chains of bureaucratic work has become one of our group\u2019s primary objectives. Once the alcohol wore off, though, Trilla was mortified that she had abandoned her assignment, but she\u2019ll get over it.<br /> <br /> With Trilla in tow and Kjell still tagging along, we went to India and then entered Naraka by diving into the Ganges river. Andy helped us transition to the Underworld, and then we spent the next four hours and forty minutes strolling down a cracked, barren road through the dry, grassy fields of Naraka. Then, right on schedule (because that\u2019s how the timing works in Naraka), we arrived at Yama\u2019s palace and were shown in by a solemn priest.<br /> <br /> Yama is very, very serious. He doesn\u2019t smile, and he doesn\u2019t have a sense of humor. Edward and Zane seemed fascinated by this. Still, he was quite hospitable and was more than willing to speak to us. When I introduced myself, he asked if I had been sent by Nuwa to arrange restitution for a soul Daji had recently eaten. The soul had purified itself and was preparing for reincarnation, and Daji needed a pure soul to overcome some sort of divine test. I guess she found a loophole. Yama was understandable annoyed, and I can understand where he\u2019s coming from, but it doesn\u2019t really bother me that Pipa eats virtuous priestesses or that Daji devours souls. I suppose it SHOULD, and the thought of doing those things myself is repellent, but I understand how dharma works. Pipa and Daji do those things because they\u2019re supposed to. It\u2019s who and what they are, so I find it hard to hold it against them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, when Yama asked if Nuwa sent me, I immediately answered yes. The look on Magnus\u2019 face when I said that was priceless and terrifying. I think he might be losing patience with me. It took some discussion before we could settle on appropriate restitution. It was Zane who gave me the perfect answer: she reminded me that Pipa had recently eaten a virtuous Chinese priestess! So I offered to bring that priestess\u2019s soul from Diyu and give it to Yama to replace the one Daji ate. Yama seemed satisfied with that, so we returned to the World to make arrangements to get to Diyu.<br /> <br /> Edward and Zane seemed okay with the plan, and Andy was reluctant but willing to go along with it. Magnus, however, was initially furious that Zane and I had engineered yet another detour through yet another Underworld. I had to explain to him that this was an opportunity for me to make a good impression on Nuwa and Daji. I\u2019m trying to find my place in my pantheon, after all, and I really don\u2019t think I\u2019m cut out for a desk job. I think I fit in better with Nuwa and her servants. I may not be as vicious and bloodthirsty as they are, but for better or worse, I\u2019m more prone to spontaneity and disorder than I am the strictly regimented order of the rest of the Bureaucracy. Once I explained that, Magnus understood my motivations better, and grudgingly agreed to help out. As he put it, if this keeps me out of a desk job with the Bureaucracy, it\u2019s worth it.<br /> <br /> We left Naraka and while we waited for Alodia to pick us up in the plane, I called Pipa and made arrangements to meet her in China. She\u2019s going with us into the Underworld to find the priestess\u2019s soul. If I have to go to Diyu, at least my girlfriend will be there to give me moral support.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m disappointed to note, however, that I\u2019m not sure my plan is really going to earn me any points with Daji or Nuwa. Pipa says they both more-or-less ignore Yama and his demands. This sort of thing is fairly common, and Nuwa usually files Yama\u2019s petitions away in the trash bin. I guess I should have consulted the Yi Jing before I settled on this scheme, . I haven\u2019t really received many omens lately, after all. Maybe Fate is being petulant because I\u2019ve been taking her for granted. In any event, it\u2019s too late to back out now, so I may as well go through with the plan. At the very least, it should help grease the wheels when we return to Naraka to search for the Pestle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> You can too be a pirate in a paddle boat! Even when it\u2019s all swan shaped. We showed it, me and Ned, even if she fucked off for the fun part. That just meant I had to yell Fire! and make the explosion noises and throw the snowballs.<br /> <br /> See, the Loa blokes gived us a pirate ship, to get home and all, yeah? But I promised I\u2019d make Ji-Woo a swan boat, so I did, once we wasn\u2019t underwater no more. Ji-Woo said it were proper metal, but Mags said it weren\u2019t even though it were all dark and shadowy. So I set us going round and round the big boat on account of it were big and slow and a spoilsport and we was small and fast and fun.<br /> <br /> That were getting all sorts of aggro from Mags, and he frozed all the water! He couldn\u2019t freeze all the water, not really, or else the big boat would be stopped too, so I threw the swan boat to where there were only bits of ice. Ned rode the boat all the way til it landed, but Ji-Woo stayed up in the air when it fell down again. Then Mags got the skeletons to shoot the cannons, boom splish! at us! They only hit us a little, so I took some of the underwater shadows and made me a littler cannon (on account of my boat were littler). I couldn\u2019t make the parts what go boom! so I just made those noises after Ned said fire cause that\u2019s how pirate ships work. Summat yells fire and then the cannons go boom. I didn\u2019t have no cannonballs, so I pretended and throwed snowballs instead.<br /> <br /> Ned fucked off after that, but me and Kel played pirates until we got back to Ireland. It were loads more fun than slapping people with pickles. I dunno why you\u2019d do that with a well ace pickle, but I think they meant sex stuff, on account of Mags said I had to be older, like Jester always did about sex stuff, and Ji-Woo said I had to be a boy, which is the same. I thought that were tickle though. You still shouldn\u2019t do that with a pickle any road.<br /> <br /> Kel still don\u2019t like the Unseely much. He runned with me instead of riding the horses cause they weren\u2019t growed up. I were still leading the way with the ladle though. Kel kept taking the piss out of Urtalien too, on account of him not being well hard like me and Kel. I guess he don\u2019t like the Seely neither, cause he took the piss out of Treela until Ji-Woo told him to bugger off, but nicer. Urtalian were still nice though. He\u2019d figured out where the other bit, the pestle, were. It were in Neraka, which I didn\u2019t know where it was, but Ji-Woo said it were Rajani\u2019s gang\u2019s dead place. I kinda hoped it\u2019d be in our dead place, but then there\u2019d be trouble or summat probably, so I guess it\u2019s good it\u2019s not. Kel says there\u2019s ocean of milk in Neraka, which sounds right tasty, but Ned said that meant breasts, which aren\u2019t tasty at all.<br /> <br /> Urtalien weren\u2019t too happy, nor Andy, when Ji-Woo said we should maybe give one of the bits to the Seely. They still made time though, Ji-Woo and Urtalien. See, Treela from the Seely found out about the cauldron cause of the torc. She\u2019s only like 2 of my hands tall and has really crazy hair, and wings, but not as pretty as Ji-Woo\u2019s. Ned thought she was far away, she was so small. Then again, Ned were proper high. The little fairy lady didn\u2019t like that. She didn\u2019t like nobody talking about her fairy dust neither, unless they was courting, which is like bonking, but old fashioned, I think. She wants to court Balder, and that\u2019s why she won\u2019t talk to Gloria for Ji-Woo. It\u2019s ok though, on account of Ji-Woo sent Yi-sheng to ask her what were going on.<br /> <br /> Treela thought the Unseely were gonna make a zombie apocklips, which is bad, cause people might die from zombies. That\u2019s why she didn\u2019t want them to get the cauldron or nothing. Cause they\u2019re capreeshis. Ji-Woo says we are too. Treela likes using big words. Ji-Woo tried to get her to have a tiny cup of absinthe, and said later we ought nick her so she can have fun too. It\u2019s right and all - she didn\u2019t look like she were having much fun, even if she said she were wild and free. She had glasses and paperwork! That\u2019s the opposite. For now though me and Mags are gonna play music while the others snog.<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t even know how it\u2019s my fault this time. But I guess it is. I did remember how Pipa ate that priestess. But I didn\u2019t eat the priestess, or the Indian bint\u2019s soul the Yama bloke were so upset about. I didn\u2019t even nick Treela! She came by herself.<br /> <br /> See, Mags told this silly story about when Thor got all dressed up like a girl and tricked some giants. He made it so we drinked every time loads of things happened, so Treela decided she wanted to go on an adventure too, and draw using regular sized pencils and Mags broke her desk. He don\u2019t like desks. Treela kept saying things were the tits too. Ji-Woo made her fancy clothes, and Ned made her a joint. He\u2019s a boy again now, so it were ok that Ji-Woo stole his shirt to make into little clothes. Ellodia were still a girl, but she\u2019s a slag anyhow, so she took her shirt off too.<br /> <br /> We all took naps on the plan, cept for Ned on account of he were driving. I played Ji-Woo a lullaby and then falled asleep under the chairs. It\u2019s right cozy there. I should remember to put the glass scorpion thing in the plane. It\u2019s even more comfier.<br /> <br /> Once we\u2019d got to the Gangees River (and knocked over loads of people\u2019s houses, cause Ned is not the best at landing), I fixed Ji-Woo\u2019s hangover and we all hopped in the river. Ned drank some first, so\u2019s he could make an antidote and all, but nobody else drunk it, so he didn\u2019t get to spit at nobody. After we was swimming for a bit, we showed up at a big open place, with one road and a whole bunch of grass. Ned wanted to smoke it, but it were just lawn grass, not grass-grass.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo said it were gonna take 4 hours and 20 minutes no matter what we walked like, so Mags just took 4 steps and zooped up at the end. I walked in slow motion, sometimes, and did somersaults in the grass sometimes. That were a little fun at least. Yama were dead boring. He didn\u2019t look like he ever did somersaults or played pirates. He were all over green though, with red clothes. It were kinda like Christmas, cept he didn\u2019t have a big beard or a bell or nothing. Kel said he were a god on account of he didn\u2019t snog his sister, which is right strange. He thought we\u2019d come from Noo-Wa and Da-Ji, and Ji-Woo said we did. He were all upset cause Da-Ji ate summat who was all pure and were going to be reincarnated. And cause Ji-Woo\u2019s gang makes fun of him a lot.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo didn\u2019t want to rat Da-Ji out, and he wouldn\u2019t say nothing else who would make up for it. That\u2019s when I thought of the live person Pipa\u2019s ate, and maybe we could trade her ghost? Ji-Woo thought that were a great idea, cept she didn\u2019t want to go to Di-Woo. Mags were well upset though. But it were to make Da-Ji and Noo-Wa like Ji-Woo so\u2019s she wouldn\u2019t have to have a desk job, so he said ok, cause he really don\u2019t like desks.<br /> <br /> So now we\u2019ve got the plane back and we\u2019re going to meet Pipa at Di-Woo. Ellodia brought some footballers with her and so Mags is yelling at them on account of they\u2019re banging in the main room. It\u2019s right funny to watch Mags get all yelly at summat not me. And this time it\u2019s not my fault, even if Andy said!<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLVII</i><br /> <br /> So\u2026I did not have a specific way to deal with Trilla planned, but shainghaiing her into a magical adventure wasn\u2019t it. Not that I am complaining, mind, I think it was hilarious.<br /> <br /> Of course, I also thought provoking them with Alodia was hilarious, so my judgment is suspect.<br /> <br /> I should mention the Priestess thing was all Zane\u2019s player\u2019s idea. This is why I don\u2019t pre-plan how they will solve problems; it is more fun to watch them work. I had not, truthfully, planned a Di Yu detour, but that\u2019s fine, should be interesting.<br /> <br /> So yea, good on them for thinking on their feet. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 04-22-2015, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T02:15:51-07:00","id":507868,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to watch the group try to get back on track. Let\u2019s see if they succeed.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLVIII</i><br /> <br /> <u>Six Underground Part XII</u><br /> <br /> <b>Ji-Woo\u2019s Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Diyu</b><br /> <br /> So, this entry is going in the private journal because Yisheng does not need to put this one on the official Bureaucracy record, what with us kidnapping a virtuous spirit from Diyu and everything. Speaking of kidnapping, it turns out Zane is pretty good at it. She didn\u2019t believe us at first when we told her so. She even seemed offended. But then we reminded her of Rumpelstiltskin, and Treela, and now the virtuous priestess\u2019s spirit, and poor Zane had to admit we were right. Wouldn\u2019t it be amazing if her legend grew into some sort of fae kidnapping, changeling thing? Of course she would only kidnap children if their parents deserved it. \u201cYou better be good to your children, or else the Zanewoogandr will come steal them away!\u201d Or something.<br /> <br /> Maybe that would be awful.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we infiltrated Diyu and met Pipa there. I was so happy to see her! She was a bit more reserved, but I think she liked the spine whip I gave her. While we were navigating the Bureaucracy offices in Diyu, I tore up some paperwork I stole from a passing functionary demon and used the scraps to read some omens. I learned that the priestess\u2019s soul was already waiting outside the 10th Court to be reborn. She didn\u2019t have to do a tour through any of the hells, which is nice. The omens also revealed to me the exact location of the last piece of the Dark Cauldron set: the Pestle is in Kakola, Naraka\u2019s Realm of the Unforgivable, a bottomless pit where the Devas cast the worst and most irredeemable of souls. That sounds awful. Also, the maggot hag, whom Fate refers to as the Matron, is already on her way there! So we have to hurry. Magnus was grumpy about that. He thinks we\u2019re wasting time in Diyu, and maybe he\u2019s right. After all, I volunteered to steal this soul mainly to make a splash with Nuwa and Daji, and they probably won\u2019t care all that much that I\u2019ve smoothed things over with Yama. On the other hand, Daji at least might be pretty amused that we are kidnapping a soul from the Bureaucracy to give it to the Devas.<br /> <br /> Of course, I\u2019m still worried about Gloria, especially after the omens told me she was no longer in Helheim (she\u2019s in Michigan now). That\u2019s good, but I also learned that Hel DID have her way with Gloria . . . sort of. But not like she wanted. I don\u2019t really know what that means, but I\u2019m dying to find out. This Gloria thing really has a grip on my curiosity. Also, Magnus was unhappy to learn that Yisheng had delivered my message, which means Gloria might have a thing for him now. Maybe. I didn\u2019t receive any omens about that. The good news, though, is that Angrboda didn\u2019t get any of our DNA, so I guess the Zanewoogandr won\u2019t be stealing children from misbehaving parents any time soon.<br /> <br /> Also, Pipa is hot.<br /> <br /> But seriously, Andy needs to stop messing with my omens. He and Treela started playing Memory with the scraps of paper I was using to read Fate. Gods know if that changed my readings. Actually, I\u2019m getting really tired of all these shenanigans. Sometimes I feel like I can\u2019t even have a conversation without one of us going off on some tangent or doing something absurd. I\u2019m pretty laid back, but I think this Underworld journey is getting to me, because I really need some chill time, and I wish we could stay on track. Normally, when chaos sends things off the rails like this, I just leave and settle down somewhere else. But I can\u2019t do that now because I have to be more responsible.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we hatched an amazing plan to get the priestess to come with us willingly, if under false pretenses. We decided that was better than going through all the Bureaucracy paperwork, because who has time for that? The plan was to have Pipa sneak into the holding area outside the 10th Court where the priestess\u2019s soul was waiting to be reborn. Pipa would menace the spirit, frightening the priestess so much that when Zane showed up and offered to help her escape, she would hop right into Zane\u2019s kidnapping bag (the one we used to get Rumpelstiltskin back to England). Pipa kept talking about eating one of the priestess\u2019s arms just to make it really convincing, but I told her she shouldn\u2019t do that.<br /> <br /> So, Edward caused a distraction by rocking out in the office of the functionary demon who was overseeing the 10th Court, and Pipa approached the priestess. She said, \u201cYou were a good dinner, and you\u2019ll be a better dessert!\u201d Then she took a bite out of the priestess\u2019s shoulder. Oh Pipa. Sigh.<br /> <br /> The priestess tried to run while guards converged on Pipa, but Andy used his illusions to confuse the guards, and Pipa escaped. Zane intercepted the priestess and convinced her to jump into the bag so that we could get her to safety, and then we left the 10th Court as quickly as we could. I used the chaos of Edward\u2019s impromptu one-man concert to steal the priestess\u2019s paperwork, so there should be little evidence that she was ever even there! Magnus wasn\u2019t happy that Edward carved \u201cGrimstad\u201d into one of the 10th Court desks. He doesn\u2019t like anything that ties us to our misdeeds. He was super-grumpy, so I reminded him that this was all to keep me out of a desk job in the Bureaucracy. That didn\u2019t help. He\u2019s still upset at Zane for her role in all of this.<br /> <br /> So now we\u2019re off to Naraka again.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m tired of Underworlds, so I\u2019ll be glad when this odyssey is over. I\u2019ve been feeling a little put-upon lately, and the fact that I can\u2019t just leave makes it worse. I mean, I know I\u2019m largely responsible for extending the length of our journey at least twice, and I\u2019m okay with that. It\u2019s just that all the random crap that keeps happening in between is starting to get on my nerves.<br /> <br /> Also, I\u2019m not sure Pipa is very happy about me wanting to get involved more with Nuwa and Daji. I thought maybe she would be happy for the opportunity to work together a little more, and she hasn\u2019t been very excited about it. I think she\u2019s jealous of me and is worried that Daji or Nuwa might steal me away from her. I told her she doesn\u2019t have to worry about that, but I don\u2019t think she believes me. It makes me sad.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <b>Naraka</b><br /> <br /> We are on our way to Kakola, the Realm of the Unforgivable, and the bottomless pit where the Pestle lies forgotten. The Pestle isn\u2019t in the pit, of course. It really is bottomless. But it\u2019s somewhere near it.<br /> <br /> We turned the priestess over to Yama. He didn\u2019t seem pleased\u2014I don\u2019t think he ever does\u2014but he seemed satisfied, and was courteous enough to grant us free passage through Naraka. We headed to Kakola as quickly as we could, and managed to catch up to Indra, who was on his way there to repel the invading forces from Crom Cruach and the Deathlords. He was completely drunk in a terrible hurry. He shared some soma with us. I hadn\u2019t had any before, so I tried it, and it hit me hard. I spent most of the rest of the trip completely drunk.<br /> <br /> The problem with Indra is that he is loud and obnoxious and he likes to fight. And he wasn\u2019t content to just charge through the jungle, beating up poor Nemean beasts just because they were there. He had to get US involved too. I was just trying to stay focused and out of the way when suddenly the big red-skinned bastard threw a gigantic tiger at us. I completely lost my shit and threw it back with Taiyi, which annoyed Zane and Magnus, both of whom wanted to beat something up. Zane went charging after the tiger, and Magnus would have joined her if an enraged Nemean hippo hadn\u2019t blundered into him.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I didn\u2019t know what the fuck was going on, but I wanted it to stop. Clearly, we weren\u2019t going to be able to avoid a fight, so I whipped out my guns and started shooting. The soma was screwing with my aim, though, so my bullets flew wild. I had to pause a moment and refocus to gather my wits while Andy blessed me, and then I was able to help finish the fight. Edward insisted on taking the tiger\u2019s corpse with us so he could get a huge tiger-skin rug later, so Andy raised it as a zombie and it\u2019s still following us around.<br /> <br /> I told Pipa not to let me have soma again if we might be going into battle. She agreed that would be for the best.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we just passed through a part of the jungle that is cloaked in a deep darkness within which one must one\u2019s darkest fears. I thought that actually sounded interesting. Not fun, mind you, and certainly terrifying, but I\u2019m actually rather curious what my darkest fears are. I mean, I face claustrophobia all the time, but surely that isn\u2019t my deepest, DARKEST fear. And I really felt like that might have been an important step on our Underworld odyssey. So I was very disappointed when Indra yelled, \u201cWe don\u2019t have time for this!\u201d and summoned a lightning storm that cleared the darkness long enough for us to pass through without being harassed by shadows of our inner demons. Magnus, Kjell, Zane and Edward really seemed to get into the spirit of things, though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, our raucous little band has almost reached Kakola. I hope things go well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> I guess Andy\u2019s right, and I am a master kidnapper. Only I never napped kids, just nasty Rumpole Wilsons and ghosty ladies. I weren\u2019t even lying too much like he said, on account of I did stop Pipa from eating her up. But I am good at nicking things, even when they isn\u2019t things but people instead. I wouldn\u2019t go nicking no kids from their mums and dads though, unless their mums and dads were rotten, yeah? And if I did, I wouldn\u2019t go giving them to no whore.<br /> <br /> Any road, our plan worked well good. We had to go into a big cave place to get to Di-Woo, on account of Mags didn\u2019t want to get stuck jumping down no well. Ji-Woo weren\u2019t too happy, about that nor the footballers, but she\u2019s not good at being grumpy, not like Mags is. She smiles too much. But that\u2019s ok, seeing as her smile is right pretty. Pipa met us once we was inside, so that made her less grumpy. Specially since Pipa liked her present so much.<br /> <br /> Di-Woo is right strange. All the blokes what work there have animal heads, like they was in a farm, horses and oxes, yeah? There\u2019s loads of paperwork, but I didn\u2019t have to steal none on account of Ji-Woo tore some random papers up and they said where the priestess what Pipa ate was. They also said where the pestle was, and Gloria. She\u2019s in Michigan, but Ned thinks it\u2019s Minnesota, or maybe Wisconsin. We\u2019re gonna go visit her, but after we get done. Mags said so. The tore up papers also said the half-lady with the maggots was trying to get at the pestle, but weren\u2019t there yet.<br /> <br /> We decided to steal the priestess instead of talking with Crimson Shadow, he\u2019s one of them blokes with the oxes heads, on account of Mags doesn\u2019t like desks, and Ji-Woo don\u2019t like paperwork. Treela kept going on about kidnapping, and Andy did too, cept he were saying it\u2019s ok, mostly cause the little fairy said it weren\u2019t. He also said that diamonds came from her ass, which don\u2019t sound comfortable at all.<br /> <br /> We was trying to be sneaky, so when Ji-Woo changed clothes into official type clothes, I made me some what looked like it. It were comfortable and all flowy, even if it were a dress. Pipa\u2019s right though, there\u2019s loads of things to grab onto if you was fighting summat dressed up like that. Andy used Treela\u2019s dust to change his clothes too, and Ned put on a tablecloth.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo were gonna use her gaver badge thing that were really a fancy mirror makeup thing to get them to let us in, but instead Ned started talking to him. He were talking proper bollocks, and rocking out, and carving Grimstad on the desk so\u2019s Ji-Woo could stamp it and everything. It were right distracting. Then me and Pipa snuck in, I was the sneakiest, and Pipa bit the priestess! She weren\u2019t supposed to do that, she were just supposed to scare her so\u2019s I could rescue her by putting her in the bag Jester gave me for Rumpole. Least she\u2019ll have some foods in there. It\u2019s a good place to put it on account of nobbut\u2019s gonna look in and nick it. Maybe it\u2019ll be distracting from the biting bit. Andy took the mick out of me when I asked if he could fix ghosts, on account of he does death-y things, cause I\u2019m supposed to do heal-y things, but I can\u2019t seeing as she\u2019s a ghost. Maybe Yama can fix ghosts.<br /> <br /> Things got crazy for a bit, but Pipa were able to get out cause Kel made her look like a guard, and so we went back to the plane. There weren\u2019t no footballers this time, but there was two of the blokes with horse heads dancing. They buggered off though. Ned tried to get Ellodia to go to Minnesota, but Ji-Woo and Mags said no. Pipa wanted to eat Ellodia, and Ji-Woo said maybe, but Ned said no that time.<br /> <br /> When we get back to the Gangees River place, we\u2019re gonna get to jump out of the plane, on account of me not wanting Ned and Ellodia to knock over everybody\u2019s houses again. Mags is being grumpy about that too, even though it\u2019s ace, cause it\u2019ll be fast and all. But that\u2019s why it\u2019ll be ace!<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> Dad -<br /> <br /> It were bloody brill! We did get to jump out of the plane! Well, Mags pushed Ned, and Ji-Woo and Pipa and Andy flied off, but Mags and Kel dived in, and I jumped in sploosh! with a giant splash. And nobody\u2019s tent house thing got knocked over!<br /> <br /> The rest of it were pretty exciting too, after we walked for forever again and gave the priestess to Yama. This time Ned told stories and Mags sang, so the walking were fun at least. But after that, we had to catch up with a big red bloke named Indra, what had the best booze. It made your head get big and red and made me better at punching and everything. He had a big beard too, but not a Christmas-y beard or nothing. He were proper excitable. He yelled everything. And punches giant tigers!<br /> <br /> I were gonna go help him punch tigers, cause that\u2019s ace, but then he throwed us one! But then Ji-Woo throwed it back without even touching it, so I runned and jumped on it. It were proper hard to hit, but I did anyways, but it were well hard too, so I mostly just knocked it off balance and Ji-Woo shot it lots. She had to squeeze her head first though, on account of it were too big for her to shoot properly. Andy helped too, but throwing her some of Treela\u2019s tiny pants. There were also a gianter hippo, what Ned and Mags roughed up. And a big gorilla, what Kel took care of. Indra started hitting one of his tigers with one of his hippos, and then decided it were taking too long.<br /> <br /> So he got even bigger, and throwed lightning everywhere, and nutted trees and all the giant animals fucked off. Ned wanted to skin the tiger, but there weren\u2019t time, so he carried it after Andy made it come back alive and I were riding it. Indra kept throwing lightning about, specially once we got to the dark bits. We was supposed to confront fears what kept us from being righteous, or summat like that, but he said we got no time, like, We! Do not! Have time for this! and lit it all up with loads and loads of lightning. I think Indra\u2019s my favorite from these blokes. Mags\u2019s too.<br /> <br /> On the other side of the dark bits, there were all sorts of fighting. Undeads, and charnal giants and dragon skeletons were fighting loads of pain demon things. There were a big hole they was fighting around, what Ji-Woo said were bottomless and Ned said had the pestle at the bottom. There were also a waterfall into the hole, what were kinda stinky. Indra ran right off into everything, and we got ready to bust some undeads up, and find the pestle.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLVIII</i><br /> <br /> The Bag was of course from the <u>Twilight Zone</u> storyline. Which was a hilarious moment when Saltmarsh Andy was claiming Zane was a professional kidnapper, which she denied\u2026then had to admit she had a magic kidnapping bag.<br /> <br /> Conclusion of this story next time\u2026comments and questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-08-2015, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T22:45:42-07:00","id":539246,"title":"","content":"Last session of our Six Underground Story, let\u2019s catch up<br /> <i><br /> Session XLIX</i><br /> <br /> <u>Six Underground Part XIII</u><br /> <b><br /> Ji-Woo's Visions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Naraka</b><br /> <br /> I am so glad our Underworld odyssey is over. I hoped that it would end with a big, triumphant bang, with everyone being really badass and glorious and all. But I should know better than to get my hopes up. I mean, sure, some of us were incredibly glorious, and the battle was dramatic and amazing, if you\u2019re into that kind of thing. But I spent most of it with maggots crawling out of my eyes or into my nose and mouth. I don\u2019t know how I held it together and did my job. If Edward hadn\u2019t come along to save me, I think I would have completely lost my shit. As it was, the fight pretty much broke me by the end, so it\u2019s a good thing Pipa and Zane were there to give me the moral support I needed.<br /> <br /> Things started out well enough. Deva demons were fighting against a small army of charnel giants led by five deathlords, one of whom was mounted on a sleek skeletal dragon. The maggot-hag Matron was calling the shots, and she made a bee-line for us as soon as we arrived. Magnus went berserk and charged the enemy head on with Edward and Kjell in his wake. Andy laid low and supported us with his magic, as usual. Pipa transformed into her demon form and engaged the charnel giants alongside Indra. Meanwhile, Zane made her way to the edge of the bottomless Pit of the Unforgivable and I soared over it, looking for the Pestle, which I suspected was resting somewhere in broken Hindu ruins covering the upper walls of the pit.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Zane and I did not go unnoticed. The Matron leapt on Zane, who fought back hard but got a face full of maggots for her trouble. The worms were disgusting, and way too big, and they WERE the Matron. The maggots tried to burrow into Zane\u2019s mind so that the Matron could possess her, but Zane is made of sterner stuff than that.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the Matron knew exactly what I was up to and tried to stop me. She did something that caused maggots to crawl from my eye sockets. It was excruciatingly painful, and I started to freak out, screaming the whole time. I barely managed to keep it together, though, and even though I couldn\u2019t see, I focused my mystical senses on my surroundings, which granted me a clairvoyant view of the battlefield and the inside of the pit. Pretty smart, huh? Fortunately, the maggots swarming from my eyes stopped after a few moments and I could see again, but I think I\u2019ll be traumatized by that experience for the rest of my life!<br /> <br /> Anyway, it was about then that one of the Deathlords Magnus was fighting hit me with his plague magic. I sickened quickly, and as the weakness overcame me, I faltered in my flight and dropped straight into the pit. I was fine, really. It didn\u2019t take me long to regain control. But I was still weak, and I wouldn\u2019t be able to handle it if another one of the Deathlords decided I needed more of the same, so I was glad when Zane came leaping into the pit screaming my name in a panic. I caught her, spun us both around, and then launched her out of the pit, and while we were touching briefly, she healed my illness. Everything would have been just peachy except that the Matron, who was still squirming around on Zane as a group of big, disgusting maggots, decided that I would make a much more delicious snack. She swarmed onto me and started trying to burrow into my head. I tried to shake her off, but I couldn\u2019t. I couldn\u2019t even grab her and toss the maggots into the pit! They were too fast and wriggly and slimy and oh my god I\u2019m going to vomit and then have a breakdown and then vomit again.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Sorry about that, Yisheng. But the Matron really did a number on me. Anyway, I couldn\u2019t shake her off, but I was able to divide my attention enough to keep her at bay while still looking for the Pestle. Also, I screamed a lot. Unfortunately, Zane was also having a hard time. The deathlord on the dragon was shooting her with black arrows, and her shots were true enough to pierce Zane\u2019s tough hide. I had to help my best friend, so I whipped out my pistols and started shooting the deathlord and her dragon, not that I did much damage at first.<br /> <br /> With everything else I had going on, I couldn\u2019t very well keep up with what was happening with Magnus, Edward, and Andy, but I could feel Andy\u2019s blessings giving me the strength and skill I needed to fight despite the maggots gnawing at my flesh. Then the deathlord\u2019s dragon swooped down, snapped up Edward and swallowed him. He went careening through its empty rib cage screaming something like, \u201cI\u2019m Ji-Woo!\u201d because he was flying . . . sort of. Then he fell out of the rib cage and the dragon swatted him toward Magnus with its tail.<br /> <br /> Magnus didn\u2019t look twice. He just saw something flying his way and with a ferocious roar, he caught it and threw it back at the dragon with every ounce of his berserker strength. It wasn\u2019t until after Edward was flying back at the dragon that Magnus realized what he had done! The look on his face was priceless! Edward\u2019s tough, though, so he was fine. He cracked a few of the dragon\u2019s ribs and then bounced off.<br /> <br /> By that point, the Matron had worn me down. I couldn\u2019t stand her maggots all over me any more. One was starting to burrow into the back of my head, and I could feel them squirming their way under my clothes. To make matters worse, the dragon had just spewed a stream of maggots all over me as I was maneuvering around it. I felt violated and sick, and I couldn\u2019t hold it together anymore. Then, just as I was about to completely lose it and have a breakdown, Edward came falling right at me, yelling, \u201cI got you, Ji-Woo!\u201d I was so shocked I didn\u2019t even flutter out of the way, and Edward slammed into me and we tumbled through the air together for a moment before I lost him and he went flailing to the ground. He took my top with him along with all the maggots! I was finally maggot free! Edward was my savior!<br /> <br /> Also, I was somehow wearing his Hawaiian shirt.<br /> <br /> Anyway, free of the maggots, I was able to gather my wits and my composure, and that\u2019s when I spotted the Pestle resting in an alcove on a ledge some distance from the lip of the pit. I telepathically told Zane where to find it, and she zoomed off into the pit. She can scramble over walls like they\u2019re level ground, so I wasn\u2019t worried about her.<br /> <br /> Then I turned my attention to the dragon and its deathlord rider. I was sick and tired of that jerk shooting at my friend, and I was upset about the maggots, so I unleashed hell on her. A few shots later, and the deathlord was little more than a twice-dead corpse plummeting into the bottomless pit.<br /> <br /> The fight was nearly over. I surveyed the battlefield in time to see Magnus freeze the Matron-maggots in a colossal sheet of ice along the cliff edge. Then he slammed his axe into the ground with an earth-shattering blow that sent one whole edge of the pit cascading into the bottomless depths. The Matron-maggots went down with it.<br /> <br /> A few charnel giants were left. Edward must have landed right in the middle of them, because they were trying their best to beat him to a pulp. I soared down to the ground, drawing some of Indra\u2019s lightning with me. I channeled the lightning through my guns and then blasted the four giants with four quick shots, one each. The winds and lightning followed each starfire bullet, slamming into the giants with enough force to blast them over the edge and into the bottomless pit. Edward almost went with them, but Zane caught him just as she sprang up and out of the pit with the Pestle safely in hand.<br /> <br /> With the battle over, I just collapsed to my knees, voice hoarse from screaming and arms wrapped around me as I tried to stop myself from shaking. Yisheng, I was deeply traumatized by those inescapable maggots, burrowing into my flesh and mind. I was miserable. Pipa showed up then and did her best to comfort me. We got out of Naraka pretty quickly after that. I needed a long shower. We all did.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <b><br /> Berlin</b><br /> <br /> We had a legendary celebration once we all got back to the world and managed to clean up. At Magnus\u2019 insistence, we all got laid, even Zane, who turned into rakish guy Zane for the occasion. We went to Berghain, of course. I stuck with Pipa. I needed some serious chill out time, so I got lost in my absinthe and Pipa\u2019s arms in the chill trance lounge. I was probably a little more clingy than usual. I was feeling really vulnerable, and I needed my girlfriend. She\u2019s always affectionate and sassy, but she\u2019s not always the warmest of companions. I guess being cynical, jaded, and predatory will do that. This time, though, she went out of her way to be sweet and caring. I love her so much.<br /> <br /> Sadly, Kjell\u2019s gone back home. I\u2019ll miss the big guy. He was fun.<br /> <br /> Later, we made sure Treela returned safely to the Seelie Court with the Pestle, and then took the Ladle to the Loa. Everyone seems content with the arrangement, even if the Unseelie Court is a little miffed that they didn\u2019t get to keep everything, just in case they need an army of undead someday. Whatever.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> So, I finally met up with Gloria in Michigan. That\u2019s where she lives, apparently. She is very charming, but not especially my type. Sadly, I don\u2019t think she\u2019s Magnus\u2019 type either, though maybe that\u2019s for the best. After all, Magnus has a kid on the way with another woman.<br /> <br /> I would like to say that my curiosity has been sated, but it hasn\u2019t . Sure, I know what Gloria was up to in Helheim now, but that knowledge has only unearthed new mysteries. It turns out Gloria was sent to Hel by Frigg, Sif, and Freya to befriend Hel and find out what Hel\u2019s up to lately. She\u2019s been gathering a number of mysterious relics, and Frigg especially wanted to know why. Freya was the one delivering supplies for Gloria\u2019s dolls to use for their puzzles and traps.<br /> <br /> In the end, Gloria didn\u2019t really learn much about Hel\u2019s plans before Sif swept in and rescued her, though she DOES suspect that Frigg has a theory about where the relics are coming from and why they are in Helheim. So now, of course, I\u2019m very curious about what Hel\u2019s up to. It\u2019s probably not good.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Gloria did confess that she ended up feeling sorry for Hel. The two of them even became close. She wasn\u2019t very specific about that, but she DID insist that she and Hel did not sleep together. Now Hel is sending Gloria relics and flowers, still trying to woo her, I suppose. It\u2019s kind of pathetic, really. I asked if Grimstad\u2019s\u2019 love song and my letter had awakened any interest in Magnus, and she did seem intrigued, but she\u2019s fallen head-over-heels for Sif. She wouldn\u2019t stop gushing about how Sif heroically charged in to rescue her from the Underworld, all golden locks and radiant beauty and sparkles and rainbows. You\u2019d think Gloria was some sort of fairytale princess. I mean, that IS how her legend is shaping up. Obviously.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the Bureaucracy knows anything about Hel\u2019s collection of relics? Get on that, Yisheng. I need to know!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zane\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Mags said it were my job to keep Ji-Woo safe, and that were my only job on account of me not doing good when I has two jobs, like when I were supposed to nick the priestess and keep Ji-Woo from stamping things. I\u2019d\u2019ve been better at the stopping Ji-Woo part if I knowed she shouldn\u2019t be stamping things. But Mags were getting all fighty angry so I didn\u2019t argue none. I did have a bit of a butcher's though, for starters.<br /> <br /> Course, maybe he\u2019s right, seeing as the first things what happened was the old maggot lady making maggots come out of Ji-Woo\u2019s eyes. I gave the bint what for and nutted her good, but that just made her turn into more maggots and try to get to my brains again. My brains is well hard too though, so she didn\u2019t get any of them. But then Ji-Woo screamed again (she did that a lot - I don\u2019t think she likes maggots none) and started falling into the pit instead of flying like she were supposed to! She looked all sicky and her eyes was closed and it were right awful.<br /> <br /> I jumped out after her to see if I could fix the sick and maybe knock her into a wall so\u2019s she wouldn\u2019t be falling for forever and ever and ever. She waked up when I fixed her, and started flying properly again, and even caught me so\u2019s I spinned around and landed just on the edge of the pit. I tried to give the maggot bint the twos, but she had gotten all maggoty on Ji-Woo when she caught me! That were not on, but they was both proper high up, so I couldn\u2019t do nothing.<br /> <br /> There was five of them death lords and 4 charnal giant blokes, and a dragon, like I said, what were fighting us. Indra and Pipa and Kel and the demon-y blokes were fighting loads more too. Indra kept getting bigger and bigger and more red. He\u2019s the best. Cept for us and Mags. He thought Kel were ace too, on account of Kel were cutting the dragon\u2019s wing off while they was riding it over the pit. Boys are right strange.<br /> <br /> Ned and Mags were busting up the death lords and death lady lords but good, cept one was up on the dragon what kept breathing out maggots. That one kept shooting me with arrows what hurt like a dickens. The bugger shot one in my hand while I tried to crawl out! Then the two giants axed me into the cliff, but I came back poof! in their shadows and tried to push them off the cliff. They was too big, so I just gave them a two finger salute and turned invisible.<br /> <br /> Then things got weird. The dragon tried to eat Ned, but he just fell out of its arse, on account of it were a skeleton dragon. Then it hit Ned with its tail at Mags, and Ned thought he were flying so he said he were Ji-Woo. Ji-Woo flied into the dragon\u2019s middle, so she said she was Edmund and shot the the death bow lord lady, on account of she\u2019s my mate, Ji-Woo is.<br /> <br /> Then Mags caught Ned and was all fighty angry, so he throwed him back up at the bow death lady lord. Ned smacked her on the nose, bop! but then falled down again. Ji-Woo was screaming some more, on account of the maggot bint, so Ned traded shirts on his way down, cept Ji-Woo\u2019s shirt weren\u2019t real, so he didn\u2019t have a shirt no more and she had one of them Hawaiian shirts and it weren\u2019t buttoned up or nothing. But all the maggots falled off! Plus, Ji-Woo found the pestle and told me where it was in my brains. It\u2019s much more good to have Ji-Woo in my brains than maggots.<br /> <br /> The pestle were down in the pit, so I used my superpower to walk on walls. I had to run really far, but I\u2019m proper fast, so I found it right quick and just where Ji-Woo said and then put it in the Rumpole bag. On the way back up, the whole cliff fell off over my head. I almost knocked my hat all the way down the bottomless pit! I grabbed it at the last minute though. The rocks and stuff was all full of ice and frozed up maggots, so hopefully the maggot bint is falling forever and ever and ever.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo throwed giants in the pit too, but not at me. She stoled Indra\u2019s lightning and shot them kapow! so hard they falled off. Ned were climbing on of thems, so he falled off too, but I jumped proper quick and catched him all invisible so he thought he were flying again. He started talking like a church man, but in Spanish. Ned is even more strange than most boys.<br /> <br /> When I got up carrying him, the dragon and the last of the death lords blokes was running away. Ji-Woo weren\u2019t too good, but she were just ew-sicky on account of the maggots being yucky and not sick-sick and plus she screamed enough she couldn\u2019t talk right. I gived her hugs and then Pipa did too. Mags told her to get a shower. That\u2019ll make her feel better for certain sure. Showers feel well nice.<br /> <br /> I got to keep the pestle for now, on account of it\u2019s too big for Treela. She gets it later though and Andy\u2019s gang gets the cauldron and the Loa gang gets the ladle, so\u2019s they can all be safe and everybody\u2019s happy, or not happy. Ned kept asking me for it to use for his weed, but Ji-Woo gived it to me, so he doesn\u2019t get it.<br /> <br /> Ji-Woo just came back from the shower and Mags said we was all gonna go get laid, me included, so Ji-Woo winked at me and pulled my ear and now I\u2019m boy Zane again. Time to have fun!<br /> <br /> Zane<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLIX</i><br /> <br /> Sorry about the break. We finished the story, then the next session Ji-Woo\u2019s player had to miss and the next one I was to be out of town on that night, so no game for two usual meetings. There will be a game in two weeks and new journals continuing in four. Will see you then.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu 